window.FWN_RE_EVOLUTION_ONLINE_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_RE_EVOLUTION_ONLINE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1401,"title":"Chapter 1401: No favorites","paragraphs":["Liam’s eyes locked onto the golden hue dancing before him, shimmering like a mirage against the blood-red sky. \"Let’s see what you really are.\" He dashed forward to grasp the golden hue before it disappeared. He only barely managed to do it when the next one sprang up a few miles ahead of him.","He would have missed it entirely if it had not been for one of his minions loitering around the area. Liam once again switched places with his minion and continued moving forward to grab the next golden wisp.","He was losing minions left and right but he did not care. A treasure in this place was likely big enough to compensate all of his losses.","Liam instantly dismissed his other minions in the other parts of this world and sent out all of them spread in the direction he was headed toward. Even if he missed a single golden hue, he would lose the tracks and the treasure at the end of this trail.","As if this was not complicated enough, Liam suddenly had a weird feeling. It was as if he was being watched. As if he was being followed.","He couldn’t exactly pinpoint why he felt it or where this person might be watching him from but he got a strong feeling that something was off and he was inclined to trust his gut instincts.","A prickling sensation crawled up the back of Liam’s neck. He halted mid-step, scanning the horizon in every direction— an ocean of sand streaked golden beneath that unnerving crimson sky—until his gaze landed on nothing in particular.","There was no obvious sign of a pursuer, no telltale shimmer that betrayed another’s presence, or even a blip in the mana. Yet still, the feeling persisted. Even when he jumped from one soul body to another, the person somehow stuck to him.","\"Show yourself,\" Liam muttered under his breath.","Silence greeted him, broken only by the hushed whispers of the desert sands. He waited for one more moment before quickly turning and following his golden wisp.","Liam pressed forward, ignoring the lingering chill that clung to his spine. The golden wisp danced just ahead, drifting tantalizingly through the shimmering waves of heat rising off the desert floor.","Sure, he was worried about his pursuer but he had a friend to take care of someone like that and that friend was about to come out any time now.","Liam’s lips curled upwards into a grin as soon enough the sky started changing colors and the clouds started gathering. Usually, he would run away right at the moment but this time he had to stop because the golden hue was hovering nearby and it hadn’t moved yet.","The next second right on cue, the clouds churned and a bloody wicked lightning bolt descended.","Liam stood tall and accepted it. He did not even bother erecting any dao shields. He simply took the brunt of the attack just because he could. The lightning bolts got exponentially stronger and he had no problems in receiving at least the first couple of bolts.","A sharp crack split the air, and Liam felt the bolt’s power snake down his spine in a dizzying rush. For a heartbeat, he was blinded by the flash, every nerve alight with crackling energy. The desert wind howled and then followed the pain.","The intense energy wrecked him from the inside out. However, thanks to his superior regeneration, his forged body was repairing itself fast enough. Then came the second bolt. Blood trickled from the corner of Liam’s mouth as this one was slightly too much for him to handle.","It was at this point a loud shriek came and a figure split apart from him. More accurately, a small bug jumped out of him.","Liam’s eyes snapped down at once. There, on the sand at his feet, scuttled a tiny, hideous insect-like creature. Its chitinous hide glistened darkly, and its mandibles clicked in panic. It seemed dazed by its abrupt ejection from Liam’s body and thrashed at the scorching grains of sand as if it had never felt the heat before.","A ripple of realization crept over Liam. This was the presence that had shadowed his every step. The stalker wasn’t perched on a distant dune, cloaked in illusions; it had been riding inside him all along.","He grimaced, wiping the blood from his mouth with the back of his hand. \"So that’s what you are.\" The next bolt was ready to descend so Liam did not waste time and instantly squished the bug, processing its soul into a minion. At the same time, he switched places with another minion, narrowly dodging the lightning bolt at the very last moment.","He would have switched with another minion to get away from the next bolt but it did not help very much. Neither did minor teleportation. The lightning bolt had a mind of its own and would descend wherever he was about to appear.","The only solution was running. For some reason, the bolt seemed to respect that. Maybe the system event was designed like this. Erecting dao fields also helped. Liam used a combination to run away from the bolt like usual.","The only plus point was that the golden hue became a lot brighter after the last tribulation lightning. It disappeared and reappeared a couple of times before finally, a golden pillar shot up to the sky for a brief second.","The treasure-seeking potion did not exactly play favorites. The bloody thing just about informed everyone in the vicinity about the location.","Liam’s face twitched but he did not care.","In front of him, the dunes shifted revealing something glossy and metallic. \"This is weird.\" He had expected some sort of ancient ruins but the thing in front of him was all metallic and rigid and the structure instantly reminded him of golems for some reason.","But the problem now was... how the hell was he supposed to get inside this huge metallic thing? Was it a building? A box? A humongous treasure chest?","Liam did not have a lot of time to figure it out as he could sense two more auras headed his way."]},{"number":1402,"title":"Chapter 1402: Care to team up?","paragraphs":["\"I am definitely not alone anymore.\" Liam swung around to face his new companions who had arrived at the spot in the blink of an eye.","One of them was wielding daggers, one in each hand and was covered from top to bottom in black cloth. The man unmistakably was an assassin and he was capable of blurring himself and appeared like a mirage one place one second and the next place the next second.","His movements were very unique and mysterious. His entire body seemed to blur and reshape, as if tethered only loosely to reality. The assassin’s voice was as muffled as his features, leaking out from behind layers of dark cloth.","\"It’s rude to hog the treasure,\" he said, tone light yet laced with threat.","\"Funny,\" Liam retorted. \"I’d be delighted to share...though from the look of things, your approach is more slash-and-grab than let’s-talk-over-tea.\"","A faint shimmer rippled over the assassin’s form. With a barely perceptible shift of weight, he vanished again, the air where he’d stood warping like a desert mirage. Instinctively, Liam tensed, scanning the immediate surroundings.","The shadowy figure reappeared behind him in a swirl of disturbed sand, daggers held in a relaxed grip that suggested lethal expertise.","\"I’ve seen my share of illusions,\" Liam coldly smiled. \"But yours...that’s a neat trick. I would love to learn it.\" The assassin didn’t reply, only angled his head to eye the half-opened metallic edifice. His hands on the other hand were already coming for Liam’s throat.","Liam felt the hairs on his neck bristle with warning as the assassin’s daggers slashed forward—so quick that it almost seemed the glint of steel materialized from thin air. Rather than recoiling, Liam dropped his weight and pivoted on one foot, just barely leaning out of the blade’s path.","A gust of sand exploded between them, kicked up by the assassin’s rapid movement. Slash. The man’s second dagger cleaved a tight arc through the air, aiming for Liam’s chest. However, before he could reach him, black chains sprang up from the ground, chains that reeked of death and decay.","They bound the assassin and held him in place. The man’s eyes widened in shock. He tried blurring again but he couldn’t make a single move against the nether chains. A startled hiss escaped the assassin as he strained against the entangling chains, their dark links rattling with every futile twitch.","Liam held the guy in place as the next one showed up, a figure robed in faded crimson silk stitched with cryptic sigils, holding a slender staff of twisted ebony gripped in one hand.","\"Nothing like a good struggle over treasure, eh?\" the newcomer purred, glancing from Liam to the snared assassin. The man’s voice carried a note of twisted amusement. \"It would appear I’m fashionably late to the show.\"","He bent slightly, observing the nether chains with a keen, unsettling interest. Black coils reeking of rot and grave-soil twitched in response, as if aware of his gaze. The assassin hissed again, fighting to blur away—but those death links held fast.","Liam indifferently glanced at the man. The guy prodded the nether chains with his staff, setting off another rattling vibration that caused the assassin to jerk in renewed panic. \"An intriguing bind. You dabble in necromancy, don’t you?\"","Liam’s eyes narrowed. \"I can dabble in a lot of things when the mood strikes but something tells me you’re not here to chat about magical theory.\"","\"Straight to the point. Good. We’ll get along famously.\" The robed man’s grin widened. Then he tilted his chin toward the half-exposed metallic monolith in the distance. \"I followed the golden pillar and got here. Let’s just say...my curiosity got the better of me.\"","The robed stranger shifted, hooking a thumb under his hood to lift it back slightly. Deep-set eyes shimmered with a calculating gleam. \"The structure is fascinating, isn’t it? A sealed fortress, by the looks of it. Care to team up?\"","The stranger swept a hand theatrically. \"It’d be easier if we’re not all at each other’s throats. Not that your friend here seems the cooperative sort.\" He flicked a knowing glance at the assassin.","Before Liam could answer, the assassin snarled again, voice muffled. \"I’ll kill you both...once I’m out of these damned chains!\"","Liam exhaled a quiet laugh, turning to the robed man. \"You see the predicament. With this one so eager to slit throats, and who knows what else lurking in that fortress, I’m not exactly in a trusting mood.\"","\"You needn’t trust me. You just have to work with me for the time being. I am going to fight with you at the end no matter what. Going to need that treasure for myself. That’s a given. Until then we can help each other out, don’t you think? Besides...\"","The stranger tapped the side of his staff against the sand, conjuring a tiny ripple of purple sparks. \"I have something that could help with the tribulation lightning, the bane of this place. Allow me to demonstrate it.\"","The next second, blinding electric currents assaulted the assassin. They completely demolished Liam’s nether domain and took over the area. It only lasted for a moment before revealing scorched earth and no sign of the assassin.","Liam nodded and did not say anything. He was not really pleased at the display as it had cost him a corpse but at least the soul was his for taking. He silently stood as he processed the soul into a minion.","He observed the stranger to see if had something to say but it looked like he couldn’t sense the soul processing. After a few seconds, Liam decided to go along with the guy’s plan. He lacked knowledge about this place and he might as well see if this guy knew anything.","\"I am Jonah.\" Liam introduced himself.","\"As for me, you can call me...Nolan,\" the guy said, sweeping out an arm in a half-bow. \"Jonah and Nolan. It almost sounds like we could be longtime friends.\""]},{"number":1403,"title":"Chapter 1403: Breaking and entering","paragraphs":["\"Ha ha, I see you’re not one for idle chatter. I won’t push your patience any further—let’s cut straight to business before more uninvited guests show up. I suspect you’re already pondering whether to team up with me. Allow me to put that doubt to rest for you.\" The robed guy Nolan started walking back.","\"You should do the same.\" He winked at Liam before his entire being started crackling with lightning.","Nolan’s eyes flashed with excitement as he raised his staff high, summoning a surge of raw, violet lightning that cascaded from his fingertips. At his command, the sky started changing.","The storm overhead roiled violently, drawing forth the raw fury of tribulation lightning from the churning clouds. The two forces met in a spectacular collision—a searing bolt of combined power that slammed into the metal fortress with an ear-splitting crash.","In that brilliant, fleeting moment, a small, jagged hole was blasted into the fortress’s surface, sending shards of molten metal and sparks spiraling into the air. The impact reverberated through the walls as if the ancient structure itself groaned in protest.","\"By the gods, did you see that?\" Nolan exclaimed, his voice edged with both triumph and urgency. He glanced upward at the swirling storm. \"If I’m not mistaken, that opening won’t stay open for long. We’d best get through, and fast.\"","\"Understood,\" Liam replied, his eyes locked on the pulsing breach. They only had a couple of seconds before the hole closed completely. The two of them shot forward and landed inside just in time.","From the explosive lightning outside, one would have expected the inside to be damaged at least a little, but what Liam saw shocked him. The walls had already fully repaired themselves, and there wasn’t as much as a scratch on the inside.","The hole they had come in had also completely vanished. It was as if they had somehow teleported inside.","\"Self-healing, quite elegantly so,\" Nolan thought out loud. \"If only we could harvest some of this metal.\"","The exact same thought was running through Liam’s mind, but the man in front of him was shaking his head. \"We better give up on that. This place is extremely bothersome. They should be here any time now if I am not wrong.","Even as they were talking, the ceiling in front of them started moving. The small metallic tiles in the wall started building onto themselves, and a protrusion jutted out as if it was going to come down the next second and bar them from going forward.","Liam swung his head around to see that another similar event was happening behind him. \"We need to keep moving.\" Without wasting any time, he dashed forward.","\"No, we cannot pick a direction just yet. We need to see where they are coming from.\" Nolan shouted, but Liam did not care.","Seeing that, Nolan gritted his teeth and followed Liam. It was just in time—two thick metallic slabs slammed down behind them, sealing off the path they’d just left. The deafening clang of closing metal echoed in the corridor. There was no turning back now.","\"Damn it,\" Nolan muttered, his eyes flashing as he tightened his grip on his staff. \"You should not have done that.\"","Liam didn’t slow down. \"We need to keep moving.\" He pointed at the ceiling that had once again started to bubble up.","Nolan looked like he wanted to say something, but in the end, he too had to agree with Liam and continued running. The two of them ran at an explosive speed, and yet the corridor seemed to be endless.","Metal slabs slammed behind them one after the other. The more they increased their speed, the more the walls reacted to them.","Metal slabs slammed into the walls behind them in rapid succession. Each collision reverberated like the toll of a death knell, and the fortress itself seemed to shudder in response, rearranging its interior with ruthless efficiency.","The corridor twisted and turned endlessly without any exit in sight. The two of them ran for a couple of hours before they finally ran into something akin to an exit or, more specifically, a dead end.","Both men skidded to a sudden halt at a dead end. Nolan’s heavy breath filled the silence as he surveyed the sealed corridor, the walls reassembled with an almost deliberate precision. \"Shit! Is this where we started?\" he panted, his eyes darting about in disbelief.","Were they running around in circles? The man who had seemed confident before now no longer appeared all that composed.","\"I thought you knew about this place.\" Liam raised a brow.","\"Not everything, damn it.\" Nolan chewed his fingernail, looking around in confusion. \"Let’s try breaking these damn walls.\"","Liam nodded. \"I agree, but we should try breaking the inner wall, not the outer wall.\"","\"Okay. Put your strongest leg forward.\" Nolan declared, and he began gathering a ball of threatening energy in his palm—a swirling mass of violet lightning and raw arcane power. The energy crackled and pulsed, ready to explode.","Liam prepared his attack as well, icy cold energy swirling in front of him.","\"Now!\" Nolan shouted, and with a fierce cry, he hurled the swirling sphere of violet lightning at the inner wall. Liam was about to do the same when he started the familiar metal bubbling over their head.","In that split second, he thought of an idea and sent his icy power shot up above rather than onto the inner wall.","\"What?\" Nolan was shocked and was about to complain when he noticed that a small hole had appeared above their head. It was impossible to go through the hole, but now that there was an opening, Liam tried minor teleportation and ended up on the other side of the wall.","Nolan’s eyes widened on seeing what had happened. The hole was closing in fast. Liam simply watched, not in the least bothered to cast another attack to widen the hole. Gritting his teeth, Nolan tried the minor teleportation with nothing to lose and thankfully ended up on the other side too."]},{"number":1404,"title":"Chapter 1404: You paranoid maniac","paragraphs":["After joining Liam, Nolan gave him a death glare and gritted his teeth, but the man had no time to speak his mind. The hollow space above the tunnel was rapidly closing in as the metallic walls of the fortress once again began to adjust and remodel.","By this point, Liam was pretty sure that the damn thing was alive. It sensed every little thing and adjusted its strategy accordingly, all in fractions of seconds, and everything aimed to kill the intruders.","Liam’s gaze instantly shifted upwards. It seemed counterintuitive, but he had a feeling that they should be going upwards rather than inwards.","The structure was buried in the sands, which meant there shouldn’t be anything upward, and yet the ferocity with which the fortress was attacking them was higher when they tried moving up.","Maybe there was some spatial distortion at play, which made them think up was down and down was up. The walls were quickly closing in, and they only had a split second to make a decision.","Liam did not bother consulting with the guy as he once again aimed an attack at the upper ceiling that had started to bubble. Nolan saw what was happening and begrudgingly did the same.","With their combined effort, they easily blasted a hole in the structure again. Without hesitation, the two of them used minor teleportation and appeared on the other side. They had to repeat this a dozen times when even Liam began to wonder what the hell they were doing here.","Finally, after the fiftith time, they teleported into what looked like a room. A huge metallic chamber with no windows or doors. The chamber was utterly silent save for a low, almost imperceptible hum.","Liam’s eyes widened as he hurriedly looked around, trying to figure out what was going on. Nolan, on the other hand, let out a hysterical laugh. \"We are finally here, damn it. This is where we were supposed to begin. Prepare yourself. The worst is coming and my reserves are almost empty.\"","Liam met the man’s gaze, and there was madness in his eyes. Before he could wonder if the other party was doing something to sabotage him, the walls around them started shifting. Twelve protrusions appeared on the four walls surrounding them, and each protrusion morphed itself into a humanoid figure.","More specifically, like a metallic golem—except these were no ordinary constructs. Liam watched in awe as these golems shifted in forms like a much more complex, expensive version of the ones in Transformers, and their hands turned into guns.","Mana sizzled from the guns, potent, concentrated mana that was capable of blasting a hole in any Dao field.","\"Hey Jonah, this is where you are going to be happy you teamed up with me.\" Nolan suddenly spoke up. \"Guard me. Give me a few seconds, and I can disarm all of them! Ahhhh! Just trust me for once, damn it! Otherwise, both of us are going to end up dead in the next second.\"","Liam indifferently prepared to deal with the golems in the way that he would. All twelve of them were preparing a synchronized attack, and there was no time to counterattack first, so he instantly started erecting dao fields left and right.","An ice barrier sprang up first, followed by nether. The twelve metallic golems unleashed their synchronized salvo of sizzling mana, and the barrier shuddered under the barrage. From the looks of it, two barriers were simply insufficient to hold back the attack.","\"Here. This should buy you some time.\" Nolan threw out a talisman. Liam was a little shocked to see the effect of the talisman. It somehow amplified the effect of his dao fields.","Liam’s nether ice field became more than just a shield—it transformed into a resonant lattice of frost and nether might. The talisman’s energy interwove with his dao fields, intensifying the barrier into a crystalline dome that shimmered with black veins.","Each facet of the barrier now pulsed with a rhythmic cadence, absorbing the sizzling mana blasts like a magnet for raw, dissipating energy.","\"Hold it for a few seconds. Please just trust me this once, you paranoid maniac.\" Nolan shouted again.","Liam’s face twitched. No matter who it was, he was not prepared to trust a random person in a dangerous place like this. But he had definitely earned at least a few seconds of trust with the talisman. He acted as if he was going all out and maintained the barrier.","Surprisingly, just like the guy had advertised, he had somehow managed to snake his purple lightning into the first golem, and soon the entire golem began to glow purple.","Sizzling sounds came from different sections of the golem, followed by sparks and metallic groans. Soon parts of the damn thing started to explode. Small, small interruptions started cascading, and in the blink of an eye, the entire thing exploded in the face of the other eleven golems.","\"Not bad!\" Liam was visibly impressed. He glanced at Nolan pensively, which made the man shiver. \"This is my arcane lightning. You cannot replicate it. You need me to get through these sentinels.\" Nolan blurted out as if he could read the thoughts running in Liam’s mind.","Liam could only chuckle lightly. \"Do I look like that much of a villain to you?\"","Nolan rolled his eyes and replied with a sharp glance before turning back to his work, his hands crackling with violet energy as he hurled another surge of arcane lightning at the next golem. The creature shuddered under the assault, its metal plating fracturing as sparks and molten fragments cascaded into the air.","Nolan managed to move the golems close to one of the walls of the room before they exploded. The blast revealed a small opening through which Liam could see the outside. Not that it helped. There was only metal everywhere, just like the same metal they were currently inside.","Every inch of this place was a freaking metal coffin and they had to be careful. Otherwise, they could simply be buried in her forever."]},{"number":1405,"title":"Chapter 1405: Elemental King","paragraphs":["\"Keep those barriers strong!\" Nolan shouted over the clamor. \"I need every second I can get to disarm these sentinels!\"","Liam nodded without breaking his concentration. It was not difficult for him to maintain two dao fields simultaneously, but it was a bit too stressful to keep it up for so long without going all out. \"You need to hurry.\"","The next few seconds were touch and go, but eventually, the two of them managed to get blasted out of the small confined room. It would have been good news if not for the long, endless tunnels they found themselves in once again.","At least this time, the walls were not closing in on them.","\"Fast. Fast. Run quickly. The main vault should be in one of these corridors.\" Nolan shouted as he ran forward. Within seconds, another golem popped out of the wall. The entire corridor was starting to show similar reactions. \"Jonah. Jonah. Take care of this. Guard me. We will die otherwise.\"","Liam started erecting dao fields again, blocking them from the mass shooting that was about to happen. This time, there was simply no way two shields were going to be enough. He had to bring out the next dao field as well.","He decided to go with the earth field, trying to get a little more defense, but at the last moment, he ended up choosing fire. Something was off. Liam could feel the heat in the surroundings starting to rise.","Before Liam could piece together the anomaly, a figure emerged at the far end of the tunnel—a man in a tattered robe that seemed to flutter in an invisible wind. He looked human enough, but there was something unsettling about his presence.","It took Liam a few seconds to focus his gaze; then, he noticed the stranger’s eyes, burning brightly. It was not just his eyes. It was everywhere. Streaks of fiery glow covered his entire body. The rest of his body was surprisingly flesh.","This was the first time Liam was seeing someone like this. Another human-related race?","Near him, Nolan was not nearly as calm as Ethan. \"Fuck!!! What’s an elemental king doing here? Damn it. I spent all of my resources to prepare for this event, and an elemental king had to show up? This is complete bullshit!\"","The corridor’s oppressive heat and the roar of metallic golems faded into a heavy silence as the robed stranger—this elemental king—advanced toward them. His fiery glow painted shifting shadows along the metal walls, and every step he took sent ripples of heat over the floor. It was as if the man himself was forged out of a living flame.","The elemental king stopped a few paces away, his gaze sweeping over all the chaos. The next second, an intense flame rippled out of him.","Liam acted instantly and no longer held back. Six different dao fields erupted from Liam in unison, each one channeling a primal force, all swirling around him like a living, crackling storm. The combined energies burst forth in a dazzling display of power, weaving together to form a radiant shield that pulsed with every beat of his heart.","Nolan gaped in shock. \"You can do this?\" His gaze turned from the Elemental King to Liam. He looked as if he was seeing monsters everywhere. \"How can you possibly block his attack? Oh, thank god. Oh, thank god.\" The man literally started weeping.","Liam’s lips twitched into a small, wry smile. \"Why don’t you stop crying like a girl and help me here. We could use one more.\" The damned guy’s attack was so strong that the heat was still seeping through. \"Do you have any more of those talismans?\"","Nolan, still sniffling and wide-eyed, glanced between Liam and the fiery chaos. \"This is insane,\" he muttered, half to himself. \"I never imagined we’d be in a firefight with an elemental king...and you’re blocking his attacks. How are you blocking the attack of a king? Are you a true royal?\"","\"Just shut up and hand me a talisman,\" Liam shouted.","\"No. I don’t have it anymore. How many do you think I could sneak into an event like this? Are you crazy?\" Nolan shouted in exasperation, but the next second, he shut his mouth. \"I am sorry, your highness. I shouldn’t have. Please forgive me. Please.\"","Seeing that the man had completely lost it, Liam used every bit of power he had left in his cores to block the attack. Thankfully, they were not the only ones affected by the attack. He could sense the impenetrable metallic fortress crumbling under the assault of the Elemental King.","Holes appeared in the walls all over the place. The metallic golems were ripped into shreds. Liam grabbed the guy and used Minor Teleportation. They needed to get the hell out of there asap.","He did not stop or look back, only using the skill again and again to get as far away as possible. So far, he had only run into opponents he could easily deal with, but this time, he could feel that he was clashing with someone in a league of his own.","This would only result in more and more loss. Maybe it was time to get the hell out of here. Liam’s mind spun as he continued to move through the corridors. He had no rhyme or reason to choose that path. He simply ran as fast as he could.","Thankfully, the Elemental King didn’t seem to be following them. He must have been exploring this place just like they were and wasn’t all that keen on chasing the two of them.","Liam only stopped after several minutes, and when he finally couldn’t engage in minor teleportation again. He was almost fully spent and had only barely escaped, but that did not matter to the metallic walls around them.","Another round of protrusions started appearing on the walls as a new batch of fresh metallic golems emerged to take care of the intruders."]},{"number":1406,"title":"Chapter 1406: Long time no see, Liam Chang","paragraphs":["\"Highness, we are totally fucked. Royally screwed. Even my arcane lightning is not enough to escape this nonsense. What the hell is this thing?\" Nolan screamed at the top of his lungs as he ran as fast as he could, clinging to Liam for dear life.","\"Just shut up and run!\" Liam calmly retorted. However, his face was pale as he tried to maintain the Dao fields constantly. The two of them were running away from the many, many golems popping out of the tunnels.","Fighting these golems was messy and difficult but not impossible. But they were forced to run thanks to the damned Elemental King. That being set off a chain reaction which was now resulting in explosions left and right all over the place.","One after the other, golems and corridors were exploding. There was only fire and smoke everywhere, peppered with spatial tears.","\"Highness, we’re losing ground!\" Nolan yelled again, his voice raw with panic as he clung to Liam’s arm. His eyes darted wildly, searching for any sign of escape in the infernal chaos.","Explosions rocked the corridor as if the very fabric of reality were tearing apart. Amid the cacophony of fire and shattering metal, Nolan’s scream faded into a strangled cry.","Liam, barely keeping his Dao fields intact, sprinted through a maze of burning debris and jagged spatial tears. The air was thick with smoke, and every step threatened to plunge them into collapsing voids.","\"Keep moving! Don’t look back!\" he shouted, his voice steady despite the turmoil. His magic pulsed around him—a tenuous barrier fighting to hold back the raging inferno and the relentless surge of exploding golems.","Liam’s mind raced, trying to decipher the shifting maze as spatial tears rippled unpredictably across the floor. Each tear was a window into a void of chaos, where the laws of nature seemed to disintegrate. If they accidentally ran into a tear, that would be the end, but they couldn’t exactly stop running.","\"Your highness, maybe we should consider retreating.\" Nolan was on the verge of tears. Liam couldn’t argue with him. Maybe this was truly the end of this event.","On their right, two more figures appeared. It looked like they had just now escaped from the corridors and stepped into the main building. The two of them were wearing red robes, and they had the telltale vampiric blood magic swirling around them.","However, before they could even understand where they stepped, an explosion boomed right on their faces, and the two did not even have time to activate the exit tokens as they were blown to smithereens.","Seeing that, Nolan gritted his teeth and made the decision. \"Jonah, your highness, I sincerely hope we meet again.\" He no longer hesitated and activated the exit token. But something was wrong. His exit token was not working.","Liam frowned. The next second, his instincts screamed that he was in extreme danger, and he had a feeling it was not just because of these explosions. He immediately gritted his teeth and erected yet another Dao field.","His skin was cracking. His muscles were tearing. His body couldn’t handle the stress of having seven dao fields up at the same time, but Liam firmly believed that he was going to die if he did not do this.","He turned to see what the hell was going on when he froze with complete and utter shock. Standing right behind him were two familiar figures. Two people he couldn’t forget even if he wanted to.","\"Long time no see, Liam Chang.\" Mia’s cold voice snapped him out of his trance as he stared at the woman he didn’t think he was going to see in the foreseeable future. Standing next to her was the prick from the divine temple, the paladin who had been the right hand of that bitch.","Mia’s eyes, as cold and merciless as winter’s frost, fixed on him. \"The rat has been skulking in the shadows for far too long,\" she continued, a venomous edge underlying every word. \"And now he’s come crawling back into our midst.\"","Liam’s heart pounded in his ears, his mind reeling from the sudden, jarring reunion amid the inferno of collapsing corridors. His body, already strained by the impossible burden of seven dao fields, trembled from exhaustion.","The paladin’s lip curled in disdain as he regarded Liam with thinly veiled contempt. \"You greedy little thing. You should have stayed hidden. You came chasing after a golden event, and now you have nowhere to go.\"","Liam did not care about him. What he said did not matter. His gaze was fixed only on Mia as he clenched his fists. How was she here? They let her out?","The only reason he was so focused on Derek and did not think about Mia for the time being was because she was trapped in the divine realms. Without getting smack dab in the middle of those people, there was simply no way to rescue her, and that required him to be stronger, much stronger. Otherwise, it would simply be a suicide mission.","However, she was now standing right in front of him. His eyes turned cold, and killing intent filled him. He was not happy to see her here.","Because if they felt comfortable enough to send her out on system events, then that meant... The Mia he knew no longer existed.","\"What did they do to you?\" Liam shouted.","\"Watch how you talk, brat. You are not talking to that disloyal bitch anymore. You are talking to a high priestess of a divine temple. So you better watch your damn tongue, you filthy rat.\"","Liam’s face turned ugly. What did that mean? What happened to Mia? He had no idea, and he had no way of knowing it. But one thing was sure. He was getting the hell out of here, and he was taking her with him.","Everything can be figured out late. For now, he simply needed to take her and leave. \"Mia!\" He called as he dashed forward at full speed."]},{"number":1407,"title":"Chapter 1407: You are coming with me","paragraphs":["\"Mia!\" Liam shouted, lunging forward despite the searing pain in his limbs and the roaring chaos around him. Every fiber of his battered body screamed to stop, yet the thought of leaving her behind—of letting the Mia he once knew be swallowed by darkness—drove him on.","Her eyes, once warm with a familiar light, now glowed with an icy detachment that made his heart wrench. The divine aura that clung to her like a second skin was unmistakable—a far cry from the woman he remembered.","As he neared, the flames and falling debris seemed to slow, the inferno of collapsing corridors and shuddering golems fading into a dull roar behind his pounding pulse. \"Mia, come with me!\" he demanded.","A cold laugh echoed in the tumult—a sound that belonged not to the woman he knew but to a stranger wearing her face. \"Why don’t you make me? I want to see just what sort of a person that stuck up cunt lost to. He He. You are the first person in a thousand years to make her go crazy.\"","Liam did not plan on engaging with her. He knew Mia was in there somewhere. She had to be. Everything could be figured out later. He simply smashed through her defenses and grabbed her hand before activating the exit token. \"You are coming with me.\"","Mia simply shrugged. She did nothing to stop Liam from grabbing her hand.","And the next second, he understood why. His exit tattoo was not activating. He could hear Nolan’s scream in the distance. \"Your highness, it’s not working! It’s not working!\"","Liam tensed up. He let go of Mia, feeling that something was wrong, but Mia grabbed his hand instead. \"You should have stayed hidden and lived out the rest of your life like the rat you are. You are going to regret coming here.\"","Liam’s eyes turned pitch-black. He unleashed his nether core and his nether dao field, which coalesced into writhing, inky tentacles of raw nether energy that shot forth like living shadows.","They lashed out, slicing through the chaos of exploding corridors and disintegrating golems, each tendril carrying with it the weight of his rage and desperation.","The air around him seemed to distort as his power surged, a dark counterpoint to the blazing inferno. With every lash of those nether tentacles, fragments of shattered metal and roiling fire were torn asunder, momentarily pausing the collapse of the ancient structure.","Liam’s vision blurred with fury as he turned toward the paladin. \"Let her go. Let me leave.\" He roared as nether plunged towards the paladin like a tsunami.","\"Perfect synchronization? How do you possess a power like this?\" Both Mia’s and the paladin’s eyes widened in shock. Mia immediately distanced herself by shooting back away from Liam. However, it was too late.","Liam’s nether tendrils completely arrested and prevented her from moving even an inch. \"If I was at my full power, you would already be dead!\" Mia spat out. Liam did not care. He was only able to retain this state for a couple of seconds. He needed to make it count.","He once again activated the exit token, trying to get out of here and take Mia with him, but things were not so simple. It looked like the paladin was the one holding all the cards in his hand. But that was not a problem.","As long as the target was not a transcendent, Liam had little to worry about. The nether tendrils immediately shot toward the paladin. His attack was only slightly shy of the power exhibited by the Elemental King.","The paladin’s face contorted in fear and anger. Even though his words demeaned Liam, the look on his face made it clear that he wasn’t going to take any chances.","\"You have gone on for long enough. You need to be erased.\" Before Liam’s nether shackles could reach him, the man spat up something. A drop of golden liquid appeared in front of him. A pulse of pure power rippled from the liquid.","\"By the power of my divine dao, face your retribution! The righteous shall prosper, and the disloyal shall perish. Die, you wretched creature who has sinned!\"","The next moment, the world stopped. An unbelievable amount of power washed over Liam. All of his dao fields seemed to shudder, but he held on. His nether dao field became pitch black, as if the endless abyss itself was acting as a barrier for the attack.","Liam could sense that his exit token was active once again. He did not know how long he could hold out against the attack. He knew he needed to take the chance to leave. That was the rational thing to do. This was not an opponent or rather an attack he could face at the moment, but he refused to budge.","He was so close to bringing back Mia. How could he leave now?","It was an impossible decision that he did not want to take. Not again. He couldn’t do it to her again. His body was already in tatters from using so much power, power that did not belong to a simple awakener. He was struggling, grasping for straws.","\"You are a stubborn fool!\" Mia’s voice sounded. Something seemed to stir in her eyes, but she snapped out of it. She glanced at the paladin next to her, who was frozen to the spot, the aftereffect of using such a powerful skill, a skill strong enough to rip open his cores and his dao seeds.","She was not willing to fight to the death over an enemy she did not care about all that much. She glanced at Liam one more time before activating the escape token on her hand.","\"Think about Alex and Rey!\" She heard Liam shout one more time as her body vanished from the metallic chaos. Behind Liam, Nolan also shouted something as his body vanished as well. The escape tokens were once again active.","The entire place was collapsing and Liam was locked into a fight to death with the damned paladin. It was at this time that the cauldron on Liam’s chest pulsed once again."]},{"number":1408,"title":"Chapter 1408: Going, going and gone?","paragraphs":["Liam gritted his teeth and unleashed everything he had at the paladin. However, the drop of golden liquid he used was way too powerful to deal with. It was as if the thing affected time itself.","Liam couldn’t breathe. He couldn’t think. His dao fields were all crumbling one after the other. He was only barely holding on. However, right at this critical moment, the cauldron on his chest pulsed.","\"The other side is using a divine treasure. It’s only fair that you used yours too.\" The familiar arrogant voice sounded in his mind, and the next second, a strong suction force erupted from the cauldron.","Broken pieces of metal chunks, smoke, debris, and all sorts of things started flying into the cauldron. Shockingly, this was followed by the paladin.","Liam’s eyes widened in shock as he watched the cauldron actually suck the man inside. He blinked twice as he couldn’t believe it but it was very real.","Everything around him was intact, except the paladin was now missing.","Liam wanted to ask the cauldron senior what exactly had happened, but the glow on the cauldron had already faded. Also, this was not the time or place to worry about this. Everything around him was exploding left and right.","Liam found that he was now able to move. He immediately tried to activate his exit token and get the hell out of there, but he was once again unable to activate it.","What the hell was happening? He lifted his head in panic, and the paladin was still nowhere to be seen. So why was he not able to leave?","This fucking golden bubble!","He needed to break this somehow. He took a deep breath and started to fully activate his Dao seeds again, but then he suddenly stopped. He waited a moment and observed. Something was off. The golden bubble was there around him, but it wasn’t doing anything at all.","His movements were restricted, and his mana reserves were low, and yet nothing was happening. Not even the explosions were reaching him.","Now that he saw it, the golden bubble was actually protecting him from everything? Liam did a double take as he tried to wrap his mind around this concept. Was this golden bubble actually helping him?","He had no idea how this treasure worked. The paladin took out the liquid and then was sucked into the cauldron. Now, without any direction, the golden liquid ended up helping him.","Liam’s lips tugged upward into a smile. This was an unexpected gift. His grin widened as he watched everything around him explode and repair repeatedly. It seemed that the Elemental King was giving the metallic building quite a fight.","Right now, he was simply a silent spectator watching everything go down from the convenience of his golden bubble. Only popcorn was missing.","Liam was amazed as he continued to watch everything for hours and hours. What sort of power did the Elemental King hold to put up such a fight?","The world beyond his shimmering prison continued its relentless cycle of explosion and reconstruction—a maddening dance of creation and destruction. Finally, after what seemed like an eternity, the explosions slowly started to die down.","The power of the golden bubble was also starting to wear off. It was still protecting him, but he was now able to move freely. Wherever he moved, the bubble moved with him.","With a big grin plastered on his face, he started exploring the metallic ruins. Electricity crackled here and there, and the previously impeccable metallic interior was now covered in soot and smoke and broken parts. There were even huge gaping holes in some places.","The metallic golems no longer popped out. Everything was peaceful. The building finally died?","Liam casually walked forward when, all of a sudden, a dangerous feeling welled up in his heart. He felt as if he was going to face some crisis that was going to determine his life or death. He froze for a moment, wondering what to do, and then it happened.","The next second, a huge explosion rang out. An explosion of epic proportions, something that Liam couldn’t comprehend. Everywhere around him, reality started blurring. Spatial tears started showing up left and right.","The metallic structure convulsed violently, its beams and panels buckling as if caught in the grip of some colossal, unseen force. Reality itself seemed to splinter before Liam’s eyes, as spatial tears widened into gaping voids that revealed fragments of alternate worlds—a kaleidoscope of chaos and possibility.","Liam’s heart pounded as he stood transfixed in the midst of the unfolding apocalypse. The once-familiar metallic corridors now twisted in impossible angles, their surfaces morphing under the raw, untamed energies unleashed by the explosion. At that moment, every instinct screamed at him to flee, and he started running.","He used every bit of power he had left and focused it all on his speed. He did not dare use minor teleportation as it could land smack dab in the middle of the void.","The golden bubble around him was also starting to wear thin. What the hell happened? Did the entire building self-destruct to keep the Elemental King out? There was no sign of that mysterious being as he started to run to safety at top speed.","The ground under him was only barely stable as he ran from one spot to another. He would only just barely move when a spatial tear would appear in the spot. His heart pounded loudly. He had never been in a peril like this. This was what an exploding world felt like?","He ran and ran and ran without stopping until suddenly, the golden barrier around him was only barely visible. His exit token became active yet again, and he was now able to leave this dreadful place.","But just as he was about to activate his exit token and slip away from the crumbling nightmare, Liam’s eyes caught sight of an anomaly in the distance. Amidst the chaotic ruins, there was a single structure that stood stable like a lone sentinel—an island of calm amid the storm."]},{"number":1409,"title":"Chapter 1409: Born with a divine spoon","paragraphs":["Liam’s pulse raced as he fixated on the anomaly—a lone structure that defied the surrounding chaos. Unlike the battered, collapsing edifice around him, this edifice stood firm, its polished metal and etched runes glowing softly in the distance. It was as if a protective calm had been woven into it, an invitation amid the destruction.","Surely, this had to be the room where the treasure was. Nothing else would explain what was going on. The question was whether he should risk everything and claim the treasure or if he should simply take the easy exit.","Liam had already started running forward towards the mysterious room. Of course, he had to take it. There was simply no other option.","A golden event that had brought out divine temple participants and some mysterious elemental king definitely had something good to give. He was not about to pass up such a good item.","Liam made a last-ditch effort to reach the isolated space, ignoring everything else. The good thing was that he did not have to work hard to block any attacks anymore.","Everywhere around him, there were spatial tears. Everything around him was getting sucked into the void. The explosions couldn’t even reach him anymore. The void was taking care of everything for him.","However, escaping that void was the biggest headache he had at the moment. Thankfully, Liam had something he could actually use. The movement technique from the assassin class awakener from earlier.","He only had a rudimentary understanding of it and had never practised it before, but he had absorbed all the information from the soul when he had processed it. He should be able to do it.","Liam dashed forward, his footwork suddenly becoming a blur of precision and agility. He weaved through the chaos with uncanny grace, each step a calculated evasion of the gaping spatial tears that threatened to swallow everything in their wake.","The void’s pull was relentless, but Liam moved as if time had slowed for him alone, every nimble pivot and decisive leap drawing him closer to the luminous anomaly. Electricity crackled around it, protecting it from stray spatial explosions.","However, it was clear that it wouldn’t be able to hold out for long. Maybe a few seconds at best. Liam frowned. Would he be able to reach it? He was able to move through the chaos using the new footwork, but his speed was simply not enough to get there.","Just as he was thinking about it, another figure appeared in the vicinity. The Elemental King!","Liam’s eyes widened in shock. This guy was still here. Just how powerful was this being? The entire building wanted to take him out, and he came out on top? The whole world was collapsing because of him, and yet here he was, totally indifferent to everything.","Liam was no longer confident. There was a thin line between confidence and overconfidence, and he felt as if he was about to cross it. He definitely did not want to face this madman.","The myriad realms were vast, and he did not dare think that he could stand toe-to-toe with the strongest. Many beings were born with a divine spoon and were strong even before they stepped out of their mothers’ wombs. It would be stupid to rush blindly into a fight with someone like this. He had already gotten the cauldron. Perhaps it was time to run after all.","Though Liam was taking stock of the situation, the other party did not seem to care at all.","The Elemental King did not care about Liam or about the spatial tears popping out everywhere. In his eyes, only the treasure room was there. He calmly moved through the tears as if he were taking a stroll in the park. He casually dodged tears left and right, not in the least anxious or nervous.","Liam clenched his fists. Was this the pride and power that came from being born as one of the superior races of the myriad realms? Snapping him out of his thoughts, a loud boom rang out.","Liam snapped to look at the treasure room when he saw that a huge spatial tear had finally wreaked that single room as well. One wall of the room was completely decimated, and now a big spatial tear decorated it instead.","This made entering the space so much complicated. Not just that, but the entire structure was seconds away from collapsing completely.","Liam’s heart raced, and his eyes filled with madness. The Elemental King still remained indifferent to everything as if he was a God above all of this. Was this it? Was this the difference he would never be able to bridge? Liam refused to accept it.","He gritted his teeth as he suddenly had an idea. Sure, he learned a footwork that would help him tremendously in this situation, but then again, he was at best an amateur at it. Why use an amateur to do the job when he could get an expert to do it?","He summoned the newest soul he had forged, which was none other than the assassin. He then sent the soul forward, ordering it to get to the treasure room.","\"Work, damn it.\" Liam was almost activating his exit token just in case the Elemental King decided to wipe him out because of this. But even so, he watched in awe as his minion wonderfully obeyed his orders.","The soul minion skillfully weaved through the chaos, its ethereal form a flickering shadow against the backdrop of collapsing reality. It darted between the gaping spatial tears and errant explosions, its every movement calculated to avoid the void’s ravenous pull.","Drawing closer to the treasure room, the minion focused on the singular beacon of divine light that still pulsed from within the damaged edifice.","Before it lay a once-hallowed chamber now marred by a massive spatial tear—a jagged scar where reality itself had splintered.","The tear twisted the room’s wall into a chaotic fracture, threatening to obliterate the sanctuary in mere seconds. Yet, the assassin soul advanced undeterred, gliding past the edge of destruction as if dancing on the brink of oblivion.","And then it actually succeeded in entering the god damn room!","The soul minion stood right in front of the treasure!"]},{"number":1410,"title":"Chapter 1410: A half victory?","paragraphs":["Liam couldn’t believe his eyes, and for the first time, the Elemental King paused in the middle of his stride, his eyebrow raised. Liam did not know if it was his imagination, but the flame streaks on the man’s body became brighter as if they reflected his emotion.","Obviously, the person was not going to react well to his treasure getting stolen from him after he had put so much effort into it. Liam would be a fool to think otherwise.","However, he did not care. His minion was standing right in front of the damned treasure and he was not about to whimp out now!","Liam instantly sacrificed the minion and switched places with him. The Elemental King growled from the distance, the man’s anger louder than the spatial explosions.","And then a massive flame emerged.","Liam did not wait around to find out what exactly the attack did. His gaze locked onto the small vial in front of him. It was a vial with a clear green liquid. It seemed weird considering the fact that he had raided a metallic structure with golems. He expected something along those lines.","But what exactly was this vial? Perhaps the real treasure was something else? Did he need to search this room? Was there a hidden trap door?","Numerous questions popped into Liam’s mind, but he did not dare delay any longer. Without any hesitation, he finally activated the exit tattoo, and the next instant, his body vanished into nothingness.","Liam’s entire body became drenched in sweat, and even as he exited, he could feel the pair of molten lava-like eyes fixated on him. The anger within those eyes was burning boundlessly and threatened to consume his very soul.","Even if he was a second late, he couldn’t imagine the consequences. His scalp became numb at the thought. The burning memory of molten, wrathful eyes, the Elemental King’s gaze, was seared into his very soul. The taste of near-certain retribution lingered bitterly on his tongue.","That guy was definitely going to come after him.","As his vision cleared up, he once again found himself in the eternal sword palace quarters. But Liam immediately tore a teleportation talisman and returned to Earth without even taking a second to breathe.","The small green vial was still in his hand as he finally appeared in the system shop, a shocked Tilia staring at him, gobsmacked.","\"Liam!\" The fairy rushed to him with a face full of worry, and only when he saw his reflection in her eyes did he notice that half of his body was missing.","Liam bitterly smiled. This time, he really had been far too close to death. He was about to take out his healing potion from the storage space when suddenly, the green liquid from the vial floated up. It shot forward and turned into a mist before completely disappearing into Liam’s body.","***","Rey gasped as he struggled to adjust to the water all around him. \"This treasure hunt sucks! This stupid event officially sucks!\" He shouted out in frustration. Normally, one shouldn’t be able to communicate in water, and somehow, inside the treasure hunt event, he could.","He was also able to breathe and see. Not that any of it helped. He freaking hated being in the water. As luck would have it, he felt a slight pressure from the water on the side, probably a sign that something was fast approaching him.","Of course, it had barely been a couple seconds since he stepped into the event, and he was already facing some monster. How the hell was he supposed to shoot an arrow in this water? He retrieved a long spear he had stored in his space ring.","An Epic-grade spear that was crafted by one of the talented blacksmiths in the guild, a real up-and-comer. It gave him a total of 100 bonus stats, along with a couple of special effects. Not bad. He couldn’t complain. It had been a while since he used it, but hey, he could wield it just fine.","Rey swung around, gritted his teeth, and thrust the spear forward into whatever was coming. He instantly regretted his decision as lightning crackled around the long creature, and his spear became a conductor for the magic.","It lit up like he had plunged it into some insane power grid, and his body flailed from the attack.","Rey’s body jerked like a puppet on malfunctioning strings as the electric shock surged through him, and he couldn’t help but let out a blood-curdling scream that echoed through the water. For a split second, everything blurred—a mix of flashing blue arcs and the monster’s enraged roar.","\"Are you freaking kidding me?!\" he yelled, struggling to get his bearings as the water churned wildly around him. The beast, its form flickering with electric pulses, prepared to attack again.","Rey quickly adapted. He had read about these types of beasts before. Usually, their insides were the safest target area. As the giant eel prepared to chomp a big piece off of him, he quickly thrust the spear once again, this time aiming for the mouth.","The attack hit it amazingly well, and the creature screeched and thrashed in pain. It wasn’t completely dead yet, and this gave an idea to Rey.","\"Tame.\" He activated the skill. He had a couple of slots open just for this purpose and decided to use one. With his heart hammering in his chest, he extended his arm, letting his aura wrap around the creature.","The eel’s frantic movements slowed, its eyes dimming from a ferocious glow to a kind of mellow, almost curious stare.","\"Hell yeah,\" Rey muttered under his breath, a grin breaking through despite the pain still buzzing in his muscles. \"Guess I’m the boss now.\" The creature, still massive and powerful, now floated by his side as if it were waiting for his next move.","Rey’s mind raced with crazy ideas—maybe he could ride this electrified beast, zoom past the rest of the treasure hunt, and show everyone how to really crush this event. Yup, this was going to be amazing!"]},{"number":1411,"title":"Chapter 1411: You bitch!","paragraphs":["Rey grinned like he’d just unlocked the ultimate cheat code. Without missing a beat, he leaned forward and gave the electrified eel a little nudge. The creature zipped forward like a turbocharged submarine, and Rey practically clung on, adrenaline and wild excitement coursing through him.","The water blurred into streaks of neon as they shot past clusters of sparkling coral. Rey’s mind raced with ideas—maybe he could hack the treasure hunt’s code by riding this glitchy beast right into its heart. \"Alright, you crazy, electric bastard, let’s see how fast you can go,\" he muttered, half-laughing and half-cursing.","The main objective of the event was to collect these special materials called tea-egg pearls. They were called tea egg pearls because of the special patterns on top of these pearls. They were quite famous because these things helped in contemplating one’s dao.","They also helped in the event’s progress. The more pearls, the higher the points, and whichever factor obtained the maximum points, they would win the treasure hunt. It was as simple as that. But there was a catch.","Once you collect a pearl, you start glowing in the dark waters. One would become a beacon for attracting all sorts of trouble. Also, the pearls could be consumed instantly to become stronger. But these consumed pearls did not count towards the total points. They still make you a beacon with the glowing aura, though.","Rey’s grip on the spear tightened as he spotted something shining in the distance. \"Hey, slow down,\" he muttered, though his pulse was already racing. He commanded the eel to go towards the pearls. The beast instantly shot forward as soon as it saw the pearls. It looked like it was not just the humans who coveted these pearls.","Rey lunged for the pearl without a second thought. His fingers closed around it as if it were an old friend, and he couldn’t help but let out a cocky laugh. \"Wow, that was easy,\" he muttered, admiring the gem’s flawless surface for a split second. But before he could revel in his effortless win, the water around him exploded with raw, predatory energy.","In the blink of an eye, ten vicious sharks materialized, their eyes cold and hungry, slicing through the dark water like silent assassins. The sharks circled him, their razor-sharp teeth glinting under the pulsating glow of his newly acquired tea-egg pearl. Rey’s heart pounded hard as he tightened his grip on the epic-grade spear, every muscle tensing for the fight of his life.","What followed was a blur of adrenaline and chaos. For several minutes, Rey danced with death beneath the dark waves. He ducked and dodged, parrying the sharks’ relentless attacks with quick, desperate thrusts. Each swing of his spear sent bursts of electric energy arcing through the water, and every dodge was a narrow escape from snapping jaws.","Just when the situation looked its bleakest, the water exploded in a flash of divine light. Cutting through the turmoil, Alex burst onto the scene. Her armor shone like a beacon, and her sword blazed with righteous fury as she carved through the shark pack with swift, surgical precision.","With a few decisive swings, Alex forced the sharks into retreat, their predatory formation dissolving into the dark abyss. She skidded to a halt beside Rey, who was still reeling from the intense battle. Breathing hard and dripping adrenaline, he looked up to see her smirking, half-teasing, half-relieved.","\"Can’t do anything without your sis, huh?\" she chided, her tone light but carrying an unmistakable edge of concern. Rey managed a crooked grin, the taste of danger and victory mingling in his mouth as he clutched the glowing pearl tightly.","\"Whatever. I would have dealt with them, you know. It was just taking time because of this damn water. I hate it. I hate it.\"","\"Oh, shut up, you spoilt brat. Now, give me a ride.\"","\"I don’t think your fat ass can fit in-\"","Alex grimaced.","\"I mean, two of us will slow down my buddy. How about I find another one for you?\"","Alex rolled her eyes as she swam a few paces away, already scouting for another mount. Rey let out a derisive chuckle, shaking his head. \"Yeah, right. You always think you’re so perfect, don’t you?\"","\"Keep dreaming, brat,\" Alex shot back over her shoulder, smirking. \"I’m just here to keep you from getting yourself killed. Besides, you know I’m the best backup you’ve got.\"","Moments later, Rey reappeared with a second beast—a sleek, armored sea turtle with a shell that shimmered like a circuit board. \"Behold, your new chariot,\" he declared, raising an eyebrow at her. \"Two rides are better than one. Now, hop on before those sharks decide to throw us another surprise party.\"","\"By the way, what are we doing about these pearls?\" Rey asked Alex as she was curiously eyeing the sea turtle. He would be lying if he said he wasn’t tempted to use them right then and there.","\"You know we need those pearls for points, little bro,\" she replied, her tone mixing playful sarcasm with genuine caution. \"Remember, the goal is to rack up points. Consuming them early might give you a temporary boost, but it won’t count toward our win—and besides, it might make you an even bigger target. So hand them over to me.\"","\"Ya. Ya. I understand.\" Rey let out a sigh and handed the pearls to her. The next second, Alex shamelessly tossed the pearls into her mouth.","Rey’s eyes widened in shock and betrayal.","\"What? I never said I couldn’t handle being a target. Do you know how difficult it is to have a husband who constantly outshines you? A single idiot like you would never understand the problems married life brings.\"","\"You bitch!\" Rey’s face twitched. \"This is not fair. You cannot take mine. Why don’t you go find some pearls on your own?\"","\"Oh, stop arguing like a brat and stand guard for me. I feel some breakthroughs coming.\" Alex happily whistled and closed her eyes as the divine glow around her started becoming brighter.","\"You fucking bully!\" Rey’s heart hurt, but ultimately, he did not care. He silently stood guard for his sister as she quickly processed the pearls."]},{"number":1412,"title":"Chapter 1412: A dutiful wife","paragraphs":["\"Alex, I am seriously going to kill you. The next pearl is mine. Fuck. We should at least keep some pearls for the event. What the hell are you doing? What the hell are we doing? Bro will be mad if we screwed up this event. You are going to make us lose!\" Rey shouted as he watched Alex gobble up the twenty-fifth pearl.","Alex paused mid-chew, her eyes widening in mock surprise as Rey ranted. \"Oh, come on, little bro,\" she drawled, wiping a stray bit of pearl residue from her lips. \"You know I’m doing this for us. More power means more options—and trust me, I’m not just eating them for the hell of it.\"","Rey’s face contorted with equal parts fury and disbelief. \"More options? What options? We’re supposed to be winning this event. Bro, he is gonna flip out and divorce you, you crazy woman!\"","Alex scoffed, floating closer with a half-smirk. \"Look, genius, the pearls aren’t just points—they’re our secret weapon. If we’re gonna survive the next wave of bullshit, we need the firepower. And besides, if we play it safe, we’re just another bunch of wimps waiting to be ambushed. I’m doing this for our future victory!\"","Rey shook his head, frustration mingling with reluctant admiration. \"You’re seriously insane.\"","She flashed him a mischievous grin. \"Relax, bro. We’ll figure it out. Think of it as investing in our own badassery. Once I’m fully powered up, we’ll hit the next stage so hard they won’t know what hit ’em.\"","Rey muttered under his breath, \"Damn, Alex... One of these days, you’re gonna get us into trouble, and I swear—\"","\"—I’ll save you from that trouble,\" Alex interrupted, playfully elbowing him. \"Just trust me, alright? Now, enough bitching—let’s move before the next wave of idiots shows up. And maybe, just maybe, I’ll save a pearl for you next time.\"","\"Was that not enough for a breakthrough?\" Rolling his eyes with a reluctant smile, Rey sighed and adjusted his grip on his spear. \"Yeah, yeah. Let’s roll, sis. Just don’t make a habit of devouring our future wins.\"","Alex let out an equally loud sigh. \"When are you going to get it? Only a naive idiot would save every single pearl they came across!\"","\"Sis! Sis!\" Rey suddenly called out with a shocked expression.","\"What?\" Alex grumbled. These pearls were making her crazy. It was as if she was on the verge of something, but she just needed an extra push. \"Did you spot more pearls?\" she spat out.","\"Hell, ya! Look there! Look at that glow! There are a lot of pearls in there, and the glow is white, which means they haven’t been consumed yet. We have hit the jackpot!\"","Alex stared dumbfoundedly for a moment before she laughed like a manic villain. \"We have hit the motherlode of stupid. Come on. Let’s go and take those before someone else snatches them.\"","Clearly, they were not the only ones eying the prize. Alex and Rey could already spot a lot of monsters gathering in the region.","And just as they pulled in they also saw a pair of red cloaks. These men had blood-red eyes and reeked of blood mana.","\"Vampires!\" Alex hissed. They had finally run into the opposition. The treasure hunt even started with the four clashing factions starting in their own corner, but it looked like everyone had started to wander into the enemy territory.","\"No, Alex look.\" Rey pointed to the woman who was clutching all those pearls. \"Ah, damn it.\"","Alex was equally shocked. It turned out that the naive and stupid were their own naive and stupid. Shen Yue and Mei Mei both were frozen solid as they stared at the insane amount of killing aura directed at them.","Of course, the next second, a loud roar erupted as an azure serpent popped out from somewhere, creating a barrier of water around the two, not letting anyone near them. This was followed by a barrage of ice spears shooting out of the barrier.","\"Hiltha is here.\" Alex smiled, shaking her head. Hiltha was the ice elemental spirit Mei Mei had bound to. It was too bad that of all the naive idiots they could run into, this group had run into this particular duo. The two might be a little slow on some things but they were sure as shit not weak.","Alex and Rey did not have to intervene at all as they watched the ice elemental spirit and the legendary tier azure serpent handle everything. The serpent basically snacked on all the monster fishes without leaving them any chance for escape.","As for the vampires, they decided that it was better for them to run for the time being. This was where Alex stepped in. \"I did not allow you two to leave.\"","[Divine Calling]","A pillar made of divine light shot up from the depths of the ocean waters, extending all the way to god knows where. Chains erupted from the pillar and shackled the two vampires, completely arresting them.","\"I had a little theory,\" Alex spoke as she swam toward them. \"If I kill you, will you spit out the pearls you already ate?\"","The two vampires looked at her in fear. \"We are the Fourth Lord’s men. You should know better than to touch us. Leave us this instant, and we shall forget all enmity and grant you—\" one of the vampires stammered, his voice low and venomous, his eyes darting nervously as the divine chains pulsed with celestial fire. The other one was trying very hard to break free, but he just couldn’t.","Alex’s gaze hardened, and she scoffed. \"Grant me what? Your sorry excuses? I’m not here to negotiate with spineless leeches. Besides, if you knew who my husband was... you will shit your pants. Die.\"","The two vampires couldn’t even put up a fight as their bodies drifted away lifelessly in the ocean. Naturally, Alex did not let those bodies go to waste. As a dutiful wife, she saved every body in her spatial ring."]},{"number":1413,"title":"Chapter 1413: A simple multi-use healing potion?","paragraphs":["\"This is huge.\" The realization sent a shiver down Liam's spine, his fingers tightening around the vial. His mind raced with possibilities, his pulse hammering with excitement. But that rush of adrenaline quickly turned into a heavy weight in his chest as a chilling thought crept into his mind.","The Elemental King.","That monstrous being was now hunting him. One more powerhouse was now after him.","The sheer magnitude of what he had done hit him like a big ass truck. He had stolen from a creature born purely out of Dao, a force that transcended ordinary existence. The Elemental King wasn't just strong—he was a walking embodiment of laws and power, the kind of existence that Liam wasn't even sure he could reach in his lifetime.","Would he ever reach that level?","That doubt gnawed at him, but Liam forced himself to push it aside. It was pointless to dwell on what he didn't have.","What he did have was an absolute cheat.","He glanced at his inventory and exhaled deeply.","The Stone Tablet - a relic that held mysteries far beyond his current comprehension. The Mysterious Cauldron - a powerful alchemical artifact that had transcended its limits and become a being beyond his understanding.","And now, this green liquid - a catalyst so powerful it could elevate his craft to a level no ordinary alchemist could dream of.","If all of this wasn't enough to skyrocket his Alchemy Dao, then he didn't know what was.","But there was one thing he still lacked.","Alchemical Knowledge.","Liam clenched his fists. For a while now, especially after he had started digesting the memory fragments of the two Transcendent alchemists he had claimed, he had come to a humbling realization—his so-called Grandmaster title was laughable in comparison.","It was as if he had cheated his way into the rank.","Compared to those two geniuses, he was a mere beginner, a child dabbling in an art he barely understood. His foundation was shaky, his comprehension incomplete. He had been making do with raw talent, instinct, and sheer force of will, but that wouldn't be enough anymore.","Now that he possessed three divine—or possibly celestial—tier treasures, the next step in his journey was clear.","He needed to master alchemy.","True mastery. Not just techniques but understanding.","And from the memory fragments he had stolen, he knew exactly where to go to gain that knowledge.","There existed a place, a hidden Alchemist Sanctuary, where true prodigies and masters of the craft honed their skills. If he could make it there, he could fill the gaps in his fundamentals, refine his techniques, and perhaps most importantly, develop a method to break through to the Transcendent Realm with his multiple Daos.","That was the real goal.","Liam's head ached from thinking about it. He needed to break through yesterday.","Time was running out.","It wasn't just about him anymore.","Mia. Derek. He had finally stumbled upon breadcrumbs that could lead him to both of them. The weight of his responsibility pressed on his shoulders, urgency fueling his every thought. If he wasted time, if he hesitated, he could lose his chance to bring them back.","That wasn't an option.","His gaze turned ice-cold as he finally shifted his focus to the prisoner trapped within his cauldron.","A slow smirk played on Liam's lips.","He still had work to do. He raised his hand to touch the cauldron tattoo on his chest. \"Senior, is it possible for me to talk to that guy?\"","For a minute, there was no response, but suddenly, Liam felt a warmth spread on his chest. A voice sounded in his mind. \"I have sensed your intent. You have decided on the path to further your Alchemy Dao. As a reward for your intent, I will allow you to interact with the prisoner as you please.\"","Liam was pleasantly surprised. He did not think the man would agree so easily. This was his chance. This guy was his key to finding out everything about the game world and where Mia was at the moment. This guy was the key to finding out every single detail about the divine high priestess.","The enmity between him and that woman was something that couldn't be erased. Only one of them can live and he was determined to be that person.","Liam's smirk deepened as he felt the warmth fade from his chest, signaling that the cauldron had granted him access. This was huge. The prisoner inside the cauldron wasn't just some random captive—he was a living treasure trove of information.","And Liam intended to wring every last secret out of him.","Taking a deep breath, he placed his hand over the cauldron's surface and willed it to establish a connection. Instantly, the temperature in the room shifted, a subtle pull of energy washing over him as his consciousness was drawn into the cauldron's internal space.","The moment his vision adjusted, he found himself standing in a dark, misty void. The air crackled with suppressed power, and in the distance, a silhouette of a man sat cross-legged on a floating stone platform. His body was wrapped in chains made of pure Dao energy.","Liam walked forward slowly, studying the figure. His once majestic robes were now tattered, his armor and items strewn about like trash, his long, golden hair flowing in the non-existent wind, but his posture remained regal, as if imprisonment was nothing more than an inconvenience to him.","Golden eyes flickered open, sharp and piercing, locking onto Liam with an intensity that could shatter mountains.","Liam's face twitched. This guy was in such a high spirit for someone being held captive. He first needed to do something about it. He was definitely not pleased with the holier-than-thou smug look on his face.","As soon as the thought crossed his mind, the environment around him responded. The air suddenly became colder, and swirls of nether started appearing all around him. The next instant, the comfortable look on the paladin's face started to change as the chains wrapped around him tightened, rather violently."]},{"number":1414,"title":"Chapter 1414: I dont like the look on your face","paragraphs":["In an instant, all the other types of energy from the room got sucked up and the entire place became filled with nether.","\"That feels nice.\" Liam smiled. \"How about you? Do you like your current accommodations? Hospitality is a very important part of where I come from. We love to welcome you with open arms.\"","As soon as he said that two giant hands made of pure nether reached for and grabbed the paladin, completely suffocating him.","If it had been a normal attack, it probably wouldn't have mattered, but the attack was full of dao. It was Dao-infused suppression. Liam could clearly see the impact it had on the paladin and yet, the man seemed to be completely fine, not showing an ounce of pain on his face.","\"Bravo.\" Liam clapped his hands. \"I really applaud your mental strength and persistence. But don't you think that this place is awesome too? A treasure I managed to find in the system event. I think I can do whatever I want here. And I intend to fully test it out today.\"","Silence.","Liam's smirk widened as he leaned forward, his voice low and edged with danger. \"By the way... what were you doing in that system event?\" His eyes gleamed, watching for even the smallest reaction. \"You shouldn't even be at the level of an awakener. And Mia—\" He paused, his voice turning sharp. \"That's not really Mia, is it?\"","Still, the paladin said nothing.","Liam's fingers twitched again. The nether hands twisted violently, their grip tightening around the prisoner's form, pressing harder, suffocating. \"Wow, you are really resilient. Let's see for how long though. I have some free time on my hands and I can be a villain all day long.\"","However, before Liam could cast the next attack, something changed. A huge tremor rocked the world and Liam started trembling. Fear and horror gripped his face as the entire place became filled with the unmistakeable divine energy.","In front of such pure divine energy, the nether did not stand a chance and was driven away in an instant. For the first time, the paladin's face showed a flicker of emotion. His eyes widened as arrogance and hope filled his eyes.","He watched Liam scream in utter dread before his entire being simply blasted apart into golden light specs. \"No.\" Only his scream echoed in the empty world. The entire world glowed brightly as the silhouette of a new figure appeared.","The words dripped with something beyond anger—disgust. The kind that was reserved for things beneath notice, for creatures that had already proven their uselessness.","The paladin's lips parted as if to speak, but the moment he did, the divine presence tightened, suffocating not with chains, but with sheer authority. His hope shattered just as fast as it had appeared.","\"I told you to handle everything,\" she continued, her voice smooth yet cutting, like a blade made of light itself. \"And now, because of your incompetence, I had to step in.","\"A disappointment.\"","Silence followed.","For the first time, the prisoner inside the cauldron looked small.","His arrogant posture faltered, his golden eyes darkening as the realization settled in. The flicker of defiance that had burned in him just seconds ago vanished like a candle smothered by an unforgiving storm.","She wasn't here to rescue him. She was here to punish him.","The figure of radiance stood before him, her presence warping the space around them. Though her features were still veiled in divine light, her eyes were piercing, sharp, like celestial spears carving into his soul.","\"Tell me.\" Her voice was calm, but the air shivered around it. \"Did you manage to get the item at least?\" The paladin clenched his fists. He knew there was only one correct answer.","And he didn't have it.","His silence spoke louder than any words. The divine presence intensified, the entire void trembling beneath the weight of her displeasure. The golden glow in the chains darkened, their inscriptions writhing like wounded creatures.","The paladin's body tensed as if bracing for the inevitable. And then...","PAIN.","A blinding spear of pure divine energy shot forward, slamming into his chest. It wasn't physical. It wasn't even just spiritual. It burned his very essence.","The paladin let out a soundless gasp, his body convulsing. His golden aura flickered violently, breaking apart like shattered glass. And yet, he did not scream.","He refused.","Even as his entire existence felt like it was being unwoven, he forced himself to endure it. The divine figure sighed, shaking her head as if his suffering bored her. \"You disappoint me.\"","The paladin staggered, his breath coming in ragged, uneven gasps. His once-pristine golden armor was cracked, his body trembling from the remnants of divine punishment. Still, he forced himself to look up.","\"Liam,\" he rasped, the name tasting like venom on his tongue. \"He took it.\"","Silence.","Then, a flicker of something unreadable passed through the divine figure's expression. She paused for a moment before laughing, a laughter that was soft, amused, and dangerous.","The paladin's heart sank. Because in that laughter, he heard something terrifying. The divine figure slowly tilted her head, her radiant eyes gleaming with something predatory.","\"Liam, huh?\" She took a single step forward and the entire world trembled. \"If that small insect can beat you again and again, you are no longer needed to serve me. You are completely and utterly worthless. You can disappear just like how he disappeared. You have led me to him and now you are no longer needed.\"","The chains around him shuddered violently as if sensing the divine decree before even he could. The once-glowing inscriptions began to fracture, their golden light dimming, and fading.","The paladin's body stiffened. \"No,\" he whispered, his voice breaking.","The divine figure only smiled a cold and indifferent smile. Her hand rose, glowing with the unyielding radiance of pure law.","The paladin lunged forward, his chains clanking loudly as he instinctively tried to reach toward her. \"Wait! I... I have something else for you. I did not return completely empty-handed. Wait. My priestess, please wait.\"","He let out a shaky breath and another drop of golden liquid floated out of him."]},{"number":1415,"title":"Chapter 1415: My priestess","paragraphs":["The divine high-priestess silhouette looked down upon the golden droplet with contempt clearly written on her face. In front of her, such a thing did not amount to much at all. It seemed as if she was simply going to dismiss that droplet without much of a thought.","The paladin rushed to explain before she did something drastic like that. \"Wait, my priestess. That is not a normal treasure. I found it inside one of the main vaults of the Pantheon faction. It has to be extraordinary I am sure of it.\"","The words tumbled from his lips desperately, his golden aura flickering like a dying flame. He knew one misstep, one wrong breath, and he would be erased, just like Liam.","For a moment, the divine high priestess remained motionless, the golden droplet still suspended between her fingers. Then, ever so slightly, her eyes narrowed.","The pressure in the void shifted. The paladin felt it immediately, the subtle, almost imperceptible change in her stance. To an outsider, she still looked like an untouchable goddess, her expression cold, unreadable.","But he knew better. The mere mention of the Forgotten Pantheon had changed something. Even if she wouldn't show it, even if she wouldn't acknowledge it, the weight of those words had struck a nerve.","The golden droplet pulsed in her palm, resisting her grasp, the fragment of ancient power within it seemingly rejecting her divinity. A speck of something beyond her control, no matter how insignificant.","The priestess exhaled softly, the barest trace of amusement curling at the edge of her lips. \"You truly are pathetic, clinging to scraps like a drowning man to driftwood.\" She let the words settle, her voice smooth, almost bored.","The paladin lowered his head, swallowing his frustration. \"Perhaps. But even scraps from a place such as that... hold weight, my priestess. You of all people know that sometimes scraps can hold true power that one hadn't seen in an entire era.\"","The priestess let out a small hum, tapping a finger against the floating droplet. It shuddered, glowing faintly, but didn't shatter under her touch. Her radiant eyes shifted back to the kneeling paladin. \"You are selling this way too much. And you are certain this came from the Forgotten Pantheon?\"","The paladin forced himself to nod. \"I swear it on my very existence, Priestess. It was buried deep, hidden away. I do not believe they intended for it to ever be found.\"","A long silence followed. The high priestess tilted her head, considering his words. Her fingers closed around the golden droplet, and for a brief second, the air crackled with an immense surge of divine energy, as if she intended to destroy it outright.","But she didn't. Instead, she let her hand fall to her side, the golden droplet vanishing into the endless folds of her radiance. She was keeping it.","\"Fine. You have proven to be useful enough for me to keep you on for some more time. This is your last chance. If you fail again, don't bother staying alive. I will hunt you down and kill you myself. There is nothing I hate more than a failure.\"","\"Yes, my priestess.\"","\"By the way, where did that cunt go? She did not return to the temple after the event. Did she run off by herself again?\"","The paladin flinched slightly at the priestess's choice of words but quickly lowered his head even further. He knew better than to react, especially when her irritation was so palpable. The fact that she was even asking about her meant that she was already displeased.","He had to tread carefully.","\"My priestess,\" he began cautiously, his voice even but submissive. \"High priestess Morencius left the event without me. I have no idea where she went because she did not discuss any of her plans with me. Do you want me to try and track her using one of the soul marks?\"","The divine high priestess's expression didn't change, but the void itself seemed to tighten around them, as though reality itself recoiled from her displeasure. The pressure was unbearable.","The paladin clenched his fists. He had expected this reaction, but that didn't make it any easier to endure.","\"I see.\" The priestess's tone was unreadable.","The paladin hesitated before adding, \"There is a possibility she has aligned herself with someone else... or is searching for something on her own.\"","At this, the priestess's gaze sharpened, her divine radiance flaring slightly, sending golden ripples across the space. \"Aligned herself? With who?\"","The paladin swallowed. \"It is only speculation, but... she was asking me a great deal about the true royal families. I think that was just a ruse to cover up what she was really interested in.\"","\"We heard the reports about the movements of the vampire dogs and I have a feeling she is interested in them. She thinks they are onto something. I think that is the reason why she tagged along with me in this event. She wanted to run into some of those dogs to interrogate them.\"","The divine high priestess remained silent for a long moment, her expression unreadable. The golden ripples from her aura slowly faded, but the pressure in the void did not lessen. If anything, it only deepened an invisible weight pressing down on the paladin's very soul.","\"She is not foolish enough to defect,\" the priestess continued as if thinking aloud. \"But she is ambitious.\" Her golden eyes flickered with something sharp, something knowing. \"And ambition has led stronger creatures than her to ruin.\"","The paladin hesitated. \"Shall I—?\"","\"Let her run.\" The priestess's voice was absolute. \"If she wants to play games with corpses, let her waste her time.\" She exhaled, amused. \"She has never understood the fundamental truth, has she?\"","The paladin did not answer.","The priestess smiled, slow and cruel. \"It does not matter what secrets they uncover. What scraps of ancient power they dig up. They are still lesser beings.\" Her divine radiance pulsed once, the sheer force of her conviction shaking the void itself.","Then, she waved her hand dismissively. \"Still, it would be a shame to lose a useful pawn. Send a shadow to observe her. Do not interfere. I want to see just how far her delusions will take her.\"","\"Yes, my priestess.\"","Satisfied, she turned away, her thoughts already elsewhere. Then, after a pause, she added, \"And while you're at it, give me the trigger for the soul mark. I personally want to keep an eye on that cunt.\"","The man nodded weakly and raised his hand, producing yet another golden droplet. The droplet floated toward the priestess's silhouette, disappearing in the golden radiance.","The paladin finally let out a sigh of relief thankful that all of his offerings had been accepted. The high priestess had been in a particularly volatile mood today, and he had barely survived the encounter. He knew better than to think himself truly safe, but at least for now, he had bought himself more time.","However, just when he thought he was saved the priestess yet again glared at him with killing intent. \"Why are you still mute? What about the other things? Do I have to spell everything out on my own?\"","The paladin blinked in a daze. \"I...\"","\"What about that stone tablet? What about that worthless vermin Crawford? Do you also have the marks for them? I need all my assets back to initiate the next plan. Why are you continuing to be useless and waste my time?\"","The paladin quickly scrambled to produce two more divine droplets but he suddenly stopped. \"I do not sense the marks-\" He started explaining when he suddenly stopped. The look on his face changed into absolute horror when he suddenly realized something was off.","\"My priestess, why is my divine droplet still intact... my pries\" He stopped midway when he realized the entire thing was a ruse from the beginning.","The paladin's breath hitched, his body stiffening as a realization colder than the void itself settled into his bones. This... wasn't real.","Or rather, she wasn't.","His golden eyes flickered, darting to the priestess's form, but her expression remained unreadable, the same piercing radiance, the same untouchable divinity. Yet now, it was as if he were seeing past it, past the illusion, and past the oppressive presence.","The divine high priestess was not standing in front of him. This entire time, she had never been here at all. And yet, the weight of her will, her suffocating authority, it had all felt so real. His mind reeled. How?","His divine essence screamed at him, warning of something fundamentally wrong. It was as though reality itself was twisting around him, shifting in ways that were impossible.","Then it hit him. The cauldron. He was still inside the damned cauldron. The priestess was not there. She did not come here for him. She probably couldn't even sense him.","The paladin's eyes widened in horror, his body trembling as an unsettling, suffocating presence loomed behind him. He was not alone. Slowly, so painfully slowly, he turned his head.","And there he was.","A shadow at the edge of the void, woven from the deepest abyss, tendrils of nether curling from his form like wisps of smoke, his black eyes filled with killing intent.","Liam.","The paladin's throat tightened, his divine instincts screaming to flee, but he couldn't move. The world had already bound him. A slow, deliberate chuckle echoed through the void. \"Took you long enough,\" Liam's lips curled upwards into a cold, chilling smile. A smile that sent shivers down the paladin's spine, freezing him to his very core."]},{"number":1416,"title":"Chapter 1416: Took you long enough","paragraphs":["The paladin watched Liam walk to him in utter shock and horror. The man was calmly smiling but that only made it worse. It was the smile of a predator, one who had already closed the trap and was now watching his prey realize it far too late.","\"I have to admit,\" Liam continued, voice smooth, almost amused, \"I thought you would have better mental strength than that. Dude, you folded so quickly. I have seen pigs have better mental resistance.\"","\"You are alive.\" The paladin repeated looking in a daze.","\"Ya, no shit, Sherlock. You really do think of me as an insect, don't you? Is that why your mind was so weak that it fell apart so easily? You don't think someone from a trash planet could stand up against someone like you or that bitch?\"","The paladin shook his head. \"No, this is my priestess punishing me. I will not show weakness to my priestess. This is all just an illusion.\"","Liam chuckled darkly, the sound echoing ominously through the void. \"Denial? Cute. But I'm afraid this isn't one of your divine hallucinations. No judgmental goddess watching from above. No cleansing fire waiting to redeem you. Just you, me, and a whole lot of regret.\"","The paladin's hands trembled as he instinctively tried to summon divine power—but nothing answered his call. No light. No warmth. No divinity. No guidance. Just the suffocating chill of nether creeping up his spine.","\"This... this isn't real,\" he muttered again, but the tremor in his voice betrayed the growing doubt gnawing at the edges of his mind. \"You're not supposed to be alive. She... she erased you.\"","Liam's grin widened, cruel and knowing. \"And yet, here I am. Funny thing, really. You all walk around like you own reality, like fate and divinity bend at your feet. But you never stop to think, what happens when someone refuses to follow the script?\"","He stepped closer, nether rising in his wake, slithering like living ink. \"What happens... when the 'villain' rewrites the story?\"","The next second, divine energy once again flooded the space and Liam's figure let out an agonized shriek before disappearing. The priestess made another appearance.","\"You disappoint me. I told you to get rid of that annoying pest and yet all you do is fail over and over again. You were defeated by the illusion of someone dead. Why should I continue wasting my time with someone like you?\" A cold laughter resounded.","The paladin shivered as he looked up again with hope in his eyes. He did not dare to believe this. He refused to believe this and yet this was the truth, so how could he not believe it?","\"You are pathetic. I told you to erase that world out of existence. No one should come to know what we have been doing. I told you to take care of it and yet nothing has come of it.\"","The paladin's throat bobbed as he struggled to breathe beneath the crushing weight of her words. The divine pressure pressing down on him now was not just power, it was contempt. It was judgment. It was the slow, deliberate dismantling of what little worth he had left in her eyes.","\"My priestess,\" he croaked, trying to find some thread of redemption to cling to, \"I would not have lost. I had the perfect opportunity to right all the wrongs and erase him once and for all, but the Elemental King...\"","\"Excuses!\" Snapped the priestess.","\"I will release you now. Consider what happened just now as a punishment for your actions. If you fail me again... Go take care of that blasphemous world and make it disappear from the myriad realms.\"","\"Yes, my priestess.\" The man answered with determination in his eyes. \"It is only a matter of time. I have already conferred with the divine oracles. That world is not for long. Their elites are going to face a major catastrophe soon. None of them will survive it. I am sure of it. Even if their world is now hidden with the karmic link we have with the world it is impossible to evade our eyes for long. I will exterminate that world for you, my priestess. This is my unbreakable vow to you, my priestess \"","The priestess said nothing for a long moment. Then, with a cold flick of her hand, the pressure around him lifted, and the golden chains that had shackled his soul unraveled and vanished into the air like mist. The void pulsed once more with divine light before dimming.","\"Go,\" she said. \"Cleanse the filth. Erase the shame. If that world still dares to breathe when the cycle turns, know that your existence ends with it. Wait. What about the system event then? Did you manage to locate what we needed?\"","The paladin's face immediately changed. His mind was in a mess again. Something snapped and suddenly he found himself shackled all over again in suffocating nether.","\"Tch. Tch. Two times in a row? Now that's really pathetic. What is wrong with you? At this rate, you are going to get some achievement for the best whistle-blower. You are so bad that everyone is going to think you simply giving me all the information I want willingly.\" Liam shrugged. \"I think it's only a matter of time before that divine bitch pays for all of her sins.\"","\"No!\" The man screamed in terror and agony. \"Don't talk about her like that. An insect like you can never even get near her. Your body will vaporize before you even step into our world.\"","Liam grinned, utterly unbothered by the paladin's panic. The suffocating nether continued to coil around the man like a thousand venomous serpents, constricting, sinking deep into his very soul. \"That's good to know. See that's one more piece of information you have given me. So I cannot enter the divine realms without a body of a certain degree of divine affinity.\"","The paladin looked slightly startled but he did not care. \"It doesn't matter. You will never be able to reach my priestess.\"","Liam smiled silently. He walked closer to him and then leaned in. \"Sure, I might not be strong enough to ever step into one of your divine realms but she can come to me, right? You know that bitch very well after all. Don't you think she will come running to me if I toss a breadcrumb her way?\"","The paladin's eyes widened in horror as he bent his head low, unwilling to look up any longer.","\"Don't worry. Very soon she will be joining you. I will lay a trap for her so perfect she'll think it was her own divine will leading her into it,\" Liam whispered, his voice dripping with venomous promise. \"All I need is the right lure. And thanks to you... I know exactly what bait to use.\"","The paladin trembled, a low, guttural sound escaping his throat, half denial, half despair. Nether licked at his limbs, feeding off his fear, amplifying it. His connection to the divine was flickering like a dying star, and in this space, Liam's space, he was powerless.","Liam's words continued to taunt him when another vicious cycle once again started. Liam's image exploded with a shriek and the divine priestess appeared in front of him yet again."]},{"number":1417,"title":"Chapter 1417: And yet, here I am","paragraphs":["While Liam calmly observed the chaos within the cauldron space, the archaic voice sounded in his mind. \"Brat, you have some skills, I must say. This is entertaining. I have not been this entertained for a long time.","Liam's lips curled into a subtle smirk. \"I aim to impress,\" he replied inwardly, keeping his focus on his soul avatar wreaking havoc in the cauldron's depths. Using the cauldron itself wasn't that complicated as all he needed was to use his will but creating a soul avatar on the other hand...","However, unexpectedly Liam had somehow managed to grab the interest of the senior. He needed to make this interaction count. He needed this chance to learn more. A technique casually dropped by the senior was so powerful. He needed more.","The cauldron spirit chuckled, a sound that sent a ripple of power through the mental connection. \"Entertainment aside, you've managed to extract more from that divine puppet than I expected. But understand this, what you're treading into now... isn't some mid-tier power struggle or clever plan.\"","\"You're poking the rim of a throne that's stood for eons. The sacred lineage of the divine priestesses is a long one. It is bigger than your world, even this entire sector. The divine rulers belong to one of the ancient clans and as a high-priestess, she is bound to have their blessing. If she comes for you, and she will, it won't be as prey. It'll be to annihilate.\"","Liam nodded. \"Then I'll be ready.\"","There was a pause, and then the voice became serious. \"Then you'd best get stronger, brat. Much stronger. And quickly. Because whether you realize it or not, she and me, we've already placed our bet on you.\"","Liam's heart thudded. Was he referring to the stone tablet?","\"Senior,\" Liam quickly spoke up before the archaic voice disappeared without any notice. The man only spoke when he wanted to and only revealed himself on his whim, so it was best to not delay anything. \"Senior, about the soul avatar technique, is it possible-\"","\"Let me stop you right there, brat. You are a greedy little rascal, aren't you? Do you always aim for what is beyond you?\"","\"Please forgive me, senior. I must ask. If my soul strength is high enough, then is it possible for me to project more than one soul avatar at a time? And project it outside?\"","There was silence for a moment, like the cauldron itself was weighing the absurdity of the question. Then, a low rumble of laughter echoed through Liam's mind, genuinely amused.","\"Hah! You really are a mad one,\" the cauldron spirit laughed. \"You think you're ready to split your very essence and throw it around like a child playing marbles? You are still in the awakening realm. What you are talking about is something that Dao lords barely dare to try. Only the Dao masters are capable of such a feat.\"","Liam didn't respond. He stood there, eyes calm, expression resolute. The silence on his end said everything. He wasn't joking. He wasn't fantasizing. He was asking because he was already halfway down the path.","After a long moment of silence, the archaic voice sounded again. \"It is possible... but it's not merely about soul strength. The technique you performed just now was an echo, a projection, anchored and fed by this cauldron. Without my support, your soul would've torn like paper in a storm. To make an avatar on your own, you would need control, balance, and a comprehension of your Dao so complete that even a moment of hesitation could unravel you.\"","\"But... it is possible. I've seen it before. There were once awakened kings who walked the myriad realms with three avatars roaming three battlefields at once, one gathering resources, one spreading their doctrine, and one unleashing slaughter.\"","Liam's eyes gleamed.","Then, almost fondly, the spirit rumbled, \"Fine. I understand why you want to walk down this path. As a soulmancer, this path is ideal for you. I will teach you the next step. Survive your next breakthrough and I'll show you how to make the first real soul avatar. One unanchored. One fully your own.\"","Liam took a deep breath and bowed his head, his fists clenched with anticipation.","\"Thank you, senior. I won't disappoint you.\"","There was no response in return which meant that the cauldron had gone silent again. Liam spared one more glance at his Soul avatar sitting inside the cauldron and torturing the paladin. His gaze turned cold and he started to walk out of the system shop.","On his hand, the two divine droplets floated. Whatever was happening inside his being, inside the cauldron was one thing, but there were other matters on the outside he needed to pay attention to.","Liam connected to his spatial artifact, placing the two divine droplets. He was not sure how to remove the restrictions on these. It was going to take some time. After depositing the droplets, he let his senses probe the spatial artifact one more time before closing it.","Nothing inside had changed at all. The dragon lady was still acting or maybe she really was in some deep meditation. Either way, she showed no signs of reaching out to him. His army was still inside. Now that the system event was complete, he needed to head to the nether half of the world and release them.","As for completely unlocking the spatial artifact and merging Crawford's complete soul with it, he still did not feel comfortable doing it. He has a feeling doing something like that might trigger some sort of tracker.","Ultimately, the item was something he had taken from within the game. He did not want to press that trigger unless he was ready to face consequences. Especially now that the world was safely hidden for the time being.","\"Everything in due time.\" He mumbled to himself as he walked out to meet Tilia.","\"How did everything go? Are you alright?\" The fairy was waiting for him, right by the doorstep, her face full of worry.","Liam smiled as he gently patted her. \"I am fine. See.\""]},{"number":1418,"title":"Chapter 1418: Soul avatar","paragraphs":["Tilia's anxious eyes moved, examining Liam from head to toe as if expecting him to suddenly crumble into dust despite his reassurances. But when she felt the steady pulse of his mana and saw the calm in his eyes, her tense expression finally softened.","Liam chuckled at her cute reactions. \"Say, do you know how to unlock something that is encased in some sort of divine blood or divine liquid or whatever this thing is?\" He fished out the divine droplet and showed it to Tilia.","The fairy's eyes quickly widened. \"Where did you get this from?\" She stared at the droplet unblinkingly, bringing her slender finger towards it in a trance. However, as soon as she went near it, she took her finger back in a rush as if she got burned.","\"If I am not wrong, only someone with a high divine affinity, like a ridiculously high divine affinity, should be able to analyze it and see how the restrictions can be undone.\" Tilia paused and then added with an odd expression on her face. \"Maybe your red-headed wife can decipher it for you.\"","Liam laughed. \"You mean Alex? What? Are you guys fighting?\"","Tilia puffed out her cheeks, her wings flaring slightly in indignation. \"We're not fighting. I just don't like how she treats me sometimes. She is just rude to me for no reason. It's infuriating. I-\" She stopped suddenly, realizing that she had gone overboard.","Liam's grin widened as he crossed his arms, leaning against the nearest wall with a relaxed posture. \"Go on,\" he said, his tone teasing. \"Don't hold back on my account. Tell me all about how terrifying Alex is.\"","Tilia turned beet red, her wings fluttering erratically behind her. \"She's not terrifying! She's just... smug. And loud. And she always acts like she knows better. Even when she does know better!\" The fairy huffed again, then turned away, her voice dropping to a grumble. \"It's hard to argue with someone who's always charging into danger and still somehow pulling everyone out of it.\"","Liam let out a soft chuckle. \"She does have a talent for chaos,\" he said, then glanced at the droplet still faintly pulsing in his hand. \"Let her come back, and I will see what she can do about this.\"","His mind, however, briefly went back to what that paladin had said. Was there really some danger to the elites of this world? Or perhaps the man was simply spouting nonsense, knowing he had already fallen for the trap?","He had already asked his soul avatar to focus on this, but it would take some time to get some meaningful information. Would it then be too late to warn them about it?","Liam then thought of something. What if they were already in danger? \"Tilia. Tell me what you know about this treasure hunt event. Has it started already?\"","Tilia blinked, her brows furrowing as Liam's tone shifted from playful to serious in an instant. \"Hold on, I'll check.\" She tapped her fingers on the system screen. \"","\"It has started,\" she said, voice clipped. \"In fact... It's already two phases in. And—\" her expression darkened, \"I'm detecting energy surges way beyond what's allowed for the current tier of players.\"","Liam's eyes narrowed. \"What kind of surges? What are you talking about? Isn't a system event supposed to be tampering-proof?\" Even as he was saying it, he did not believe it since he had personally witnessed how crazy a system event can be, but he still hoped that it was not true. \"Can you tell me anything more at all?\"","Tilia shook her head. \"All I can see is that this event was supposed to be restricted to awakeners, and yet there are two transcendents inside the event at the moment. There are two more hours left. We cannot do anything about it. No one can enter it. No one can exit it. No one can do anything about it. I am sorry.\"","Liam clenched his fists. He did not like this at all.","\"They took your legendary pets with them. They are well prepared, and they have all made tremendous progress in their paths. You have to trust them.\"","Liam remained silent for a while before nodding. He then walked over to the main guild base, Luna popping out of him as they reached it. She immediately tried to hog Liam's ears, but several guild members recognized her and came to pay respects to her, keeping her very busy.","Liam quietly went to his room and lay on the bed. He closed his eyes and restarted his soul cultivation for his second constellation.","He then stopped and took out the soul minion of the first guy he had encountered in the desert world, the guy who kept trying to stick a soul mark on him again and again. He couldn't help but wonder if he could do something similar and tag his personal soul mark on someone else.","He then thought of something even ridiculous. What if that soul mark was enough to temporarily form a small and dispensable soul minion? Could he trade places with such a soul minion?","Liam's mind raced with ideas. He closed his eyes to contemplate the new idea. Sure, there might be legendary pets and they might have become more powerful, but when it came to family, it was simply not enough. It would never be like he was personally guarding them.","At the same time, he couldn't do anything openly. If they knew that he was always on standby to rescue them, their growth would be hampered. The only option here was to stick a soul mark on them without their knowledge so Liam could keep an eye on everything that was going on.","Sure, some might call this controlling and paranoid behaviour. But fuck them. He did not care what it looked like. He just did not want to feel this helpless again. It was not their fault that he kept making enemies everywhere he went.","\"One more hour...\" Liam waited patiently, and soon, the time was here.","His heart raced as he instantly teleported to the system shop to find out what was going on. The first thing he saw was the grim expression on Rey's face as he slowly walked out. Something was wrong. Something had gone terribly wrong."]},{"number":1419,"title":"Chapter 1419: Something wrong","paragraphs":["\"Bro, she is never going to let me forget this. Alex is already a Transcendent.\" Rey looked up and spoke. \"She broke through before me. Fuck. Fuck my life.\"","Liam stared at Rey, blinking once.","\"That's it?\" he asked, half-expecting Rey to say someone had died or a portal had opened into hell. \"You scared the hell out of me, and you're having a breakdown over Alex transcending first?\"","Rey ran a hand through his hair, clearly distraught. \"You don't get it, man. I've been one step ahead of her the whole damn time. The whole time! Now I'm the sidekick again. The comic relief. The handsome comic relief, but still—this is tragic.\"","Liam couldn't help but chuckle. \"Rey, she broke through, which means she probably saved your ass somewhere in there. Again. Be grateful. You can have your ego crisis after we confirm everyone's alive.\"","Rey grimaced. \"Ugh, I hate how reasonable that sounds.\" He sighed and rubbed his temples. \"But yeah... she's fine. Shen Yue's fine. Mei Mei is fine. Everyone's fine... We won the damn event. Bro, I am going to secluded training for a bit. I will see you in a bit. Don't mind me.\"","The guy sounded as if he was joking, but he genuinely looked depressed. Liam did not bother with him anymore as more and more people started appearing behind Rey.","A bright redhead caught his eye, and the next moment, he was toppled over by a blur of energy and flying hair.","\"Liaaam!\" Alex crashed into him, tackling him in a full-body hug that would have broken bones if he were anyone else. \"You won't believe what I did!\"","\"I think I have a guess,\" Liam groaned, patting her back. \"Maybe something that starts with a T and ends with ranscendent?\"","Alex pulled back just enough to smirk at him, her eyes glowing with power that hadn't been there before. \"Damn right. You should've seen the look on everyone's faces when it happened. It was chef's kiss—especially Rey's. I thought he was going to melt.\"","\"He almost did,\" Liam laughed.","Alex burst out laughing and then looked Liam over. Her smirk faded into something softer. \"You okay? You look... tired. And worried. Everything went well. There was a moment of touch and go, but Eldrin stepped up.\"","\"Eldrin?\"","\"Yup, what are the odds? He became a transcendent too. With both of us around, we completely smashed the event and bagged the win. The system event-\" She started then she suddenly stopped as her gaze met Tilia's. \"How about we go somewhere private and discuss the rest?\"","Liam only briefly managed to glance at Shen Yue and Mei Mei before Alex decidedly dragged him back to the guild base, to his private quarters and then to the huge master bedroom inside. \"I missed you so much.\" She gave him a big hug and then pulled him to the bed.","Liam smiled as he felt her hands wrap around him. Her body was warm and her presence was the same—fierce, grounding, chaotic in the best possible way. He let her hold him, his fingers brushing lightly against her back as he closed his eyes for a second.","\"I missed you too,\" he murmured. He knew he had some difficult news for her, so he indulged her for the next few hours before Alex finally gave in and collapsed, her slender naked body curled up at his side.","Liam gently patted her. \"Are you okay?\"","Alex bit her lips in embarrassment. \"No way. I can't go again, you monster.\"","Liam chuckled, brushing a strand of red hair away from her face as she buried it against his shoulder. \"That's okay,\" he murmured. \"I have a lot to discuss with you anyway.\"","Alex's eyes fluttered open at the shift in his tone—light-hearted, but lined with something heavier. She pushed herself up on one elbow, her expression sobering. \"What happened?\"","Liam didn't answer immediately. He stared at the ceiling for a moment, his fingers idly tracing patterns against her arm. \"I ran into Mia,\" he finally said. \"And not just her. There was a paladin with her... the same guy from the tutorial world.\"","Alex's breath caught. \"Wait. You're serious? Mia? As in, our Mia?\"","Liam nodded slowly. \"It wasn't a dream or a trick. She's real. Alive. But... not the same. Something's wrong. She didn't recognize me—not really. It was like talking to a puppet with a familiar face.\"","He sat up now, resting his elbows on his knees. \"I think there might be a soul possessing her or something like that.\"","Alex's eyes reddened. All the happiness from her face instantly drained and she sat up tears spilling from her eyes. \"Why? Why did they do this to her? Oh, god. Oh god. What am I doing... I am here celebrating for such a small thing while she is... oh god... Mia is suffering, isn't she... Liam... please... do you think she is suffering... oh god, I am really useless. I have let her down. I can't... I can't...\"","Liam turned to her quickly, catching her trembling hand in his. \"Hey. Hey, Alex. I don't know everything yet. But I'll find out. I promise.\" His voice was steady, the same unshakeable resolve that had carried him through countless battles and monsters, but in this moment, it was for her.","Alex clutched Liam's hand like it was the only thing keeping her grounded. Her entire frame trembled, tears dripping silently down her cheeks. \"She was always stronger than me, you know?\" she whispered hoarsely.","\"Always the calm one. The one who held my hand when I was scared of the dark, who stood up for me when I got into fights at school. I promised her I'd protect her too one day. And now... now I don't even know where she really is.\"","Liam gently pulled her in, wrapping his arms around her as she curled into him, her body shaking with quiet sobs. \"You're not useless,\" he murmured. \"Don't ever say that. Mia's still in there. I know it. Otherwise, the paladin would not have accompanied her.\"","Liam nodded. \"I am sure of it. Whoever is inside her hasn't completely erased her yet. There's still time. We can get her back.\"","Alex didn't say anything at first, just held onto him like the world might fall apart. But after a few minutes, her sobs lessened, and her breathing steadied. When she pulled back, her eyes were bloodshot.","\"Then we're going to burn down every world, every realm, every divine palace if we have to. I want my sister back.\" She stood up and a robe materialized from her space ring, covering her body. \"Where is that paladin now?\"","Liam looked up at her and shook his head. \"You cannot see him right now. He is somewhere inside me.\" He stood up and placed his hand on her shoulder. \"Calm down. He's still alive. Barely. I left a soul avatar to keep digging into him. And we're getting results. Slowly, but surely.\"","\"Give me just a little more time and we will go and search for her. I promise you. If they couldn't destroy or didn't destroy her soul until now, then the chances are we still have some time. Trust me. If we become impatient, then we might just lose her permanently.\"","Alex's fists clenched.","She bit down on her lip, every muscle in her body tight with restrained fury. For a long moment, she said nothing—just breathed, her chest rising and falling with uneven force, until finally, she exhaled in one long, trembling breath.","\"Okay,\" she said. The word was a whisper, but it was laced with enough steel to carve through stone. \"Okay. I'll wait. But I'm not going to sit still. I'm going to get stronger, Liam. So strong that when the time comes, I won't just stand behind you—I'll be beside you. I want to be the one to bring her back.\"","Liam gave her a small nod, his eyes full of quiet pride. \"That's all I ask.\"","Alex stepped closer, pressing her forehead against his. \"Just... don't shut me out. Not with this. Not with her.\"","\"I won't,\" Liam promised. \"And there is a way you can help me out right now.\" He took out the drop of golden liquid from his spatial artifact. \"This is something I took from him. Can you figure out how to break down the divine barrier around it?\""]},{"number":1420,"title":"Chapter 1420: Mia?","paragraphs":["Alex's eyes narrowed as she examined the golden droplet hovering in Liam's hand. The air around it shimmered faintly as if reality itself hesitated to touch it. She didn't reach for it right away—her transcendent senses stretched forward first, probing the liquid from all sides.","But the next second, the liquid unravelled completely, coming undone in Liam's hand. It looked like a divine affinity was all it required to unlock the droplet. The paladin must have really believed the illusion to have simply handed over the treasure just like that.","This was good news because this meant Mia's soul mark was also in their possession.","\"Let's wait first before opening the soul mark. I need to prepare more for that.\" Liam explained.","Alex nodded. She was impatient in getting to Mia, especially when they were so close to her but she was also not foolish enough to think they could simply charge in without consequence.","Her eyes lingered on the golden mist now dispersing into Liam's palm, the remnants of the divine droplet dissolving like morning dew touched by sunlight. \"Yeah,\" she said slowly, \"we can't afford any mistakes. Not with her.\"","Liam pulled her closer and gently placed a kiss on her forehead. He then turned his attention to the small crystal that now lay on his palm. \"What do you think this is?\" He mumbled, and all of a sudden, a system prompt flashed in front of him, completely surprising him.","[Ding! System Over-ride Command]","[Ding! Error]","[Ding! System Over-ride Forced]","[Ding! Error]","[Ding! System Over-ride Successful]","[Ding! Welcome to the Eternal System. Do you wish for greatness? Do you wish for supremacy? Do you wish for unlimited power? Do you wish to alter your path? Do you wish to accept the Eternal System's offer? Yes / No]","Alex took a cautious step closer, sensing the sudden shift in the atmosphere. \"What happened, Liam? What is this?\"","\"See for yourself.\" Liam handed the crystal over to her.","Alex reached out slowly, her fingers brushing the crystal in Liam's palm—and instantly, her expression tensed. A sharp breath escaped her lips as she too pretty much received the same system messages.","She blinked, stunned. \"What the hell is this artifact? Did it just offer to replace the system rules?\"","Liam's gaze remained locked on the crystal. \"It's connected to the Eternal System. Whatever that is, it just hijacked the current framework. The paladin should have gotten it from one of those old worlds. This shouldn't be a simple thing.\"","Alex's fingers curled into a fist. \"Or maybe a doorway. A crack in the system. A backdoor placed by someone, maybe even a God. Just how powerful did they have to be to create something like this...\"","Liam's brow furrowed, his thoughts racing. \"A God... or something worse. Something before the Gods. If this thing really has the power to override system control, it means the Eternal System either predates the current structure... or was designed to oppose it. I am not sure if this thing is safe to use.\" He wasn't sure which possibility was more terrifying.","Alex nodded slowly. \"I agree too. Besides, it's asking if I want to change my path. I have no intention of doing that.\"","\"Hmmm.\" Liam hummed in agreement. After talking with her for some more time, he left the room and walked over to the ground floor to find the others.","Shen Yue and Mei Mei were sitting at a long table in the guild's central hall, surrounded by food, drinks, and a few empty potion vials—clear signs they'd just wrapped up a serious recovery session after the event.","Mei Mei noticed him first and immediately waved him over. \"Brother!\" she called, her voice bright and bubbly. \"Took you long enough to come say hi. Thought you got kidnapped by sis Alex.\" Mei Mei giggled, her small hands stuffed with candied fruit. \"She tackled him like a wild beast.\"","Liam smiled faintly and sat across from them. \"You all did well. I heard you cleared the event.\"\\\\","Shen Yue smiled, quickly standing up and serving some food to Liam. Even though there were plenty of maids available to do things like this, she liked to personally see to Liam's meals when he was around—an old habit that hadn't faded, no matter how far they'd come.","\"Of course we cleared it,\" she said, placing a plate of roasted beast meat and spirit fruit in front of him. \"You didn't expect anything less from us, right?\"","Liam accepted the food with a small nod of appreciation. \"No, I didn't. But I also heard the event wasn't exactly... standard.\"","Shen Yue's cheerful expression dimmed just a little. She sat back down, brushing a lock of hair behind her ear. \"Yeah. Without Alex and Eldrin, we wouldn't have lasted.\"","Mei Mei nodded along enthusiastically, her cheeks puffed up like a squirrel. \"The vampires were strong. They were using some sort of poison that spread through the water and weakened everyone.\"","Liam patiently heard the two of them as they described the treasure hunt event. After a while, Mei Mei bid farewell and left for secluded training. The effects of the pearls they had all consumed still hadn't worn off, pushing their foundations closer to the edge of a breakthrough. She skipped away with a quick wave, humming something under her breath.","Shen Yue lingered, sipping a clear tea that shimmered faintly with some sort of calming herb infusion. She sat beside Liam again, her expression quiet, thoughtful.","\"I am sorry about earlier. I had some difficult news for Alex, so I just left with her.\" Liam explained. Shen Yue nodded gently. \"It's okay. I don't mind.\"","\"Are you sure?\"","\"Yes. Of course.\" Shen Yue smiled. Liam gently pulled her closer and kissed her cheek. He then started telling her everything that happened in the system event.","\"You met Mia?\" Shen Yue was utterly shocked. \"We need to bring her back home. Both Alex and Rey...\"","Liam pressed her hand gently. \"Yes, I know. There is also something else. Let's gather for a guild meeting.\""]},{"number":1421,"title":"Chapter 1421: Do you wish to accept the Eternal System’s offer?","paragraphs":["While the guild was gathering for a meet-up, Liam filled Shen Yue in about the paladin and the weird treasure that he had obtained from him. Shen Yue silently listened to him, but when they were about to head out for the guild meeting, she stopped him.","\"Liam, I have a selfish request to ask of you.\"","Liam turned to her, a faint crease forming between his brows. Shen Yue didn't usually preface her words like that—not with him. \"What is it?\" he asked softly.","She hesitated, her gaze dropping to the floor for a second before lifting to meet his. \"If... if this Eternal System thing really does what it claims—if it can rewrite paths, break rules, change destinies—I want you to consider using it on me.\"","Liam blinked, caught completely off guard. \"What? Why would you—\"","\"I know I am asking too much. I know there is probably someone else in the guild who has contributed more and who deserves more to use such a treasure, but I want to be selfish this one time, please. Let me use it.\"","Liam pulled her closer and hugged her, fully understanding what she was trying to say. Shen Yue sobbed in his arms, quiet and restrained, like she had been holding it all in for far too long.","Her fingers clutched at the back of his robes, and for a moment, all the strength she usually wore like armor cracked—revealing the fear beneath. Not fear of death, but of being left behind. Of becoming a shadow in a world that demanded more and more from them every day.","\"I don't want to be the one you have to protect all the time,\" she whispered into his chest. \"I want to be someone who protects you, too. Even if just once.\"","\"I don't want to... I want to stay by you... just like Alex... I want to walk beside you. I don't want to age while you are still young. I don't want to die while you are still alive. I want to live a long and happy life with you. I want to do my little part to help you when needed.\"","\"I want to be someone you can rely on. I want to be someone who can protect Mei Mei and the guild. I don't want to be weak and helpless anymore.\"","Liam closed his eyes and held her tighter. \"Yue, you already do. More than you know. It's not that I don't want you to use this. I am telling you this is very risky. I have no idea or control over what is going to happen.\"","Shen Yue didn't flinch. Her grip on him only grew steadier. \"I know. I understand the risks, Liam. But if there's even a chance—just a chance—that it can give me a path that lets me walk beside you... then I want to take it.\" She pulled back slightly, enough to look into his eyes, her own gaze burning with a rare determination.","Liam stayed silent for a long while. \"Fine. You can use it. But first, I need to talk to Eldrin and Tilia. I don't care about using this treasure. I just don't want to lose you. Mei Mei is not the only one I care about. I need you in my life too. I don't want to throw all this away on a whim.\"","He took out the crystal and looked at it again. \"If this is how you feel, then just give me some time, and I will find something else for you. I will help you find more opportunities. There is no need to throw everything away on something unknown and strange.\"","He was about to place the crystal back again when the cauldron senior's voice rang in his ears. \"Brat, you are thinking too much. If it is something found in a system event, then you can confidently use it. There shouldn't be too many risks. I can guarantee you 90% that this thing is safe, and it is something crafted by those freaks, so it should be powerful.\"","\"Senior, can I trust that?\" Liam asked inwardly, his eyes never leaving Shen Yue's hopeful face.","The cauldron snorted. \"Boy, if this thing was truly a cursed abomination, it would have already tried to rewrite your soul the moment you touched it. The fact that it asked first? That means it follows rules. Rules that you wouldn't understand, but rules nonetheless. If that lass wants to become a freak like you, then this is really her best chance.\"","Liam's gaze shifted from the crystal to Shen Yue and back again. He sighed. \"Alright, Senior. I'll hold you to that 90%.\"","He looked back at Shen Yue and handed the crystal over with deliberate care. Her fingers trembled slightly as she took it, but her eyes remained steady. \"Are you sure about this?\" he asked one final time.","\"I've never been more sure of anything,\" she whispered, clutching the crystal to her chest. \"No matter what happens, thank you for believing in me. I will not let you down.\"","Liam gave her a grim smile. \"Idiot. Don't think too much. Only think about protecting yourself and your mind. Do you want to activate it now?\"","Liam would have preferred to talk to the elf or Tilia but the cauldron senior had weirdly chosen to come out at this time. More than the elf or Tilia, he was more capable of protecting Shen Yue if something bad happened. It was better to do this now while he was still paying attention and out and about.","Shen Yue hesitated for only a heartbeat before nodding. \"I am ready.\"","She took a deep breath, then held the crystal out in front of her. The moment she fed a trace of mana into it, the air changed.","[Ding! Eternal System detected user affinity.]","[Ding! Host accepted. Initiating synchronization...]","[Ding! Do you want power? Do you want to protect the man you love? Do you want to not feel helpless? Would you like to overwrite your fate path and forge a new path through the Eternal System? Warning: This choice is permanent.]"]},{"number":1422,"title":"Chapter 1422: I have a selfish request","paragraphs":["Shen Yue gasped as she snapped out of the trance she was in. She did not know when, but just as she read the system messages, her mind felt a little blurry. She felt extremely tempted to accept the choice.","It was also telling her all the right things as if the system prompt was tailor-made for her. As if it had already read her mind.","This was not a good thing. She looked up at Liam, and she knew he would instantly shut this down if she told him. So she bit her lips and accepted the prompt.","A system event treasure couldn't be a bad thing, right?","The moment Shen Yue accepted the prompt, the crystal started glowing with a bright golden light, and every bit of it shot towards her. The last of the golden light surged inward, disappearing into her chest like a sun being swallowed whole.","Her knees buckled slightly, but she caught herself, steadying her breath as a new energy surged through her veins—foreign yet intimately familiar, like meeting a version of herself that had always been buried under layers of expectation and fear.","Liam noticed the sudden shift in her expression. Her lips were slightly parted, her breath coming in shallow bursts, and a strange ripple danced across her irises. \"Yue?\" he asked, stepping forward with concern.","\"I... I'm okay,\" she lied quickly, forcing a smile. \"I think it worked.\"","Liam didn't buy it entirely. His eyes narrowed slightly, catching the faint tremble in her hands. \"Did something happen?\" he asked, more softly this time.","She shook her head. \"It just... took a lot out of me. I need a moment.\"","Liam was quiet for a while, then gave a slow nod. \"Alright. But if anything feels off—even slightly—you tell me. Immediately.\"","Shen Yue nodded, but deep down, a flicker of doubt crept in. What exactly had she just accepted?","As if answering her doubts, a system prompt flashed in front of her. Before she could read that, the prompt transformed into a small cat.","Shen Yue blinked in confusion as she stared at the cat.","Not a digital projection or some ethereal spirit—but a very real-looking, very smug little feline. It had sleek black fur, eyes like polished amber, and a tail that moved with lazy, deliberate grace. It blinked once at her, gave a yawn that showed too many sharp teeth for comfort, and then spoke.","\"Well, that was dramatic,\" it purred, voice smooth as silk. \"You mortals and your flair for the dramatic. But congratulations, initiate. You've just joined a very exclusive club.\"","Shen Yue staggered back a step. \"A... what?\"","The cat licked its paw nonchalantly. \"Oh, don't worry. You're not hallucinating. I'm the guide—well, sort of. You unlocked the Eternal Path Fragment. That means you get me. And I get you. Until you either ascend... or explode. But let's be optimistic.\"","\"Explode?\" Shen Yue echoed weakly.","The cat tilted its head. \"Metaphorically. Mostly. Depends how stubborn your soul is.\" It leapt up onto her shoulder as if it belonged there and nestled in like royalty. \"But we'll get to all that. For now... let's just say your destiny has taken a detour. And trust me—you are going to love this.\"","The room spun for a heartbeat as Shen Yue tried to process everything. A smug, talking cat perched on her shoulder? Exploding souls? Eternal Path Fragment?","And Liam—Liam was standing just a few steps away, still watching her closely, unaware that a cosmic upgrade in feline form had just claimed her like a chosen artifact.","She forced herself to stay calm. Her heart was still pounding in her chest, but her breathing slowly evened out. \"You're not going to explain everything now, are you?\" she muttered under her breath, more to the cat than to Liam.","The feline gave a delighted little purr. \"Oh, absolutely not. Where's the fun in that? You'll get the pieces in fragments. Just like everyone else before you. Besides, you wouldn't understand it all yet. Your mortal brain is still... squishy.\"","Shen Yue scowled, brushing a hand against her temple like she could somehow wipe away the smugness radiating off the creature. \"Can you at least tell me your name?\"","The cat's tail flicked, and it practically smirked. \"Names are powerful, girl. But you can call me Umbra for now. I've been many things. Guide. Lurker. Doom of Realms, once upon a time. But mostly, I'm your eternal headache.\" It paused. \"Oh, and one more thing—don't tell the soulweaver. Not yet. He'll ruin the calibration.\"","\"The who?\" Shen Yue asked, confused.","\"Liam,\" Umbra replied, stretching with a languid yawn. \"Now smile. Pretend everything is fine. It'll keep your ascension arc more entertaining.\"","Shen Yue clenched her fists, but she shook her head resolutely. The next second, she simply spilled everything to Liam.","\"A talking what?\" Liam was shocked.","Umbra, still draped across Shen Yue's shoulder like a pampered prince, yawned theatrically. \"Oh, come now, Soulweaver. Don't be so dramatic. I'm an interface. A facilitator. A rather fashionable manifestation of a very old and very exclusive system.\"","The next second, the cat became visible to Liam, and he could suddenly hear his voice.","Liam's expression shifted from wary concern to stunned disbelief the moment the sleek black feline shimmered into visibility before his eyes. For one second, it was just Shen Yue standing there, eyes wide and shoulders tense. The next—a talking cat appeared like it had always belonged in their world.","Even with all of his improved senses and perception, he couldn't sense the cat at all.","\"You've got to be kidding me,\" Liam muttered, staring at the creature now curled smugly around Shen Yue's shoulders like a scarf.","Umbra blinked at him with all the arrogance of a minor deity inconvenienced by lesser beings. \"I assure you, I am not. And now that you can see me, that means the 'calibration' is complete. Hooray for trust.\" It flicked its tail with a flourish, as if proud of its own dramatic timing.","\"Congrats, girl. You just made your life infinitely more difficult.\""]},{"number":1423,"title":"Chapter 1423: Umbra","paragraphs":["\"Why can I see you now?\" Liam asked sharply.","\"Because she told you,\" Umbra said with a smirk. \"Which means you're now part of the equation. So I had to update your perceptual permissions. You're welcome, by the way. Not everyone gets to admire this glorious visage.\"","Liam stepped closer, his gaze hardening. \"And what exactly are you? What is your role in this so-called Eternal Path?\"","Umbra gave a long-suffering sigh. \"Think of me as a guide. A mentor. A translator for the gibberish that is about to start rewriting your girlfriend's metaphysical blueprint. I help her survive the process... assuming she listens to me. Which, so far, she has not.\"","Shen Yue winced slightly, but Liam gently took her hand. \"Are you okay?\"","\"I think so,\" she whispered, her voice steadier than before. \"It's... overwhelming, but not painful. Just... strange. I don't feel weaker. If anything, I feel more. Like something inside me finally woke up.\"","Liam studied her for a long moment, then nodded once. \"Good. But if this thing—\" he shot a glance at Umbra, \"—so much as breathes wrong, I will find a way to remove it.","\"Oh, I like him,\" Umbra purred. \"So protective. So paranoid. This is going to be fun.\"","Liam didn't respond. He only pulled Shen Yue gently into a hug, murmuring into her hair, \"Whatever this thing is... we'll deal with it together. Don't worry and don't keep anything bottled up inside.\"","Umbra shrugged. \"You have to now. The moment she included you, everything became different. Now the system expects more from her because it already assumed you would be helping her.\"","\"I will be helping her.\" Liam's voice was quiet, but it rang with that steel-core certainty.","Umbra yawned, clearly unimpressed. \"Touching. Now if the two of you are done making heart-shaped promises, we do have work to do. Eternal Paths aren't exactly cakewalks. There are trials. And no, I don't mean the usual 'kill ten dire wolves and bring me their tails' nonsense.\"","Liam's eyes narrowed. \"What kind of trials?\"","Umbra's amber eyes gleamed like twin moons. \"The kind that test the soul. Her desires, her fears, the very foundation of her being. If she passes, she evolves. If she fails... well, let's try not to worry about that.\"","Shen Yue took a deep breath. \"When do we start?\"","\"You already did,\" Umbra replied, curling its tail around her neck like a smug scarf. \"The moment you accepted that fragment, your old path died. Now we see what kind of fire you're really made of.\"","Liam looked at Shen Yue once more, silently reaffirming what he had just said aloud. \"I had built up some dao of demonic summoning and a small seed of enchantment, both of which are now gone.\"","\"And for good reason. You did not like either of them now, did you?\" Umbra casually asked. \"The Eternal Path doesn't carry baggage. It burns away what doesn't serve your true self—even if you haven't figured out who that is yet. That's the fun part.\"","Liam's jaw tightened. \"She spent years building that. You should not have erased that progress just like that.\"","Umbra rolled onto its back across Shen Yue's shoulder, paws in the air. \"Oh, boo-hoo. Progress built on compromise is like stacking sandcastles in a storm. Your soul already chose something different. I didn't erase anything—she did. The Path just cleared the clutter.\"","\"Now what do I do?\" Shen Yue asked in confusion.","Umbra let out a delighted little trill. \"See? Now that's the spirit. Let go of what you were to become what you might be.\"","Shen Yue was about to open her mouth when Umbra interrupted her. \"That's fine. If you already knew it, you would have started walking that path long ago. Let me enlighten you. What you really like to do is cook.\"","Huh? Both Shen Yue and Liam looked shocked.","Shen Yue blinked. \"I... what?\"","Liam raised an eyebrow, clearly just as thrown off. \"Cooking? That's your revelation?\"","Umbra, still draped dramatically across Shen Yue's shoulder, waved a paw with the air of an oracle revealing cosmic truths. \"Not just cooking, girl. Creation. Nourishment. Alchemy in edible form. The act of transforming the mundane into magic. Your soul sings not when you destroy or fight, but when you create. When you nurture, when you infuse things with intention.\"","Shen Yue looked down at her hands, her mind spiraling. She did like cooking—but it had always been something small. Something she did for the guild, for Liam, for Mei Mei. Not something she'd ever thought of as... her core.","\"I always thought that was just...,\" she whispered.","Umbra's tail flicked smugly. \"And you mortals always think your strength has to come from swinging swords or mastering spells. But there is strength in creation.\"","Liam looked at her, something dawning in his eyes. \"You never liked to fight from the beginning. It was my mistake shoving the pair of legendary daggers in your hand.\"","Shen Yue shook her head. \"No. It is not you. It is me. I made the wrong choice. You were always charging ahead, fighting monsters, building the guild. I didn't want to be left behind. So I told myself... if I learned to fight, maybe I could keep up. Maybe I could protect you too.\"","Liam reached for her hand again, holding it firmly.","Umbra gave an exaggerated sniffle from her perch. \"Aww. So touching. Shall I start composing the ballad of the blade-turned-baker?\"","Shen Yue ignored the cat for once, her gaze still locked on Liam's. \"But if what Umbra says is true... if there's really a path for me that's based on what I love, not just what I forced myself to become... then I want to try it. Really try.\"","Liam's eyes softened, pride and quiet awe flickering behind the steady weight of his expression. \"Then I will support you with everything I have.\"","\"Good job, Mr. Husband,\" the cat purred, his voice laced with teasing approval. \"You better keep that promise because in a few years, this woman you're holding so dearly will be crafting elixirs so potent, so divine, that ancient beings from forgotten sectors will claw their way across dimensions just for a single drop. Realms will weep. Gods will beg. Culinary sects will build shrines in her name.\"","He flicked his tail smugly and gave Liam a once-over. \"So if you thought you were the powerhouse in this relationship, better start preparing yourself for the day she eclipses you.\"","Liam opened his mouth to respond, but Umbra waved a paw dismissively. \"Ah-ah. No protests. No more heart-shaped promises. We're on the clock now. The Eternal Path doesn't wait, and your girlfriend just got her soul blueprint rewritten into something deliciously unpredictable.\"","Then the cat's tone shifted—playful, but commanding. \"So off you go. Shoo. I've got a raw prodigy to whip into shape, and we're starting with essence-infused turnips.\"","Shen Yue blinked. \"Turnips?\"","\"Yes, turnips. Deal with it.\"","\"Every legend begins with something humble,\" Umbra said, already leaping toward the center of the room and conjuring a kitchen space out of thin air. \"Now, let's make some turnip soup. Show me what skills you got.\""]},{"number":1424,"title":"Chapter 1424: A new path","paragraphs":["The next second, Liam found himself unceremoniously tossed out of his own guild base—the heavy doors slamming shut behind him with a finality that made his eyebrow twitch.","He stood there in silence for a moment, arms crossed, staring at the ornate wood. \"Did I just get kicked out by a talking cat?\" he muttered to himself.","His expression darkened. He didn't like this. Not one bit. The Eternal System, the smug little furball that now seemed to have wormed its way into Shen Yue's fate—it all left a sour taste in his mouth. Too many unknowns. Too many risks. He didn't trust the system.","But even so... he'd seen the change in Shen Yue's eyes. The way her shoulders squared just a little taller. The way she'd spoken—not with hesitation, but conviction. For the first time in a long while, she'd looked like someone stepping into her own light.","Liam exhaled, slow and deep. He would give it time. A little time. But if that cat so much as made her cry, then everything would change.","Liam looked at the door again and let out a sigh. He then left the guild hall and headed for the system shop. He had some work of his own to get done. With the treasure hunt event wrapped up, he headed for his next goal to join an alchemy sect.","While the sword sect helped him a little, to truly figure out and utilize the three priceless treasures in his hand, he needed to take matters more seriously and focus on his Dao of alchemy.","He has been stuck in the Awakening realm for far too long. Everyone else was moving forward. Soon, his strength would become a joke if he didn't find a solution to his problem.","In deep thought, Liam walked past an eager Tilia, straight to the teleportation portals. The fairy pouted but did not disturb him from his thoughts.","Liam stepped into the teleportation array, the runes beneath his feet humming with life. The world blinked out in a kaleidoscope of color as the unsettling feeling of teleportation began and ended in the blink of an eye.","When he opened his eyes again, he stood in the middle of a disorienting mist.","Hmmm? Liam took a step back. He should be standing in the Green Mountains, a world not too different from the Purple world. While the Purple world was suited for sword art cultivation, the Green Mountain was a paradise for alchemy.","There were multiple sects here, and one of them stood above all the rest, the Green Mountain sect, the sect that was big enough to engulf the whole mountain and claim dominance over it.","An old monster is rumored to be the head of this sect, but no one has seen him in centuries. Nevertheless, the sect is the best when it comes to alchemy, and it was the best option Liam had to completely master his three treasures.","This was the only way he was going to find the answer he was seeking. If there was anything that was going to help him on the path of the many daos without losing himself, it was these three treasures.","Liam steeled himself as he tried to sense the surroundings beyond the mist that was swirling around.","The mist clung to Liam like a second skin, thick and perfumed with herbs both fragrant and bitter. Each breath he took was like sipping from a cauldron mid-brew—rich with power, volatile, and strangely invigorating.","It wasn't just mist. It was spiritual fog, saturated with ancient alchemical residue. Every molecule buzzed with half-forgotten knowledge and a thousand failed experiments. It was easy to get lost in the mist, but every second spent here was worth a thousand years of cultivation.","If he could just stay in this mist forever, he would be able to gain a lot.","Even better, if he just becomes a part of this mist, then he would have already attained Godhood.","Liam narrowed his eyes.","The thought hadn't come from him.","It was subtle, barely a whisper in his mind—sweet and seductive like the pull of a siren. He stopped walking and took a deep breath, grounding his consciousness. This place... was already testing him. The mist around him was alive, hungry, and feeding on his mind.","The fog was trying to blend into his spirit, whispering truths and lies alike. He could feel knowledge blooming in his mind, new concepts of spirit integration, pill sentience, elemental balancing between fire and metal—but it was coming too fast. Too easily. It was all a lie.","His body instantly shot up, trying to get away from the mist. He continued shooting upwards like a projectile for a good few minutes, and he was yet to see the end of the mist. He tried going forward and back, and it was the same result.","Finally, he tried using his sprouted dao seed of alchemy, and the next second, the mist around him instantly dispersed. He found himself standing in front of a small building with a single counter.","A soft bell chimed above the counter as Liam landed lightly on the stone floor. The mist behind him collapsed in slow swirls, reluctant to release him, but utterly suppressed by the pulse of his alchemy seed. The building was small—absurdly so. It looked more like a modest apothecary tucked away in a sleepy village than the entrance to the greatest alchemy sect in the Green Mountains.","There were no grand gates. No heavenly beasts guarding the entrance. Just a wooden counter, and behind it, a disinterested old man lounging on a stool, chewing on a dried spirit root as if it were jerky. His robes were plain brown, stained with scorch marks and long-forgotten concoctions. His aura was... nonexistent. Ordinary. Which, to Liam, was far more terrifying than a tyrannical display of strength.","The man lazily looked up at him and raised an eyebrow. \"That was impressively fast. You must be a good seed.\""]},{"number":1425,"title":"Chapter 1425: You must be a good seed","paragraphs":["The old man's voice was hoarse. There was no warmth in it, but neither was there scorn—only the faintest trace of interest.","Liam didn't respond immediately. He was still adjusting. The spiritual fog had faded, but the imprint of its temptations lingered like embers in his soul. He could feel it—the subtle warping of thoughts that tried to twist desire into delusion.","\"I'm here to join the Green Mountain Sect,\" he said at last.","\"Mmmhm. And the mountain has already sensed your interest, which is why you are standing here. But tell me, kid, why alchemy? You seem to have several options in front of you. Why choose alchemy?\"","Was this also a part of the test? Liam was thinking about what to say since he might get booted out based on his answer. \"I want to strengthen my foundation, and I am pursuing alchemy because it is the root of all creation, the flow of essence, the harmony of opposites, the laws that shape everything from a drop of poison to a divine elixir.\"","The old man stared at him for a moment before breaking into an amused chuckle. \"What a load of bullshit. Let's say you are already a part of the sect, and I have let you walk inside. Now tell me, why do you want to pursue alchemy?\"","Liam paused a moment, and then he looked at the old man straight in his eyes and spoke. \"Because I like it. It will give me the power I seek, and therefore I want it.\"","\"Don't you like your other paths? Those would also give you the power you seek.\"","Liam smiled. It would be easier if he could say he had three priceless treasures that probably even this old man in front of him would kill to have, but he couldn't, so he simply shook his head. \"I want them all.\"","The old man chewed thoughtfully on his spirit root and gave a quiet grunt. \"Fine. Go inside.\"","Immediately, a simple gate appeared in front of him. Liam was surprised that their conversation ended abruptly, but he didn't care too much about it. He bowed and turned to leave when a voice boomed in his mind.","Sever the other paths.","The many veil the true.","Fragments cannot forge fate.","Offer the whole... or be forgotten.","Liam's mind shook as he heard the voice and the words, but when he turned around to look at the old man, he was no longer there.","The words still echoed in his skull, ancient and sharp, as if carved into the marrow of his thoughts.","\"Hmmm. The myriad realms have not gone to shit. There are good seedlings all around.\" Liam heard the cauldron senior's voice now.","Liam waited to see if the senior would say anything else, but there was only silence. He stood for a moment and simply walked ahead. His choice might look foolish to others, but he knew what he was and what path he wanted to follow.","It might be a greedy, all-consuming path, and maybe giving it all up and choosing one might make his life easier. However, he was too stubborn to give up just yet.","Only someone who went through two lifetimes of utter helplessness and desperation would understand his need for strength and power. He was not ready to give it all up so easily.","Liam silently continued walking on the path, though all around him, nothing seemed to be changing. There were just trees and plants and a few herbs here and there, but nothing much was special about the place.","It was fine. He needed the time. Either the mist or the words from the old man made him slightly unsettled about his path. He did not like it. The walk helped. It helped to clear his mind and strengthen his resolve.","Liam walked for a long while, at least he felt it was long. But surprise, surprise, when his mind was somewhat settled, a new gate appeared in front of him. \"What a mysterious sect.\" He was already liking this place. He smiled and walked in.","This time, a more familiar sight awaited him. Tall buildings etched with runes stood proudly under a clear blue sky. Stone walkways crisscrossed through tiered gardens and herbal groves, winding between bubbling cauldrons the size of carriages and towers shaped like furnaces. The scent of rare blossoms danced in the air.","Simple robed men and women quietly bustled through the space, their expressions can and focused. Just ahead, a plaque shimmered with golden script: Hall of Emberlight – Third Tier Initiates.","\"So I am a third-tier initiate?\" Liam smiled and walked into the huge building right next to the plaque. He assumed this was where everyone started, or at least the third tiers. He was not offended by such a grade. In fact, he welcomed the challenge to prove that old man wrong.","The Hall of Emberlight was quiet, its doors wide open and welcoming. Behind a semicircular stone desk sat a man who looked like he'd been born annoyed and had never grown out of it. He wore a dark-brown uniform robe marked with the insignia of the sect, a single leaf.","His hair was scraped back tightly, and his thin lips were permanently curled into something between a sneer and a yawn. He barely looked up when Liam entered.","\"Name?\" he asked, voice flat and clipped.","\"Chang Xuan.\"","This was the name his parents had often said they wanted to give him, but in the end, they chose a mixed name instead. Liam decided to go with this one.","\"Third-tier initiate?\" the man asked with a faint smirk, finally glancing up as if just now confirming what he already assumed. \"Figures. You new ones always come in like wide-eyed dreamers.\"","Liam was pretty sure that only third-tier initiates came this way, and the guy was acting as a world-class detective for no reason, but he let it go. This was still the first day. He needed to keep a low profile.","\"Low-profile.\" He again repeated under his breath."]},{"number":1426,"title":"Chapter 1426: Third-tier initiate?","paragraphs":["Liam flipped a token in his hand, which transferred a bit of knowledge into his mind. Apparently, living quarters here weren't lavish towers or royal hotel rooms. No, they were caves.","Literally caves, crude, stone-carved hollows embedded into the sheer face of a cliffside that bordered the outer sect. No doors. No windows. Just formations hollowed out. \"Third tier,\" Liam muttered, half amused. \"Of course it's caves.\"","Still, he didn't complain. It was better this way. No distractions. No comfort to dull the edge of his hunger. Just him and the cauldron.","Liam settled in and meditated for the rest of the day, focusing on strengthening his soul. The next morning, he went back to the main reception desk.","\"Chang Xuan is it?\" The same clerk gave him an annoyed look. He then passed him a scroll and a small pouch. \"Here is the recipe for the month. Your target is to make 2 sets of dozen potion vials. The purity has to be at least 50%. If a single one dips below that, it won't count.\"","\"And if I don't meet the quota?\" Liam asked, already knowing the answer.","The man didn't even bother to smirk. \"You're removed from the sect. Immediate revocation of entry permissions. You'll be barred from returning under any identity or token. We don't do charity here.\"","Liam simply smiled and nodded. He then left for his cave.","The next morning, he returned. \"What? Did you burn through all of your herbs in a single night? Heh. What did you think? I am sitting here every day just to hand you brand new sets of herbs every day? Do you think we are running some sort of charity?\"","Liam did not respond. He silently took out the completed quota of vials and placed them on the desk. The clerk's eyes instantly widened in surprise. \"You finished the entire batch in a day?\"","Liam only nodded. He refrained from correcting the guy. It had barely taken him an hour to finish the potion.","\"Ughhh. Huh...\" The clerk stammered as he started checking the potion quality. \"These are impeccable. At least 70% purity.\" He blurted out. He looked up and saw that Liam was still waiting there with the same smiling expression on his face. \"I... I...\"","Liam helped him out. \"I am here for the next assignment.\"","\"Right.\" The clerk hurriedly nodded. He then fumbled beneath the desk and pulled out another scroll and a new pouch. \"Another assignment.\"","Liam silently took the items and once again returned to his cave. The very next day, he was back. The clerk gulped. This time, he did not say anything unnecessarily. He didn't bark, didn't smirk, didn't even blink more than necessary. His hands moved quickly, professionally, as he accepted the vials Liam placed on the counter.","Each one gleamed with a gentle luminescence, their liquid contents clear and vibrant, balanced to the point of harmony. The clerk checked them one by one. Once again, the purity of the potion was well above average.","The clerk gulped and looked at Liam again. \"Next assignment?\" Liam smiled.","The same event continued to happen for the next several days, and slowly, the name Chang Xuan started to become popular in the Hall of Emberlight.","By the end of the first week, Liam had returned five times, each time with perfectly brewed potions that exceeded expectations. Seventy percent purity became eighty percent. Then eighty-five. His worst vial still outperformed the best of his peers.","Whispers started spreading. At first, it was among the clerks. Then it reached the initiates. \"Who's that newbie in Sector C?\" \"He's just third-tier, right? Then how the hell is he turning in elder-grade batches?\"","Soon, a change happened. When Liam submitted the next set of vials, the clerk this time handed him a red-marked scroll. \"The elders sent that one,\" the clerk muttered, noticeably more respectful than before. \"If you manage to concoct the potion, then you can take the advancement exam.\"","Liam raised a brow, receiving the scroll and the pouch with interest. He was truly enjoying his time at Green Mountain. It was a simple life with nothing except meeting a small goal he had made for himself every single day.","For some reason, it felt relaxing and refreshing. Just the quiet bubbling of the cauldron, the scent of herbs in the air, and the satisfaction of control. Here, in this unassuming cliffside cave, Liam, or rather Chang Xuan, could lose himself in the purity of craft.","However, he still had responsibilities that he couldn't shirk from. So just like all the other days, he carefully studied the recipe, fully understood the process, and concocted the potion. The first batch he made shockingly reached a purity of 90%. But he purposefully diluted it and then returned to the desk for yet another submission.","The clerk hurriedly received the vials and directed him to the exam halls. Apparently, the advancement required both practical knowledge and theoretical knowledge. Liam had no problems with either.","All these days, he had been slowly refining the souls of the two alchemists, and their knowledge was more than sufficient to answer all the questions in the exam. By now, he had fully assimilated most of their knowledge and made it his own.","Liam entered the exam hall where a single stone desk awaited him in the center, lit by a hovering orb of soft golden light. As he sat, the orb flared slightly and projected a long scroll into the air before him. Words etched themselves across it in glowing ink.","[Green Mountain Sect - Alchemy Theory Evaluation]","There was no pen. No paper. The test would be mental—read, think, and imprint your answers onto the scroll with your will alone. If your understanding was shallow, the scroll would remain blank.","The first question appeared.","\"Describe the inverse reaction between Spiritroot Vine and Coldfire Lotus when subjected to a rotating flame array. Include all volatile compounds released.\"","Liam's mind sharpened.","He wasn't relying on memory. He was relying on lived experience, albeit someone else's. The soul fragments he'd absorbed had brewed these combinations dozens of times. He knew not only the right answer, but why it was the only one that would keep your cauldron from exploding into a frozen inferno.","Line after line, a glowing script began to appear in the air as Liam calmly answered each question. Some were obscure. Others tested creativity, asking for theoretical combinations never attempted. By the end, he had answered all questions to satisfaction.","The orb dimmed. The scroll vanished. Silence fell. Another pulse of light, and a jade emblem floated before him, etched with a stylized flame surrounded by three ascending rings.","[Second Tier Initiate - Green Mountain Sect]","Liam accepted the token, tucking it into his robes. And so, on his 33rd day of arriving at the Green Mountain, Liam was promoted from a measly third-tier initiate to a not-so-bad second-tier initiate."]},{"number":1427,"title":"Chapter 1427: Advancement exam","paragraphs":["A second-tier initiate, revered as an elder of the Green Mountains by those outside the sect, lived a life vastly different from the common initiates scraping by in crude caves.","Their chambers were no longer damp stone cubbies but well-furnished quarters lined with carved bookshelves, fragrant with herbs and alchemical reagents. They no longer fetched water or tended furnaces for others; now, junior initiates bowed in their presence, eager to curry favor.","More importantly, they had access, true access. Vaults of rare alchemical formulas, aged journals from long-dead masters, annotated scrolls whispering lost techniques.","They were allowed into the lower floors of the Grand Repository, where tiered permissions decided who could read which ancient texts. What a first-tier might glimpse once a year through a cracked door, the second-tier could pore over for days under quiet candlelight.","But perhaps the greatest privilege was connection. Other sects treated them as emissaries of the Green Mountains, powerful in both knowledge and influence.","Whether trading ingredients, attending auctions, or representing the sect in cross-valley symposiums, they walked like true elders, only a step away from ascending further.","Liam's first few days were interesting, considering he had no connections whatsoever with the many worlds of the myriad realms. There was no one queuing up outside his quarters, wanting to give him commission for pill making or potion brewing.","Liam did not care. He was happy and content with simply accessing the archives and fulfilling the quota that was required of the second-tier initiates. Day in and day out, he simply continued to study, learn more, meditate on his soul cultivation and practise more alchemy. It was liberating. He was making huge progress.","Naturally, no good thing would remain unnoticed. News soon spread that there was a new elder in the second-tier initiate group. Usually, the elders were all completely booked up, no one having empty slots to accept new orders. Now that a new person had popped up several groups quickly flocked over to Liam to place their orders.","Surprisingly, Liam was also unavailable. Wondering what was happening, the many groups waited around his living quarters for days and nights. Soon, Liam's door opened. Liam walked out with a smile on his face and seeing the crowd near his home, he casually welcomed them inside, accepting orders one after the other.","All the groups were surprised. They had all come from different worlds scattered throughout the sector, and no one had expected a Green Mountain elder to casually accept so many orders. Some even began to feel apprehensive about whether the person was capable or not.","However, they could only swallow their doubts and try this one time. Otherwise, they had to return home empty-handed. The various groups once again waited anxiously outside Liam's living quarters, hoping for a miracle to happen.","Meanwhile, inside the building, Liam's figure, who had been accepting orders all this time, silently disappeared. Shockingly, another figure walked out from inside. \"Not bad for a first try clone. No one even suspected that they were talking to a clone.\"","Liam rubbed his chin in amusement and placed all of the raw materials, the recipes and the order details in his spatial ring. It had taken him a while but he had finally managed to create a soul clone of his own.","He had used a combination of techniques he had seen back at the sword palace, along with his knowledge of the myriad constellations technique and finally the knowledge in Green Mountain allowed him to complete the vague technique.","However, he was still not satisfied with it. The soul clone was not very stable. It lacked a corporeal body and couldn't exist on its own. The technique needed a lot of refinement.","On the plus side he was able to make more than one such soul clone and each clone was able to function extremely well, even hiding the unique soul aura as long as it was only for a few hours.","More importantly, all the clones were him and they had the ability to think the same as him. Their cultivation base was only partial but they were still able to think and act independently just like how he would do.","And all it would take from his side was a single thought to integrate all of their thinking and see everything from their eyes. They were him and at the same time they could also be independent of him.","\"I need more techniques to research this.\" Liam's eyes glinted with determination as more and more ideas started forming in his head. The second tier initiates only had access to so much information in the Green Mountain. Perhaps after he became a second-tier advanced disciple, he could improve his standing in the sect.","Liam still needed a lot of time to meditate on his soul strength and his new technique so he did not rush anything. He took a deep breath, and the next second, two soul clones emerged from his body.","The soul clones left a sense of weakness within the core of his soul but Liam used it as an opportunity to use the Myraid Constellations technique to further strengthen his soul. \"Perhaps a single soul could possess the entirety of a constellation?\" he pondered. \"Maybe that is the way to make them more stable.\"","Meanwhile, his other two clones immediately started working on the numerous orders they had received.","Both clones worked in seamless harmony, their movements crisp and precise as they set up dual alchemical arrays. The room was soon filled with the delicate scent of powdered lotus, flamefruit resin, and starlight flowers.","The clones moved quietly, measuring, grinding, infusing with none of the hesitation or clumsiness of assistants. They didn't need instructions. They were Liam.","As cauldrons bubbled and the gentle rise of medicinal mist warmed the chamber, Liam sat in a corner, completely still, eyes half-closed. A faint shimmer hovered around his soul core as the Myriad Constellations technique worked in tandem with his depleted spirit.","Each clone pulled threads of his essence outward, stretching them like astral filaments. The experiment was dangerous. Overextending a soul could lead to collapse, but Liam wanted to see how far he could go."]},{"number":1428,"title":"Chapter 1428: Partial success","paragraphs":["The next day, the gate of Liam's quarters opened again, and one of Liam's soul clones stepped out with a smile, greeting everyone in the vicinity. \"Please come inside to collect your orders.\"","The emissaries from the various sects and clans were completely dumbfounded. Their orders were all completed in a single day? This was unheard of! No elder in the entire Golden Pavilion possessed such an ability.","\"This guy should have definitely ruined all of our herbs, and now he is putting on a show to explain that.\"","\"Maybe he just robbed us all, and he is going to say that the herbs were ruined.\"","\"What a scammer!! How could such a person be admitted into the Green Mountain sect? I have never heard of something like this happening before.\"","\"Maybe the Green Mountain sect is just not as great as before. Maybe even the esteemed Green Mountain is starting to decline.\"","Several wild rumors started spreading around. To prevent any foul relations from taking root, many of the emissaries directly left the area. After all, there was no point in going inside and creating a scene.","In the end, even if Liam turned out to be a scammer, they couldn't do anything about it. If they had a dispute with any elder of the Green Mountain, then all the elders would think twice before accepting their future orders. It was best to leave this matter as it is and consider the cost of herbs as a loss, and move on.","Liam's soul clone, standing on the other side, couldn't help but frown at this development. He was welcoming everyone with a big smile, but these guys seemed extremely upset. Many directly left the area? What was going on? Soon, more and more guys started leaving without as much as a word.","Thankfully, a couple of people still bothered to come inside. He brought them over and seated them on a wooden bench in the living room. He then calmly took out each person's potion vial and handed it to them.","The custom in the Green Mountain was to just give a single vial of the potion, even though multiple vials could have been brewed. For every vial, a new order has to be placed, and three sets of the same herbs have to be given.","The alchemists were never held responsible, even if all three sets of herbs were completely ruined. They only needed to mention that the potion brewing did not go well this time around. The other party simply couldn't do anything about it.","But when Liam's clone handed over the potions, what happened next was entirely unexpected.","The first emissary, a short, sharp-eyed man in golden robes from the Thundercloud Sect, uncorked his vial and took a whiff. His eyes widened. He dipped a testing strip into the liquid and watched it change color, bright silver with a faint violet gleam.","His hands trembled.","\"This... this is a seven-star grade!\" he whispered in disbelief. \"Impossible. I gave him materials that would barely scrape five stars at best.\" A seven-star grade was the assessment given for a potion with more than 70% purity.","The others who had entered and received their potions blinked in confusion. One of them hurriedly uncorked their own vial and performed a quick test. Another stunned gasp. Another seven-star result.","A third emissary, more composed and skeptical, examined his vial with a specialized spirit-inscribing monocle. The moment he saw the concentration lines inside the liquid, his jaw dropped. \"This is on par with an elder grandmaster's work... and he returned the leftover herbs as well?!\"","The room fell silent as realization dawned on each of them.","They hadn't been scammed.","They had just received alchemical products that were far superior to what they'd ever gotten from the famed elders of the Golden Pavilion. And this newcomer had completed every order in one day. With change.","The emissaries who had walked out in suspicion were already halfway down the mountain, stewing in their assumptions. But those who stayed?","They began sweating bullets, not from fear, but from a sudden panic. They had just stumbled upon a monster in alchemist robes, and they might've just ruined their chance to establish a relationship with him early.","\"Please inform your clans,\" the clone said with a calm smile. \"I will accept repeat orders every fortnight, but only from those who collect personally. If you leave early, your order will be voided.\"","With those words, a new storm quietly began to form within the Green Mountains. And this time, it wasn't alchemy that was spreading like wildfire, it was Liam's name.","The incident quickly became famous, and word of mouth got around so fast that the next day an even bigger crowd gathered in front of Liam's quarters. Those who had left hastily the previous day fully regretted their actions and came back with their tail between their legs.","The crowd outside Liam's quarters the following morning was nothing short of chaotic.","Disciples, emissaries, rogue cultivators, merchants, everyone wanted a piece of the mysterious elder who had completed over a dozen high-purity commissions overnight.","Most were holding fresh herb bundles wrapped in enchanted cloth, clearly here to place orders. Others came simply to apologize, hoping to mend the damage they had caused by walking out prematurely.","\"Senior! We were misinformed! Please allow our sect another chance!\"","\"We brought premium spirit herbs this time! Just take a look!\"","\"Our Thundercloud Sect Patriarch himself wants to send an official invitation. Please consider visiting our compound in the Heavenly Grove Sector!\"","Liam, watching through his clone's eyes while seated deep in meditation, raised an eyebrow but remained calm. The crowd's reaction had been predictable. In a world where connections often held more value than merit, true excellence had a way of disrupting all existing hierarchies.","His clone, projecting the same serene presence, stepped outside and politely raised a hand.","\"I appreciate everyone's enthusiasm,\" the clone said evenly. \"However, I cannot take every order.\" Instantly, dozens of heads turned toward him with anxious expressions. But the next words offered both relief and confusion."]},{"number":1429,"title":"Chapter 1429: A scammer?","paragraphs":["\"There will be a draw,\" Liam continued. \"Each clan or sect representative may drop their name and order description into this urn.\" He placed a big, shimmering, inscribed urn at the steps. \"Ten orders will be accepted every day. Fair and square.\"","Everyone nodded in amazement. This only added to the mystique surrounding Liam. No one could accuse him of favoritism, and yet the exclusivity now turned each slot into something even more precious.","Liam's soul clone retreated as gasps and muttering erupted around the urn. Inside his real quarters, Liam's lips curled into a faint smile. He was more than satisfied with this progress. His knowledge of alchemy was improving by leaps and bounds.","Coming here was indeed the right decision, but he did not plan to stop with that. He now had a powerful background, and he planned to utilize it completely.","Along with the orders, Liam started accepting invitations to various clans and families across the numerous worlds in their sector. There was only so much knowledge he could learn from the basic system information scrolls. The real deal had to be traveled and procured.","He had a feeling that he was standing on the cusp of a turning point, and he was going to see it all the way through.","At first, the invitations were casual, but slowly Liam started spreading the rumors about researching a new pill formula that involved soul strengthening.","As a part of this research, he also spread the word that he was collecting some soul cultivation manuals. Technically, whatever he said wasn't even a lie. So it was more than convincing enough for the many families to rush to curry favor with him.","If he indeed became successful in such an endeavour, then they wanted to be first in line to obtain that godly pill or potion. Soul cultivation was one of the most difficult aspects of increasing one's power, and typically, many people lagged in that.","Things continued in this manner, and Liam made it a point to accept invitations and visit many places regularly. He learned a lot about many things, amassed a small fortune of rare raw materials, but as far as his main goal was concerned, he had made zero progress in that area.","Finally, after three months, Liam found a small clue. A guy from one of the smaller sects in a beast world had a shockingly high soul strength for his current level.","Liam instantly ordered his soul clone to get back and met with the man in person. It only took him a second to confirm. The guy indeed had an unusual soul strength.","After some casual conversations, it was easy to squeeze out an invitation from the guy. Liam immediately made the trip to the small world that lay in the midst of the vast Leviathan Beast Empire.","Liam had gone as far as to eat a grand feast with the man who not only spared no expenses but also recounted in length about the glory of their world and all the famous high points of his life. After sinking half a day into this endeavour, he finally had something decent.","Apparently, this small world called Mistshadow Vale had once housed a powerful but now-forgotten sect whose legacy was rumored to be scattered across the dense, beast-infested forests and ancient ruins. The man, eager to impress Liam, revealed that he had stumbled on one such ruin, a crumbling pagoda nestled at the base of a shadowed waterfall.","The local sects considered the place cursed, the forest thick with spirit beasts, but the man had dared venture there once on a dare.","He had found nothing but overgrown corridors and a few scraps of tattered scrolls. Yet one of those scrolls had a distinct rune, the same one that now pulsed within him like a hidden sun strengthening his soul every day.","Liam couldn't believe that a single rune could have such a big effect, but unless he checked the ruins himself, he had no other option but to believe the guy's story.","Liam's eyes gleamed. Mistshadow Vale. He needed to thoroughly examine this place. He continued chatting with the guy until they eventually reached the system shop of their small clan territory.","Almost immediately, two people rushed to welcome them. \"Grandmaster! Welcome! Welcome! We must have done great deeds in our past life and gained glorious karma for your esteemed excellence to pay a personal visit to our small clan.\"","The compliments were so thick that Liam had to stifle a chuckle. \"You're too kind,\" he replied lightly. \"I was just in the area and decided to relax a little by visiting a new place. Please don't make it sound so exaggerated. This is just a small visit.\"","The two men exchanged glances and then happily led Liam to a grand feast. The table practically buckled under the weight of roasted spirit beasts, fragrant soups, and exotic fruit wines. The clan had truly gone all out to impress their guest.","Liam sipped at a clear, sweet wine and smiled politely at the main host, a burly man with a tiger-shaped badge on his chest. \"Your hospitality is unmatched,\" Liam said. \"Can you tell me more about your world? As long as I am here, I wouldn't mind heading out and tempering myself in the wilderness. My master always says that even an alchemist must train his combat.\"","The host's eyes lit up at the suggestion. \"Ah, Grandmaster, you truly are different from the average alchemist,\" he said with a wide grin. \"Most refuse even to set foot outside their sect walls, but you are bold and courageous! I see now why you are so renowned.\" He praised Liam endlessly and then came to the main point.","\"This world of ours may be small, but it is full of opportunities... and dangers.\" He gestured grandly with his cup. \"We are surrounded by the Leviathan Beast Empire, and many of our lands have never truly been tamed. Spirit beasts roam freely, and old sect ruins dot the forests and canyons. Adventurers, both juniors and seniors, come here seeking fortune or challenge.\""]},{"number":1430,"title":"Chapter 1430: Just a casual visit","paragraphs":["Liam's smile widened, though his eyes remained sharp. \"That sounds like exactly what I'm looking for. Do you have any recommendations for places to train? Maybe a region with higher-level spirit beasts or a ruin that has yet to be fully explored?\"","The man hesitated for a split second and then continued. \"There are many places that are good for exploring. These are actually closely guarded secrets of the Leviathan beast clan, but since you are our special guest, of course, I am more than happy to share them with you.\"","\"Thank you. I will keep this favor in mind.\" Liam nodded thoughtfully.","The man then talked about various locations and the suspected treasures in them for the next hour. Rare herbs, rare beast nests, old ruins, it looked like the place was really full of prime spots for making progress.","After a while, the discussion ended, and Liam leaned back with a smile. \"Thank you. I'll also be needing a guide and a few supplies. After that, I can handle the rest.\" He continued chatting with the man for some more time before retreating inside the chamber they had prepared for him.","As soon as he entered, several seductive maids rushed to his side to attend to him, but Liam quickly sent them away, lying down on the bed and closing his eyes. In truth, he was not interested in these ruins at all. There might be precious treasures scattered around here like pebbles, but the only thing he cared about was that rune.","He closed his eyes, meditating on the rune for a while to see if he could glean any insights into it, and then proceeded to practise his soul cultivation for the rest of the night.","The new day arrived sooner than expected as time passed by in a jiffy.","Morning sunlight filtered through the embroidered drapes as Liam opened his eyes, the glow of soul energy still faintly flickering around him. His cultivation had gone smoothly. The more he meditated on that rune, the more he felt it wasn't just a random inheritance left behind in some forgotten ruin.","In a weird way, it was calling to him. Now that he was here in this place, he could feel it more than ever.","Liam rose from the bed, changed into a new set of robes, and stepped out just as a knock echoed at the door. The clan had prepared everything.","A lean, sharp-eyed young man with a beast-fur cloak introduced himself as Grell, a native tracker of the region. \"I'll guide you as far as the waterfall,\" he said, bowing deeply. \"Beyond that, I dare not go.\"","Liam nodded. \"That's more than enough.\"","With the clan leader's blessings and a small pouch of high-grade supplies, mostly food, Liam and his guide departed. The journey through the area was stunning and treacherous in equal measure. In just a few miles, they had encountered several beasts, though nothing that could truly threaten Liam.","He needed new souls anyway, so he did not mind grabbing whatever he could find. Half a day later, after navigating a narrow cliff path and crossing a moss-covered rope bridge, the sound of crashing water filled the air.","\"There it is,\" Grell whispered, pointing ahead.","Liam stepped forward, his eyes locked on the faint outline of a pagoda shrouded in mist at the base of the roaring waterfall. The stone looked warped, almost melted in places, and thick vines clung to it like skeletal fingers.","This was the first famous ruin in the region, the abandoned pagoda ruins. Grell quickly apologized and dismissed himself, leaving Liam all to himself.","Liam took a minute to observe the surroundings. Only after being completely sure that he was not followed and that no one else was around him, he finally made his move. He turned away from the famous ruin he was supposed to explore first and instead headed over to the Mistshadow Vale, the only place he was interested in.","His speed instantly exploded, and he cut through the forests as if he had crossed them a thousand times already. Soon, he reached the specific location. Unlike the previous place, this one was not particularly deserted, but Liam did not care. He already activated Stealth.","He quickly arrived at the temple ruins the guy had described. Liam took another step forward when suddenly an odd feeling washed over him. It felt as if suddenly there were a thousand eyes on him.","Liam frowned and double-checked his stealth. Everything was fine, and no one seemed to have noticed them. Then who exactly was looking at him? He shook it off and started cautiously walking towards the ruins.","The temple was more like a broken skeleton than an actual structure. Stone pillars jutted out from the ground like shattered bones, most of them half-swallowed by moss and time. A jagged set of stairs led down into what looked like the temple's sunken foundation, now a half-buried cavern cloaked in shadows.","Liam stood still at the edge, letting his senses stretch. There it was again, the feeling.","This place was connected to him in a way that he simply could not explain. Was it perhaps a trap? He did not know. There was only one way to find out. Without hesitation, he started climbing down the stairs to the main part of the ruins.","He descended the cracked stairs slowly, looking around at the walls. He half expected something monstrous to break out of the walls and come at him any moment.","The stairway opened into a circular chamber, its roof collapsed in several places, letting shafts of sunlight stab through the gloom. But what drew Liam's eyes was the center of the chamber, an ancient altar, smooth and unblemished despite the decay all around it.","And carved into its surface was the rune.","As soon as Liam entered the circular chamber, his stealth no longer worked, and he was instantly exposed. The few people meditating around the altar flashed their eyes open and stared at him, their eyes completely bloodshot.","Then unexpectedly, they opened their mouths in unison and all started chanting at the same time.","\"You are not one of ours. Yet you carry the mark.\"","\"You are not one of ours. Yet you carry the mark.\"","...","..."]},{"number":1431,"title":"Chapter 1431: Face to face with the rune","paragraphs":["The chant echoed through the chamber like an incantation pulled from the marrow of the world. The words weren't merely sound, they were pressure, heavy and ancient, grinding against Liam's very soul.","However, Liam's soul was now strong enough to withstand a simple assault like this. He gritted his teeth and simply shielded the attack. The air grew dense, every syllable a nail pinning reality to something older and deeper than what should exist.","Liam didn't flinch. He stood his ground at the threshold, his gaze sweeping across the room. The figures weren't just random cultivators. Maybe they once were, but now they were just soulbound husks.","Their skin was pale and waxy, their auras hollow. They weren't dead, but they weren't fully alive either. Caught in a liminal space, perhaps still clinging to the altar's power like moths to a dying flame.","A whisper echoed in his mind. \"They failed.\"","His eyes snapped back to the rune on the altar. The very same symbol that had haunted his meditations now glowed faintly with an inner fire. It pulsed once, and the chanting ceased as suddenly as it had begun.","The husks lowered their heads. Then, one by one, they slumped forward, their bodies dissolving into faint trails of soul essence that flowed toward the rune.","Liam didn't step back, even as the air quivered and the altar trembled, even as the entire temple felt like it was shifting on some unseen axis.","\"You have come.\" The voice was back, calm, deep, eternal. \"Will you succeed, where the others failed?\"","Liam raised his hand and stepped closer to the altar. \"I don't plan to fail. Let's begin.\" He instinctively knew what to do as he pressed his palm to the rune.","The next second, his consciousness was hurled inward, plummeting into a churning void of soul force, memory fragments, and alien landscapes. Here, time did not flow forward. There was no direction, no light, no ground. Just will.","And the trial began.","Liam felt the pressure of countless eyes, some familiar, others alien, and many that didn't even feel mortal. They weren't physical, but impressions in the soul-space. Whispers flooded him, not in words but in truths, raw, unfiltered shards of understanding that pierced deeper than language.","\"Name yourself.\"","The demand echoed, not in the air, but within Liam's core. It wasn't asking for a title or a name from the tongue. It wanted his essence, the truth behind every mask he'd ever worn.","Liam gritted his teeth. A flame burst around him, not fire, but soulfire. Blue, white, and strange colors without a name. It stripped him bare. Every weakness, every regret, every selfish act, and moment of hesitation was dredged to the surface and peeled away like rot from bone.","Memories flashed in his mind. Long forgotten ones of his first kill, the betrayal that hardened him, the faces of those he couldn't save. Each one carved away part of him. He screamed in pain as he felt as if his soul was going to be torn apart.","But he did not yield. At the center of the pain, Liam reached something buried and silent. A heartbeat. He reached into the fire. The flame coiled into his hand, becoming a brand, no, a sigil, that seared into his soul. The rune.","This was the true rune that was hidden in the ruin, not the other one the other guy obtained. That was merely an imitation the person had copied from a distance, but this was the true heritage, and now it belonged to Liam.","The void shattered. Light surged.","And Liam awoke on the altar, his palm still glowing. Around him, the ruined temple was still and empty. The husks were gone, dissolved into ash. Only silence remained.","But inside him... the rune now burned with power.","Liam was completely drenched in sweat from top to bottom. His mind was exhausted, and his soul was close to cracking and shattering. He had only barely pulled through. It was good that he visited this place after strengthening his soul to a good state. Otherwise, there was no telling what could have happened.","Even if he had come here a few weeks earlier, he would've been reduced to nothing more than another husk, just like the others, bound eternally to chant before the altar of failure.","Liam steadied his breathing, his entire body trembling under the weight of what had just been seared into his being. The rune was no longer a symbol to him. It was alive. It pulsed faintly beneath his skin, nestled in his soul like a buried star.","When Liam tried to reach it, a system notification suddenly popped up.","[Soul Rune of Origin: Awakened]","Effect: Enhances soul regeneration by 30%. Increases resistance to soul-based attacks. Enables soul imprinting.","Liam blinked. \"So the system recognizes this progress?\" He was pleasantly surprised. This was not much but this was definitely more information, something he could search with. He chuckled weakly, his voice hoarse. \"Worth it,\" he muttered, even as blood trickled from his nose.","For a long moment, he didn't move. He simply sat there in the ruins, letting the last vestiges of the soul trial drain from his bones. Then, with a sigh, he stood.","The moment he did, he felt the world respond. Somewhere in the distance, spirit beasts howled. Trees bent toward him. Even the wind changed direction.","Somewhere, in some sealed part of some hidden world, something ancient stirred awake.","Liam stood frozen. He couldn't move. He could feel something but he did not know what exactly was going on. The next second he heard a vague phrase in his mind.","\"The next heir of the league of soul weavers... the grand throne awaits you...\"","The words weren't loud. They didn't echo with majesty or thunder across his consciousness like divine proclamations. No, they came like a secret, a whisper passed through the breath of time itself. But the weight of them struck harder than any spiritual attack Liam had ever faced.","He stumbled slightly, catching himself against the altar, his breath ragged. The league of soul weavers? He had never heard of such a thing. His mind reeled from the knowledge as if he had just learned of something that he should not know.","For a moment, everything froze. The rune on his palm dimmed too, like it was falling asleep now that its job was done.... But Liam's senses were sharper than ever.","Even with his soul battered and frayed, he could feel a new strand of energy coiling in his core. It was different from mana or vitality. It was older, more refined, threadlike, almost as if it could be woven into something else.","He instinctively opened his soul sea. There, suspended within the haze of his essence, was a thread of glowing silver-blue energy. One strand. Alone.","[Soulweaver Thread (1/999)]","A single soul-thread of creation.","Liam inhaled sharply. There it was another system notification. What the hell was going on? Was this a part of his soulmancer legacy? He stood still as he pondered the words that were spoken. They seemed to convey a lot more than just a bit of information.","But no matter how much he tried, he wasn't able to even go near that profound truth. It was as if the thing was far beyond his reach.","All around him, the ruins started to tremor and quake. Dust rained down from the cracked ceiling. The stone beneath Liam's feet rumbled as hairline fractures spiderwebbed across the chamber floor.","Liam did not care. He erected a strong barrier before he sat down to meditate. Even as the entire ruins crumbled around him and many screams sounded in the distance as other beings rushed to get out of the ruins and to safety, Liam continued his meditation without a care in the world.","Finally, after two entire days, he stood up to leave the place. He had gained a lot more here than he had ever expected. But then again, he only felt as if he had more questions now than before. No matter how much he tried, he was always facing one roadblock or the other.","What is the way out? What is the path for him to inherit his complete legacy? He clenched his fists in frustration and determination. He would not fail or give up. Even if the path ahead was difficult, he would somehow surmount it and grab his fate by whatever means necessary.","His robes were torn, his body was sore, but his eyes burned with something indescribable. He glanced at his palm where the rune had faded to a dull shimmer, now lying dormant under his skin. He took one last look at the now-collapsed temple behind him. What was once a forgotten ruin was now a buried grave.","Liam then silently left the place, disappearing into the shadows.","Whatever the League of Soul Weavers was... whatever the Grand Throne entailed... Liam had finally found a clue and taken the first step. He was not going to stop until he owned the entire legacy."]},{"number":1432,"title":"Chapter 1432: The league of soulweavers","paragraphs":["Liam returned to the main palace area almost immediately. All around him, there was chaos and confusion. Shouts rang out. Beastkin guards scrambled to their positions. Several elders were in heated discussions, their auras flaring with suspicion and unrest.","It looked like he had once again started something in this world but he did not wait around to deal with the aftermath. He didn't even glance around to see what storm he had set in motion.","He walked straight through the rising madness as if it didn't exist. He didn't pause or even glance toward the central courtyard where the clan elders usually gathered.","He had no intention of participating in the fanfare anylonger. Without so much as a nod to the guards, he cut across the palace hallway and headed directly toward the system's teleportation portals.","He tapped the glyph for the Green Mountain region without hesitation, vanishing in a shimmer of pale light.","There were two reasons behind his decision. The first was simple: he didn't want to waste time.","After what he had just experienced, the awakening of the rune, the emergence of the soulweaver thread, and the whisper of an ancient inheritance, it felt absurd to stay and indulge in pointless social rituals.","Time was a currency he couldn't afford to squander, not when he had barely survived the last ordeal. There was too much to unpack, too much to understand, and lingering in that world served no purpose.","The second reason, however, was far more critical. Liam had learned the hard way that nothing in this world remained hidden for long. Power always left a ripple. The moment he'd awakened the Soul Rune of Origin, he had felt something. Staying back, flaunting his presence, or attracting even the slightest bit of attention could be fatal.","He wasn't being paranoid. He was being practical. Experience had taught him that the most dangerous part of unlocking power wasn't the trial, it was what came after.","That world may have been rich with opportunity, rare herbs, alchemical wonders, secret beast nests but it wasn't worth the gamble. Not this time. Liam didn't need another trinket or hidden scroll. What he needed now was understanding.","The safety and solitude of the Green Mountains would give him exactly that. There, surrounded by layers of spiritual formations and far from prying eyes, he could study the rune etched into his soul and understand everything on his terms.","What he needed now... was clarity.","Liam cancelled all of his orders for the next several days and fully focused on his soul cultivation. It looked like his soul cultivation technique was indeed compatible with the new rune in his soul.","In fact his first constellation now started further expanding with the rune in the center.","Liam felt a little nervous as he had no idea what he was doing. He was completely in uncharted territories and it felt dangerous. It would be better if he could learn more about this rune before proceeding.","After spending several days on the rune, he finally decided to pause this for a while. There was also the second thing he wanted to focus on, the soulweaver thread.","Liam decided to take a day's break before tinkering with that.","His mind was frayed from days of nonstop meditation, and his soul, though bolstered by the rune, was still recovering from the intense awakening ritual. He wandered the quiet paths of the Green Mountain Sect, letting the crisp spiritual air clear the fog in his mind.","The mist that clung to the cliffs, the distant cries of spirit beasts, the soft whisper of wind through bamboo groves, all of it helped him to relax. He decided to make a trip to the main market place of the sect where various trades typically happened.","However, alchemy sect elders like Liam were rarely seen in these areas. It was only the newbies who wandered here hoping to gain some sort of benefit to make a breakthrough.","Liam drew more than a few glances the moment he stepped into the marketplace. Most of the sect disciples present were either outer disciples or lower-tier initiates.","They had only ever heard of the elusive Grandmaster Alchemist, rumors, legends, and hushed tales about the rising star who defied sect traditions and earned direct recognition from several Elders. Yet none had actually seen him walk among them like a normal person.","The crowd instinctively parted around him. Some bowed slightly, others merely stared in awe. Liam just smiled and continued walking.","Stalls filled with spiritual herbs, beast pelts, forged weapons, and glittering talismans lined the streets. A few traveling vendors even hawked oddities from distant realms, dusty relics, bottled luck, and even tamed parasites rumored to enhance spiritual perception.","Liam browsed casually, not truly looking for anything in particular, letting his thoughts wander. He then wandered around all the way to the main records building where all sorts of information was stored. This was a sect exclusive resource that only elders were able to access.","The towering records building stood at the edge of the inner sect grounds. Liam stepped through the arched doorway, greeted by the familiar scent of ink, old parchment, and alchemical herbs.","Rows of floating scrolls and translucent index tablets floated across the inner hall like fish in a still pond. Elder-ranked alchemists and archivists occupied various alcoves, either deep in study or carefully scribing newly confirmed formulas into the eternal ledger.","The moment Liam entered, a silence fell. Even among elders, his presence was an anomaly. He had not climbed the ranks through centuries of slow advancement or political maneuvering, he had shot through them like a comet, powered by results, purity, and daring.","A few came to greet him and Liam simply exchanged formal greetings with them and proceeded to browse through the records room. He moved deeper into the archive, bypassing the public shelves and accessing the private chambers with a flick of his sect badge.","He then started randomly browsing through everything. Hours slipped by quickly as Liam continued to be engrossed in reading various types of things such as the correct flame handling technique, how to form a contract with a fire spirit, and even records about some rare herbs that were extinct now. High rewards were offered for these rare herbs even within the sect.","Most of the scrolls he pulled weren't directly related to the Soul Rune or the soulweaver thread but that didn't matter. He was simply reading to relax.","Soon almost an entire day went by and Liam decided to head back to his quarters. However, just as he stepped out of the records tower a familiar face crossed his path. For a moment, Liam almost froze in his step and his eyes widened in shock.","How could he not recognize this woman? This was the person from whom he had stolen the golden cauldron! He had taken it from her right from under her nose!","And this person was from here?","The woman in front of him was none other than the same woman he had encountered back in the system golden event when he had pillaged and plundered some sort of ancient ruin to get some weird powerful soil particles.","He had no idea about the presence of the golden cauldron but clearly she knew. She had come there to claim it. But in the end, he was the one who took the prize home.","He was not sure if she saw him back then or not but judging from the encounter just now he seemed to be safe. He quickly adjusted his expression and continued walking as if nothing was wrong.","Inwardly, he was sweating bullets. What were the chances for this to happen? This lunatic girl just had to be from Green Mountain?","Back then within the system golden event this same woman had cursed him repeatedly for destroying the whole ruin and the treasure along with it. He had cursed him and called him a blasphemer and even cursed his nine generations and forefathers.","Did she even know that in the end he had managed to obtain the cauldron? Probably not.","It was not like she could track something so powerful. For all intents and purposes he was a completely innocent person.","Liam gave a polite nod and started walking back to his quarters. As he crossed the woman and walked away, he could feel the person turn and look at him. A chill ran down Liam's spine.","\"Who is that?\" The woman asked.","\"That's the newest elder, Miss Nyx.\" Someone near her explained.","\"Hmmm... I don't know why but I feel as if I had seen him before.\" The woman then turned her head and started walking away.","For a moment, Liam stiffened but thankfully she did not seem to recognize him. So much for a day of rest and relaxation. He had narrowly escaped from getting caught and being forced to run away from this place as well.","How could he possibly stay in an alchemy sect with numerous monsters if everyone came to know he was in possession of not one but three grand treasures of alchemy!","He had come to enjoy this sect quite a bit as it provided him a lot of peace and quiet and also opportunity to grow stronger. His alchemy knowledge alone had increased by leaps and bounds ever since he got here. He also managed to find a clue about his soulmancer inheritance. He did not want to leave this place just yet.","Liam let out a sigh as he arrived at his quarters. Maybe his time here was indeed coming to an end. He couldn't push his luck too much after all. The three grand treasures were his sureshot path to power and he couldn't lose them no matter what."]},{"number":1433,"title":"Chapter 1433: Unexpected meeting","paragraphs":["The next morning, Liam made a strong decision and started working on some loose ends and outstanding orders. He had seen a big red flag the day before, so it was best to get out of there while everything was fine and peaceful.","He hired an attendant from the sect just for this purpose. Send him out on some errands and at the same time asked him to spread around that he was going to be leaving for another training session in a nearby world.","Everything was working out smoothly, and Liam was almost ready to leave, but coincidentally, on the morning he was planning to set out, his attendant came back with some unexpected news.","Apparently a new announcement had arrived from the top, and the sect treasure lands were opened, and all of the disciples would be allowed inside in another three months.","This sudden news made Liam frown a little. While he did not want to risk anything for the sake of new treasures or small trinkets, he also knew that this could be a huge opportunity. The golden cauldron elder talked about unlocking the stone tablet, and this could be a key opportunity in doing that.","On the other hand, there was a high chance that he could expose himself by participating in the trial.","\"No. I should not be swayed.\" Liam firmly stood by his decision and was still sticking to his original plan of leaving the sect. There was no point in taking a risk, especially with that lunatic woman around. There was no telling what might happen.","However, right at this moment, the ancient voice of the golden cauldron boomed again. \"Brat, you better not run away because of one measly girl. Do you think that such a young girl could possibly sense me if I don't wish to reveal myself? You do not have to be so paranoid.\"","Liam paused. The cauldron's words made him think. He knew from experience that he always had to be four steps ahead of everyone in order to survive but he did not want to take the senior's words lightly.","This was the first time the cauldron was encouraging him to do something. Perhaps there really was something inside the treasure lands that could help him a lot. It was a soft nudge but the push from the cauldron was still there.","Liam was not a fool to ignore the words of a heaven-breaking treasure. He considered the pros and the cons again and this time the pros weighed a lot more than the cons. It seemed like he had to take this risk after all.","When the attendant returned to the quarters, Liam once again sent him out to spread the information that he wasn't going anywhere. With that, Liam busied himself again in studying the rune and the soulweaver thread.","He spent the next few days in contemplation but he did not make much progress. While he had already hit the roadblock when it came to runes, the soulweaver thread sat like a stone in his soul space unwilling to budge. He couldn't understand it at all.","Liam decided to head to the records tower once again to look for some inspiration. Hopefully, he did not run into that person again. On the way to the tower, he coincidentally came across some people discussing loudly about a runic language class offered by one of the sect main core disciples.","The main core disciples were elders who had been with the sect for decades after decades and perhaps even centuries. These people had immense knowledge when it came to alchemy, many of them already at dao lord rank and dao monarch rank.","The class was also an open class that anyone could attend. The class was probably introduced in link with the treasure lands to prepare the newbies for the event. Liam decided to sit in the class and improve his own knowledge about the runic language.","The lecture hall was a vast, tiered amphitheater carved directly into the side of the mountain, its interior humming with faint formations that preserved every spoken word like an echo within jade.","Liam quietly took a seat near the back, blending in with a cluster of outer disciples and inner sect initiates, all of whom buzzed with excitement and nerves.","Moments later, a ripple of silence swept the room as the core disciple entered. Elder Sun Lei. He looked unassuming, no long beard, no flashy robes. Just a serene man with silver hair tied in a single loop and piercing eyes that seemed filled with wisdom. He didn't announce himself. He didn't need to.","He simply raised a hand and the air shimmered. A glowing rune appeared midair, composed of curves and angular strokes Liam had seen only in the oldest scrolls. \"This,\" Elder Sun began, \"is not merely a symbol. It is the crystallized memory of the universe. To read it is to remember what creation has forgotten. The ancient language of every type of energy.\"","Over the next hour, the elder walked them through foundational components of the ancient runic script, what are some of the basic runes, how runes play a role in magic and activation of spells and how one shouldn't rely solely on the system for these things and have to delve deeper into runic language to remove the system which usually acts like a moderator between man and magic.","Liam sat straighter at those words. Remove the system? That wasn't something he'd ever heard someone say aloud. Everyone else either relied on it blindly or treated it as a god-given layer of reality. But here was a Dao Monarch-level cultivator casually stating that it was merely an interpreter, a middleman between will and the world.","Elder Sun Lei continued, \"When you write a rune, you are not drawing. You are invoking. Every stroke is an intent. Every curve, a channel. The system offers ease, yes but ease dulls the edge. Those who walk the path of true runescript will one day sever that leash.\""]},{"number":1434,"title":"Chapter 1434: New development","paragraphs":["Liam's pulse quickened. He was beginning to see the shape of a deeper truth. Maybe this was why the Soulweaver thread was inert. The system didn't know what to do with it. It couldn't process it. The rune in his soul was a fragment of something beyond the system's framework, an artifact of raw, pre-systemic creation.","He leaned forward as Elder Sun traced a particularly intricate rune in the air. \"This glyph is called Tiiran. It means 'rooted resonance.' You'll find it at the heart of most ancient arrays designed to stabilize consciousness across dimensions. By merely looking at this rune, many have even achieved breakthroughs.\"","The elder continued the lecture as he effortlessly conjured more runes into the air, each glowing with distinct frequencies that hummed in resonance with the room itself. \"Runes like Tiiran are not mere marks. They are living scripts. Fragments of intent that bind space, time, and self together. And when you trace them, you are not copying symbols. You are aligning your essence with primordial law.\"","Liam's heart pounded harder. He couldn't help but be envious of the young scions of ancient clans who would have gotten to sit in many lectures such as this and be exposed to knowledge that was so hard for him to come by. Unlike him, who was scraping by wherever and whatever he could get, the geniuses of the big families would have had an entirely different life.","Liam stopped his mind from wandering and snapped back to pay full attention to the class. The class was so mentally taxing that even he had to pay extra attention just to not lose focus. The knowledge and profundity in every single word were overwhelming to say the least.","Elder Sun's voice continued to echo through the vast amphitheater. \"Those who truly walk the path of ancient runes must first learn to listen. Not with ears. Not even with mind. But with identity. Runes are truths. You cannot forge one unless you first accept what is already real.\"","\"You must accept your path and walk forward with full conviction in your dao. Your dao is your reality, and your dao is your truth. Only by fully immersing yourself in it will you be able to fully comprehend the rune script for your path.\"","The lecture continued for the next hour, and overall, it was an extremely short amount of time, especially considering the lifespans of people who had gathered here, but no one felt that it was short at all. Everyone walked out of the classroom completely dazed and exhausted, including Liam.","He immediately returned to his quarters and focused once again on going over what was taught in the class today. His attendant helped him procure more reading materials from the records tower, and Liam busied himself studying the various things about runic language.","He had yet to come across anything related to his soul rune, but it did not matter. The language of the ancient world was fascinating by itself, and he could already feel some of his skills improving by leaps and bounds as he began to understand the runic script behind them.","He could only curse his ignorance for not doing this earlier and familiarizing himself with the rune language at a deeper level.","Liam immersed himself in study like a starving man thrown into a banquet of truths. Each new scroll, every etched sigil, and obscure commentary from ancient alchemists peeled back another layer of the world's design. The runes weren't just tools, they were living pathways. Threads of intent, forged even before the System.","He began to see patterns in spells he'd cast for years, structural flaws he'd never noticed, inefficiencies that were now painfully obvious. And all of it traced back to runes. Their arrangement. Their harmony. Their identity.","The more he delved into the structure and rhythm of these primordial glyphs, the more he began to understand the small components that made up the origin rune sitting in his soul. Perhaps if he were able to gain some more insights, he might even be able to understand a good amount of the rune and break through his block point.","Soon, an entire week passed by just like that, and it was once again time for another lecture. Liam hurriedly walked to the lecture hall and sat down in the back. He had a lot of questions and doubts in his mind, which he hoped to be able to understand through this lecture. He was really looking forward to it.","Time ticked by, and the lecture was about to start. The doors of the classroom banged open, and when Liam looked up, a familiar face walked inside. Standing in front of him with simple robes and her long hair fluttering about was none other than that lunatic woman, Nyx.","So she was a core disciple of this sect? That was just perfect. Liam frowned. He did not want to meet this woman ever again and yet he had willingly walked into a lecture hall for a lecture given by the same woman.","Liam thought about it for a moment and then decided to take it easy. It was a big lecture hall after all. There was no need to fret. If this Nyx had something to teach, then he was all the more willing to listen and to learn. He would just be one among the masses. There shouldn't be any issues.","Nyx didn't even glance at the crowd as she walked to the center of the amphitheater.","\"Most of you were taught to fear instability,\" Nyx started. \"To avoid conflict within your soul, to treat imbalance as a sickness. But the truth is that evolution is born from discord. You want to awaken your path? Break it first. Shatter what you think you are.\"","She then began showing some of the basic alchemical runes. Each one emanated power and was very awe-inspiring just to even watch. Everyone jotted down all the details, down to the last stroke of the rune, including every word out of her mouth, without missing even a single thing.","Soon, the time passed, and the one-hour mark was almost over, the lecture coming to an end. Liam had also gained a lot from the lecture this time. Her teachings were in no way lesser compared to the teachings of the elder, and many gaps in his knowledge were filled.","Attending these types of things was definitely better than simply reading notes from a book. The insights gained were more profound and elaborate.","At this time, Nyx suddenly raised her hand again, and a single rune formed. This was a unique rune in the sense that it did not have a stable form at all. It was chaotic, twisting, as if it didn't want to exist in one form. \"This is the Rune of Transmutation,\" she said softly as everyone in the huge space watched the rune in awe.","Liam's eyes were wide as he was completely focused on this rune. Surprisingly, this rune structure was very similar to the soul origin rune, and as she explained the details behind the rune, many things immediately became clear to him. He slowly went into a trance as he listened and comprehended at the same deepening his understanding more and more.","And then it happened. A Dao pillar erupted all around him, fully enclosing him, indicating the creation of a new Dao seed in the soul."]},{"number":1435,"title":"Chapter 1435: Her again?","paragraphs":["Gasps rippled through the amphitheater like a stone dropped into a still pond. Disciples turned in their seats, craning their necks to catch a glimpse of the phenomenon. Dao manifestations during lectures were rare. Unheard of, even. But there, Liam sat, motionless, completely absorbed, while a translucent pillar of dao energy surged skyward around him.","What others did not see was that ancient glyphs shimmered within the column, some familiar, most unrecognizable, all pulsing with a strange rhythm as if answering a call from beyond the heavens. The Dao pillar was not a normal one at all, as the insight he had gained this time was far from ordinary.","Nyx's expression didn't change, but her gaze sharpened. For a moment, she said nothing, allowing the rune she had conjured to dissipate silently into the air. Her eyes locked onto Liam's form with an annoyed expression. \"Who is this disciple? Doesn't he know Dao breakthroughs need to be attempted in isolation to gain maximum benefit?\"","Her attendant quickly walked over and filled her in on the details. \"He is the recent shooting star who has become very famous.\" Nyx once again did not like what she was hearing. The reason why alchemists in the sect did not entertain orders left and right was because they did not want it to affect their Dao progress.","But once again, this man did not respect traditions. Instead, he treated his time like a cheap commodity and was concocting pills and potions like a common whore. Nyx's opinion of Liam crashed and plummeted as she would never condone such frivolous, flashy actions, which disrespected the great Dao of alchemy.","She did not interrupt Liam's breakthrough, but her aura flickered, cool and disdainful. This kind of recklessness, this display, went against every foundational principle she'd been raised to uphold.","Pill concoction was sacred. Alchemy was an art that demanded solitude, reverence, restraint. And yet here he was, this so-called rising star, forging Dao seeds like some street performer juggling flame.","To her, it wasn't just improper, it was dangerous. Showmanship invited instability. Instability corrupted understanding. What would happen if every half-trained disciple began chasing breakthroughs in public? If every seed sown came with applause instead of introspection?","Nyx turned slightly, her voice cold and clipped, though still too low for most in the amphitheater to hear. \"No discipline. No respect for process. If he crashes, let it be known that he built his foundation in a theater instead of a temple.\"","But even as the words left her mouth, a strange contradiction gnawed at her. Despite everything she despised about the moment, the Dao pillar surrounding Liam was pure and mysterious. Her intuition told her that there was something very special about it.","Moreover, the dao pillar seemed to last for more than five breaths, which was the usual time for a breakthrough. Nyx's expression changed more and more as these five breaths became ten breaths, and then the ten breaths turned into an entire minute.","Finally, after an entire minute and a half, the light of the dao pillar started fading. Nyx's narrowed eyes betrayed her inner storm. She had seen dozens, no, hundreds, of Dao seeds take root over the years. Some were impressive, even brilliant. But none had ever sustained a Dao pillar like this.","Her annoyance was replaced by a tense silence. She didn't understand this... couldn't understand it. She hated that.","Across the hall, disciples had long ceased pretending to take notes. All eyes were on Liam, their awe simmering between reverence and envy. Some whispered, others simply watched, spellbound.","Finally, someone spoke out loud. \"Perhaps he took a forbidden pill?\"","Nyx's attendant leaned in again, voice a whisper. \"Should I disrupt it, Elder? Perhaps he—\"","\"No,\" she snapped, sharper than she intended. \"Let him finish. If he dares to burn so brightly, let us see whether he can survive the flame.\"","However, the others were not so calm and composed. The discussions and the commotions in the room became louder and louder until finally Nyx snapped and asked everyone to disperse. The idiot might not know how to respect the Great Dao of Alchemy, but she knew how to respect a fellow disciple's path.","No one dared to disobey her, and within a few seconds, the entire area became quiet and empty except for Liam and Nyx. During the entire time Liam remained in that state of transcendental stillness, his eyes closed, face serene, as though he were listening to the song of the cosmos itself.","Nyx gave him one final look and then turned around and walked away indifferently. Each to their own. She couldn't care less about what this person did with his path.","As the last echoes of retreating footsteps faded from the stone walls of the amphitheater, the great hall fell into a profound silence, broken only by the gentle hum of Liam's fading Dao pillar. The ancient glyphs had mostly vanished, but a few lingered in the air like afterimages burned into reality.","Liam sat in the center, still unmoving, still caught in the final moments of his internal transformation. Somewhere deep within his soul space, the soul rune pulsed with quiet vitality, and beside it, the previously inert Soulweaver thread shimmered.","Outside, word of the event was already beginning to spread. Disciples rushed to share their version of what they had seen, and suddenly, Liam became even more popular.","Inside the empty lecture hall, Liam finally stirred. His eyes opened, not wide, not startled, but with a calmness that hadn't been there before. He breathed once, deep and steady. He finally had a better understanding of the origin rune in his soul and knew exactly how he needed to use his soulweaver thread.","He stood slowly, stretching his fingers, letting the silence settle into him. \"Let's see where this path takes me,\" he murmured to no one in particular. Without another glance back, Liam left the amphitheater, stepping into the mountain wind and returning to his quarters.","He needed to get back into secluded meditation once again, but this time he was sure he would make another breakthrough because the new dao seed he had just gained was something far from simple."]},{"number":1436,"title":"Chapter 1436: A street performer disrespecting the great dao","paragraphs":["Liam spent the next several days silently meditating in the same spot in his room. The room had arrays for ambient mana and focus, and was top-notch without him doing anything. The sect's living quarters were tailored to the needs of its disciples, and Liam's current status as an alchemy prodigy ensured he had access to some of the best.","Walls lined with subtle rune formations breathed in tandem with the flow of mana, drawing in spiritual energy from the surroundings and concentrating it in a delicate spiral around him. The floor beneath his seated form faintly glowed, stabilizing his body and spirit, and dulling all sound from the outside world.","Days passed in near-perfect stillness. Liam didn't move, didn't speak, didn't eat. His breathing was imperceptible.","Within his consciousness, however, there was nothing but motion, threads of thought spinning together with strands of soul, the newly formed Dao seed slowly solidifying in his core. He was not just stabilizing the seed. He was integrating it and letting it grow roots into his being.","This newly formed Dao seed was very different from the others. In fact, it wasn't a newly formed Dao seed at all in a way. This was the same soul dao seed that he already had. He had had a soul dao seed since the time he figured out how to heal his soul using his soul minions.","However, right now, this dao seed had completely broken down and reformed. While previously he wasn't able to extract much from the dao seed in the way he had extracted power from the other dao seeds, now everything was different.","Liam could feel the new dao seed, which was in the shape of a small shard, deeply embedded into his very soul. At first, it looked still and dormant just like before, but that all changed when he started practising the soul cultivation technique.","The speed of his soul cultivation technique had now increased by leaps and bounds. He was now not too far away from forming his second constellation. The progress he had made in just these few weeks were tremendous when compared to his progress before. Not to mention forming a second constellation was a lot more difficult when compared to forming the first one.","This was not the only new development. When Liam took a closer look at the new soul dao seed, he found a small rune now inscribed within in. He was only able to see it after he became more familiar with his dao seed and this rune was none other than the origin rune.","He still hadn't quite grasped the complete meaning of the origin rune. He could only draw the similarities between the origin rune and the transmutation rune. But this in itself had deepened his understanding to such an extent that he was able to break down his old soul dao seed and reforge a brand new one.","The new one looked a lor more profound and grander when compared to the old one. He was also able to use the dao energy of the new soul dao seed to boost his attacks and not just soul attacks. Though the both dao seeds were similar, they were completely worlds apart when it came to quality and profoundity.","Liam couldn't help but be in awe every time he connected with the dao seed. If there were myriad paths in front of him, then one path had suddenly become a grand and golden one. Walking in this path gave him a very different feeling than walking in his other paths.","This one was a lot deeper than all the others. His understanding in this one was several times higher than all of the many dao seeds he possessed, making them all feel shallow and ordinary. It felt very wrong for all the other dao seeds to exist in the presence of a grand dao seed such as this.","Liam continued to immerse himself in understanding his dao seed more and more. He even tried to use his soul weaver thread with the help of this dao seed but it looked like that part still needed a lot more effort from him.","Despite the tremendous strides he had made, Liam knew this was only the beginning. He had barely even scratched the surface of the newly formed dao seed. He continued training his soul strength and connecting with his new dao seed and just like that the next several days flew by.","Soon it was time for the sect's treasure lands to open up. In this time, Liam had already sent out his attendant to gather all sorts of information about these treasure lands. He also personally set out to gather more details.","There were two things he came across in this time. The first being that his reputation had somehow skyrocketed yet again, his name becoming famous in all corners of the sect, thanks to his very public dao seed breakthrough.","Liam awkwardly cringed when he heard about this but he did not care. The gains he had this time was a lot greater. If he had done something like pause or forcibly refrain the breakthrough from happening, then who knows if he might have ended up with the same dao seed or a different one.","Dao seeds were not so simple that he would be bold and daring to pause and breakthrough according to his will and whim.","The second important information was about the treasure lands. Apparently, it was an ancient pocket world which was the main reason why the sect had grown so much in the past several centuries. So the treasures inside could potentially be fate-breaking.","There was no way to monitor what went on inside and everyone who entered the treasure lands did so at their own risk. Once inside, the protective hand of the sect did not apply. There were no elders watching from above, no talismans that could teleport one out at the last moment.","The moment a disciple stepped into the treasure lands, they became both hunter and prey, and only their skills, cunning, and fate determined whether they walked back out or became another ghost haunting the ruins.","There were several strongholds of the sect inside the treasure lands and several maps that talked about relatively safer regions and more dangerous regions.","As long as one stuck to the safer zones, there would be no risk to one's lives. Accordingly, the gains would also only be moderate. However, the treasure lands were so amazing that these moderate gains themselves were enough to push one's level to the next realm.","Rumors swirled around what could be found inside: broken inheritance grounds, elemental nodes, ancient beasts in hibernation, soul-tempered weapons, and even the lingering wills of long-dead cultivators that tested passersby for compatibility. It was the kind of place that could reshape one's path entirely... or end it abruptly.","There was also a rumor that the founder of the sect was inside the treasure lands. The story went that the founder managed to come across an ancient inheritance, and ever since then, he had been undergoing secluded meditation in the treasure lands.","Liam silently observed all the information he received about the treasure lands and fully prepared himself before setting out of his quarters on the opening day.","It was time to finally go inside and see for himself exactly what these treasure lands were and why even the cauldon senior had nudged him to pay attention to it."]},{"number":1437,"title":"Chapter 1437: The new dao seed","paragraphs":["Liam stepped out into the morning mist, his figure wrapped in silence as the sect buzzed with anticipation.","Today, the gates to the treasure lands would open. He wasn't the only one who had spent the last few days in seclusion; across the mountain range, countless alchemists had been preparing, refining pills, sharpening weapons, and doing painstaking hard work.","The air near the sect's central plaza was filled with tension. Sect elders, alchemists who stood at the peak, who had already reached Dao lord rank, stood watch in silence. Their expressions were unreadable, though most wouldn't step through the gates themselves. This was a trial for the younger generation.","Liam's arrival did not go unnoticed. Whispers rippled through the crowd like wind through dry leaves. Some gazes held awe, others jealousy, a few even fear. Many had seen the dao pillar during the lecture.","Others had heard how it lasted longer than any other in recent sect history. A few had even claimed that some sort of ancient beast roared from within his dao pillar. The rumors had become extremely exaggerated.","Ignoring it all, Liam calmly moved to his assigned position, atop a platform. Multiple floating platforms could be found in the plaza, each one housing a top-tier alchemist of the Green Mountain sect.","Soon, it was time, and one of the sect elders stepped forward. He took out a strange token from his spatial ring and activated it. The next second, a purple color portal materialized into existence.","All conversation ceased. Even the wind seemed to pause. The moment had arrived.","The elder holding the token spoke a few brief words. \"The gates to the Treasure Lands are now open. Your fate is your own.\"","As if answering his words, the portal flared. From its swirling depths came a pressure that suppressed everyone in the area.. Some disciples flinched. Others stared, entranced. Liam narrowed his eyes. There were several powerful auras within the portal.","\"Only step inside if you are sure of it. You have 1 minute to decide.\"","Immediately, one by one, many platforms shot toward the portal. The top alchemists, each brimming with ambition and years of training, stood tall and silent as they passed through the veil. Despite the danger, no one wanted to miss this opportunity.","Liam willed his platform to enter the portal, and the next second, he shot forward towards the portal as well. He stepped through without hesitation, letting the vortex swallow him whole. But the next moment, he froze as a familiar feeling gripped him.","\"A soul frayed by the weight of unseen sins... Temper it in silence, and it may yet be unbound. Righteousness is not a sanctuary, it is a crucible. Only the tempered endure.\"","\"The next heir of the league of soul weavers... the grand throne awaits you...\"","Liam's entire being trembled from the inside out. His very core shook as the familiar words reached his ears. Some of it he had heard before, and some of it he had not. As he crashed into the world, he finally understood why the cauldron senior had nudged him in this direction.","Another part of his soulmancer's legacy was here!","It had been so close to him, and he was this close to losing it permanently!","Liam clenched his fists. It did not matter. Now that he was here, this piece of the legacy was also fated to be his and his alone.","Inside the purple portal, a vibrant green world extended before him in all directions. It was clearly the best environment for nourishing all sorts of herbs and plants. Liam hovered in place for a brief moment, eyes wide, chest rising slowly as he took it all in.","He then shot forward in a particular direction. He felt an unmistakable pull in that direction, and he was pretty sure the next part of the legacy rested there. However, just as he charged forward, a powerful aura appeared in his path, and before he could realize he was facing something huge and monstrous.","A tail came whipping down at Liam, and he immediately used his domains to block the attack. Only that it was no use. The power of that monstrous beast was so strong that he was simply flung aside.","Liam was about to immediately teleport and disappear when a familiar voice sounded in his ears. \"Why are you always so reckless?\" A woman appeared between the tail and him, and a massive cauldron descended from the sky, directly crushing the monstrous beast under its weight.","One shot kill!","Nyx elegantly floated in front of Liam, her face cold and aloof. \"When you enter a foreign and dangerous territory, you need to proceed cautiously, not run around like a madman.\" Came her words of wisdom.","Liam's face twitched. The one person he did not want to meet inside this place had somehow found him moments after he stepped inside. What the hell was happening right now? He did not bother to stop and talk to her and instead continued trying to teleport the hell out of there.","Nyx snorted. \"You cannot teleport within these treasure lands. Don't you know anything about this place?\"","Liam bitterly smiled as the next moment he switched with his clone and disappeared from there anyway.","Nyx's face turned unsightly. She had just helped this bastard, and yet all the gratitude she got was this. \"Bastard.\" She muttered under her breath, clenching her fists.","She was only used to people revering her and respecting her whenever they saw them. This was the first time someone had run away like he had seen the plague the moment he had laid eyes on her, despite her saving him.","\"Why is he behaving like this? Did he think that I was going to come after some paltry herbs he had managed to acquire here? Hmph. What an ignorant idiot.\" She continued cursing Liam for a few seconds before leaving the place as well.","Meanwhile, Liam reappeared in another place and wiped a drop of sweat from his forehead. That was close. He could still clearly feel the pull towards the direction he needed to go, but getting there was not going to be an easy task."]},{"number":1438,"title":"Chapter 1438: The gates are now open","paragraphs":["It took about five hours, but after several detours and three life-or-death battles, Liam finally made his way to the location where he was feeling some sort of pull, a pull that tugged at his very soul, as if a hidden string were drawing him closer to something ancient and vital.","Liam slowed down as he suddenly felt a new presence and an especially strong one at that. To make matters worse, the place he needed to go was right in front of him. A tall and ancient-looking pagoda with twenty floors.","Liam cautiously inched towards the pagoda using every expertise he had on stealth skill, in which he had actually made quite a lot of progress after killing that assassin from another world and studying his soul.","That too, he was so close to his destination. He decided to bite the bullet and take the risk. Of course, as fate would have it, the presence of the opponent only grew stronger the closer he got to the pagoda.","Ten meters from the entrance, a ripple passed through the air, barely visible, like a mirage. Liam froze. Something massive shifted on the roof of the pagoda. A tail? No... a tendril. No wings. It was hard to say.","The entity was veiled in some sort of illusion. This guardian, or whatever it was, hadn't attacked. Not yet. But Liam knew. One wrong move, one breath too loud, and he'd be fighting something far beyond his current tier.","He exhaled slowly, sweat beading along his spine. The pagoda was now just a few feet away from him, but there was a sort of forcefield in the area that made him hesitate. It was almost as if... taking one more step would mean death.","Liam let out a sigh. He had no heart to go back empty-handed, especially when what he wanted was right here. At the same time, he did not want to take the risk, knowing that your opponent outclassed you so much. Walking ahead now would only be a suicide.","He stood at the spot, not wanting to go either forward or backward, gritting his teeth in frustration. Not wanting to give up after coming so far, he finally decided on a path and made sure that his backup escape minion was in position.","Teleporting out of danger was not the issue, but sometimes, when facing someone stronger, even that split second might not be there. He might end up dead before he could even think of teleporting.","However, that woman, Nyx, did say that he could not teleport here. His skill worked differently, and the opponent might not be aware of it. He could use this to his advantage. This was barely enough reasoning, but he made up his mind and decided to go along with it.","Liam sucked in a deep breath and took a step forward.","Almost instantly, a strong and powerful aura washed over him. A being dropped down from the top of the pagoda and landed in front of him. It had a scaly body, and its eyes were cruel, vicious, and slit-like.","It grinned at Liam with a mocking expression and raised its claws. Everything happened too fast, and Liam barely had time to react. However, the next moment, something even more unexpected happened.","The gates of the pagoda that were closed up until now suddenly started opening. Liam looked at the pagoda in shock. To his surprise, the creature in front of him seemed equally shocked. Everything that happened after that was a complete blur as Liam reacted instinctively.","The creature, all of a sudden, lost any and all interest in Liam and its gaze became completely fixated on the pagoda. It ignored him altogether and shot forward towards the open doors at top speed.","Liam was tempted to run in the other direction, but his gut feeling told him to enter the place. It was calling for him, and for some reason, he knew that the gates had opened for him and not the creature.","Throwing all caution to the wind, he too shot forward towards the open gates. But his speed couldn't match the creature's. He only reached it after that scaly creature. However, while he was able to smoothly enter the pagoda, the scaly creature was unceremoniously thrown out right in front of his eyes.","In fact, Liam could see the being thrown out just as he stepped in.","The scaly creature growled and roared in rage and defiance as it swung its claws, releasing a powerful fiery slash that ripped the very space in front of it. Liam's eyes widened at the power contained in the attack. The attack was steeped in the Dao of fire.","But before the attack could even touch Liam, an invisible barrier sprang up, right after which, the pagoda doors once again tightly closed shut right on the face of the scaly creature.","Liam staggered back and fell from the sheer impact. He panted and finally took in everything that had happened in the last second. His heart was beating out of his chest. He had only barely escaped with his life, coming so close to being eaten alive by that damn thing.","\"Was that a draconic creature?\" Liam leaned back on his palms, eyes still fixed on the tightly shut doors of the pagoda. Outside, the enraged roars of the scaly beast echoed faintly, muffled by the thick walls of this otherworldly structure.","The crushing pressure that had stalked him outside was now gone, as if the pagoda itself had accepted him.","He swallowed, still stunned. The beast had been tossed out like garbage while he was accepted. Now he had no doubt that he had indeed come to the right place. Just where the hell was he?","He could only hope that this time around, he would be able to get more information than the bare minimum scrap he had obtained last time. He expectantly looked around, but there was nothing on the ground floor.","Liam stood up and dusted his back. It was fine. There were still many floors, and there was bound to be something or the other on one of these floors."]},{"number":1439,"title":"Chapter 1439: In and out","paragraphs":["\"Are you serious? There is nothing inside?\" Liam was shocked. He had searched for the past two hours, scouring this place from top to bottom, running around on all the floors, and yet there wasn't a single thing in the whole building.","\"You have got to be kidding me.\" Liam did not understand. Why did he feel the pull towards this building if there was nothing inside? Why did that creature outside try to enter so badly if there was nothing inside? Why did the gates of the building open for him and throw the other guy out?","It just did not make sense.","Liam sat down and decided to meditate for a bit before thinking about what to do next. There were also some powerful souls he had captured on the way to the building. He stopped his meditation and thought of something. He then began to forge the beast souls.","He took the pulsing orb of soul energy, and as usual, he compressed it again and again until it became a small bead. A stream of memories flowed into his mind.","Liam closed his eyes as he absorbed all the memories. He needed more information about these treasure lands and this building, and more importantly, about the creature who was most definitely waiting for him outside.","One by one, he saw through the scenes of the beast's life as they flashed across his mind. The beast had been born here and had also grown up here.","It had a pretty simple life. It hunted other creatures and devoured them. Eventually, it picked up the Dao of Earth and became pretty adept at it. The one thing that stood out in its whole lifetime was its fear of the scaly creatures.","Liam was right. The moment he had seen the slit like eyes and the superior scales and the way the creature moved, he had a feeling that these creatures had at least some amount of dragon bloodline in them.","And just as he thought, these creatures were indeed related to dragons. They were called Draluras, and they occupied most of these treasured lands. In fact, this beast was of the understanding that these guys were the owners of the whole thing, this entire world.","Most of its family members had fallen prey to these Draluras, and apparently, the beast was only alive since it hadn't broken through to the next transcendent yet. The Draluras made it a point to hunt any beast that stepped past this threshold.","Some thought it was to make the beast meat more nutritious, while others thought this was because the Draluras did not want anyone to become strong enough to threaten their rule.","But in the end, it doesn't matter. Anyone who stepped into the transcendent rank instantly became a threat to the Draluras. That is, if they stepped into their territory.","To hide their presence in this world, the Draluras had allowed many other beasts to become stronger, even power up to higher ranks than transcendents, and these were the beasts that typically people who entered this world encountered.","Liam only managed to slip into their territory unnoticed thanks to the superior stealth skill he had taken from that assassin, the ghost walking skill. However, even that was not helpful as he eventually got caught by the Dralura who was guarding this building. Or maybe trying to get in.","The beast had no thoughts about this building as such. It only knew that coming near this building was an instant death sentence, and no one was allowed near it.","Liam let out a breath and finished forging the soul. He had hoped for more information, but this was all he had. Unless he hunted down one of those Draluras, he doubted if he would get any more than this.","The next instant, Liam summoned the recently forged beast and commanded it to search the building. However, just as the soul minion appeared, something unexpected happened.","All of a sudden, the entire place became completely foggy, dense white fumes swirled into existence, pouring down from the higher floors like a waterfall of mist. Liam's eyes narrowed, his body instinctively shifting into a battle stance.","A moment later, he couldn't help but relax as the energy around him was extremely familiar. In fact, it was the one he was most familiar with, and it was the one that made him the strongest. Soul energy! All around him, there was soul energy!","Soul energy... thick, potent, and pure, far denser than anything he had ever cultivated before. It wasn't just lingering in the air; it was alive, almost sentient, brushing against his skin like unseen fingers trying to probe him, test him, recognize him.","His body instinctively began to absorb it, greedily pulling in the essence with every breath. And this one didn't resist him. It welcomed him. All of the energy gushed into his body.","His eyes widened. This place wasn't empty. It was the treasure.","He immediately closed his eyes and started using his soul cultivation technique. This was the perfect chance for him to form his second constellation. He rapidly began to form one star cluster after another, when suddenly he felt a movement in the depths of his soul.","The soul weaver thread he had in his being was finally responding.","Liam's body trembled. So, the thing needed a soul energy concentration of this level to awaken? He did not know, but now that it had finally responded, he was not planning to miss this chance.","Liam immediately took out his soul weapon, the Black Dragon sword. When he had obtained the soul weaver thread, this was the first idea that came to his mind. He could use the soulweaver thread to activate and finally complete the Black Dragon sword.","He gently placed the sword on the ground and then guided the soulweaver thread toward it. The dense white soul energy began to swirl violently around him. The sword trembled slightly in his hands.","Liam bit his lip, blood trailing down his chin as he poured more and more soul energy into the thread, binding it to the Black Dragon sword. The soulweaver thread lit up, glowing with an ethereal silver-gold hue, and began to sink into the weapon's core."]},{"number":1440,"title":"Chapter 1440: Draluras","paragraphs":["Liam held it down with all he had, but to his shock, the next second the whole thing exploded on his face. If he hadn't instantly formed many soul barriers in front of him, half or more of his body would have once again evaporated.","Liam staggered back, coughing violently as the thick smoke and shattered soul essence scattered around him. His vision blurred, his chest burned, and the soulweaver thread in his hand writhed like a snake pulled from fire, still intact, but unstable.","The Black Dragon sword lay a few feet away, now humming lowly, its surface cracked and bleeding fine streams of black mist.","\"Are these two incompatible?\" Liam did not understand. He had almost lost both of these precious items in a single attempt!","\"Damn it...\" Liam wiped the blood from his mouth and knelt beside the weapon, his brows furrowed in pain and confusion. The connection had almost worked. The soulweaver thread had responded. So why had it detonated?","Maybe if he tried again, he could understand something. He decided to take a break and focused on soul cultivation some more, but his soulweaver thread was only becoming more and more unstable.","It felt as if he did not use it right now, he was going to lose it anyway.","Liam gritted his teeth and came to a decision. He needed to try this again. But the sword was not the right answer. He closed his eyes, and several options went through his mind. In the end, he decided to bet on something ridiculous.","Liam summoned a soul clone of himself. With the abundant soul energy all around him, he was able to conjure the strongest soul clone he had ever made. Sucking in a big breath of air, he once again started the same process.","But this time, he guided the soulweaver thread toward the clone instead of the weapon.","\"It's probably going to fail again, but now I will understand why I am failing.\" Liam closed his eyes as he gave his utmost focus and concentration to both himself and the clone. Part of him was controlling the soulweaver thread while part of him was observing everything that happened from the point of view of the clone.","Thankfully, he had enough mental strength to do something like this.","Soon, the thread made contact, and the clone shuddered violently. The thick fog around them spiraled inward, pouring more and more soul energy into the process.","Liam focused every ounce of control he had, not forcing the thread, but weaving it into the clone's essence. He threaded it through the clone's soul core, slowly and carefully embedded it right there in the core using as much soul energy as he could muster.","His hands trembled, sweat pouring down his face, but he didn't stop. He suddenly felt a shock as he faced a strong rejection from his soul clone","Liam clenched his fists. \"No. Accept it. Take it and make it yours!\" He shouted, giving the command to himself.","The soul clone convulsed in place, its body flickering as cracks of bluish soul-light split across its skin. The rejection wasn't coming from the soulweaver thread, it was coming from within. From Liam himself. The clone was him, after all, and it was resisting the transformation at a fundamental level.","Liam once again tried to force it when he had a thought. What if the soul clone was rejecting it because it simply couldn't accept? Once that idea popped into his mind, he could feel it. There was indeed something lacking.","For a soul clone to become more whole and solid, it needed something to fuel it. Like a mana core or... Liam's eyes flashed open as the obvious thought finally came to him. A Dao seed! His soul clone needed a Dao seed!","Just as he realized it, a wave of pain swept across him as his hold on the soulweaver thread became weaker and weaker. The thread was close to collapsing and exploding, taking his soul clone along with it.","\"No. I will not fail this time.\" Liam gritted his teeth and began to pump more and more of soul energy into his soul clone. This time, he also did something unthinkable. He took the part of his soul that had imprinted one of his dao seeds and ripped it apart.","White-hot, blinding, soul-deep pain tore through Liam's body. It was the kind that made one's thoughts splinter, senses collapse, and one's being feel like it was being peeled away, thread by agonizing thread.","His vision blacked out for a second as he clutched his chest, soul fracturing under the sheer madness of what he had just done.","He had torn a Dao seed from himself. The Dao seed of Fire.","Something he had cultivated, honed, and anchored deep into his being, and now, it floated between his trembling hands, raw and unstable, ready to be erased at any moment.","\"Sever what is not needed!\"","The old man's voice rang loudly in his ears at this moment. This was the old man he had met when he entered the Green Mountain sect for the very first time, the old man who had tested him, but Liam did not think much of his words at the moment.","He only knew that he was not willing to give up on any of his dao seeds. But now everything suddenly made sense.","Liam didn't waste a second. With a desperate cry, he thrust the burning seed into the core of his soul clone. The result was instant.","The clone screamed, not with sound but with essence. Its body began to collapse... and rebuild. Collapse... and rebuild. A fiery aura began to appear around it.","The soulweaver thread, now on the brink of disintegration, was pulled back into alignment like a taut wire being rethreaded into a loom. It wrapped around the core, weaving through the newly born Dao seed.","The soulweaver thread surged with renewed vigor, no longer writhing or unstable. The clone's cracked soul core melted and reformed, binding with the Dao seed, locking it in as a true foundation."]},{"number":1441,"title":"Chapter 1441: Sever what is not needed!","paragraphs":["A massive burst of soul fire exploded outward from the clone, knocking Liam to the ground and scouring the air clean of soul energy. Glowing runes lit up across the entire pagoda, on walls, floors, even hanging in the air, as if the building itself had finally recognized his success.","Massive amounts of soul energy started gathering. And standing at the center of it all... was the soul clone. If it could even be called that anymore.","The soul clone was no longer flickering, no longer unstable. It stood tall, flames gently rising from its form, eyes burning like coals. Across its chest, a faint brand glowed, the same infinity sigil that marked Liam's soul constellations.","Liam barely had the strength to stand, but he stared in awe, chest heaving with pain and pride. He had done it. He had finally done it!","Almost immediately, a stream of system notifications flashed in front of him.","[Ding! You have successfully created a Dao clone.]","[Ding! Your Dao clone now shares your Dao of Fire comprehension and evolves independently. While active, Fire techniques are amplified by 50%.]","Liam let out a broken laugh. He had lost a Dao seed. But in return... he had gained something monstrous. A soul-bound partner. A second body of fire and fate. He only barely looked at the notifications before collapsing.","The last thing Liam saw before darkness claimed him was the eyes of his clone. Soul energy continued to pour into it. Flames started gathering around it, and unexpectedly, even mana continued to pour into it. Time passed in silence.","Outside the pagoda, the Dralura beast, still pacing and snarling at the sealed entrance, suddenly froze. Its slitted eyes narrowed as it stared at the glowing pagoda. Something was not right. It immediately left the area to alert the others.","Inside, Liam remained unconscious, breathing slowly, and his soul slowly mending. A few minutes later, he stirred awake as he sensed a massive energy fluctuation near him.","\"Fuck! Did I get thrown out of the pagoda?\" He immediately became alert and ready to teleport to wherever his farthest soul minion was, but he stopped as he still found himself lying on the stone-cold floor of the pagoda.","For a moment, everything felt unreal as his gaze shifted to his newly formed soul clone, which was now simply sitting in a cross-legged position, eyes still very much alive and not empty or devoid of life. It still lacked a physical body, but it definitely had its conscience, not like the other soul clones or the soul minions he had forged before.","\"What exactly are you?\" Liam stared at it.","However, he could immediately feel the strong connection, and his mind became one with the soul clone at a single command. Liam could suddenly see from two pairs of eyes. Once again, it was very different from the connection he had with his soul minions.","This was different. He was the soul clone, and the soul clone was him. It could exist independently without him, but at the same time, it could become one with him as well. It was not a different version of him or a partial part of him. It was he wholly and completely.","More importantly, he could feel the dao seed inside his new soul clone growing at a tremendous pace as if the act of tearing it free and forging it into a second vessel had removed all shackles and limitations.","It was no longer constrained by Liam's main body or his soul bottlenecks. Now, unburdened and constantly nourished by the abundant ambient soul energy of the pagoda, the Dao seed of Fire was flourishing.","Liam's eyes glinted with a strange mix of disbelief and thrill. The Dao clone wasn't just preserving the seed, it was cultivating it faster than he ever could.","With every passing second, it absorbed not just soul energy but also latent fire-elemental mana hidden within the environment, refining itself, evolving the Dao into something even more pure and devastating.","The clone's presence became heavier, more stable. Small flickers of gold appeared along its flaming aura, signs of embryonic fire law comprehension beginning to sprout.","Liam exhaled shakily. \"It's... surpassing me.\"","The thought should have terrified him, but instead, it made him laugh again, more ragged and raw this time. Now he knew what he had to do. The path in front of him was clear now.","He had finally stepped out of the barrier that was blocking his progress! He was now free to become as powerful as he wanted!","Liam's heart beat faster as he observed the dao seed sprout into a branch. It did not stop there. The branches started multiplying, and the small seed had started to become a Dao tree right in front of his eyes.","What had once been a fragment of understanding, a single flame of insight, had now begun to root itself into the very laws of the world. He could feel it. The Fire Dao he had nurtured, broken, sacrificed, and transplanted into this soul clone was now becoming something far greater than he had ever imagined.","The tiny seed had cracked open, pushing out not just roots but branches of profound realization. Concepts began to unfurl like blooming leaves, combustion and rebirth, flame that heals, flame that consumes, flame that remembers.","Each branch represented a possible path, a flame law in embryonic form. The fire-elemental mana in the air rushed toward it like moths drawn to divine heat.","The soul clone shuddered as the process intensified, and a strange resonance passed through Liam's entire being. It wasn't painful, but it was powerful. With each new branch, the Dao Tree inside the clone became more stable, more complete.","Liam closed his eyes to focus and take in everything. He did not want to miss a single second of this progress.","Then it finally happened. All the progress and all the energy culminated in a burning pillar of Dao that shot up from his clone, extending even outside the pagoda. He had broken through.","He had finally broken through to the Transcendent realm and even reached the peak of the Transcendent realm in the blink of an eye!"]},{"number":1442,"title":"Chapter 1442: No longer shackled","paragraphs":["Liam gasped. The Transcendent realm! This was the power he had been trying to achieve for the past several months, and yet at every turn, he was met with failure. Finally, getting a piece of the soulmancer heritage helped him push past all the hurdles and step onto this new path.","Liam closed his eyes and tried to absorb everything as much as he could. He had already absorbed and accumulated countless memories about the Dao of Fire. Some of them he had made his own, and some were yet to be assimilated.","The breakthrough had also helped clear up some of the mental clogs he had in the process. If he tried to assimilate all those bits and pieces of memories again, this time his gains would be much bigger. He did not waste anymore second, closed his eyes, and dove right into it.","He had already stepped into the Transcendent realm. He had no plans to stop with just this. After stagnating for so long, he was itching to push past another breakthrough barrier. After the Transcendent realm came the Dao expert realm. He was confident he could reach here right here and now.","Meanwhile... on the outside...","A towering banner of pure Dao intent, a wildfire of spiritual authority that roared into the skies above the pagoda, was visible across the entire region.","Clouds parted violently, lightning sparked in crimson arcs, and the land itself trembled as the pillar of fire extended beyond the heavens. Every beast and cultivator within hundreds of kilometers felt it, a crushing, awe-inspiring pressure that rooted them in place.","And those who could perceive the Dao intent directly... trembled.","Because this wasn't the signature of a cultivator stepping into the Transcendent realm.","This was the signature of a being who had mastered a Flame Law and rooted it in a Dao Tree, a feat that took many centuries, if not lifetimes, to achieve.","The other alchemists froze and looked up at the phenomenon in awe. The draluras were shocked to the core. The person had reaped so much from their land's treasure that they were able to make such a breakthrough. Every single pair of draconic eyes burned with greed and envy.","They had no idea who dared to step inside their sacred pagoda, but no matter who it was, they did not plan to let that person leave the world alive.","The draluras immediately mobilized and started gathering around the pagoda. Draluras from every nook and corner of the world received the command and quickly headed over.","Within a matter of seconds, the forest outside of the pagoda became filled with the scent of blood. The draluras cleared all the monsters in the forest, not leaving even a single one behind. Bloodlust and killing intent filled the area.","In the blink of an eye, about a thousand draluras ended up gathering around the pagoda. The very forest seemed to wither under their collective aura.","From beast riders to ancestral scale elders, the entire force of the Dralura clans had answered the call, some from mountain-top thrones, others from hidden volcanic nests. All now converged on the glowing pagoda, their wings blotting out the sky","This was no longer a sacred site. It had become a war zone.","The moment the human who had stepped inside their sacred temple came out, there would be carnage!","Back inside the pagoda, Liam sat deep in meditative trance. His soul had begun to reflect the shape of the flame Dao Tree, and its branches now shimmered with threads of deeper laws. The soul clone mirrored this evolution perfectly, seated opposite him, both engulfed in golden-red light.","And just as Liam reached out to connect the deeper flame truths... the whole structure shuddered. The last bit of the soul energy left in the pagoda was stripped clean by him, and the formation of the pagoda no longer held strong.","Liam's eyes immediately flashed open in alarm, and so did his soul clone. He was not foolish enough to think that he was the strongest in the whole cosmos or even in this world.","He was still basically a beginner who had only now stepped from the Awakening rank into the Transcendent rank. It was nothing to write home about. His enemies were all a thousand times stronger than him.","He might have finally removed the hurdle stopping him from progressing further, but now he needed time to actually make that progress. He doubted he would get that time if he stayed here any longer.","Since he had pretty much accomplished every single thing he had set out to do, there was no point in staying either here or in the Green Mountain Sect any longer. Perhaps in the future, he would one day visit the sect to personally express his gratitude to the old man he had met, but now it was fucking time to run. There was no doubt about it.","Snapping out of his meditative trance, the first thing Liam did was tear up his teleportation talismans. He tried a few talismans, some to earth and some to the eternal sword palace, but none of them worked. He then remembered that lunatic woman's warning that he would not be able to teleport out of here.","Shit! He needed to get to the portal. That was the only way out of here. It was fine. He had already made backup plans for everything.","\"Seal the formation. None must escape!\"","\"Kill the intruder!\"","\"Kill! Kill! Kill!\"","\"Seize the heaven's treasure! Seize our family's treasure!\"","Just as Liam absorbed the Dao clone back into himself and activated the switch between himself and his soul clone, he felt the pagoda's sturdy ancient walls tremble and shatter.","His eyes widened in shock as he managed to get a glimpse of the army waiting to tear him apart, when his figure disappeared and reappeared somewhere else. What an astounding gathering of powerful creatures!! His body still trembled from the sheer killing intent and murderous aura in the air."]},{"number":1443,"title":"Chapter 1443: Kill the intruder!","paragraphs":["Liam shivered. The moment he reappeared in a hidden volcanic ravine far from the pagoda, he dropped to one knee, his body trembling. The afterimage of a thousand draconic eyes, glowing with murderous fury, still burned in his mind.","However, he was still not out of danger. He needed to reach the portal and get out of here and then get the hell out of the Green Mountain sect. Liam calmed down and activated Stealth. He then summoned his dao clone.","The guy couldn't exactly activate Stealth but his mana sense was a lot more powerful than Liam's. The Fire clone instantly sniffed out a couple of enemies who were pretty close to him. And they were not ordinary enemies either.","\"Two draluras.\" Liam exhaled. He had no idea how strong they were. They were most probably at least Transcendents or maybe even Dao Experts. But there was simply no way to go around them. He had to face them or at least stall them.","Liam silently summoned a few of his clones and sent them in all directions. He then rushed to the two draluras along with the fire dao clone.","The ravine's searing heat gave his Fire Dao clone a natural boost, cloaking it in an aura of hot molten lava. That would give them maybe half a second of surprise. No more.","But when Liam got a good look at both the draluras, it was immediately clear that even that small upper hand was gone.","The first dralura turned, a towering brute with molten crimson scales and a halberd that hissed with lava. The other, sleeker and leaner one had lava balls spinning around him.","Whatever slim advantage the environment granted his Fire Dao clone was meaningless now. Both enemies radiated the same affinity, only far deeper and more refined. They had most likely taken half a step into the Dao Expert realm.","This was going to be a tough fight.","The two draluras charged towards the dao clone at the same time as soon as they saw it. A wave of scorching pressure rolled out from the heavier dralura, his halberd swinging in a wide arc. Lava surged from the ground with the motion, erupting in pillars of heat that tried to cage the Dao clone.","The sleeker one moved like liquid flame, vanishing from sight and reappearing behind the dao clone. His claws sliced through the air, and the lava orbs around him pulsed with explosive force.","The Dao clone reacted instantly.","Rather than retreating or dodging, it exploded forward with reckless momentum, slamming into the heavy dralura's halberd swing. A deafening crash echoed through the volcanic ravine as molten sparks and shockwaves burst outward. Shockingly, the two draluras were pushed back.","While the draluras had refined fire affinity and combat experience, they lacked one thing Liam's clone possessed, raw destructive Dao authority. His clone didn't just wield flame. It was flame, forged through enlightenment. The dao clone's fire authority was simply purer than the two draluras'.","As the bulky dralura lunged forward with his lava-infused halberd, the Dao clone didn't dodge. Instead, it caught the weapon barehanded. The weapon hissed and sparked against its molten skin, but the clone held firm, eyes burning with unearthly calm.","In the next instant, a shockwave burst outward. The crimson-scaled brute howled in agony as his own weapon exploded in his grasp, lava shards ripping through his arm and chest. The clone followed up instantly, extending its palm and placing it on the dralura's chest.","With a low, thunderous hum, a blossom of white-hot fire burst from the dralura's core, bypassing his scales and incinerating him from the inside out. The leaner dralura recoiled in horror, but it was already too late.","The Fire Dao clone blurred forward, leaving behind trails of cinders. It split into seven afterimages and all seven struck at once. The lava orbs around the dralura detonated prematurely in a panic-triggered defense, but the clone's strike tunneled through the defense, piercing straight through the dralura's chest.","There was no time for a scream. Only a sudden silence as both enemies dropped, completely dominated in their own domain. The clone stood amidst the scorched battlefield, its molten skin dripping, breath steady.","Liam, watching from afar, exhaled sharply. Thanks to the solid foundation he had laid, it looked like his fire clone had the ability to even fight with someone of the next rank.","Liam did not waste this chance. He immediately grasped the souls of the two draluras, powerful dense souls and started processing them. He absorbed the dao clone back into him and focused as he went through the memories of the two high-level draluras.","It looked like he was mistaken about one thing. These two were still in the transcendent rank. Their extra edge had come from their innate physical superiority.","Unfortunately, the two corpses were damaged so much that none of this innate physical strength probably remained but still the two corpses were quite valuable nonetheless. Liam placed the two corpses in his storage space and then summoned his newly forged draluras.","The souls of the two draluras, though battered and cracked, still retained a dense reservoir of memories and instinct. It took him a few good minutes to do this but these minutes were well spent because it looked like these two draluras were quite knowledgeable about this world.","More importantly, they knew the ins and outs of this place and how exactly to get to the portal without attracting further attention. They remembered the terrain, the patterns of patrols, and the fastest, least-monitored paths to the portal.","Liam followed the two and quickly arrived at the main portal without any further trouble. He immediately dismissed all of his soul minions in this world and then stepped into the portal without hesitation.","On the other side, the chaotic but relatively peaceful central plaza of the Green Mountain sect buzzed with activity. Many heads turned towards him and recognized him as one of the participants of the treasure lands."]},{"number":1444,"title":"Chapter 1444: Superior","paragraphs":["Liam could immediately sense many eyes on him. Most of them were looking down at him as he probably was the first person to return from the treasure lands. But Liam did not care about these people at the moment. He was out of the fire and now he needed to get out of the frying pan too.","He had already vacated his residence and packed everything up. So there was no reason for him to linger here. He immediately took out a teleportation token when suddenly the portal flared up and more people began to appear.","Nyx was the first to step out and many gasps could be heard on her arrival. After all, the treasure lands had just opened and no one expected a powerful figure like Nyx to step out so soon. But maybe someone powerful like her had already secured something truly priceless and hence she came out? Many people began to speculate many things.","The only problem was her face. Instead of a triumphant look, her face was filled with horror and dread as he hurriedly stumbled outside. She also looked as if she had been through a lot and had only barely survived. Just as everyone wondered what was going on, Nyx started shouting at the top of her voice.","\"Sound the alarm! Call the seniors! We are under attack!\"","The entire plaza fell silent for a moment. Then chaos erupted.","\"What is she saying?\"","\"An attack?\"","\"Is the treasure realm collapsing?\"","\"No, look at her, she's terrified!\"","Sirens hidden deep within the mountain echoed out, their long, keening wails vibrating through the very bones of the Green Mountain Sect. Defensive formations shimmered to life across the sky. Elders shot into motion, and portals blinked open as higher-level powerhouses began to arrive in flashes of light.","Liam stood amid the maelstrom, eyes locked on Nyx. Her face was pale, streaked with ash and blood, her robes in tatters. This wasn't just panic. This was trauma. Something had truly gone wrong inside.","But even more troubling to Liam was the timing.","She came out barely a minute after him. That meant the attack was happening now. He watched as Nyx teleported away from the treasure lands portal and started casting all sorts of defensive barriers around it.","The other powerhouses also got the message without her having to explain and everyone looked warily at the treasure lands portal.","On the side, Liam already activated the teleportation token without hesitation. He had no interest in staying back and watching where this was all headed to. In fact, he had a pretty good idea where.","Obviously, the damned draconic beast creatures had followed him right into the Green Mountain Sect!","And he was not planning to stay back and fight them. Sure, he might gain a lot here from a large scale war like this but greediness could lead to his demise. He had finally found to way to break through and he was not going to die now.","A blinding white light covered him and the teleportation token activated without any issue. Once again many heads turned towards him. Everyone could clearly see him all ready to run. The powerhouse remained indifferent but many of the seniors and elders looked angry and disgusted.","Nyx, in particular, stared at him as if he had personally killed her entire family.","Liam did not care. No one stopped him and that's was all that mattered. The portal sputtered once again, quickly grabbing all of the attention back to itself. Just as Liam's teleportation began and the world around him started to twist and change, he could clearly see the next being that stepped out of that portal.","And it was not a disciple of the Green Mountain Sect.","The pair of draconic eyes instantly fell on Liam but it was already too late. Just as the roars of many more draconic creatures sounded, Liam was long gone. He could no longer see the Green Mountain Sect anymore or any of the chaos.","He was once again standing in a familiar system shop and it only took a moment before Tilia rushed over to him. \"Liam! Are you okay?\" The fairy did not even see him and this was the first thing she blurted out.","Liam smiled bitterly. \"I have truly worried everyone, haven't I?\"","Tilia stuck out her tongue. \"Nothing like that at all. I just don't want something to happen to my whale customer.\" She giggled.","Liam only slightly smiled. He turned to look at the spot where he had teleported to, the center of the rune as a small feeling of guilt appeared within him.","Normally he wouldn't care. He would just be glad that he was not knee deep in shit but this time it felt a little different. It was not that he cared about the sect or anyone in the sect. It was more about that old man.","He was grateful to the old man. It was not like they were master and disciple or anything like that. It was just a small interaction they had which barely lasted for a second and yet Liam couldn't deny that he owed that old man something.","Maybe that was why this particular escape left a bitter taste in his mouth. He had brought a disaster upon the sect and yet had ran away from there as if none of it mattered to him. It did not and in some ways, it did.","Liam closed eyes and tried to settle himself. The draluras were powerful. There was no doubt about it but the sect wasn't helpless either. Both the sides were powerhouses. He, on the other hand, wasn't in any condition to help them even if he stayed back.","The chances of his being useful was extremely small. There was a bigger chance for one of the big guys to directly one shot him.","Liam let out a sigh. Even though he could justify his actions again and again, he couldn't deny the small guilt. He silently resolved to help out the Green Mountain Sect in the future if he got another opportunity to do so.","After that, he did not dwell on it anymore. \"Let's go. I have a lot to discuss with you.\" He smiled at Tilia and the two of them started walking out of the system shop portal room."]},{"number":1445,"title":"Chapter 1445: Under attack!","paragraphs":["\"Fire attuned worlds, huh?\" Tilia tapped her fingers on the table. \"There are indeed some worlds like that but they are extremely harsh. The well known ones at least.\"","Hmmm... Liam frowned. An extremely harsh environment might not be the best for what he was after. In an extremely harsh environment there won't be many living beings and souls for him to harvest. It would only delay his progress.","Sure, he could always make his fire clone sit there and meditate and gain enlightenment the natural way but that would simply be a waste of his skillset and abilities.","Seeing his expression, Tilia again suggested. \"There are some alternatives. I am sure there are more worlds with the environment you are looking for. These would be more suitable for training. Its just that these worlds are often under the control of other empires.\"","\"If you give me some time, I can try to gather more information on these worlds. I do have to warn you that it might take a while. These secrets will not be easily shared. Powerful clans consider these resources as their top secret and hoard them without giving access to anyone else. Sometimes not even their closest allies.\"","\"Our world is already hidden and we do not have any faction backing us. I will try my best to obtain the information through back channels but I am really out of my depth here.\"","\"That's fine.\" Liam nodded. \"Don't worry about it. You do not have to waste your time on this. I have some other sources where I can look for these worlds.\"","Without hesitation, Liam activated his teleportation token for the Eternal Sword Palace and entered the purple world. His status there was no less than his status in the Green Mountain Sect. He was able to easily obtain information and to his surprise he was even able to obtain some tokens of entrance to these worlds.","Of course, he had to pay the merits for these things through pill concoction which he finished in the next couple of days. Soon, it was time for the big move.","Liam summoned his fire dao clone and looked at his counterpart from top to bottom. \"I guess you are as ready as you will ever be.\" He smiled bitterly. He then summoned Luna from his soul space.","\"Master! I don't want to go~\" The little fox immediately whined but Liam put on a stern expression. \"Its not good for you to be always cooped up inside. Don't you want to come out and play?\"","\"But I want to play with you master~ not him~ nyaaa~\"","Liam chuckled. \"Are you a cat or a fox?\"","In the end, Luna reluctantly agreed. Liam gave the teleportation token to his clone, and Luna snatched it from him. \"I will activate it. He might screw it up!\"","Liam was speechless. He wanted to clarify to the little monster that the clone was also him, just the same, but he decided to let the little beast have her way. Why ruin a good surprise?","A minute later, a portal shimmered open, rippling with threads of violet flame. Luna's tails stood on end as she nuzzled with Liam one more time before jumping into the portal. The dao clone then exchanged a nod with Liam before stepping in as well.","When the token pulsed, the fire dao clone and Luna vanished into the blazing void. The connection between them thinned until it was a faint ember at the edge of Liam's consciousness.","He exhaled, letting his mind drift through that fading bond, feeling the oppressive heat, the roar of molten rivers, the endless red dunes of a sun-scorched world. The two of them had already spotted their first prey.","A red-skinned salamander. The beast looked ordinary, but that was only for a second. As soon as it sensed a new presence, the beast lit up like fireworks, a terrifying aura rolling off of it. Luna wouldn't have it. In turn, she unleashed her own terrifying aura, making the salamander take a step back.","Liam's clone, on the other hand, silently lifted his hand and sent out a blast of attack.","The blast wasn't grand or ostentatious, just a flicker of condensed fire essence, refined to perfection. It streaked across the air like a needle of sunlight, piercing through the salamander's defensive flames before the beast could react.","A dull thud echoed through the wasteland as the creature's molten body collapsed into the sand, steam rising in lazy curls. The clone's crimson eyes didn't waver. One hand stretched out, and a faint stream of fiery soul essence drifted toward him, vanishing into his palm.","Luna's tails bristled in delight. \"Hmph! That's what happens when you glare at us!\" she declared, puffing up her fur as if she had done all the work. The clone didn't respond. His focus had already shifted to the next prey.","Liam sensed the antics of the two through his connection and chuckled. That clone would now walk through storms of fire where even metal melted like wax, seeking to master the flame laws faster than any mortal could. Hopefully, Luna would gain something as well. Her growth had pretty much stagnated.","However, he couldn't let the two of them have all the fun. He stretched his hands, let out a yawn, and then sat down. He then pulled up some old system contracts that he hadn't bothered to check in a while.","Naturally, there was a reason for it. Sometimes it was best not to suffocate some people and allow them to grow on their own terms. But that did not mean he had completely forgotten about them. Someone out in the vast wide multiverse owed him something and it was now finally time to collect.","\"Now... where is that shady guy?\" With a smile, Liam tugged at the system contract of an old buddy, a buddy who excelled at divination. A buddy whose only flaw was that anything he divined revealed the exact opposite of what the divination result should have been.","\"Where are you, my old friend?\""]},{"number":1446,"title":"Chapter 1446: Where are you, my old friend?","paragraphs":["The system contract trembled as Liam pulled on it, like a spider thread plucked in the dark. Somewhere far away in the multiverse, a man sneezed violently. At the same instant, a crystal ball shattered, a divination array exploded into smoke, and a very tired cultivator stared at the smoking ruins of his workshop with dead eyes.","\"I knew it,\" he muttered hoarsely. \"I knew I should've lied low today.\"","\"Master, is everything alright?\"","\"Master, how could the divination array explode like this?\"","\"Master's divinations are always perfect. This is... this is... impossible!\"","Several beauties rushed towards him, their silk sleeves fluttering as they crowded around the ruined table. One supported his arm, another hurriedly wiped soot from his cheek, while a third stared at the shattered crystal ball with her eyes wide.","The man opened his mouth, then closed it again. His lips twitched. How was he supposed to explain this? He forced out a hollow laugh. \"It's nothing... merely an old friend clearing his throat.\" The beauties froze. Old friend? What old friend? Their master had never mentioned anyone like that before.","But it looked like their master had no mood to chit-chat with them today like he always did. He seemed extremely flustered and in a hurry to go somewhere. Unfortunately, before he could flee, the world twisted. Space folded inward like a closing fist, and he was yanked bodily through a screaming tunnel of light.","\"Amitabah!\" Only a scream was left behind as the person disappeared and reappeared. He landed face-first on cold stone, robes tangled, dignity in shambles. \"Amitabah... \" The man scrambled up, wild hair tied with talismans, eyes darting in every direction, filled with horror and dread as if expecting a terrible nightmarish creature.","\"Please let it not be him. Please let it not be him.\"","And once again... it looked like the goddess of fate had decided to fuck with him today.","As he turned around, cold sweat trickling down his forehead, the familiar face he absolutely dreaded came into view, seated far too casually for someone who had just ripped him across the multiverse like a misplaced bookmark.","Liam rested one arm on his knee, fingers loosely interlaced, his expression calm to the point of being infuriating.","The diviner's knees nearly gave out. \"A-Amitabah...\" he croaked again, this time sounding less like a prayer and more like a plea bargain. In this vast, endless multiverse, how did this bastard once again find him?","Liam tilted his head slightly and smiled. \"Relax,\" he said mildly. \"Why do you look so stressed, my old friend? Aren't you happy to see me after all this time? Or have you forgotten me already?\"","The monk laughed awkwardly, trying to salvage the situation. \"Ah ha ha ha. Of course not, master. Why would I not be happy to see you? This poor soul is extremely indebted to you. Our karmic threads are so tightly intertwined that even the heavens get headaches trying to untangle them.\"","He clasped his hands together in a hurried salute, bowing a little too deeply, a little too fast. \"This humble monk merely did not expect such an... auspicious reunion today. My joy was simply too overwhelming, that's all.\"","His smile twitched at the edges, eyes flicking around as if searching for an escape route that definitely did not exist.","\"Cut the crap already.\" Liam chuckled coldly. \"Listen well. Everything that happened in the past can stay in the past. I have no interest in forcing servitude on you. If you'd like, I can even release you from the system contract you signed.\"","\"Amitabah!\" The monk's eyes instantly widened in shock. \"Your kindness knows no bounds. This monk did not expect this old friend to be so generous. I have indeed made a grave mistake. Please forgive this poor soul.\"","He bowed again, this time so deeply his forehead nearly struck the stone. \"This monk has reflected deeply on his past arrogance,\" he said with solemn sincerity, voice trembling just enough to sound convincing.","\"If Senior Brother is willing to sever the contract, then this life, no, ten lives of accumulated merit still wouldn't be enough to repay such benevolence.\" He straightened slowly, then froze, as if a delayed realization had struck him.","\"...But,\" he added carefully, \"a man as magnanimous as Senior Brother Liam would not summon this poor soul across the multiverse merely to offer freedom. This monk dares to ask, what task does Senior Brother wish me to perform before this great kindness is bestowed?\"","Liam smiled. \"Nothing too big. Just a bunch of small favors. A handful of divinations. Path to a handful of harmless places. Nothing too big at all.\"","The monk's face went stiff. His throat bobbed as he swallowed. Anyone who knew Liam even a little understood that nothing too big translated to world-shaking consequences for everyone except him. Still, the monk forced a smile so serene it could have passed for enlightenment.","\"Amitabah... of course, anything for you. A handful of divinations is nothing to this poor soul. The thing is... this poor soul is in the middle of a karmic yatra at the moment. If you can give me a few decades, I will be ready to assist you with my mind eye sharp and focused.\"","The monk spoke the words quickly, smoothly, like a well-practiced mantra, already preparing the excuse to sprout wings and flee across three layers of reality the moment Liam blinked.","Liam didn't blink. Instead, he sighed, long and patient, as if indulging a child who still believed time was negotiable. \"Decades?\" he repeated softly. \"That's not gonna work for me. How about right now?\"","\"But Amitabah... I am in the middle of a karmic yatra! My powers are absolutely horrendous at the moment. I am utterly useless. I will only be a burden to you, especially if you ask me to accompany you to any of these places.\"","Liam chuckled. \"Don't worry about it. I will protect you. And if the danger is too much, I wouldn't go there either. You really have nothing to fear.\" Liam smiled again, a very calm and gentle smile. However, that only made the monk shiver from top to bottom.","He gulped as he quickly did a mental divination for his fate for the next few months.","Glorious heavenly light.","For any other divination master, this would mean extremely good luck, best luck, or even heaven-defying luck. However, the monk's face only contorted into a constipated one on seeing this prediction.","Yup, he was fucked. Fully and truly fucked."]},{"number":1447,"title":"Chapter 1447: Amitabah!","paragraphs":["A few hours passed by. The monk slowly opened his eyes again. No miracle had occurred. There was no heavenly intervention. No sudden enlightenment that would save him from this disaster.","Liam was still sitting there. He was still smiling and still waiting.","\"...Senior Brother,\" the monk said carefully, voice unusually dry. \"Before we proceed... this humble one would like to confirm something very small.\"","Liam raised an eyebrow. \"Go on.\"","\"Do I really have to come with you? Isn't it better if you go by yourself? I will only drag you down.\"","Liam chuckled and remained silent.","The monk inwardly muttered a few curses and once again tried his best. However, no matter how many times he divined, the result was the same. His spectrum of fortune had somehow shrunk, always showing the same single black outcome.","He had never heard of such a phenomenon occurring in the entire history of divination. Perhaps one world might be gravely dangerous and show an ominous divination score, but every single time, obtaining the same result?","Death followed this guy everywhere he went!","Liam was basically a walking disaster!","If he ended up following him, then for sure, he was going to die a miserable dog death pretty soon. Nope. Nope. Nope. He was not ready to die yet, dammit! He was only just now truly starting to enjoy his life. What he needed to do now was somehow get back to his temple and his followers!","Fuck this bastard.","The monk gnashed his teeth and spent a few more hours trying to find a way out of his predicament. Unfortunately, every road led to the same destination.","Death.","No matter how many techniques he used, no matter how many futures he observed, the result remained unchanged.","Death.","Death.","Death.","Death.","\"Fuck me.\" He cursed and racked his brain. This bastard's bad luck was simply too strong for him to deal with it all by himself. He needed someone else. He needed a backup. A bright smile suddenly appeared on the monk's face as a plan formed in his mind.","He inwardly praised his genius for coming up with something so amazing and devious and opened his mouth when suddenly the space in front of them rippled.","\"Someone is teleporting here.\" Liam immediately became alert.","The next second, a person stepped out of the spatial distortion, which made the monk's eyes widen in shock. \"How... why... why are you here?\"","Even Liam was utterly dumbfounded.","Standing in front of them was none other than the Oracle, Kaden. The same person whom the monk had wanted to call just a second ago. However, he hadn't actually called him. He only thought about it, and the person was already here!","In the end, it was exactly what he wanted, but this only made everything so much worse. Why was this problematic guy here, and that too, he had come here all on his own?! Liam did not look like he used the system contract to force-teleport the guy, and yet he was here.","\"How are you, Liam Chang? It's been a while...\" Kaden smiled.","Liam smiled in return, coldness seeping into his gaze.","\"You do not have to concern yourself with me. I am merely here because my path led me here. We have unfinished karmic debt between us, and fate tells me that the time is nigh for us to come together again.\"","The monk opened and closed his mouth speechlessly. This person willingly came here? Alright, this would only make everything that much simpler for him. Unfortunately, it looked like he had once again assumed things too soon.","The very next moment, Kaden sat down, a golden circle appearing around him. \"Give me some time, and I will decipher what fate has in store for us.\"","He did not bother explaining anything else, and to the monk's surprise, Liam also did not ask him anything further. As if that was that, Liam once again turned to pay attention to the monk.","\"Ah... fuck me sideways...\" The monk let out a sigh and accepted his fate. \"One second, senior brother... I think I know where we need to go first.\"","....","A few days later...","AAAHHHHH!","A scream resounded as a chubby man in plain white robes trembled from top to bottom. \"Not me. Not me. Not me. Get him, dammit. He is the one hunting you.\"","Standing in front of him was a huge wyvern about to smack the shit out of him, but the very next second, a volley of attacks fell onto the massive beast. One after another, powerful blows struck the beast, and even though it felt impossible, the beast, just like the ones before, dropped dead in the end.","Liam casually sat down and extracted the soul, immediately converting it into a soul minion. \"This is the tenth one. Not bad.\"","For days, they had been jumping from one world to another, all with the promise of holding something potentially fate-changing. However, it had simply been one strong beast after another.","The monk thought that he was done for in the very first world, but somehow, they were still standing. The beasts were clearly a level above them, and yet the bastard somehow managed to dominate them in the end. He just couldn't understand how.","\"Senior brother, what technique did you use? That wyvern was on the verge of ascending. Yet you managed to easily subdue it. Could it be you are targeting its soul?\"","Liam smiled but did not answer him. \"Where are we headed next?\"","The monk cursed inwardly and sat down, once again using his skill. An hour later, the whole process was over, and they had a set of new coordinates. \"Senior brother, shouldn't we take a break first? I feel like if I had some more time, I could divine something truly terrifying! How about we go back and see what that other guy is up to. Let me tell you. That guy is up to no good. We need to keep a close watch on him. Trust me. I have a real knack for these things.\""]},{"number":1448,"title":"Chapter 1448: This is unfair","paragraphs":["Liam looked at the monk and listened to him, only to shake his head at the end. \"No.\"","The monk's smile froze. \"...No?\"","\"No break,\" Liam said calmly. \"And we're not going back.\"","The monk's shoulders slumped instantly. Of course. Why would fate ever be kind? \"Amitabah,\" he muttered and sighed dramatically, which Liam ignored.","\"Give me the coordinates.\"","The monk hesitated for a moment. Then sighed again. He extended his hand, and a faint ripple of light appeared, forming a set of symbols in the air. A teleportation circle as well promptly appeared, and just like that, the hunting resumed again.","A few more days later... a similar scene repeated again.","\"Aaaaahhhh!\"","A loud scream tore through the air as the monk was dragged across a jagged stretch of blackened ground, his robes caught on something that was very much alive and very much trying to eat him.","\"Senior brother! Senior brother! Please! Please! I will really try my best next time. Please save me this once. Aioooo! I am dying here! Please!\"","A massive, tar-like limb rose from the ground, stretching unnaturally as it chased after him. The surface of the land rippled like liquid shadow, countless eyes opening and closing beneath the black crust.","The monk tripped and rolled, crashing face-first into the ground. \"Amitabah!\" The limb slammed down right where his head had been a split second earlier.","Liam stood a short distance away, completely untouched. He casually sidestepped another shadowy tendril, as if avoiding rain. \"Why are you panicking so much?\" he asked calmly. \"It's not that dangerous.\"","The monk froze for a second. Then slowly turned his head. \"Not that-\" He choked as another tendril brushed past him, missing his face by an inch. \"-dangerous?!\"","Behind him, the ground split open. Another dozen tentacles erupted from the ground. Just as everything was about to turn disastrous, a thousand swords, no even more appeared, filling the air like a storm of light. A blinding golden brightness flooded everywhere and when the monk was able to see again, the black thing was no longer alive.","\"Amitabah...\" The monk collapsed flat on his back, arms spread out, staring blankly at the sky. When he woke up again, Liam was still there, sitting in front of him with a gentlemanly smile on his face.","\"You demon!\" The monk shrieked. Realizing that he had spoken out loud, he quickly corrected himself. \"Haaa... Ha.... I didn't mean you. I thought we were still back there, senior brother.\"","Standing near him, Alex chuckled. \"Sure, you definitely did not call my husband a demon.\"","\"Of course not.\" The monk had a completely serious face.","\"Right. I almost forgot how shameless you were.\" Alex scoffed and then stopped paying him attention, turning back to Liam. \"Are you going back out there again?\"","Before Liam could answer, the monk quickly blurted out. \"No. No.\" He couldn't care less about how Alex treated him. All he cared about was getting out of this thing alive. \"Senior brother, even I cannot continuously divine one fate encounter after another. You have to give me some time.\"","Liam showed no expression on his face so he quickly added. \"My accuracy depends on it. Just give me some time and see for yourself. You will definitely get better results.\"","Liam still did not look convinced and the monk started sweating. Luckily for him, another voice interrupted them. \"Give him the time he needs. I have something for you.\"","Everyone turned around to see Kaden standing there with a scroll in his hand. \"Your fate is changing in exactly an hour. Take this and go. Your life and death will depend on what happens in the next hour.\"","Alex rolled her eyes. \"That's awfully convenient. If Liam came back two days later, you'd still hand him the same thing and deliver the same rehearsed lines, wouldn't you?\"","Kaden smiled. \"Miss Alex, you don't believe in what I do, do you?\"","Alex did not say anything.","Giving a glance at the monk, Kaden continued. \"Perhaps you have only met people who did not give you much reason to believe.\"","The monk stiffened.","Alex crossed her arms. \"Or maybe I just don't believe people who speak in vague riddles and call it wisdom.\"","Kaden smiled faintly, completely unbothered. \"Doubt is natural. It is also... predictable.\"","Alex raised an eyebrow. \"Oh?\"","\"Yes,\" Kaden said calmly. \"People doubt what they cannot see. They mock what they cannot understand. And when the result arrives...\" His gaze shifted slightly toward Liam. \"...they call it fate.\"","\"Liam coming here today, right now, right this moment is fate.\"","\"Sure.\" Alex scoffed again. She placed a kiss on Liam's cheek and prepared to leave, not wanting to disturb him anymore.","However, before she could leave, Kaden suddenly looked startled. \"Wait, Miss Alex. What if I tell you that our conversation right now is also fate?\"","Alex froze in her steps.","\"What do you mean?\" Liam asked.","\"You should take her with you this time. Trust me.\"","\"Hmmm?\" Liam raised a brow. If Kaden handed him a set of coordinates, he did not mind going there and checking things out but as for as trusting him went... \"I will think about it..\" Liam replied.","Kaden shook his head solemnly. \"There is no time to think about it. Leave now and leave with her. This is all I can do to help you. The rest depends on you.\"","He handed over the scroll to Liam and then right in front of the monk's eyes, he teleported and left.","\"what the fuck? Senior brother! That bastard left?! He left just like that?!\" The monk started freaking out. \"How could he leave just like that? Both of us are your slaves! We are supposed to serve you for all eternity! He can't leave yet! Come on, senior brother. This is bullshit!\"","Liam ignored the monk as he stared at the scroll in his hands. It was a teleportation scroll. He took a minute and closed his eyes. When he opened his eyes again, there was no more hesitation. \"Alex, let's go.\""]},{"number":1449,"title":"Chapter 1449: This too is fate","paragraphs":["Liam looked at the monk and listened to him, only to shake his head at the end. \"No.\"","The monk’s smile froze. \"...No?\"","\"No break,\" Liam said calmly. \"And we’re not going back.\"","The monk’s shoulders slumped instantly. Of course. Why would fate ever be kind? \"Amitabah,\" he muttered and sighed dramatically, which Liam ignored.","\"Give me the coordinates.\"","The monk hesitated for a moment. Then sighed again. He extended his hand, and a faint ripple of light appeared, forming a set of symbols in the air. A teleportation circle as well promptly appeared, and just like that, the hunting resumed again.","A few more days later... a similar scene repeated again.","\"Aaaaahhhh!\"","A loud scream tore through the air as the monk was dragged across a jagged stretch of blackened ground, his robes caught on something that was very much alive and very much trying to eat him.","\"Senior brother! Senior brother! Please! Please! I will really try my best next time. Please save me this once. Aioooo! I am dying here! Please!\"","A massive, tar-like limb rose from the ground, stretching unnaturally as it chased after him. The surface of the land rippled like liquid shadow, countless eyes opening and closing beneath the black crust.","The monk tripped and rolled, crashing face-first into the ground. \"Amitabah!\" The limb slammed down right where his head had been a split second earlier.","Liam stood a short distance away, completely untouched. He casually sidestepped another shadowy tendril, as if avoiding rain. \"Why are you panicking so much?\" he asked calmly. \"It’s not that dangerous.\"","The monk froze for a second. Then slowly turned his head. \"Not that-\" He choked as another tendril brushed past him, missing his face by an inch. \"-dangerous?!\"","Behind him, the ground split open. Another dozen tentacles erupted from the ground. Just as everything was about to turn disastrous, a thousand swords, no even more appeared, filling the air like a storm of light. A blinding golden brightness flooded everywhere and when the monk was able to see again, the black thing was no longer alive.","\"Amitabah...\" The monk collapsed flat on his back, arms spread out, staring blankly at the sky. When he woke up again, Liam was still there, sitting in front of him with a gentlemanly smile on his face.","\"You demon!\" The monk shrieked. Realizing that he had spoken out loud, he quickly corrected himself. \"Haaa... Ha.... I didn’t mean you. I thought we were still back there, senior brother.\"","Standing near him, Alex chuckled. \"Sure, you definitely did not call my husband a demon.\"","\"Of course not.\" The monk had a completely serious face.","\"Right. I almost forgot how shameless you were.\" Alex scoffed and then stopped paying him attention, turning back to Liam. \"Are you going back out there again?\"","Before Liam could answer, the monk quickly blurted out. \"No. No.\" He couldn’t care less about how Alex treated him. All he cared about was getting out of this thing alive. \"Senior brother, even I cannot continuously divine one fate encounter after another. You have to give me some time.\"","Liam showed no expression on his face so he quickly added. \"My accuracy depends on it. Just give me some time and see for yourself. You will definitely get better results.\"","Liam still did not look convinced and the monk started sweating. Luckily for him, another voice interrupted them. \"Give him the time he needs. I have something for you.\"","Everyone turned around to see Kaden standing there with a scroll in his hand. \"Your fate is changing in exactly an hour. Take this and go. Your life and death will depend on what happens in the next hour.\"","Alex rolled her eyes. \"That’s awfully convenient. If Liam came back two days later, you’d still hand him the same thing and deliver the same rehearsed lines, wouldn’t you?\"","Kaden smiled. \"Miss Alex, you don’t believe in what I do, do you?\"","Alex did not say anything.","Giving a glance at the monk, Kaden continued. \"Perhaps you have only met people who did not give you much reason to believe.\"","The monk stiffened.","Alex crossed her arms. \"Or maybe I just don’t believe people who speak in vague riddles and call it wisdom.\"","Kaden smiled faintly, completely unbothered. \"Doubt is natural. It is also... predictable.\"","Alex raised an eyebrow. \"Oh?\"","\"Yes,\" Kaden said calmly. \"People doubt what they cannot see. They mock what they cannot understand. And when the result arrives...\" His gaze shifted slightly toward Liam. \"...they call it fate.\"","\"Liam coming here today, right now, right this moment is fate.\"","\"Sure.\" Alex scoffed again. She placed a kiss on Liam’s cheek and prepared to leave, not wanting to disturb him anymore.","However, before she could leave, Kaden suddenly looked startled. \"Wait, Miss Alex. What if I tell you that our conversation right now is also fate?\"","Alex froze in her steps.","\"What do you mean?\" Liam asked.","\"You should take her with you this time. Trust me.\"","\"Hmmm?\" Liam raised a brow. If Kaden handed him a set of coordinates, he did not mind going there and checking things out but as for as trusting him went... \"I will think about it..\" Liam replied.","Kaden shook his head solemnly. \"There is no time to think about it. Leave now and leave with her. This is all I can do to help you. The rest depends on you.\"","He handed over the scroll to Liam and then right in front of the monk’s eyes, he teleported and left.","\"what the fuck? Senior brother! That bastard left?! He left just like that?!\" The monk started freaking out. \"How could he leave just like that? Both of us are your slaves! We are supposed to serve you for all eternity! He can’t leave yet! Come on, senior brother. This is bullshit!\"","Liam ignored the monk as he stared at the scroll in his hands. It was a teleportation scroll. He took a minute and closed his eyes. When he opened his eyes again, there was no more hesitation. \"Alex, let’s go.\""]},{"number":1450,"title":"Chapter 1450: Seeing her again","paragraphs":["The scroll in Liam’s hand ignited. Space tore open before him, forming a stable, glowing passage. Without hesitation, Liam stepped through. Alex followed, and the portal snapped shut behind them.","The moment the world stabilized, a violent wave of demonic energy slammed into them.","Liam narrowed his eyes.","They had appeared in the middle of a battlefield.","An enormous army of demons stretched across the land ahead, while beyond them stood an equally vast force of vampires. The two armies were already locked in combat, turning the entire region into a sea of blood, fire, and shattered earth.","Millions of demons surged forward beneath black banners, their bodies covered in scales, horns, claws, and burning demonic markings. Some towered like giants, while others flew overhead on leathery wings, raining dark flames onto the battlefield.","Facing them were the vampires. They moved with terrifying speed. Figures dressed in crimson and black flashed between the demonic ranks, tearing through armor with claws and blades. Blood-red energy filled the sky as thousands of vampires transformed into enormous bats, mist, or monstrous winged forms before diving back into the battle.","The sounds of fighting were deafening. Every few seconds, another section of the battlefield vanished beneath a blast powerful enough to flatten mountains.","Alex acted fast and immediately tried to put barriers around them, but it was useless. This was not a place where she could matter.","These were not ordinary demons or vampires. Even the weakest soldiers possessed considerable strength, while powerful auras could be sensed everywhere. Several figures fighting high above the battlefield radiated enough pressure that the space around them constantly distorted.","Then a thunderous roar shook the heavens.","\"Crimson filth! Today your bloodline ends!\"","A gigantic demon descended from the clouds, wielding a black axe large enough to cleave a fortress apart. Opposite him, a pale man wearing an elegant crimson coat floated calmly in the air.","The vampire smiled. \"You’ve been saying that for three thousand years.\" His crimson eyes flashed. The blood covering thousands of corpses below suddenly rose into the air. It gathered behind him.","A vast crimson ocean formed across the sky.","Alex stared upward. She had never seen something like this before. The mere presence of the attack was enough to put pressure on her.","The vampire raised one hand. The entire ocean of blood transformed into countless spears. Then he brought his hand down. The sky turned red.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Thousands of demons vanished beneath the barrage.","The demon general roared and swung his axe, releasing a wave of black energy that tore through the blood spears and continued straight toward the vampire army. The earth split open beneath it.","Liam and Alex were standing directly in its path. Alex’s expression changed. They couldn’t possibly handle something like this.","One blood spear was coming straight for them. Pressure exploded. There was blood everywhere. Alex could only attempt in vain to block the attack before her barrier was shattered.","\"Liam!\" She shouted just as the blood spear was about to decimate both of them. However, at the very last moment, the spear was stopped mid-air, and it collapsed and exploded as if it had hit something.","Alex stood with her mouth wide open. She quickly focused all of her mana sense to understand the situation and finally she saw it. The two of them were in fact not open and exposed. There was a thick misty barrier surrounding them.","She gulped as she opened and closed her mouth. She then turned towards Liam whose eyes were now misty white. All around him mist had gathered and though it seemed feeble and about to disturb, none of the attacks could even come close to this mist.","A smile bloomed on Alex’s face. In all this chaos, she had forgotten. She might be surrounded by monsters all around, but the person standing next to her was the biggest monster of all.","She silently stepped back and started observing. Her combat skills were useless here. Even her tactical skills were useless here, but observing something like this on a grand scale was a heaven sent opportunity by itself. She calmed herself and focused on her dao and her training, no longer bothered by the death and destruction piled up all around her.","Liam also did the same thing. He was strong here, in the midst of a battleground full of dead souls wasting away, but he did not want to go all out just yet. He was only slowly siphoning and using soul energy without inhaling everything in sight.","This was because things did not make sense just yet. This was a grand battle between demons and vampires, but what were they doing here? Why did that guy send him here? Was this all a trap after all?","Even as Liam thought about it, suddenly something stood out. Back on Earth, vampires had shown up right after the apocalypse. Could these vampires have anything to do with the vampires back on Earth?","Liam tried to gather some information through the memories of the vampire souls. He slowly manipulated one soul after another, harvesting one at a time. But it was of no use. The vampires and demons falling into his hands were lower-tier soldiers. They were strong, no doubt, but they weren’t important enough to know anything.","Liam did not rush. He couldn’t afford to make any mistakes here. A small slip and he would instantly be found out. There were powerhouses far stronger than him all around him. This was not some place he could mess around without consequences. Staying here every second was a risk in itself.","But Liam waited. He trusted that man and his skills. So he waited.","Time slipped by quickly, and by now he had gathered hundreds of thousands of vampire and demonic souls. Liam continued waiting and observing. In the meantime, the tide of the battle had quietly changed. In the beginning, the vampires appeared more powerful and even looked as if they were going to slaughter the demonic army in a one-sided battle.","However, right now things did not look so good for the vampires. The demons slowly took the upper hand in the fight.","Was this the message? Was this the warning? Were the demons about to invade Earth?","Liam mulled over many possibilities when suddenly something unexpected happened. A divine brilliance erupted in the battleground. In the midst of the fight between the demons and the vampires, a third party unexpectedly arrived.","Liam froze in shock. Alex shuddered.","When the Oracle first asked Liam to take Alex with him, he had made some guesses, and this was one of them, but he never did think it would actually end up becoming true.","Arriving on the battlefield one after another were divine priestesses and paladins. More shockingly, five heavenly figures descended. Amidst those five figures was the silhouette of someone Liam recognized immediately. His expression changed.","No fucking way.","Standing beneath the descending pillars of divine light, clad in pristine white cloth and surrounded by a halo of golden radiance, was none other than Mia."]},{"number":1451,"title":"Chapter 1451: The blood court and the celestial court","paragraphs":["Liam stared at her. It was definitely her. The same Mia who had once stood beside him. The same Mia who had disappeared without a trace. But it was also not her. Just like before, she was someone else.","The woman descending from the heavens looked exactly like Mia, but the aura surrounding her was completely unfamiliar. Divine energy rolled off her in terrifying waves, each pulse causing the demonic energy covering the battlefield to hiss and retreat.","Even from this distance, Liam could feel it. She was strong. Far stronger than the Mia he remembered.","Beside him, Alex had stopped breathing. \"Mia...\"","Liam glanced at her. Alex’s face had gone completely pale. Her earlier calm had disappeared, and she looked shaken. \"What the hell is she doing here? Why is she here? Why didn’t she come back?\"","Liam silently held her hand. \"Wait. We need to wait.\"","He turned his attention back to the sky.","The arrival of the divine forces had completely changed the battlefield.","The demons who had been pushing forward moments ago abruptly stopped. The vampires also pulled back. Even the two monstrous figures who had been trying to kill each other earlier separated without hesitation.","For the first time since Liam arrived, the demons and vampires seemed to agree on something. Neither side was happy to see the newcomers.","The five figures descended slowly. Mia stood among them, but she wasn’t at the center. That position belonged to a tall man dressed in flowing golden robes. His long silver hair fell loosely behind him, and a radiant golden crown floated several inches above his head.","Two armored men stood to his right. Mia and another woman stood to his left. All five possessed overwhelming auras. But the silver-haired man was different.","Liam’s mist thickened around himself and Alex. \"Don’t use your mana sense on them,\" he said quietly. \"We need to stay hidden. Otherwise, we could lose Mia forever.\"","Alex immediately understood. She nodded and suppressed her aura.","Liam knew that this battle, this event meant something, but he still couldn’t figure out what. Were they here to rescue Mia? That seemed impossible considering the players on the battlefield now. He couldn’t even fathom what rank these people were currently. Dao Grandmasters? Dao Kings? Or perhaps even higher?","Above them, the silver-haired man surveyed the battlefield. His expression was one of complete indifference.","Thousands of corpses littered the ground. Rivers of blood flowed through enormous cracks. Mountains had been shattered. Millions of soldiers stood ready to tear one another apart. Yet the man looked at all of it as though he were staring at insects fighting in the dirt.","Then his gaze shifted toward the demon army. \"So many years...\" His voice wasn’t loud. Yet somehow, every living creature on the battlefield heard him. \"...and your kind still hasn’t learned its place.\"","The gigantic demon wielding the black axe slowly turned toward him. The demon’s face twisted. \"Celestial bastard.\" Dark flames erupted from his body.","Boom!","The ground beneath him collapsed for miles. \"You dare come here?\"","The silver-haired man smiled. \"Why wouldn’t I?\" His gaze moved toward the vampire army. The vampire in the crimson coat was no longer smiling.","In fact, Liam noticed something interesting. The vampire looked worried. The vampire slowly wiped blood from his cheek. \"Three thousand years without showing your faces,\" he said. \"And suddenly the Celestial Court sends five Archons.\"","The silver-haired man ignored him. Behind him, the divine army moved. Thousands of paladins simultaneously slammed their weapons against their shields.","Boom!","The sound shook the battlefield. The priestesses raised their staffs. Golden formations appeared across the heavens. Within seconds, half the sky was covered in enormous divine runes.","And the war began again.","Only this time, there were three sides. Divine light crashed downward. Dark flames surged upward. Blood filled the heavens. The entire world seemed to explode.","Liam’s soul mist trembled. His eyes brightened. Soul energy filled the battleground as the carnage once again began. Even though he was only slowly siphoning souls, the number of new souls in his possession had already crossed a million.","He couldn’t focus on other things anymore. Memories of the souls flooded his mind, and dao insights started filling him up. He already possessed a partially formed demonic dao core and a divine dao core. And now a blood dao core also appeared.","These dao cores started rapidly developing. Every bit of experience and insight gathered by the fallen souls belonged to him now.","This place was insane.","Everywhere he looked, beings who had spent centuries, some even millennia, cultivating their respective Daos were dying by the thousands. Their bodies were destroyed, but their experiences remained etched into their souls.","And Liam was taking all of it.","Boom! His power exploded exponentially. It was growing at a ridiculous pace, but the familiar problem showed up soon enough. His soul was a lot stronger now. His body was a lot stronger now. His mind was definitely a lot stronger now. Still, the problem remained. He simply couldn’t handle anything beyond the transcendent rank.","Despite an abundance of souls all around him, he was forced to stop harvesting them. The last time this happened, he had found the mysterious soul thread, which helped him create a soul avatar and push past this hurdle.","And now he was once again back in the same place. He needed another soul thread. Otherwise, he simply wouldn’t be able to move forward.","Liam gritted his teeth. Pain flared up. Unwillingness filled his heart. The battle around him was not a normal occurrence. This kind of opportunity would not come again. But he was once again pushed back to a useless and vulnerable state, permanently relying on soul threads.","Running into a soul thread was a fortuitous event. If he had to count on something like that to once again become stronger, then his path ended here.","Liam refused to accept that. There had to be another way.","He had already done it once. The soul thread had allowed him to create the soul avatar, but that didn’t necessarily mean a soul thread was the only way to do it. Perhaps he had been looking at the problem backward all this time.","Liam closed his eyes. The battlefield disappeared. The deafening explosions faded into the background. The screams of millions became distant. Even Mia temporarily vanished from his thoughts.","His attention turned inward. His soul avatar floated silently within his soul space. Could he possibly create another soul avatar like this even without the soul thread? With all of this soul energy freely available, why shouldn’t something like that be possible?","Liam gritted his teeth and acted. A massive amount of soul energy rushed toward his soul avatar. Pain exploded through his head. He nearly lost consciousness on the spot.","The soul avatar trembled violently as cracks appeared across its body, but Liam did not stop. He knew exactly what he wanted to do. The first soul thread had given him a shortcut. It had provided the foundation around which his soul avatar had formed.","But now he already possessed a soul avatar. Why couldn’t he simply use that as the foundation?","Liam pushed forward.","Instead of trying to create something from nothing, he forced the enormous mass of soul energy to gather around his existing avatar. He studied every part of it as closely as he could, using the original as a mold.","The process was excruciating.","The soul avatar was not simply a miniature copy of his body. Every inch of it was impossibly complex. Soul energy flowed through countless pathways, intersecting and overlapping in patterns Liam had never consciously noticed before.","And running through all of it was the soul thread. Liam ignored it. He copied everything else. Slowly, another figure began taking shape beside the first.","A second Liam appeared. It was crude. Its features were barely defined, and its body constantly flickered between solid and translucent, but it existed.","Liam’s heart jumped. It was working. He poured more soul energy into it. The second avatar became clearer. For a few seconds, everything went perfectly. But suddenly","Crack!","A fracture appeared across its chest. Liam’s expression changed.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","The fractures spread everywhere. \"No.\" He desperately poured more energy into the avatar. It only made things worse.","Boom!","The second avatar exploded. The backlash struck Liam like a hammer. His real body staggered. Blood flowed from his nose and mouth.","\"Liam!\"","Alex grabbed his arm, but he barely noticed. He was already looking inward again. The attempt had failed, but he was not done just yet. There was abundant soul energy all around him, more than enough to try this a couple hundred times if that was what it took.","Liam gritted his teeth and went back in again. One after another, failures quickly started mounting up. Each backlash had a strong effect, so after some time, Liam was forced to take a break to heal his soul. However, once he was sufficiently patched up, he once again dove back in.","He continued doing this when suddenly something unexpected happened. The soul energy around him doubled. The next second, it tripled. A strong wave of soul energy freshly assaulted the battleground.","Liam immediately stopped what he was doing and observed the battleground. A shocking scene was unfolding in front of him. The silver-haired man was now standing right in front of the huge demon, and he clutched the massive black axe with one hand.","Liam’s eyes widened. The weapon that had split mountains and torn apart the battlefield was completely motionless.","The demon general roared and pulled. Nothing happened.","Veins bulged across his enormous arms. Black flames erupted from his body, engulfing everything for miles around them. The ground collapsed beneath his feet as he poured more and more strength into the weapon.","Still, the silver-haired man did not move. His golden robes fluttered gently amid the raging demonic flames. Then he sighed. \"Still so weak.\"","The demon’s expression changed. The silver-haired man’s fingers tightened. The next second, his other hand moved, and a devastating explosion erupted.","Liam immediately erected several layers of soul energy barriers. However, even that was not enough. The explosion tore through the battlefield.","Liam grabbed Alex and retreated several miles in a single breath. When the storm of energy finally subsided, he looked back.","The gigantic demon was still standing. One of his four arms was gone. Half of his chest had been blown apart, and black blood poured from the wound like a waterfall. Even one of his enormous horns had shattered.","Yet the demon was laughing. \"Hahahaha!\" The sound rolled across the ruined battlefield. \"Is that all?\"","The silver-haired man stared at him without expression. Then the demon’s laughter abruptly stopped. A crimson blade had erupted from his chest. The demon slowly looked down. Blood-red energy crawled across the weapon, invading his body through the wound.","Behind him stood the vampire in the crimson coat.","\"You...\"","The vampire twisted the blade. The demon roared. At the same instant, the silver-haired man moved. Golden light flashed. His palm struck the demon directly between the brows.","Boom!","The enormous body stiffened. Then cracks of golden light spread across the demon’s body. His eyes widened in dread before the demon exploded completely.","Flesh and black blood rained across the battlefield as his enormous body disintegrated beneath the combined attacks. An unbelievable amount of soul energy erupted from the corpse.","Liam’s eyes lit up. Even without actively pulling it toward himself, his soul core trembled hungrily. What a monster. Just the remnants of that single demon contained more soul energy than countless ordinary soldiers.","Liam immediately started siphoning it away, but his attention remained fixed on the sky. The vampire in crimson pulled his blade free from what remained of the demon and looked toward the silver-haired man. A smile appeared on his face.","\"Just like old times.\"","The Archon smiled back. \"Indeed.\" But the next moment, the silver-haired man moved. His hand pierced straight through the vampire’s chest.","The vampire froze. His eyes slowly dropped toward the golden hand protruding from his body. Then he looked back up. Pure disbelief filled his face. \"You...\"","The vampire coughed out blood. \"What... are you doing?\"","The Archon’s expression hadn’t changed. Golden flames erupted from his arm.","\"AAAAARGH!\" The vampire screamed. His body began burning from the inside. He desperately tried to transform into blood mist, but golden runes had already spread across his entire body, locking him in place.","The vampire stared at the man in horror. \"You swore an oath! You said the Celestial Court would recognize—\"","The vampire’s expression went blank, and the next second his chest exploded. Blood sprayed across the sky. But the vampire was not dead yet. His severed body dissolved into crimson liquid and desperately surged backward.","The entire sea of blood surrounding the battlefield responded. It rushed toward him. The vampire was trying to reconstruct his body.","The silver-haired man calmly watched without doing anything. Then, just as the vampire had almost regenerated...","Clap. Clap. Clap.","Slow applause echoed across the battlefield.","The vampire froze. A man’s voice followed. \"Beautiful.\" The voice was smooth and amused. \"Three thousand years, and you’re still far too trusting.\"","The wounded vampire’s expression changed. A figure had appeared behind him.","A young man stood casually in the air, dressed entirely in black and crimson. Unlike the other vampires, there was almost no aura leaking from his body. Yet the instant he appeared, every vampire on the battlefield stopped moving. \"Your Highness!\" The cry spread across the battlefield.","The wounded vampire stared at the newcomer. His face lost what little color remained.","The newcomer smiled.","The vampire’s lips trembled. \"Blood Prince.\"","Liam’s entire body stiffened. This was the same vampire he had faced back on Earth. He had obtained the world seed by fighting him off. Back then, he had no idea who he was fighting against. But now... he could see clearly. This person in front of him was at an unfathomable level. He was simply far too weak in front of these monsters.","The Blood Prince casually walked towards the dying vampire. The vampire backed away. \"You were behind this?\"","The Blood Prince chuckled. \"Behind what?\"","\"You told us the Celestial Court wouldn’t interfere!\"","\"They didn’t.\" The Blood Prince gestured lazily toward the battlefield. \"Until now.\"","\"You gave us their movements. Their formations. You told us when to attack the demons!\"","\"Yes.\"","The wounded vampire finally understood. His gaze moved from the Blood Prince to the silver-haired Archon. Then back again. \"You two...\"","The silver-haired man smiled. The Blood Prince smiled with him. The vampire’s face twisted with horror. \"You planned this together.\"","\"Finally.\" The Blood Prince sighed. \"I was beginning to worry that losing all that blood had affected your brain.\"","Rage replaced the vampire’s shock. \"You betrayed us!\" The remaining sea of blood surged toward the Blood Prince.","The Blood Prince’s smile disappeared. His crimson eyes became cold. The entire ocean of blood stopped. The wounded vampire’s expression changed. Then the Blood Prince raised one finger.","The wounded vampire’s sea of blood turned against him. \"No...\" His own blood wrapped around his body. \"No! Your Highness! Wait!\" The Blood Prince looked at him without emotion. \"You seem to have misunderstood something.\"","The blood tightened. \"I did not betray my race.\"","Crack!","A huge effigy appeared, and the vampire’s body compressed.","\"I decide what becomes of it.\"","Boom!","The vampire exploded. His blood, his body, even the remnants of his power were swallowed by the crimson ocean. The Blood Prince calmly absorbed everything. Then he turned toward the silver-haired man.","The Archon extended his hand. The Blood Prince looked at it and laughed. \"Still pretending we’re civilized?\"","\"Occasionally.\"","The two men smiled.","Liam watched them from inside the mist."]},{"number":1452,"title":"Chapter 1452: Who dares?","paragraphs":["The Blood Prince and the silver-haired Archon exchanged a few more words before the Blood Prince finally turned away. With a casual wave of his hand, the enormous sea of blood condensed and disappeared into his body. A crimson tear opened in space behind him.","\"Until next time.\"","The silver-haired man nodded. \"Don’t be late.\"","The Blood Prince laughed and stepped through. The rift closed.","After that, things moved quickly. The remaining vampires withdrew first. The survivors disappeared through enormous crimson portals, leaving behind mountains of corpses.","The demonic army had already collapsed. Those who could escape fled. Those who couldn’t were hunted down by the paladins. Soon, even the Celestial forces began departing.","One golden gate after another opened across the heavens. Thousands of paladins marched through in perfect formation, followed by the divine priestesses.","The Archons left last. Liam’s attention immediately moved to Mia. She hadn’t looked in their direction even once. She simply turned and followed the silver-haired man toward one of the enormous golden gates.","Alex’s fingers tightened around Liam’s hand. \"Mia...\" She stepped forward. Liam immediately pulled her back. Alex turned toward him, her eyes red. \"Liam...\" He shook his head.","Alex’s body trembled. Mia was right there. After all this time, after searching without knowing whether her sister was even alive, Mia was standing right in front of her. And now she was leaving again.","But Liam tightened his grip on her hand. There were still too many powerful beings around them. One mistake and they wouldn’t merely lose their chance to follow Mia. They would die.","\"Wait,\" Liam mouthed silently. Alex closed her eyes. When she opened them again, she forced herself to remain still.","The golden gate swallowed Mia. Then the silver-haired man followed, after which the gate closed. Only one Archon remained now.","It was one of the armored men who had accompanied the silver-haired Archon. He hovered silently above the devastated battlefield, watching until the final paladin disappeared.","The guy then raised his hand. A strange object appeared in his palm.","Liam initially thought it was some kind of horn. But when the man brought it closer, he realized it was a conch. Its surface was pale gold, covered in tiny spiraling runes.","The Archon casually tossed it upward. The conch stopped in midair.","Wooooooom.","A deep sound spread across the battlefield. The next second every soul on the battlefield moved. Every lingering fragment of soul energy began flowing toward the conch.","Soul energy rose from the ground in enormous streams. What had previously been invisible to almost everyone now appeared like a vast ocean of translucent mist flowing upward.","Liam stared. His heart physically hurt. All of that... He had been forced to stop harvesting because of his bottleneck, but that didn’t mean the souls were worthless. Far from it. This was an opportunity he might never see again.","Millions of cultivators had died here. Many of them had cultivated for centuries, for thousands of years. And now all of it was being sucked into that damned conch right in front of him.","Liam’s fingers twitched. No. He couldn’t. The Archon was standing right there. Siphoning a million souls beneath his nose would be the equivalent of announcing his presence. Even Liam wasn’t that suicidal. But...","Did he really need a million?","His eyes slowly narrowed. Among the ocean of souls, two stood out like blazing suns. The demon general and the vampire general. Two leaders had died today and they had the most valuable souls among all. The quantity of soul energy contained within them was absurd, but that wasn’t what interested Liam most.","Liam’s heartbeat quickened. Both the demon and the vampire had clearly lived for thousands of years. More importantly, both had been important players in this war. One was a high-ranking demon. The other had apparently been important enough to negotiate directly with the Celestial Court and the Blood Prince.","Their memories could answer countless questions. The knowledge, memories and dao contained within these souls were invaluable. This could even provide him key leverage in his fight against the priestess.","This was very important. This moment could potentially define everything. Their future and lives might depend on what he did right now. Was this perhaps why the oracle had sent him here?","Liam stared at the conch. The streams of soul energy continued pouring into it. What if... His gaze shifted toward the Archon. The man appeared relaxed. He wasn’t actively controlling individual souls. He had simply activated the artifact and allowed it to do the work.","Maybe he wasn’t particularly sensitive to soul energy. That wasn’t impossible. Being overwhelmingly powerful didn’t mean being equally skilled in every Dao.","Liam’s eyes gleamed. He could test it. He would tread the waters first. If the Archon reacted in the slightest, Liam would immediately let go. He allowed an impossibly thin strand of soul mist to mix with the soul energy already flowing toward the conch.","And...","The Archon didn’t react. Instead, he walked over to the demon general’s corpse and was examining it thoroughly.","There was no point in waiting anymore. Liam decided to go for it. He immediately locked onto the demon’s soul. It towered among the others, dense black energy rolling around it. Several parts had already begun breaking apart, but the core remained intact.","Liam swallowed. That thing alone might be worth more than every soul he had collected in his entire lifetime. Don’t get greedy. He reminded himself.","Liam wrapped the faintest strand of soul energy around the demon’s soul. Then he tugged. The demon’s soul shifted a little.","Liam immediately stopped. His eyes moved toward the Archon. The man did not react at all. He quickly tugged again, harder this time.","The demon’s enormous soul drifted sideways, separating ever so slightly from the river of souls flowing toward the conch. The Archon remained completely oblivious.","Liam’s lips slowly curled upward. He continued pulling, and the demon’s soul moved toward him. He did not dare rush the process.","The conch was exerting a constant pull on every soul across the battlefield, and Liam had no idea whether the artifact itself could detect interference.","He carefully matched its rhythm, allowing the demon’s soul to drift toward the conch whenever the suction strengthened before tugging it sideways whenever the pull weakened.","To anyone watching, the movement would hopefully look like nothing more than another soul being swept around by the chaotic currents covering the battlefield.","The distance between them gradually shrank.","Liam kept most of his attention on the Archon. The man had crouched beside the demon general’s corpse and seemed far more interested in the remains than the souls flowing overhead.","He turned over several pieces of shattered armor before eventually reaching into the ruined chest and pulling out a dark crystal covered in cracks. After examining it for a few seconds, he stored it away and continued searching.","Perfect. Liam pulled harder. The demon’s soul slipped farther from the main current, and the moment it entered the outer edge of Liam’s mist, the pressure from the conch weakened considerably.","Liam immediately wrapped several additional strands of soul energy around it and dragged it deeper inside.","The entire process had taken less than a minute, but sweat had already gathered across his forehead. Liam waited several seconds, watching the Archon for any indication that something had changed.","Nothing. The man continued rummaging through the corpse. Only then did Liam finally allow himself to relax slightly.","His gaze shifted toward the massive demonic soul floating beside him, and excitement surged through him. He had actually done it. He had stolen the soul of a monster who had stood toe-to-toe with an Archon, right beneath another Archon’s nose.","Liam took a deep breath. He was not done yet. There was still one more soul. Trying to grab another soul while handling a monstrous soul like this was essentially suicidal, but it had to be done. This was his chance. He needed to push himself right here and right now. Otherwise, everything might change.","The more he saw, the more he was sure. This was it. This was the fateful encounter that could change all of their future. He had to get it done right here and now.","His attention moved toward the vampire general’s soul, and his expression immediately changed. The vampire was much farther away, already caught within one of the strongest currents leading toward the conch. Worse, the soul had started breaking apart. Thin crimson strands were being peeled from its body and swallowed into the artifact.","Liam’s eyes narrowed. If he waited much longer, there wouldn’t be anything left worth stealing. He carefully extended his soul mist again.","This time, however, the moment his energy touched the vampire’s soul, Liam felt something different. The demon’s soul had been dense and violent, but ultimately passive. This one reacted. A pair of crimson eyes suddenly opened.","The vampire was dead. His consciousness should have been fragmented, especially after the Blood Prince had destroyed his body so thoroughly. Yet something was clearly still present inside the soul.","Before Liam could withdraw, the vampire suddenly grabbed the strand of soul energy wrapped around him. The consciousness remaining inside was far stronger than he had expected. The moment it latched onto his soul mist, crimson energy surged along the connection and slammed directly into his consciousness.","Could a soul attack? Perhaps it was a special type of skill.","Liam grunted as a sharp pain tore through his head. He immediately tried to sever the strand, but the vampire refused to let go. Instead, the crimson soul energy wrapped around it and pulled in the opposite direction, attempting to drag Liam’s consciousness out of the mist.","Even dead, this bastard was troublesome.","Liam stopped trying to retreat. He strengthened the connection instead and wrapped several more strands around the vampire’s soul, intending to overpower it before the situation could deteriorate.","The vampire reacted immediately. Crimson energy erupted from its body as it struggled against both Liam and the conch, causing the surrounding river of souls to churn violently.","The disturbance was small compared to the enormous amount of soul energy moving across the battlefield, but it was no longer natural.","The Archon stopped searching the demon’s corpse.","Liam noticed immediately. His heart sank.","The armored man slowly raised his head and looked toward the conch. The pale golden artifact was still rotating in the sky, but several of the runes along its surface were flashing irregularly. Most of the souls continued pouring into it without resistance, yet one crimson soul had somehow stopped moving with the current.","The Archon’s gaze followed the crimson soul.","Liam immediately released some of the pressure, hoping the vampire would be pulled forward again and the disturbance would disappear. Unfortunately, the vampire had other ideas. The moment Liam loosened his hold, it seized the opportunity and pushed back against him even harder.","The crimson soul twisted violently. The conch trembled.","Liam cursed inwardly. The damned vampire was going to expose both of them.","The Archon stood up. His relaxed demeanor disappeared as divine energy slowly gathered around him. He stared at the struggling vampire soul for several seconds before his eyes moved across the surrounding battlefield.","Liam immediately pulled every trace of his aura inward. The mist surrounding him and Alex became completely still, while the demon general’s soul was forced deeper into his soul space, where not even the slightest trace of it could leak out.","Alex noticed the change and looked toward him. Liam didn’t have time to explain. He squeezed her hand once, warning her not to move, and returned all of his concentration to the vampire. He needed to end this now.","However, it was already too late.","The Archon’s head snapped toward them. \"Who dares?\" His voice rolled across the battlefield. Divine pressure descended immediately.","The earth groaned beneath it. Cracks spread across the already devastated ground, while countless weaker souls collapsed under the pressure and dissolved into raw energy. Even Liam’s mist compressed around him, forcing him to pour more soul energy into maintaining the concealment."]},{"number":1453,"title":"Chapter 1453: Return of the Queen","paragraphs":["The Archon’s eyes began glowing gold as his gaze swept across the battlefield. He was no longer casually looking around. Divine energy spread outward from his body in expanding waves, passing through mountains of corpses and shattered terrain as he searched for whatever had interfered with the conch.","Liam was merely a Transcendent. However, the other party was at a rank Liam couldn’t even fathom. Even though soul arts were complex and his mist had concealed him from countless powerful enemies before, the difference between them was simply too large.","The concealment did not last long. In the blink of an eye, the Archon’s golden gaze stopped directly on him. The mist shuddered. At the same instant, space hardened around Liam and Alex.","Liam had already activated the teleportation token he had kept ready since arriving on this damned battlefield, but the familiar spatial fluctuations barely appeared before they were crushed out of existence. The token flashed once in his hand and went completely dark.","A spatial lock. Liam sucked in a deep breath of air. It was about to start.","He had already expected this much the moment he decided to go for the soul. There had never been any illusion that he could casually steal something from beneath an Archon’s nose and walk away without consequences. He had simply hoped the odds would fall in his favor. They hadn’t.","\"Liam...\" Alex whispered beside him.","\"Stay behind me.\"","His voice remained calm, but his mind was moving rapidly. Teleportation was blocked. Their concealment was gone. Running through ordinary means was pointless considering how quickly the Archon could move, and fighting him directly was even more ridiculous.","Liam had watched beings who could flatten mountains get slaughtered on this battlefield, while this man had survived the entire battle without suffering so much as a scratch.","The man arrived in front of them in a single instant.","For the first time, Liam got a clear look at the Archon from close range. The man was covered from neck to toe in pale golden armor, with intricate divine inscriptions carved across every plate.","He looked surprisingly young, perhaps somewhere in his thirties, though Liam knew appearance meant absolutely nothing for beings at this level. His golden eyes moved briefly over Alex before settling on Liam.","The Archon frowned. \"A Transcendent?\" There was genuine confusion in his voice. He had clearly expected something else after discovering that someone had interfered with the conch. \"You hid from me for this long?\"","Liam understood one thing. This man probably wanted to know more about his background, and that was the only reason he was still alive. The next few seconds were probably the only time he was going to get.","Liam decisively acted. He knew exactly what he needed to do. It was now or never. He had acted with this backup plan, and now it was time to put this plan into action.","Liam fully intended to use those few seconds of curiosity before the man decided to kill him. Without wasting any time, his consciousness plunged into his soul space.","The demon general’s soul was already there, bound beneath layer after layer of mist, while the vampire general was still connected to him through the thin strand he had used to pull it away from the conch.","Liam had originally intended to take his time with both souls, slowly break them down and absorb everything they possessed without losing anything valuable. That was no longer an option.","He needed power immediately.","His entire soul was trembling from the exertion of holding these two monstrous souls, but he was no longer the same person. Even though he was on the verge of collapsing, he held on.","Liam gritted his teeth and seized the demon general’s soul. The reaction was instantaneous. The massive soul convulsed as Liam’s soul energy invaded it from every direction, tearing through whatever defenses remained after death.","Memories, emotions, and thousands of years of accumulated experience erupted into Liam’s consciousness all at once. His entire body stiffened.","The amount of information was absurd. He saw worlds he had never visited, wars fought thousands of years before he was born, enormous demonic cities built beneath black suns, creatures whose names meant nothing to him, techniques capable of destroying mountains and oceans, and fragments of Dao comprehension so dense that merely touching them sent pain ripping through his mind.","The demonic Dao core inside him reacted violently. It began spinning faster and faster as the demon general’s comprehension poured into it, and the incomplete core that had been developing throughout the battle suddenly became far more substantial. Cracks spread through its surface before closing again, each cycle making the core denser.","The Archon’s expression changed slightly. He could sense Liam’s aura rising. \"What are you doing? How are you able to stand in front of me?\"","Liam didn’t answer. He pulled harder. The demon general’s soul finally awakened.","A deafening roar exploded inside Liam’s consciousness as two enormous burning eyes opened within the darkness of his soul space. The demon’s remaining will immediately understood what was happening and fought back with terrifying force.","Liam nearly blacked out. Even dead, the bastard was monstrously strong. Unfortunately for him, this was Liam’s soul space.","Mist flooded the entire space and crashed down on the demon general from every direction. Liam didn’t bother fighting the demon’s will head-on. He had spent too much time dealing with souls to make such a stupid mistake. He isolated pieces of it instead, stripping away fragments one after another and feeding everything useful directly into himself.","The demon roared again, but its enormous form was already shrinking.","Outside, only a few seconds had passed.","The Archon watched with growing interest. Liam could feel divine energy spreading around them, sealing every possible route of escape, but the man still hadn’t attacked. Instead, his focus shifted to Alex. \"A paladin with a tier A physique? Are you from the celestial court? Why are you still here?\"","The man’s expression then swiftly changed as he sensed something else. The pressure immediately intensified. The archon’s eyes turned cold. It looked like he was done being curious. He moved his hand a little, and an enormous wave of divine energy surged towards them.","The power contained within it was enough to make the surrounding space buckle. Liam immediately understood that he couldn’t block it.","His barriers, his body, even the enormous amount of soul energy he had accumulated would be torn apart the instant that wave reached him. He didn’t try. Instead, he called for someone else, someone who could possibly block this sort of attack.","Instantaneously, his soul avatar appeared, and right next to his soul avatar was a woman. Long snow-white hair cascaded down her back almost to her waist. She was tall and strikingly beautiful, with a mature, voluptuous figure wrapped in a simple white dress. Two white fox ears rose through her hair, while several enormous tails unfurled behind her.","\"You dare attack my Master?\" Luna roared, eyes blazing.","The little fox Liam had once carried around was nowhere to be seen. She had grown. More importantly, she had become terrifyingly powerful.","Even Liam couldn’t swallow how much she had changed. He knew that she had evolved again but to actually see it in person was a different phenomenon. Her raw power was astounding.","The moment Luna appeared, an aura unlike anything Liam had ever felt erupted from her body. The Archon’s divine pressure, which had covered the entire battlefield only moments earlier, was immediately forced backward.","White energy spread around Luna in gentle waves, yet wherever it passed, the Archon’s oppressive divine power simply ceased to advance. The Archon’s expression changed. His attack arrived.","Luna raised one hand.","BOOOOOOM!","The collision erased everything around them.","The already devastated ground disappeared beneath their feet as a massive crater opened across the battlefield. Mountains of corpses were blasted apart, broken weapons vaporized, and violent spatial cracks spread outward for miles.","Liam instinctively pulled Alex closer. Yet neither of them felt anything. A thin layer of white light surrounded them.","\"She has really grown a lot.\" With a smile, Liam once again focused inward. He knew Luna could handle things for a few seconds. She was also out of her league her but Luna was a special beast. She was one of the reasons Liam dared to continue lingering in this spot.","However, even she had her limits. It was about time he stepped it up, or they all needed to get the hell out of here."]},{"number":1454,"title":"Chapter 1454: A second soul thread","paragraphs":["Liam took back his soul avatar, and almost instantly his power exploded many times over. Luna and his fire dao avatar had not been idle. With nothing holding them back and fully focused on hunting, the two of them had improved by leaps and bounds.","Thanks to this, his strain of handling two high-ranking souls immediately reduced a little. But the processing part still remained. Liam dove back inside and immediately he was in the midst of endless memories and fragments of Dao comprehension flooding him at the same time.","Maybe he could use the demon’s soul as a base and form his second avatar? What if he tried to move his demonic core into this soul and stabilize it along with his own soul energy?","The concept was easy enough but it was very difficult to actually do it. Not to mention he did not have a lot of tries left. The soul was constantly degrading. He only had a few more seconds left before he lost all of it.","Liam sucked in a breath and gave it his all. He first tried to mix his soul energy with the demon’s soul. It wouldn’t be a normal merging. It had to be mixed at a fundamental level. With the intense pressure all around him, he hurriedly attempted to do the best he could when suddenly he felt a huge backlash build up.","No. This was not the way to go. Liam withdrew quickly enough but he still injured his soul anyways.","\"Shit. Nothing is working.\" Liam cursed. Outside he could feel how much Luna was struggling. They really did not have a lot of time. Perhaps he was risking too much here. Perhaps it was time to leave.","Liam gritted his teeth unwilling to leave things like this. Running away is easy but could he afford to do that here. He had to change their fates no matter what. He once again started trying but the familiar rejection was waiting for him.","But just as he was about to bite the dust a second time, Liam suddenly noticed something strange. A small strand. An almost invisible strand of dense soul energy.","Liam’s eyes instantly widened. Could this possibly be another soul thread?","He tried reaching the small strand but it quickly slipped from his grasp. \"Come on. Come on.\" He tried again and again and again and finally he was able to lock onto it. However, the moment it was in his control he could feel it. This was not a soul thread. It was far from it. It was very weak and very flimsy.","Sure it was condensed soul energy that sort of held together everything but it was not a soul thread.","Something was not right. This strand had to be important. He had never come across anything like this before in weaker souls. Liam frowned. He quickly tried to examine the vampire soul if he could find a similar strand of condensed soul energy.","It took him a couple of seconds but he once again found a strand of soul energy in the vampire’s soul. Liam stared at the two of them in amazement when a sudden thought popped in his head.","Individually, these strands were weaker but what if he joined them together? Could that form a soul thread?","Liam’s heartbeat accelerated. It sounded almost too simple, but he couldn’t dismiss the possibility. The mysterious soul thread inside his avatar had always appeared completely uniform whenever he examined it.","He had naturally assumed that it was a single structure, some rare form of condensed soul energy that he simply hadn’t reached the level to create. But what if he had been looking at it the wrong way?","Liam forcefully pulled the two strands closer together. The difference between them immediately became obvious. He pushed them together harder. The two strands immediately rejected each other and snapped apart.","\"Of course.\" He should have expected that much.","One had developed inside a demon while the other belonged to an ancient vampire. Their soul structures, Daos, and even the fundamental nature of their energy were completely different. Simply pressing them together wasn’t going to magically produce what Liam wanted.","Outside, another tremendous impact crashed against Luna’s barrier. The force was strong enough that Liam felt the vibration even within his soul space. He needed to hurry.","His thoughts moved furiously. There was something here. He could feel it. Both strands possessed the same strange density he had sensed from his original soul thread, yet neither was anywhere close to complete. They were supporting structures inside powerful souls, but individually they were too fragile.","Liam’s attention shifted toward his original soul avatar. More specifically, toward the soul thread holding it together.","He had studied that thing countless times already, but always from the perspective of trying to reproduce its function. This time he ignored what it did and concentrated entirely on what it was.","His soul perception pressed closer. The thread expanded within his awareness. At first, he saw exactly what he had always seen before, a single impossibly thin strand of condensed soul power.","Liam pushed deeper. Pain stabbed through his consciousness. Another violent impact came from outside, and Luna’s aura fluctuated for the first time.","Liam gritted his teeth. \"Come on.\" His perception narrowed until practically his entire consciousness was concentrated on a tiny portion of the thread.","Liam froze. He saw it. He finally saw it. He had been on point all along. Dozens of microscopic patterns ran along the surface of the soul thread. Several soul threads were intertwined together to make that single strong, stable soul thread.","The question was whether they had to be compatible with each other or if they could be anything.","The answer did not matter. This was what he had at hand at this moment, and he needed to make this work. He once again tried to push the two soul threads together. This time, perhaps because he had a lot more conviction in his method, he was able to make them stick at a point.","Liam’s eyes gleamed with excitement. This could actually work. Instead of trying to make the strands intertwine together completely, he simply tried making them stick at a few points. Without wasting time, he added his own soul strand to it as well.","It took a couple of attempts, but on the fourth try he had it. He actually had a thing resembling a thread. Could this really work?","This was it. The make or break moment. He had to end this now. Their presence was already found out, so he did not bother hiding anymore. He directly started absorbing all of the abundant soul energy all around them, the massive amounts still lingering in the battlefield.","He took out his newly formed demonic core and his vampiric core together and merged them with the tornado of soul energy that was forming around the makeshift thread.","The reaction was instantaneous.","The two cores violently rejected one another.","Dark demonic energy exploded outward from one side while a sea of crimson blood energy surged from the other. The tiny thread Liam had just created bent between them, stretched almost to its breaking point as the opposing forces tried to tear the entire structure apart.","Liam’s expression changed. \"Hold together.\"","He immediately changed their positions. The demonic core moved to one side of the forming structure. The vampiric core moved to the other. Liam placed the crude soul thread directly between them. Then he released a little of his control. The cores surged toward each other.","The makeshift thread became the bridge between them. Liam began feeding more soul energy into the structure. Soul energy began rushing toward Liam from every direction.","Thousands upon thousands of dead creatures had fallen here. Even with the conch devouring the majority of their souls, enormous amounts of fragmented soul energy still lingered throughout the battlefield.","Now Liam pulled all of it toward himself. Not able to withstand his call, even the conch started trembling as if it was about to break apart.","The Archon’s expression changed. \"What the hell is he doing?\" Golden light gathered around his palm before crashing into Luna’s barrier. The impact sent another shockwave across the battlefield.","Liam instantly felt it. The archon was now going all out. Perhaps before he was simply toying with Luna, and now he was no longer playing. He gritted his teeth. He knew he was on the verge of something, but it did not matter. Luna was more important. It was time to leave after all. He might have failed here, but he had also gained something valuable.","\"LUNA! Activate the teleportation!\" Liam roared.","At the same time, he tried to pull as much soul energy as possible. He wanted to hold onto the soul avatar as long as he possibly could. Perhaps it could succeed at the last minute.","But before anything could happen, an ancient voice resonated. \"Brat, you almost have it. Do your thing. This old man will take care of the rest.\""]},{"number":1455,"title":"Chapter 1455: A true monster","paragraphs":["Liam was shocked. This was the Cauldron Ancestor.","The old man usually spoke directly inside his mind, and even then he rarely bothered saying more than a few words. But this time Liam was almost certain the voice had not been meant for him alone.","Alex had heard it. Luna had heard it. More importantly, judging from the sudden change in the Archon’s expression, he had heard it too.","Before Liam could even process that, the space directly in front of him twisted. A massive cauldron manifested out of thin air. It wasn’t the faint phantom Liam had occasionally sensed before. This time, the cauldron appeared almost completely solid.","It was enormous, easily hundreds of meters tall, its three ancient legs descending toward the ruined battlefield while its massive body covered Liam, Alex, and Luna beneath its shadow.","The surface was dark and weathered, covered in countless scratches and cracks that made it look as though it had survived wars across entire eras. Strange inscriptions covered its surface.","At the same time, the Archon’s attack crashed into Luna’s barrier.","Karakaboom!","Luna staggered. Immediately, the cauldron rang.","DONG!","The sound wasn’t particularly loud. Yet the golden divine energy filling the battlefield suddenly trembled.","The Archon’s attack broke apart. One moment, a terrifying wave of divine power was crushing down upon them. The next, cracks appeared throughout it before the entire thing shattered into countless particles of golden light, all flying into the cauldron.","The Archon stared at the cauldron incredulously. \"What is that? An artifact with a spirit?\"","The Cauldron Ancestor snorted. \"Artifact spirit?\" The old man sounded offended. \"You little brat. Your grandfather was already swallowing heavenly tribulations when your ancestors were still crawling around in the mud.\"","The Archon’s eyes narrowed, but he didn’t immediately attack. His divine sense swept toward the cauldron. The instant it touched the ancient vessel, however, his face changed. He pulled his divine sense back so violently that golden blood appeared beneath one of his eyes.","Liam stared. The Archon had been injured simply from examining the cauldron.","The old man chuckled. \"Keep poking around. See what happens. And you, brat, what are you looking at? Hurry up and get there already. This insect in front of us is nothing. Since I have decided to help you today, let’s go all out.\"","Liam clenched his fists. Things were completely out of his control. He had no idea what was about to happen. But right now, there was only one thing that he needed to do. He needed to take another step forward. He needed to finish what he started.","Focusing his full attention on the semi-formed soul avatar, he continued to draw in massive amounts of soul energy. His dao cores slowly merged with the soul avatar, and everything became more and more stable.","The crude soul thread running through the center of the avatar stopped trembling. The demonic and vampiric cores continued to resist each other, but the enormous pressure of the surrounding soul energy forced them into an uneasy balance.","Black and crimson energy circulated through the newly formed strands, passing through Liam’s own soul energy before returning to the two cores. With every completed cycle, the avatar became a little more solid.","Liam did not dare relax.","He could feel how fragile the entire thing was. One mistake and everything he had built would collapse. Worse, the two Dao cores were already becoming deeply embedded within the avatar. If the structure exploded now, he doubted he would simply lose another attempt.","It could cripple his soul. He pushed the thought aside. There was no turning back anymore. He just needed a little more, and it would become complete.","Liam pushed harder and harder until finally a second soul avatar manifested outside of him. It was a simple transcendent-rank soul avatar, but once it manifested, its rank started skyrocketing instantly.","Going from a newly awakened soul to the Transcendent rank was not a huge deal. For sufficiently talented cultivators with the right resources, that much could be accomplished relatively quickly. Everything after that was different.","Every step beyond the Transcendent rank represented an enormous transformation of the soul. A cultivator could spend tens of thousands of years strengthening their soul only to remain stuck at the same level, while reaching the ranks occupied by the monsters who had fought on this battlefield could easily require hundreds of thousands of years.","Yet Liam’s second soul avatar didn’t slow down. The moment it stabilized, the remaining soul energy from the demon general and the vampire surged into it.","BOOM!","Its aura jumped. Liam’s eyes widened. Before he could even understand what had happened, another wave followed.","BOOM!","The avatar’s body became more substantial. The faint black and crimson patterns running through it deepened, while the demonic and vampiric Dao cores embedded within its structure began rotating faster. Then another surge came.","BOOM!","Liam sucked in a breath.","The demon general and the vampire had already spent unimaginable amounts of time developing their souls. Their accumulated soul energy, comprehension, and foundations had not disappeared simply because they died.","And Liam had stolen all of it.","Normally, most of that power would have been useless to him. His Transcendent soul simply couldn’t contain it. Trying to force everything inside would have destroyed him long before he could absorb even a fraction of what those two monsters possessed.","But the second avatar had changed the equation.","It had been constructed from them. The strands supporting it had originated from their souls. The Dao cores inside it had been created from the comprehension Liam had stolen from them. Even the soul energy filling its body carried traces of their accumulated foundations.","There was almost no rejection. The avatar devoured everything. Its rank climbed again. And again. And again.","Transcendent.","Dao Lord.","The first major barrier appeared and shattered almost as soon as Liam sensed it.","BOOM!","Dao General.","The avatar’s aura erupted again, sending black and crimson waves rolling across the battlefield.","Liam’s breathing became heavier.","This was absurd.","He had expected the second avatar to strengthen quickly after its formation, but he hadn’t expected anything like this. These weren’t minor levels he was crossing. Every single rank represented a qualitative transformation of the soul, something cultivators normally spent thousands or even tens of thousands of years painstakingly accumulating.","Yet his avatar was tearing through them as though they barely existed.","Dao Master.","BOOOOOOM!","The moment it crossed into the Dao Master rank, the avatar underwent another transformation.","The previously translucent body suddenly became almost completely solid. Its features sharpened until it looked nearly identical to Liam, though the black and crimson patterns covering its body made it distinctly different from his first avatar.","The demonic Dao core settled near its abdomen. The vampiric Dao core rested near its chest. Between them ran the crude soul thread Liam had created, carrying an endless circulation of black, crimson, and pale soul energy.","Liam stared at it in disbelief.","Dao Master.","He had just created the damned thing. It hadn’t even existed a minute ago, and it was still climbing.","Standing near Liam, the Archon also stared in utter disbelief. What the hell was happening? As a divine archon, he himself was a recently ascended Dao Grand Master, and yet this guy was already a Dao Master?","Then another surge erupted from Liam. The Archon’s face stiffened. \"No.\"","The remaining soul energy from the demon general flooded into the avatar.","The demon had been a creature who had lived for an unimaginable amount of time. Every battle, every cultivation session, every soul transformation he had undergone throughout those countless years had contributed to the foundation Liam was now devouring.","The avatar absorbed all of it. Its aura rose.","Dao Master.","Peak Dao Master.","The next barrier appeared. This time it didn’t immediately break. Liam finally encountered resistance.","The archon snorted and did not waste any more time. He quickly took out a treasure. It was a small golden disk, no larger than his palm. Countless tiny inscriptions covered its surface, arranged around a single silver crystal embedded in the center.","The Cauldron Ancestor immediately noticed it. \"Oh?\"","The Archon crushed the crystal.","KACHA!","A blinding silver light erupted. The next second, thousands of attacks burst out from the golden disk.","Swords, spears, arrows, chains, enormous palms, bolts of lightning, and countless other techniques filled the sky. Every single one carried terrifying divine power, and together they formed a dense golden torrent that covered almost the entire battlefield.","However, the Cauldron Ancestor simply laughed. \"Brat, do you know who I am? This sort of attack won’t even tickle me!\"","DONG!","The cauldron rang. An enormous suction erupted. Every attack suddenly changed direction. The golden torrent that had been descending toward Liam twisted violently and rushed toward the mouth of the cauldron instead.","Swords disappeared first, followed by spears, lightning, chains, and enormous divine palms. Thousands of attacks vanished one after another until the sky was completely empty. For the first time, the Archon looked unsettled.","Meanwhile, on the side, another surge of power erupted. The soul avatar had once again broken through.","Dao Grand Master!","BOOOOOOM!","A violent wave of soul pressure swept across the battlefield. The earth cracked beneath Liam’s feet, while the remaining corpses and broken weapons around him were blasted away.","The Archon’s expression changed again.","Dao Grand Master.","The same rank as him.","He stared at Liam as though he were looking at something that should not exist. Barely a minute ago, this man had possessed nothing more than a Transcendent-rank soul. He had watched the second avatar form with his own eyes, yet in that ridiculously short period of time, it had already crossed Dao Lord, Dao General, Dao Master, and now Dao Grand Master.","But Liam barely noticed the Archon’s reaction.","The instant the breakthrough occurred, his perception exploded outward. The world suddenly became terrifyingly clear. He could distinguish individual fragments of consciousness among the countless broken souls scattered across the battlefield. Even the seemingly empty space around him was filled with countless tiny fluctuations that he had never been able to perceive before.","The enormous amount of information he had stolen from the demon general and vampire had previously been an incomprehensible mess. Hundreds of thousands of years of experience had been compressed into a storm that his mind simply couldn’t process.","Now the storm began to unravel. Memories flashed through his consciousness. There was far too much to examine now, but Liam could finally access it without feeling as though his soul was about to split apart. His mind, though, was an entirely different matter.","He felt as if he was about to lose it. It was as if his head was on the verge of exploding.","Liam roared as he felt power and madness surge through him.","Seeing this, the Archon no longer hesitated. Complex sigils appeared around him, and spatial fluctuations erupted violently from his body. He was leaving.","\"Push through it, brat. Go and kill him. Don’t let him leave.\" The cauldron ancestor roared with laughter."]},{"number":1456,"title":"Chapter 1456: Die!","paragraphs":["Liam, or rather his second soul avatar, immediately shot forward. He could feel the power surging within, and it wanted vengeance!","The Archon had already activated his escape technique. Thousands of spatial sigils surrounded his body, overlapping until the space behind him began changing. A golden passage appeared.","But before the man could step inside, crimson hands shot forward and yanked him back. \"Sit the fuck down!\" Liam roared as he finally arrived near him.","Golden divine energy erupted from his body as he twisted around and struck the avatar with his palm.","BOOM!","Black and crimson energy exploded. The avatar was thrown backward, but the Archon didn’t fare much better. His body shot through the air before he forcefully stabilized himself several hundred meters away.","He stared at the soul avatar. The crimson hands that had grabbed him were damaged, but they were already reforming. The Archon’s expression became grim. This thing really was a Dao Grand Master.","Meanwhile, Liam remained beside Alex and Luna, his physical body trembling as he controlled the avatar from a distance.","The sensation was bizarre because he could see through its eyes, feel through its body, and move its arms and legs as naturally as his own, yet at the same time he remained perfectly aware of his real body standing on the battlefield. It was almost as if his consciousness had been split between two separate existences.","For an ordinary person, processing two completely different sets of sensations at once would probably have been impossible, but Liam’s soul had already been split once when he created his first avatar, so the feeling wasn’t entirely unfamiliar.","What was different was the sheer amount of power flowing through this new body, because even the slightest movement seemed capable of releasing enough energy to devastate everything around it.","The archon did not stand idly. A golden sword slowly materialized in his hand as he raised his gaze toward the avatar. \"Whatever you did to create this abomination, you clearly have no idea how to control it. You are simply not as powerful as me!\"","Liam gritted his teeth. The bastard wasn’t wrong, but he was not about to give up now, not now when he was so close to achieving complete victory and changing his fate once and for all!","The power inside the avatar was enormous, but it was wild and unfamiliar, surging through pathways Liam barely understood while the demonic and vampiric Dao cores continued pumping out more energy than he knew how to properly use.","If he had been given a few months to study everything slowly, he was confident that his control would improve tremendously, but the Archon obviously had no intention of giving him that luxury.","The golden sword disappeared from Liam’s vision almost as soon as the Archon moved, leaving behind a brilliant streak of light that crossed the distance between them in an instant.","Liam hurriedly raised the avatar’s arms, gathering black and crimson energy around them, but his movements were just slightly too slow. The blade cut through the hastily formed defense and carved deeply across the avatar’s chest, causing a strange pain to travel through Liam’s soul as a large amount of energy spilled from the wound.","Before he could properly recover, the Archon had already turned his wrist and followed with another slash aimed directly at the avatar’s neck, forcing Liam to throw himself backward in an awkward retreat.","The Archon followed relentlessly, and within moments the difference in their ability became painfully obvious. Although their souls now occupied the same rank, the man had spent countless years cultivating, fighting, and learning how to use his power, while Liam was still struggling.","Every time Liam overcommitted to an attack, the Archon slipped around it and countered. Whenever he hesitated, the golden sword found another opening and tore chunks from the avatar’s body.","Those injuries quickly regenerated, but each restoration consumed soul energy, and Liam could already tell that blindly exchanging blows would eventually leave him with nothing.","\"You understand now?\" the Archon asked as another sweep of his sword forced the avatar backward. His confidence had returned after only a few exchanges, and the fear that had appeared when Liam broke through was rapidly disappearing.","\"You stole power that doesn’t belong to you, and now you mistake that power for your own strength. A child holding a divine weapon is still a child.\"","The words pissed Liam off, but he forced himself not to rush forward again. The bastard was deliberately provoking him, and the last several exchanges had already proven what would happen if Liam continued fighting with nothing but raw power.","He needed to calm down, understand the avatar, and figure out what exactly he had gained from devouring those two ancient souls.","Unfortunately, the moment Liam tried to focus inward, another overwhelming flood of foreign memories crashed into his consciousness, bringing with it images of battles, deaths, worlds, enemies, techniques, and experiences accumulated across stretches of time so enormous that his own life seemed insignificant by comparison.","His real body staggered as pain exploded through his head, and Luna immediately reached out to steady him. \"Master?\"","\"I’m fine,\" Liam muttered, although the blood beginning to trickle from his nose suggested otherwise.","The Archon attacked again. This time, the golden sword came from above, carrying so much concentrated divine energy that void holes started appearing. The soul avatar barely blocked the attack, taking some more damage.","The two continued clashing and clashing, and the archon only became more confident as the fight progressed. Greed flashed over his eyes, especially whenever he looked at the giant cauldron.","The cauldron was definitely not an ordinary artifact. If he could just take care of one little obstacle, he should easily be able to obtain the cauldron and perhaps even the beast.","As for the strange man controlling the soul avatar, there would be plenty of time afterward to tear apart his soul and discover exactly how he had accomplished such an impossible breakthrough.","Whatever technique allowed someone to construct a Dao Grand Master soul avatar in a matter of minutes was undoubtedly an inheritance beyond anything he had encountered before.","The thought of possessing all three treasures gradually erased the last traces of caution from the Archon’s mind. For whatever reason, the cauldron was not interfering right now. This was his chance.","His attacks immediately became more aggressive. The golden sword multiplied as he swept it through the air, producing dozens of blades that descended upon the avatar from different directions while spatial cracks opened wherever their edges passed.","Liam tried to evade, but controlling the avatar at such speeds remained frustratingly difficult, especially when every movement released far more power than he intended.","He avoided several swords before one tore through his shoulder and another entered his abdomen, causing black and crimson soul energy to spill from the wounds. A fresh wave of pain traveled through the connection and struck his consciousness.","Liam’s real body staggered again, forcing Luna to tighten her grip around his arm while Alex watched the distant battle with growing concern. The avatar was regenerating almost as quickly as it was being damaged, but the situation was obviously getting worse.","Liam could feel its reserves dropping with every exchange, while the Archon seemed to have finally abandoned any thought of escape and committed himself completely to the battle.","\"Enough.\" The Archon’s voice spread across the battlefield as the dozens of golden swords surrounding him suddenly dissolved and poured back into the original blade. Its size didn’t change, but the power contained within it increased so violently that enormous cracks spread through the space.","Liam only smiled. The demonic and vampiric Dao cores rotated violently as he dragged every bit of available soul energy toward the avatar’s chest, trying to create a defense strong enough to survive what was coming. Black and crimson power gathered in overlapping layers, yet Liam could already tell that they weren’t enough. But he did not seem to care at all.","\"Arrogance becomes your death! Die!\" The archon shouted, and his sword descended.","The world turned golden.","For a brief moment, Liam couldn’t see anything through the second avatar’s eyes except an endless ocean of divine light, within which a single sword seemed to stretch from the heavens all the way to the ruined earth below.","At the same time, another sword descended right above Liam’s original body. The archon sneered. To him, Liam’s weakness was obvious. As long as the original body was weak and fragile, this was simply child’s play. In a single attack, he was about to end the idiot.","Now, if only the cauldron and the fox continue to not interfere. The archon hastily prepared for that as well by releasing more and more attacks, creating some sort of illusion. But in the midst of all of this chaos, suddenly something unexpected barged in.","The archon froze. A hand had appeared directly beneath his descending sword.","Someone had simply reached into the path of his attack and caught the golden blade between two fingers, stopping it less than a meter above Liam’s head.","For an instant, the Archon couldn’t understand what he was seeing. Then flames erupted.","BOOOOOOM!","White-golden fire surged from the figure’s hand and raced along the Archon’s sword, swallowing the divine energy covering the blade before rushing toward his arm.","The Archon’s expression changed immediately as he released the weapon and shot backward, but the flames followed him with frightening speed, stretching through the air like living serpents.","He swept his sleeve and released a massive wall of golden energy to extinguish them, only for the fire to burn straight through it, forcing him to retreat several more times before he finally managed to break the connection.","Only then did he get a proper look at the newcomer.","Another Liam stood above the original body.","Unlike the second avatar, this one possessed none of the black and crimson patterns created by the demonic and vampiric Dao cores.","Its appearance was almost identical to Liam himself, although white-golden flames flowed continuously across its body, wrapping around its arms and shoulders before spreading behind it like a burning mantle."]},{"number":1457,"title":"Chapter 1457: A second soul avatar?","paragraphs":["\"A... second clone?\" The Archon stared at the scene in utter dread.","\"No, that would be my first,\" Liam replied, his smile widening. \"And they are not clones.\"","While Liam had been completely occupied with creating and controlling his second soul avatar, his first soul avatar had been equally busy inside his soul space.","There were millions upon millions of souls stored within him, and each one carried fragments of memories, experiences, emotions, and insights accumulated throughout their lives.","Liam had gathered so much during the battle that trying to process everything himself would have been impossible, especially when the souls of the demon general and the vampire alone contained hundreds of thousands of years of memories.","Fortunately, he didn’t have to do everything himself anymore. His first soul avatar had been working continuously.","While part of its attention had gone toward helping stabilize the newly formed second avatar, the rest had been devoted to sorting through and digesting the enormous amount of information Liam had collected.","Countless useless memories were discarded while valuable experiences were separated and gradually absorbed, allowing Liam to process everything at a speed that would have been impossible on his own.","That was also why his control over the second avatar had been improving so quickly.","The first avatar had been sorting through the memories of the demon general and the vampire, extracting pieces of their combat experience and feeding the useful portions back to Liam.","Every clash with the Archon gave it something specific to search for, and whenever it found a relevant memory or insight, Liam’s understanding of his demonic and vampiric abilities improved.","But that wasn’t all it had gained. Among the millions of souls Liam had collected were countless cultivators who had walked different paths of the Dao.","Most of their understanding was fragmented and insignificant individually, but when millions of fragments were gathered together, overlapping insights naturally began appearing.","And there was one Dao that Liam’s first soul avatar understood particularly well.","The Greater Dao of the Fire Element.","Cultivators had comprehended fire in countless different ways. Some understood its destruction, others its heat, light, purification, transformation, combustion, or even the tiny sparks from which enormous infernos could eventually arise.","Their individual understandings differed tremendously, and many were incomplete or even contradictory, but Liam didn’t need to blindly accept any of them.","He already possessed his own foundation. The first soul avatar simply used those countless fragments to fill in the gaps.","One realization connected with another. Hundreds became thousands, thousands became tens of thousands, and as more pieces fell into place, the Fire Dao core within the first avatar began undergoing one transformation after another.","Dao Lord.","Dao General.","Dao Master.","The breakthroughs came so quickly that Liam himself hadn’t noticed them while fighting for his life outside. His attention had been almost completely occupied by the second avatar, while the first continued calmly digesting the mountain of accumulated insights within his soul space.","Then it reached the peak of Dao Master. For the first time, its advancement slowed. The gap separating Dao Master from Dao Grand Master was enormous, and no amount of meaningless information could bridge it.","Millions of shallow insights remained shallow no matter how many Liam collected, but hidden among the mountain of souls were also the remnants of genuinely powerful cultivators. It included beings who had spent thousands or even tens of thousands of years comprehending their respective Daos.","The first avatar found what it needed among them. Its Fire Dao core trembled. Countless scattered insights suddenly converged upon the foundation Liam had already established, and the final barrier collapsed.","BOOM!","Dao Grand Master.","The first soul avatar opened its eyes.","White-golden flames erupted around its body before quickly contracting again, gathering so tightly that they seemed almost peaceful despite the terrifying power contained within them.","Unlike the newly formed second avatar, there was no instability in its movements and no conflicting Dao cores fighting against one another. Since it was formed on the foundation of a fully completed soul thread, it was far more powerful and stable.","Outside, the Archon stared at the two soul avatars, and the dread in his eyes deepened as his divine sense confirmed what should have been impossible.","Both of them were Dao Grand Masters! What the hell?!","Liam looked at his first avatar, then at the battered second avatar on the opposite side of the battlefield. His smile became increasingly difficult to suppress.","One had the accumulated soul foundation and memories of two ancient monsters. The other possessed his Fire Dao and had just digested some of the insights gathered from millions of souls.","And both belonged to him. Not to mention the millions of souls were only partially processed. There was still a lot more left. If he took the time to fully comprehend all the souls, then the two soul avatars would once again undergo another round of transformations.","\"Well,\" Liam muttered, wiping the blood beneath his nose as he looked at the increasingly pale Archon. \"Looks like you’re fucked.\"","Archon trembled. One Dao Grand Master soul avatar had already been troublesome enough, even when its controller barely knew how to use its power. He had managed to suppress it through superior experience and control, but even that advantage had gradually disappeared.","Now another Dao Grand Master had suddenly appeared, and unlike the unstable second avatar, this one radiated an entirely different feeling.","The Archon suddenly understood why the ancient cauldron had stopped interfering. It hadn’t abandoned Liam. There was simply no need for it to interfere anymore.","Without wasting another moment, the Archon turned around and fled. There was no hesitation this time, nor did he waste another second thinking about the cauldron, Luna, Liam’s inheritance, or any of the other treasures he had dreamed about obtaining.","Golden divine energy exploded beneath his feet as he shot toward the horizon, while hundreds of spatial sigils immediately began forming around his body. His earlier greed disappeared completely beneath the instincts that had kept him alive long enough to become a Dao Grand Master.","Unfortunately for him, Liam had no intention of letting him get away. Both soul avatars moved at the same time.","The first disappeared within an eruption of white-golden flames, while the second transformed into a streak of black and crimson energy that tore across the battlefield from the opposite direction.","Liam didn’t bother testing new techniques or trying to understand every aspect of their newfound power. He had already wasted enough time fighting this bastard, and with both avatars now standing at the Dao Grand Master rank, there was no reason to make things complicated.","The Archon had barely crossed a few hundred meters when the first avatar appeared directly in front of him.","\"Move!\"","Golden divine energy exploded from the Archon’s sword as he slashed forward, but the first avatar didn’t dodge.","White-golden flames gathered around its hand before it struck the incoming sword from the side, knocking the blade away with such tremendous force that the Archon’s entire arm twisted backward.","Before he could recover, the avatar stepped forward and drove its burning fist straight into his chest.","BOOOOOOM!","The Archon’s golden armor shattered.","His body shot backward, but before he could travel even a hundred meters, black and crimson energy erupted behind him.","The second avatar was already there.","Two crimson hands grabbed the Archon from behind while demonic energy gathered around its knee, and Liam slammed it directly into the man’s spine. A sickening crack rang through the air as another explosion sent the Archon flying back in the opposite direction, straight toward the first avatar.","Spatial sigils appeared around his body. The first avatar punched through them.","KACHA!","The half-formed escape technique shattered along with the surrounding space, and a white-golden hand closed around the Archon’s throat before he could create another one. Divine energy erupted wildly from his body as he struggled, but the first avatar’s flames burned through it while the second arrived behind him once again.","The Archon looked at the first avatar holding his throat. Then he sensed the second standing behind him. His face went pale. \"Wait. If you kill me-\"","Liam didn’t wait. Both avatars attacked simultaneously. The first avatar’s burning fist crashed into the Archon’s chest while the second drove a black-and-crimson palm into his back.","Three different powers erupted inside the Archon’s body at the same instant. His remaining armor disintegrated first. Then his body exploded. A devastating shockwave erupted.","Golden blood and divine energy scattered across the sky as the two attacks crushed him between them, but Liam had already learned enough during this battle to know that destroying the body of someone at this level didn’t necessarily mean killing them.","Through both avatars, he immediately sensed an incredibly dense golden soul trying to escape from the explosion.","The Archon’s soul shot toward the sky.","It didn’t make it far. The second avatar’s crimson hand stretched through the air and closed around it.","\"No!\" The Archon’s terrified voice echoed directly from his soul as golden energy erupted around him, desperately trying to break the crimson fingers apart.","At the same time, the first avatar appeared above him, white-golden flames gathering around its palm before forming a blazing prison that sealed off every possible direction of escape.","The Archon’s soul trembled. \"Stop! I am an Archon of the Celestial Court! If you destroy my soul, the Court will hunt you across every-\"","Liam smiled, and the crimson hand tightened, an enormous amount of power exploding. \"They are already hunting me down.\""]},{"number":1458,"title":"Chapter 1458: A new soulweaver in the cosmos","paragraphs":["Cracks spread across the golden soul. Liam grasped the soul and erased the final bits of Archon’s will attached to it. He then brought it into his soul space.","The moment the Archon’s soul disappeared, the ruined battlefield finally fell silent.","Liam remained completely still for several seconds, almost unable to believe that it was actually over.","His first soul avatar floated in the distance, surrounded by slowly fading white-golden flames, while the second stood nearby with black and crimson energy still rolling across its damaged body.","Both were Dao Grand Masters, both belonged to him, and inside his soul space was now the soul of the man who had nearly killed him only moments ago.","\"Holy shit.\"","Liam slowly lowered himself to the ground. The moment the tension disappeared, exhaustion hit him all at once. His legs nearly buckled beneath him as the pain he had been ignoring surged back through his consciousness, and Luna hurriedly wrapped an arm around him before he could fall.","Blood continued dripping from his nose. His head felt as though someone had repeatedly smashed it against a wall, and controlling two Dao Grand Master avatars while simultaneously maintaining his physical body had pushed his mind dangerously close to its limit.","Alex and Luna stared at the blood running down his face.","Liam wiped it away. \"I am fine. We did it. We did it. We changed our fate.\"","Alex and Luna stared in confusion, but the old cauldron ancestor understood everything very well. \"You really did. You stinking brat. You really did change your fate.\" His laughter rang loudly in the empty, almost fully destroyed world. \"Now don’t slack off. Finish what you started. I am standing guard for you here.\"","Liam nodded and dove back in. Now that there was no more pressure, he was immediately able to identify the soul strand in the archon’s soul.","The other two had been dark and crimson respectively, carrying traces of their nature even after Liam stripped away most of the remaining soul energy around them, while the Archon’s strand shone with a faint golden light.","More importantly, it felt incredibly complete. The demon and vampire souls had both suffered tremendous damage before Liam obtained them, but the Archon’s soul had been captured almost immediately after his body was destroyed. Its deeper structure was almost perfectly preserved.","Liam carefully separated the golden strand. The moment it came free, his second soul avatar reacted.","The crude soul thread connecting the demonic and vampiric Dao cores began trembling violently, and Liam immediately understood why.","He had constructed that thing in desperation by forcing incompatible soul strands together and using his own soul energy as a bridge, but it had always been an imperfect imitation of his original soul thread.","It had somehow survived the avatar’s insane series of breakthroughs, yet after reaching Dao Grand Master, its weakness had become even more obvious.","\"Perfect.\"","Liam didn’t hesitate. He brought the golden strand toward the crude soul thread. The demonic strand reacted first.","Black energy surged from it and immediately pushed against the newcomer, while the vampiric strand responded almost simultaneously with a wave of crimson energy.","Liam frowned but wasn’t surprised. He had encountered the same problem when he originally tried to combine the demon and vampire strands, and forcing them together had accomplished absolutely nothing.","This time, however, Liam had no enemy trying to cut him apart. He could take his time to some extent, at least.","Liam began experimenting. The first attempt failed. So did the second.","By the seventh, he had managed to connect the golden strand to the crude soul thread at a single point, only for the connection to collapse moments later when demonic energy surged through it.","The failure didn’t discourage him because, unlike before, every attempt taught him something.","Outside, Alex remained close to Liam’s motionless body while the Cauldron Ancestor stood guard over the devastated world. Luna wandered around and picked up all the drops and the corpses, including the heavy loot on the three main big shots.","Inside, Liam continued working with obsessive concentration, rebuilding connections whenever they collapsed and gradually learning how the three different strands responded to one another.","Then, after countless attempts, something finally changed. The three strands locked together.","Liam froze. For several seconds, he didn’t dare touch anything. The connection was still crude, with the dark demonic strand, crimson vampiric strand, and golden divine strand only joined together at several points rather than perfectly intertwined like his original soul thread, but none of them were rejecting the others anymore.","Black, crimson, and golden soul energy flowed through the structure in slow pulses, and every time the three energies reached one of the newly formed connections, the entire thread trembled without breaking apart.","\"It worked.\" Liam carefully sent a little more soul energy through it. The makeshift thread held.","He increased the amount again, and although the three strands trembled violently, they remained connected. More importantly, the golden strand seemed to have changed the balance between the other two.","The demonic and vampiric strands still rejected each other whenever they came into direct contact, but with the third strand woven between them, the pressure no longer concentrated entirely on Liam’s own soul energy holding everything together.","The second soul avatar immediately began changing.","Its demonic and vampiric Dao cores rotated faster as the newly reinforced soul thread allowed more energy to flow between them.","Previously, Liam had needed to carefully restrict both cores because every violent surge threatened to tear apart the crude connections holding the avatar together, but that danger had diminished considerably.","Black and crimson energy spread throughout the avatar’s damaged body, rebuilding its missing flesh at a speed that made Liam’s eyes widen. Within moments, the injuries disappeared.","The second avatar opened its eyes.","Boom!","A heavy pulse of soul pressure swept through Liam’s soul space.","The millions of surrounding souls trembled as the avatar’s presence suddenly became denser, while the unstable fluctuations that had constantly surrounded it began disappearing one after another.","Its cultivation hadn’t increased beyond Dao Grand Master, but Liam could immediately tell that its actual strength had risen considerably. Before, a large portion of the avatar’s power had been wasted simply keeping itself together. Now far more of that power could actually be used.","Liam grinned. \"Three really is better.\"","Just as he finished, many system notifications chimed in one after the other.","[Ding! You have successfully created a soul thread from foundation]","[Ding! You have achieved the title ’Soul Weaver’]","[Your perception of soul strands has been greatly enhanced.]","[Your ability to manipulate, separate, and weave soul strands has been greatly enhanced.]","[Foreign soul strand rejection reduced.]","[Ding! Soulweaver Thread (2/999)]","[Ding! You have successfully created a second soul avatar]","Liam looked at the notifications and exhaled. 2 soul threads and 2 soul avatars. Did this mean he could possibly make 999? If this was true, then the soulmancer class was absolutely broken!","Not that the class was without its own limitations. It looks like his real body is going to be lagging behind for a while. However, he was not too concerned about this. He hadn’t properly digested all the memories so he did not know for sure, but he did catch some hints on dao body for clones.","Liam had a feeling that he might be able to evolve his soul avatars more down the line. That was a problem for later. For now he needed to get out of here and first fully process all of the souls he had gathered today. Not just the dao fragments but also the memories.","These were not souls of nobodies.","Even among the millions of ordinary soldiers who had died on this battlefield, many had lived for centuries, while the stronger cultivators had accumulated thousands or even tens of thousands of years of experience.","They had cultivated different Daos, traveled through different worlds, belonged to different factions, learned countless techniques, and gathered knowledge that Liam had never even known existed.","And then there were the three monsters. The demon general, the vampire and the Archon divine swordsman. Each of their souls alone was a treasure that Liam couldn’t properly estimate.","The fragments he had absorbed during the battle had already given him enough comprehension to create new Dao cores and push his second soul avatar all the way to Dao Grand Master.","But those fragments represented only a small portion of what their souls actually contained. Hundreds of thousands of years of memories remained buried inside the demon and vampire alone, while the Archon’s soul was almost perfectly preserved.","Liam had barely scratched the surface. Cultivation techniques, combat experience, dao comprehension, secret arts, information about different worlds and knowledge about demons, vampires, the Celestial Court, and perhaps even the entire political network of the cosmos. There was a lot to learn.","And most importantly, these held answers to many of his questions.","Just as Liam was mulling over these things, all of a sudden a small cauldron appeared in his soul space. The moment he saw it, his eyes went wide.","\"Senior... This...\" Liam stammered.","The old man’s voice boomed in his ears. \"Congrats brat. You are now qualified to wield me.\"","Liam stared at the small cauldron. He knew exactly how terrifying this thing was. And finally he would be able to use this! The alchemist in him was jumping with joy.","\"Toss in your dolls and see what happens.\"","Liam smiled bitterly. Did he mean his soul avatars that he painstakingly created with his life on the life? Nevertheless, he tried it. Immediately Liam became shocked again."]},{"number":1459,"title":"Chapter 1459: Why did you come back?","paragraphs":["Liam focused on the cauldron and sent his first avatar in. Enormous white-golden flames gathered around it. Incredible pressure bore down on it from every direction, compressing the avatar until even Liam could feel the strain through their connection.","Fuck no. He just got these out after going through hell. He almost pulled it back out when the old man’s voice strictly forbade him. \"Don’t.\"","\"Senior, what are you doing to it?\"","\"What does it look like I’m doing?\"","\"Trying to cook me?\"","The old man snorted. \"If I wanted to cook you, brat, you would already be cooked.\"","\"Fair enough.\"","Liam forced himself to wait. The pressure continued increasing. His first soul avatar sat cross-legged within the cauldron while white-golden flames repeatedly passed through its body.","Every time they did, tiny specks of murky energy were forced out, so small that Liam hadn’t even been able to detect them before.","Some were remnants of the countless souls it had processed, others were fragments of foreign emotions and memories, while a few were impurities that had accumulated naturally as the avatar underwent one absurd breakthrough after another.","The flames burned all of them away. Again and again, the avatar was compressed, purified, and compressed once more.","Liam gradually stopped worrying. The process was painfully familiar. \"This is pill refinement.\"","\"Close.\"","The answer surprised him. Liam focused more carefully, and then he understood. \"Body tempering?\"","\"Closer.\" The Cauldron Ancestor chuckled. \"You keep thinking of these things as souls.\"","Liam frowned. \"They are soul avatars.\"","\"At the moment.\"","Liam’s eyes narrowed. The old man didn’t explain further. Instead, the pressure inside the cauldron abruptly increased.","BOOM!","The first avatar’s white-golden flames exploded outward before being violently compressed back into its body. Its Fire Dao core trembled, and Liam immediately felt the enormous amount of power accumulated within the avatar being forced deeper into its structure.","Every cycle reduced its size by an almost imperceptible amount while making its body increasingly solid.","Before entering the cauldron, the avatar had already looked almost indistinguishable from Liam because of its Dao Grand Master cultivation, but that solidity had still been an illusion created by extremely dense soul energy.","Now something was changing. Liam reached toward it with his perception. His eyes widened. The avatar’s hand no longer felt like an impossibly dense collection of soul energy.","There was something else beginning to form beneath it, although Liam couldn’t understand what that something was. Then the system chimed.","[Ding! Your First Soul Avatar is undergoing Primordial Refinement.]","[Ding! Soul impurities are being removed.]","[Ding! Soul foundation is being tempered.]","[Ding! Your Soul Avatar has started forming a Dao Body.]","Liam stared at the last notification. The cauldron was actually giving him a kickstart in Dao Body formation! This was insane!","DONG!","The lid opened and the first avatar shot out.","The moment the avatar stabilized within his soul space, white-golden flames erupted around its body. Liam could immediately tell that their power had increased.","\"Your doll has grown too quickly. Dao Lord, Dao General, Dao Master, Dao Grand Master... all in what? A few seconds?\" The old man snorted.","\"Something like that.\"","\"Ridiculous.\"","Liam couldn’t disagree.","\"Power accumulated quickly is still power, but its foundation needs time to settle. What I did was save you some of that time.\"","Liam nodded, immediately turning toward his second avatar.","Black and crimson energy rolled across its body while faint traces of golden light occasionally appeared along the newly stabilized soul thread.","The avatar seemed to notice his stare.","Liam smiled. \"Your turn.\" He tossed it into the cauldron.","The cauldron shook again.","Liam winced. Through his connection, he could feel the second avatar being subjected to pressure several times greater than what the first had endured.","The demonic and vampiric Dao cores rotated violently while the golden soul strand stretched between them, and for a terrifying moment Liam thought the Soulweaver Thread was going to break apart.","However, the three strands held. Then the refinement truly began.","After a while everything was completed. The two soul avatars were stable and all the loot were collected. There was no longer any need to stay here in this world. Besides if someone was tracking the guy it was only a matter of time before they get here to look for him.","But Liam already knew from the memories that no one was. After a certain rank almost everyone choses to be secretive so even after the archon died it would take a while for others to realise that. This was why he decided to stabilize his soul avatars first before leaving.","\"Are we going back to our world Liam?\" Alex asked. They had clearly survived a major disaster but Alex did not look happy at all. She looked listless and fragile, her mind clearly on Mia.","Liam let out a sigh and pulled her into his arms. \"Do you trust me?\"","Alex couldn’t hold it back anymore. The composure she had somehow maintained throughout the battle finally shattered, and she buried her face against his chest as tears began streaming down her cheeks.","\"Liam, I think she’s suffering.\" Her voice broke. \"How long has it been? She must have suffered so much.\"","Liam tightened his arms around her. \"Mia is strong. All this will only make her stronger. We need to be strong too. She is waiting for us to come and rescue her. I promise you. It will happen soon.\"","He turned to Luna and nodded at her. \"Why don’t you take Alex back home? I have some unfinished business I need to take care of.\"","Luna quickly obeyed, and the two of them teleported back. Liam stood with his two soul avatars on his side and took one last look at the devastated world before he teleported as well.","However, he did not go back home immediately. He sent his two soul avatars back to his soul space for them to slowly process all the millions of souls while he teleported.","Coincidentally, the moment he arrived, Liam found himself staring directly into a familiar face, the draconian creature, Dralura.","For the briefest instant, memories of his previous encounter with the creatures flashed through his mind. Back then, even one of them had been enough to make him cautious, forcing him to consider whether fighting was worth the risk.","This time, Liam didn’t even slow down. The Dralura’s eyes widened as it recognized him, but before it could speak, move, or gather even the slightest bit of power, Liam raised his hand.","Shing!","A thin arc of white-golden fire flashed through the air.","The Dralura froze. A line appeared across its body before the creature separated cleanly into two halves, the lingering flames consuming whatever resistance remained. Liam reached forward almost absentmindedly, caught the escaping soul, and tossed it directly into his soul space.","Liam was about to inspect it when he felt someone glaring at him. He turned.","Nyx stood only a short distance away, and judging by the expression on her face, she was considerably less impressed by his return than he had expected. \"Why did you come back?\"","Liam raised an eyebrow.","Nyx marched toward him. \"Haven’t you done enough already?\" Her anger rose with every word. \"Because of you, a lot of our sect juniors are trapped inside the Treasure World! We’re completely sealed off from it. We can’t enter, the seniors can’t enter, no one can do anything. They’re just stuck in there!\"","Liam let out a sigh of relief. He had expected a lot worse, but if it was just this much, then he should probably be able to fix it.","Looking at the relief on his face, Nyx became even more triggered. \"Do you have any idea how many people are trapped in there because of you? Their families are panicking, the elders have been trying everything they can think of, and nobody even knows whether the people inside have enough supplies to survive. And you come back after disappearing for who knows where and look relieved?\"","Liam blinked. When she put it that way, his reaction probably did look a little fucked up. \"Sorry.\" He rubbed the back of his neck. \"I didn’t mean it like that. I was just expecting something much worse.\"","Nyx stared at him incredulously. \"What could possibly be worse? Oh, did you actually want our entire sect to be destroyed? Bastard, did you come here to pick our corpses for loot?\"","Liam exhaled and turned away. He did not bother talking to her anymore. There was no point in wasting time arguing when he could simply solve the problem. Without any delay, he immediately identified the portal from which the Dralura he had killed had emerged. It was still open.","Liam walked toward it.","Nyx stared at his back. \"Where are you going?\"","Seeing Liam step into the portal, her panicked voice rang out. \"You cannot go in there. You will end up right in the middle of their settlement.\"","\"I hope so.\" Liam smiled. Space twisted around Liam.","The next instant, he emerged on the other side.","And Nyx had been absolutely right.","Liam found himself standing in the middle of an enormous Dralura settlement. Hundreds of Dralura surrounded him, with even more spread throughout the sprawling settlement beyond. Massive stone structures rose in every direction, their walls carved with strange draconic symbols, while several enormous creatures soared through the sky.","The moment he arrived, every single pair of nearby eyes slowly turned toward him.","Liam looked around. \"Huh.\"","The nearest Dralura reacted first. \"Human!\" Its roar echoed across the settlement. Weapons appeared everywhere.","Dozens of Dralura launched themselves toward Liam almost simultaneously, their powerful bodies tearing apart the ground beneath their feet as various bloodline abilities erupted. Fire, lightning, wind, and several attacks immediately filled the air.","However, the next second, these same creatures trembled as a powerful aura swept over them. The first soul avatar silently emerged beside Liam. It only took a single attack from the soul avatar to slaughter the entire dozen.","However, Liam knew that the fight wasn’t going to be an easy one. He could already sense many powerful auras stirring in the distance. Without hesitation, he ordered his second soul avatar to fight as well. He did not want to underestimate his opponents.","Leaving the fight to both his soul avatars, Liam proceeded to the spire, the same place where he created the first soul avatar. There was another reason why he had come here. It was time to see it through. He had waited a long time for this, and there was no point in waiting anymore.","The time was here and now. This was also why he did not return to Earth. What he was about to do now would determine everything from here on out. Did he really change his fate or not?"]},{"number":1460,"title":"Chapter 1460: I want him dead","paragraphs":["In a distant world, a pair of beautiful eyes suddenly opened, beautiful but filled with bone-chilling coldness. High Priestess Xerathuna slowly rose from her meditative pose.","Her long silver-white robes fell around her as she stepped down from the elevated platform. A golden mark resembling a closed eye rested between her brows, while strands of pale hair cascaded almost to her waist. There was no visible anger on her beautiful face, yet the oppressive aura surrounding her made the entire chamber feel suffocating.","She calmly looked to her right, and the golden doors opened. A paladin hurried inside and immediately dropped to one knee. \"Esteemed Goddess.\"","Xerathuna regarded him without expression. \"I ordered that I was not to be disturbed.\"","The paladin’s body stiffened. Even with his head lowered, a bead of sweat appeared along his temple as the pressure within the chamber grew heavier.","\"Forgive me, Esteemed Goddess. I would not have dared if it were anything less important.\"","\"Then speak.\"","\"We found him.\"","Xerathuna stopped. The pressure filling the chamber abruptly vanished. For several breaths, she said nothing. The paladin remained kneeling, unwilling to raise his head until her quiet voice finally reached him.","\"Say that again.\"","\"We have located Liam.\"","A faint smile appeared on Xerathuna’s lips. Finally. \"Where?\"","\"The Green Mountains.\"","Xerathuna’s smile widened. \"So the little rat has finally crawled out of whatever hole he was hiding in.\"","She had hunted Liam for far too long. After everything that bastard had done, she had expected to crush him almost immediately, yet he had somehow vanished so completely that even the methods available to her had repeatedly failed to locate him.","And now he had simply reappeared. In the Green Mountains, of all places. Xerathuna chuckled softly. \"Does he think that old bastard from Green Mountain can protect him from me?\"","The paladin wisely remained silent.","Green Mountain was not some insignificant sect that could simply be trampled whenever the Celestial Court wished. The ancient existence behind it was precisely why their people had exercised restraint there in the first place, but judging by the expression on Xerathuna’s face, that restraint had reached its end.","\"How certain are you?\"","\"Completely certain, Esteemed Goddess. Archon Von Brehalen marked him with our divine temple sigil.\"","Xerathuna’s smile disappeared.","\"Von Brehalen?\"","\"Yes, Esteemed Goddess.\"","That was unexpected. Von Brehalen had been dispatched elsewhere on Celestial Court business and had no involvement in the hunt for Liam, yet somehow their paths had crossed. More importantly, if an Archon had personally placed a Divine Temple Sigil upon Liam, there could be no mistake about his identity or current location.","\"When?\"","\"Recently. The sigil appeared within the tracking temple only a short while ago. We confirmed it against the mark already recorded for Liam.\"","Xerathuna’s eyes narrowed. \"Why would Von Brehalen mark him?\"","\"We don’t know.\"","\"Contact him.\"","The paladin hesitated.","Xerathuna immediately noticed. \"What?\"","\"We... cannot.\"","A faint pressure returned to the chamber. \"Explain.\"","\"We attempted to contact Archon Von Brehalen as soon as we detected the sigil. There was no response. We then contacted his attendants, but they do not know his current location either. According to them, the Archon departed alone some time ago and ordered that he was not to be disturbed.\"","Xerathuna remained silent.","That wasn’t particularly unusual. At their level, disappearing for months or even years without informing anyone was hardly noteworthy. The stronger a cultivator became, the more carefully they concealed their movements, cultivation grounds, inheritances, and opportunities. Even within the Celestial Court, Archons were not required to report every place they visited. Still...","Von Brehalen had encountered Liam. He had marked him. And then he had vanished.","\"Interesting.\" Xerathuna’s fingers lightly brushed the golden mark between her brows.","Whatever reason Von Brehalen had for marking Liam no longer mattered. The bastard who had repeatedly slipped through her fingers had finally been branded with something he couldn’t easily remove, and he was hiding in a place whose location was already known.","Xerathuna walked toward the enormous doors. \"Prepare the gate.\"","The paladin raised his head. \"Esteemed Goddess?\"","\"I am going personally.\"","His expression changed. \"Would that be necessary? If the Divine Temple Sigil is stable, we could dispatch—\"","\"No.\"","The single word silenced him.","\"I have made that mistake enough times.\"","Xerathuna stopped before the doors, her expression turning cold. Every time she had treated Liam as an insignificant nuisance, something unexpected happened. The bastard had survived far beyond what his cultivation and background should have allowed, and Xerathuna had finally accepted that sending increasingly stronger subordinates after him was pointless. This time, there would be no next time.","\"I want him dead.\"","Divine light began gathering around her body.","The paladin bowed. \"Understood.\"","\"Once he’s dead, recover everything.\" Her eyes became colder. \"His spatial treasures. His artifacts. His inheritance. Everything he has touched since he entered the system training world.\"","\"Of course, Esteemed Goddess.\"","Xerathuna took another step before pausing. \"And send word ahead to Green Mountain. Tell that old bastard I am coming to collect a criminal marked by the Celestial Court. If he stays out of my way, I have no interest in his mountain.\"","The golden mark between Xerathuna’s brows slowly opened. An eye of pure golden light appeared beneath it. The paladin immediately lowered his gaze as an enormous divine pressure descended upon the chamber.","\"If they don’t interfere, then fine. Otherwise...,\" Xerathuna said softly, \"Green Mountain can lose more than one disciple.\"","The paladin bowed deeply. \"As you command, Esteemed Goddess.\"","Xerathuna walked through the doors. It was time to settle everything once and for all.","Meanwhile...","Another pair of golden eyes flashed open. The Oracle drew in a slow breath. \"It has begun.\"","A few feet away, the monk paused midway through stuffing something into his mouth. He chewed twice, swallowed, and looked over with a confused expression. \"What has begun?\"","The Oracle didn’t answer immediately. His golden eyes remained fixed on something far beyond the walls surrounding them, as though his gaze had crossed the enormous distance separating one world from another.","The monk frowned and then rolled his eyes. \"You’re doing that thing again.\"","The Oracle glanced at him. \"What thing?\"","\"Acting mysterious instead of answering a simple question.\"","The Oracle ignored the complaint.","The monk sighed and scratched his bald head. \"Fine. Don’t tell me.\" His fingers moved.","A few faint symbols appeared between them, rotating slowly as the monk began a casual divination. He had already guessed who this probably concerned, and rather than wasting his breath interrogating the Oracle, he decided to check for himself.","Then the monk’s expression changed. An absolute darkness swallowed the entire divination before the symbols shattered one after another.","The monk stared at his empty hand. Then he smiled bitterly.","The Oracle’s curiosity finally overcame his silence. \"What did you see?\"","The monk laughed. \"What else?\" He flicked away the remnants of the shattered divination. \"As usual. Pitch-black darkness! That bastard will never have a good ending.\""]},{"number":1461,"title":"Chapter 1461: I’m not going to stand in your way","paragraphs":["Back in the Green Mountain Sect...","The alchemy disciples were busy cleaning up the streets after the recent Dralura attack. Broken stone littered the roads, several buildings had partially collapsed, and scorch marks covered sections of the normally pristine district where the fighting had been particularly intense.","Groups of disciples moved between the damaged structures, clearing rubble and repairing whatever they could while the sect’s formation masters worked on restoring the defensive arrays.","The atmosphere was considerably gloomier than usual.","The attack itself had been bad enough, but that wasn’t what worried most of them. Thousands of disciples were still trapped inside the Treasure World, several portals remained unusable, and nobody knew when the situation would return to normal.","Then suddenly a bell rang.","DONG!","Several disciples stopped working. Another bell followed.","DONG!","This time, almost everyone looked up.","\"What’s happening?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"Another attack?\"","Weapons immediately appeared in several hands, but before anyone could panic, a voice amplified by mana spread throughout the district.","\"All disciples remain calm. There is no attack.\"","Everyone relaxed slightly. Then...","BOOOOOOM!","A massive golden pillar of light suddenly erupted from the highest mountain of the sect. The disciples froze.","One formation after another illuminated across Green Mountain, enormous runes spreading through the sky until a translucent barrier covered the entire sect. It wasn’t the hurried activation they had witnessed during the Dralura attack either. This time, every layer of Green Mountain’s ancient defensive formation was awakening.","The disciples stared upward.","\"What the hell?\"","\"Didn’t they say there wasn’t an attack?\"","\"Then why are the grand formations activating?\"","Nobody had an answer. High above them, powerful figures began appearing, including the elders, peak masters, and Grand Elders. One after another, they emerged from secluded cultivation grounds throughout Green Mountain and flew toward the main peak.","Some of the younger disciples had never even seen several of these figures before, yet now they were appearing in rapid succession. Inside the main hall, the atmosphere was even heavier.","An elderly man sat at the head of the chamber, dressed in plain green robes. His appearance was almost disappointingly ordinary, without any overwhelming aura or visible phenomenon surrounding him, but every elder present remained standing while he alone occupied a seat.","A golden message floated before him. The old man’s eyes moved slowly across the words. Then he snorted. \"Xerathuna.\"","Several elders exchanged glances. One finally stepped forward. \"Ancestor, the message was transmitted through a Celestial Court channel. They claim that one of our disciples is a wanted criminal bearing a Divine Temple Sigil and demand that Green Mountain surrender him immediately upon their arrival.\"","The old man scratched his beard. \"Demand?\"","The elder hesitated. \"That is the wording they used.\"","\"How polite.\"","Nobody mistook his tone for approval.","Another elder stepped forward. \"High Priestess Xerathuna is apparently coming personally.\"","Xerathuna wasn’t some ordinary priestess. Her name carried weight far beyond a single world, and if she had personally decided to descend upon Green Mountain for one disciple, then whatever trouble that brat had created was clearly much larger than they had realized.","The Green Mountain Ancestor, however, remained calm. \"What did the boy do?\"","The elders looked at one another, seeing if anyone had answers. Finally, someone cleared his throat. \"We are... still determining that.\"","The old man’s eyebrow rose.","\"You received a demand from the Celestial Court to surrender one of our disciples, activated every defensive formation on my mountain, dragged me out of seclusion, and none of you thought to determine what the boy actually did?\"","Several faces became awkward. \"Ancestor, the disciple has been difficult to locate. He’s inside the Treasure World.\"","\"Then ask him when he comes out.\"","The elders stared at him. One carefully said, \"Ancestor... Xerathuna specifically warned us not to interfere.\"","The old man looked at him. \"And?\"","The elder immediately shut his mouth.","The Green Mountain Ancestor leaned back in his chair. \"I don’t care what grudge she has with the brat. I don’t care what he stole, who he offended, or how many Celestial Court robes he pissed on.\"","Several elders coughed.","\"While he stands on Green Mountain, he is a disciple of Green Mountain.\"","The hall became silent.","\"If he committed some crime, she can present the evidence, and we will judge it ourselves. If she merely wants to kill one of my disciples because she dislikes him...\" The old man smiled. \"She can try.\"","Far below the main peak, the alchemy disciples knew none of this. They only knew that every ancient formation protecting their home had suddenly awakened. Then space above Green Mountain trembled.","A thin golden line appeared across the sky. Golden light poured through the line, widening it.","One of the alchemy disciples dropped the pile of rubble in his arms. \"Uh...\"","Beside him, another disciple swallowed.","The spatial crack continued expanding until it stretched across the heavens, and an enormous golden gate gradually emerged from within it.","Divine pressure descended. Even through Green Mountain’s formations, countless disciples felt their bodies grow heavy.","Before they could recover from the oppressive sensation, figures began emerging from the gate in a steady procession, first paladins clad in radiant golden armor and then priestesses wreathed in divine light, until dozens of powerful cultivators stood suspended above the sect.","The moment the final figure stepped through the gate, every paladin and priestess moved aside and lowered their heads in unison.","A breathtaking woman emerged from between them, dressed in flowing silver-white robes that fluttered gently around her slender figure, while her pale hair cascaded almost to her waist and a golden eye slowly opened between her brows.","High Priestess Xerathuna stepped into the sky above Green Mountain, and as her cold gaze swept across the sprawling sect beneath her.","She searched for only a moment before her voice passed effortlessly through the defensive formations and reached every corner of the sect.","\"Where is Liam?\"","Xerathuna waited above the sect with her hands loosely clasped behind her back, showing no sign of impatience as the golden eye between her brows moved slowly across the mountains below.","Although layers of defensive formations stood between her and the sect, she could still sense the Divine Temple Sigil somewhere within Green Mountain’s territory, which was more than enough to confirm that the information brought to her had been accurate.","The little rat was here.","Before she could attempt to pinpoint his exact location, however, an old voice drifted from the highest mountain and passed effortlessly through the formations separating them.","\"Xerathuna, you arrive above my sect with enough people to start a war, tear open space without permission, and immediately demand one of my disciples. Has the Celestial Court finally decided that basic manners are beneath it?\"","\"So you are still alive, old bastard.\"","A chuckle answered her, and a moment later, the doors of the great hall at the summit opened as an elderly man in plain green robes walked outside. His appearance was almost disappointingly ordinary compared with the divine spectacle filling the heavens.","The Green Mountain Ancestor continued forward until he reached the edge of the sect’s grand formation, where he stopped with his hands clasped casually behind his back. Several Grand Elders followed at a respectful distance, but he paid them no attention as he examined Xerathuna and the forces gathered behind her.","\"Unfortunately for you, I still have a few years left.\"","\"A few?\" Xerathuna’s lips curved slightly. \"Judging by that face, I would have guessed a few days.\"","The old man stroked his beard thoughtfully. \"And judging by your temperament, I would have thought someone would have beaten some manners into you by now, yet apparently both of us continue to defy expectations.\"","A few Green Mountain elders immediately found the distant scenery fascinating.","Xerathuna’s smile remained, although the divine pressure surrounding her quietly grew heavier. \"I didn’t come here to exchange insults with you.\"","\"That’s disappointing. You were always much better at that than diplomacy.\"","\"Enough.\"","The amusement disappeared from her face as she raised one hand, causing a golden sigil to materialize above her palm.","\"One of your disciples has been marked by the Celestial Court,\" Xerathuna said.","\"He has stolen property belonging to us, killed those sent to retrieve it, and repeatedly escaped judgment. Archon Von Brehalen encountered him recently and personally placed a Divine Temple Sigil upon his soul, which is the only reason that little rat finally became visible to us again.\"","The old man smiled. \"So what exactly did he steal?\"","\"His accomplishments are irrelevant. I informed you of my arrival as a courtesy because of our previous dealings, but I did not come here seeking permission. Surrender Liam to me, and the Celestial Court will leave without involving anyone else.\"","\"Sure. I’m not going to stand in your way.\" The old man simply chuckled as he spread one hand toward the vast sect beneath him. \"Feel free. Be. My. Guest.\"","Xerathuna stared at him for several moments, clearly having expected resistance after his earlier attitude, while several of the Grand Elders standing behind the ancestor looked equally surprised.","They had prepared themselves for an argument at the very least, perhaps even a confrontation with the Celestial Court if matters deteriorated far enough, yet their ancestor had apparently decided to step aside without demanding so much as an explanation.","What was going on here? Why did it feel as if his attitude made a sudden 180? Just a while ago, he had been determined to stand against the divine temple no matter who arrived in their sect, and now he was being this carefree? They simply did not understand."]},{"number":1462,"title":"Chapter 1462: Hello again","paragraphs":["A faint smile gradually returned to Xerathuna’s face. \"It seems age has finally taught you some wisdom.\"","\"Perhaps.\"","\"You should have answered that way from the beginning. It would have saved us both considerable time.\"","The old man merely smiled as he stroked his beard, which only made several elders behind him exchange confused glances. They knew their ancestor well enough to recognize when he was swallowing his pride for the sake of the sect, and whatever expression currently rested on his face certainly wasn’t that.","Xerathuna didn’t bother trying to decipher it. As far as she was concerned, Green Mountain had made the sensible choice, which meant there was no longer anything standing between her and the little rat who had escaped her grasp for far too long.","\"Go. Go and drag him out.\"","The paladin standing next to her immediately bowed and stepped forward. He only examined the area for a moment before identifying a portal in the southern part of the sect.","Three unfortunate Dralura had apparently chosen the worst possible time to enter Green Mountain. They had barely emerged from the swirling spatial passage when the paladin’s attention locked onto them.","The creatures immediately sensed the danger above them. Their heads snapped upward, and the moment they saw the golden-armored figure descending from the sky, mana erupted from their bodies.","However, whatever resistance they intended to offer never had the opportunity to materialize. The three exploded instantaneously.","The alchemy disciples nearby stared in stunned silence as the creatures that had caused so much destruction throughout Green Mountain died without even managing to launch an attack.","Just how strong was he.... a Dao Grand Master? Perhaps even a Dao King?","The paladin didn’t spare the corpses a second glance. Having confirmed that the portal was stable, he descended directly toward it, while several Green Mountain elders watched from a distance without interfering because their ancestor had already made his position perfectly clear.","The paladin landed before the portal and briefly examined the spatial fluctuations rolling across its surface. Whatever world existed on the other side seemed stable enough.","More importantly, the Divine Temple Sigil they were following was connected to whatever lay beyond it, which meant there was little reason to waste time searching anywhere else.","\"He’s through there?\" Xerathuna asked from above.","\"Almost certainly, Esteemed Goddess.\"","\"Then bring him to me.\"","The paladin bowed once more. \"As you command.\" He then stepped through. Spatial energy wrapped around his body, and the golden armor disappeared into the portal without the slightest hesitation.","The Green Mountain Ancestor watched the entire exchange from high above, his expression carrying an amusement that several elders found increasingly difficult to understand. One of the Grand Elders eventually approached him and lowered his voice, careful to ensure that the Celestial Court cultivators couldn’t easily overhear.","\"Ancestor, should we really allow him to enter the Treasure World?\"","The old man glanced at him. \"Didn’t you hear me? I told them I wouldn’t interfere.\" He simply shrugged and smiled. He then turned to look at the portal as if he was waiting for something.","Although the faint smile on his face made several elders suspicious, they could only follow his gaze and wait.","Xerathuna did the same, although for entirely different reasons. Her paladin was powerful enough that there should be very little inside the Treasure World capable of threatening him. As for Liam, she did not care for him very much. What she anticipated most was something else...","\"This shouldn’t take too long.\" Xerathuna sneered as she continued watching the portal, already imagining the condition Liam would be in when Caelvar dragged him back through it.","Paladin Caelvar had followed her for centuries, and although he was merely her second-in-command, his strength was more than sufficient to deal with someone like Liam.","The little rat had certainly accumulated several unusual treasures and escape methods, otherwise he could never have survived their previous attempts to capture him, but there was an enormous difference between escaping from pursuers and defeating someone at Caelvar’s level in a direct confrontation.","The Green Mountain Ancestor heard her comment but offered no response, and when Xerathuna glanced toward him, she found the old bastard still wearing that irritating little smile.","He appeared far more interested in the portal than concerned about what might be happening to his disciple on the other side, which briefly made her wonder whether he knew something she didn’t.","Before she could dwell on the thought, the portal suddenly fluctuated.","\"There,\" one of the priestesses behind Xerathuna said.","The spatial energy within the passage churned violently, and several of the Green Mountain elders immediately focused their attention upon it, expecting Caelvar to emerge with Liam in his grasp.","Instead, a young man wearing the robes of an inner disciple stumbled through, his face pale and his clothes covered in dust, and before anyone could understand what was happening, another disciple appeared behind him. Then another.","The portal erupted into activity.","Disciples began pouring through in groups, some supporting injured companions while others carried weapons, storage bags, or whatever belongings they had managed to preserve during their time inside the Treasure World.","Several looked exhausted enough to collapse the moment they reached familiar ground, yet as they realized that they were standing inside Green Mountain again, shock rapidly gave way to relief.","\"We’re back!\"","\"Green Mountain! We’re actually back!\"","\"Move away from the portal! There are more people behind us!\"","High above, several Grand Elders stared downward in disbelief.","\"Those are our disciples.\"","\"How did they get out?\"","\"There are hundreds of them...\"","\"More are still coming.\"","The Green Mountain Ancestor continued smiling without bothering to give any explanation. He stroked his beard and let out a hearty chuckle.","Xerathuna also looked surprised, but her surprise lasted only a moment before satisfaction appeared on her face. \"You can thank me for that.\"","Several Green Mountain elders turned toward her.","Xerathuna gestured casually toward the portal. \"Caelvar must have encountered your trapped disciples after entering and decided to send them out before dealing with Liam. He has always been unnecessarily considerate toward those who aren’t involved in our affairs.\"","One of the Grand Elders frowned as he looked between Xerathuna and the returning disciples, while another appeared as though he wanted to ask how Caelvar could possibly have located hundreds of trapped disciples, organized their return, and sent them through the portal within such a short period of time.","The Green Mountain Ancestor didn’t say anything. He merely continued smiling.","Xerathuna noticed. \"You find something amusing?\"","\"Not particularly.\"","\"Then perhaps a little gratitude would be appropriate. Your people apparently couldn’t retrieve these disciples themselves, yet my subordinate has already begun solving your problem within moments of entering.\"","The old man stroked his beard, but instead of answering, he continued staring at the portal with an expression that made Xerathuna’s irritation grow.","By then, the flow of disciples had begun slowing. Hundreds had already emerged, and after several more groups stumbled through, the portal remained empty long enough that the elders assumed the first wave had finished.","Then it fluctuated again. Every gaze returned to it.","Xerathuna’s lips curved upward. \"That should be Caelvar.\"","The spatial surface rippled. Something golden appeared within it.","Xerathuna’s smile widened as the object crossed the boundary, but almost immediately, something felt wrong. It was much too small to be a person, and rather than flying from the portal under its own power, it struck the stone pathway with a heavy thud before rolling forward.","Clank.","The object rolled several feet.","Clank.","It struck a piece of broken masonry, changed direction, and continued across the damaged street before gradually losing momentum. The surrounding disciples moved aside.","For several seconds, nobody understood what they were looking at, because the object was still covered by a battered golden helmet, although several deep cracks ran through the once-pristine metal. One side had been crushed inward, while blood leaked steadily from beneath its lower edge and painted a thin red trail across the stone.","The helmet finally tipped over. A face became visible.","Shock and horror appeared on Xerathuna’s face. \"Caelvar...\" The object lying in the middle of the street was Paladin Caelvar’s severed head.","His eyes remained open, frozen in an expression that contained none of the confidence he had displayed before entering the portal. Even the golden armor protecting his neck had been torn apart so completely that jagged fragments still clung to the ruined edges beneath his jaw.","The entire Green Mountain Sect seemed to fall silent.","Several of the priestesses behind Xerathuna visibly recoiled, while the other paladins stared at the head with expressions ranging from disbelief to outright horror.","They knew Caelvar’s strength far better than anyone in Green Mountain did, and precisely because they knew it, none of them could immediately comprehend how he had entered the portal alive only to have his head come rolling back out a short while later.","Xerathuna didn’t move. Her golden third eye had opened completely.","Divine light flooded from it as her perception slammed toward the portal, no longer carrying the casual confidence she had possessed only moments earlier. She searched for Caelvar’s aura, his divine imprint, his soul, anything that might tell her that what she was seeing was some sort of deception.","There was nothing. The connection was gone. Caelvar was simply dead.","Behind the Green Mountain Ancestor, one of the Grand Elders slowly turned toward him, finally understanding why the old man had been so content to let the Celestial Court handle its own problem.","The ancestor smiled again. \"It’s best for everyone to vacate to the grand hall for now. Your barriers will not be enough for what is about to come next.\"","The elders nodded and quickly followed the instruction.","\"Get everyone away from here. Take the disciples who just returned somewhere safe, treat the injured, and activate the inner formations around the main hall.\"","The next second, divine power suddenly exploded across the heavens.","BOOOOOOM!","Golden light flooded the sky as Xerathuna’s aura erupted without restraint, and the pressure was so violent that Green Mountain’s grand formation immediately responded. Countless runes brightened across the barrier while the mountains beneath them trembled.","Right at this moment, the portal flickered again, and once more someone emerged from within. It was a simple transcendent-rank disciple.","Just as an elder was about to bark at him and ask him to evacuate, Xerathuna’s voice boomed loudly. \"Little bastard, you are finally in my grasp.\"","Rage filled her eyes as she stared at the familiar face, the same insect from that backwater world that should not even be alive today. Liam was finally standing right in front of her.","\"Die!\" Xerathuna shot forward as an enormous golden palm materialized around her hand, its surface covered with countless divine inscriptions that illuminated one after another."]},{"number":1463,"title":"Chapter 1463: Impossible!","paragraphs":["Liam looked up. Divine pressure exploded all around him.","Xerathuna’s power descended, crushing the shattered stone beneath Liam’s feet into powder and forcing the surrounding mountains to groan beneath the weight.","Golden light spread across the sky in enormous waves, and within moments, the entire world above Green Mountain had disappeared behind a brilliant sea of divine energy.","Her aura alone was much stronger than the Archon’s. However, everything was different now.","Liam did not panic at all. He briefly exchanged a glance with the Green Mountain ancestor. The old man smiled and gave him a nod. Liam returned the greeting.","At the same time, another equally shocking divine wave erupted, but this time from Liam. Or rather, from another Liam who materialized right next to him.","BOOOOOOM!","White-golden flames exploded across the heavens. The oppressive divine pressure bearing down upon Green Mountain abruptly stopped descending as a second force collided with it head-on.","For a brief moment, the entire sky seemed to divide into two distinct worlds. Brilliant golden light dominated one side, while white-golden flames consumed the other, each carrying a terrifying Dao pressure that caused the space between them to twist and fracture.","The first soul avatar stood beside Liam. Its appearance was almost identical to his. White-golden flames flowed lazily around its body, occasionally sinking beneath its skin before emerging again.","The expressions of the Green Mountain elders changed immediately.","Several of them had already reached the entrance to the grand hall, yet they stopped and turned around despite the ancestor’s earlier warning. The younger disciples might not have understood exactly what they were sensing, but the elders certainly did.","\"A... a... Dao King?\"","Xerathuna didn’t move. She was in complete and utter shock. Her golden third eye focused upon the avatar.","The rage that had dominated her expression moments earlier was replaced with disbelief as her divine perception swept across the soul avatar. \"A soul incarnation?\"","Liam heard the uncertainty. His lips curved upward.","Her third eye opened wider as she attempted to penetrate deeper into the avatar’s structure, but what she found only made her expression become more serious.","It possessed an independent cultivation foundation, a powerful soul, a functioning Dao core, and a connection to Liam so deep that the boundary between master and avatar was difficult to define.","How did the rat manage to accomplish something like this? She gritted her teeth as her power exploded again. How could something like this happen? How could this mortal stand equal to her?","Her golden third eye blazed.","He wasn’t her equal.","He couldn’t be.","She had cultivated for countless years, crossed worlds, survived divine tribulations, crushed rivals who had once been considered unparalleled geniuses, and climbed through the ranks of the Celestial Court until entire worlds lowered their heads at the mention of her name. The distance separating her from the mortal she had encountered in that insignificant backwater world should have been so enormous that no amount of talent or fortune could possibly bridge it within such a short period of time.","Yet the evidence stood directly in front of her.","White-golden flames continued colliding with her divine aura, and no matter how much power she released, the other side refused to collapse. The soul incarnation merely stood beside Liam with an indifferent expression, its long flames rolling across the heavens while the Dao surrounding Green Mountain responded to its presence.","A Dao King.","A fucking Dao King.","And the mortal who had created it was still standing there with the cultivation of a Transcendent.","\"Impossible.\"","Liam’s smile widened. That single word felt surprisingly good.","He remembered running from her people. He remembered being hunted through that training world, desperately hiding his identity and calculating every possible way to survive while people far beyond his cultivation treated him like an insect that could be crushed whenever convenient.","Back then, Xerathuna had existed somewhere far above him. Now she was staring at one of his soul avatars and calling its existence impossible.","Liam couldn’t help himself. \"Nice to see you too.\"","Xerathuna’s face darkened. \"Do you think this changes anything?\" She snorted, and a staff appeared in her hand.","The weapon was nearly as tall as she was, its shaft forged from a pale golden material covered in inscriptions. At its crown rested a crystal resembling an enormous golden eye which immediately locked onto Liam.","Xerathuna wrapped her fingers around the staff, and the divine energy filling the heavens abruptly changed. The scattered golden light began gathering toward her. Her aura compressed. The pressure increased.","The first soul avatar reacted at the same moment. White-golden flames surged around its body as its gaze settled upon Xerathuna, and for the first time since materializing, it shifted into a genuine fighting stance.","Xerathuna smiled coldly. \"You have no idea what a Dao King is capable of.\"","The golden eye at the top of her staff opened.","DONG!","A deep resonance rolled through the heavens. The white-golden sea surrounding the soul avatar suddenly sank several meters as an even more terrifying divine pressure descended from above.","Green Mountain’s grand formation flashed violently in response, and dozens of mountains trembled as countless ancient runes appeared across their slopes.","Liam sighed and shook his head. \"Yes. You are correct. I still need more experience. Please teach this one also.\"","Xerathuna raised a brow at that unexpected response just as another powerful aura erupted. Her expression froze.","The new aura did not come from the first soul avatar. It came from Liam’s other side.","Black mist seeped into the air, followed almost immediately by streams of dark crimson energy that twisted through it like veins of blood. Shockingly, there was also divine energy in the mix.","As those three energies spread through the heavens, another figure gradually materialized beside Liam. Another Liam. The second soul avatar opened its eyes.","BOOOOOOM!","A third portion of the heavens changed. Golden divine light still covered Xerathuna’s side of the sky, while white-golden flames surrounded the first soul avatar, but now black and crimson energy surged upward beside them, carrying a second Dao King aura that crashed into the already unstable balance of power.","The effect upon Green Mountain was immediate.","KACHA! KACHA!","Cracks spread through several outer barriers before the sect’s ancient formations reinforced them, while mountains that had survived thousands of years began trembling beneath three competing Dao King auras. Even the laws surrounding the battlefield seemed to become chaotic as Fire, Divine, Demonic, and Blood Daos simultaneously fought for dominance.","Nobody spoke.","The Green Mountain elders simply stared.","The Grand Elder who had identified the first avatar as a Dao King slowly turned toward the Green Mountain Ancestor, his mouth opening and closing several times before he finally managed to speak.","\"Ancestor...\"","The old man raised a hand. \"Don’t ask.\" His lips slowly curled upward, and then he started laughing. \"Ha... hahaha...\"","Several elders looked at him.","The Green Mountain Ancestor slapped his thigh. \"This fucking brat!\"","Liam heard him and grinned. He stepped forward and casually stretched his shoulders. Two Dao Kings stood on either side of him while his own Transcendent cultivation remained almost laughably insignificant between their enormous auras.","\"Alright, this should be enough. Let’s end this all here.\""]},{"number":1464,"title":"Chapter 1464: A third soul avatar?","paragraphs":["DONG!","Xerathuna attacked with her staff. The golden eye embedded at its crown opened completely. An unimaginable quantity of power compressed around the staff. Hundreds of enormous golden inscriptions appeared behind Xerathuna and rotated around one another like the mechanisms of some celestial machine.","The two soul avatars moved simultaneously. The first disappeared within white-golden fire. The second dissolved into a mixture of black and crimson mist.","Xerathuna’s third eye flashed. She turned left.","CLAAAAANG!","Her staff intercepted the first avatar’s fist before it had completely emerged from the flames, and the collision produced a circular shockwave that ripped through the clouds for hundreds of kilometers.","White-golden fire erupted around the staff and rushed toward Xerathuna’s hands, but divine inscriptions immediately appeared across her skin and prevented the flames from reaching her.","The first avatar increased its strength. Xerathuna didn’t contest it. She tilted the staff by several degrees, stepped sideways, and allowed the avatar’s own momentum to drag its fist past her shoulder. Her free hand was already moving by the time it realized what had happened.","A golden palm struck its chest.","BOOOOOOM!","The first avatar vanished into the distance. Xerathuna immediately thrust her staff backward. The second avatar materialized behind her at almost exactly the same moment. The golden eye at the end of the staff slammed into its abdomen.","KACHA!","Half its torso disappeared. The second avatar didn’t retreat. Its remaining hand caught the staff. Demonic energy surged from its palm, followed immediately by crimson Blood Dao energy that crawled along the pale-golden weapon.","Xerathuna’s expression changed. The two soul avatars were not easy to deal with at all.","White-golden flames swept through the space where her head had been an instant earlier as she appeared several hundred meters above them. Her fingers formed a complicated seal, and the enormous divine formation behind her immediately rearranged itself.","\"Celestial Prison.\"","Golden lines appeared across the sky. The second avatar released the staff just as space around both avatars divided into thousands of perfectly geometric sections. Golden barriers materialized between those divisions, transforming several kilometers of the heavens into an enormous three-dimensional prison.","At the same time, Xerathuna sent an attack towards Liam. \"Fool, puppets are only puppets. You are not a King yet. You will always be the insignificant rat that died at my hands!\"","The golden eye atop her staff flashed. A needle-thin ray of divine light shot across the battlefield.","Xerathuna had compressed a Dao King’s power into a line barely thicker than a finger. More importantly, she had timed the attack perfectly.","The two avatars were trapped inside the Celestial Prison, and although the barriers were already beginning to crack beneath the first avatar’s white-golden flames, neither could possibly break free and cross the distance before the attack reached Liam.","Xerathuna smiled. She had already understood the nature of his ability.","Those incarnations were powerful, perhaps absurdly so, but the little rat himself was still a Transcendent. His body, soul, and cultivation had not suddenly become those of a Dao King simply because he had somehow created two of them.","Kill the original, and everything ended.","However, the next second, her smile disappeared.","CLANG!","The needle-thin ray of divine light stopped less than a meter from Liam’s forehead.","Xerathuna’s eyes widened. A sword had appeared in its path.","The weapon looked almost ordinary at first glance, with a long silver blade and a simple dark hilt, yet the Dao King’s attack that should have pierced straight through Liam had somehow been stopped at its tip.","Golden light screamed against the edge as the surrounding space fractured, but the sword remained perfectly steady. A hand was wrapped around its hilt.","Xerathuna’s gaze slowly moved upward to look at the wielder. Her heart dropped when she saw the familiar face.","Another Liam stood in front of the original.","His clothes were plain, his expression calm, and unlike the other two soul avatars, there were no raging flames, demonic clouds, or rivers of blood surrounding him. He simply held the sword with one hand while staring at the divine ray pressing against its edge. Then he moved his wrist.","SHING!","The divine ray split apart. Two streaks of golden light shot past Liam from either side and disappeared into the distance, where they pierced through several mountains before finally dissipating.","The sword avatar lowered its weapon. An incredibly powerful sword aura emerged from its body.","Xerathuna’s face stiffened. Even the Green Mountain elders were shocked. They had barely recovered from the appearance of the second soul avatar when another wave of Dao pressure swept across the sect.","Compared to the violent manifestations of the first two, this aura was remarkably restrained, yet the moment it appeared, every sword within Green Mountain reacted.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","Thousands of swords trembled inside storage rings, weapon halls, disciples’ hands, and sealed caves. Some began humming against their sheaths, while others pulled toward the sky as though responding to something they instinctively recognized.","Several Sword Peak elders shot to their feet. One elderly swordsman stared at the figure standing before Liam, and his expression gradually transformed from confusion into disbelief.","\"Sword Dao... Such pure sword dao...\"","The avatar raised its sword. An invisible line seemed to extend from the blade all the way to Xerathuna, and although nothing had actually crossed the distance between them, her third eye contracted as an instinctive sense of danger ran through her.","The old swordsman’s lips trembled. \"Another Dao King.\"","Xerathuna staggered back. Who were Dao Kings?","They were existences who stood at the summit of countless worlds.","Reaching the Transcendent realm was already enough for an ordinary cultivator to leave lesser worlds behind and begin pursuing the true Daos. Dao Lords could establish great factions, Dao Generals could dominate entire regions, and Dao Masters were powerful enough that even major forces treated them with respect.","As for Dao Grand Masters, every single one represented an accumulation of talent, resources, fortune, and countless years of cultivation that ordinary beings could scarcely comprehend.","But Dao Kings were different. The leap from Dao Grand Master to Dao King was a chasm that had buried countless geniuses.","A cultivator had to push their understanding of the Dao beyond comprehension alone and establish an authority that could directly impose itself upon the laws of the world.","Their soul underwent another qualitative transformation, their Dao foundation became terrifyingly difficult to destroy, and their lifespan was measured on a scale that allowed entire mortal civilizations to rise and disappear while they remained in secluded cultivation.","Even within the Celestial Court, Dao Kings were not disposable soldiers.","They were entrusted with worlds, armies, temples, and territories spanning distances that mortals could not cross in a lifetime.","When disputes between beings of this level escalated into genuine battles, whole worlds could be destroyed as collateral damage, which was precisely why Dao Kings rarely fought without considering the consequences.","Xerathuna herself had spent an unimaginable amount of time reaching this realm. She remembered every bottleneck, every tribulation and every near-death experience.","Even someone like Von Brehalen, who had only recently entered the Dao Grand Master realm, had already been considered an extraordinary existence worthy of becoming an Archon of the Celestial Court.","Given enough time, resources, and fortune, perhaps he could eventually have attempted the step into Dao King. Yet the mortal standing before her had somehow crossed that distance three times without even crossing it himself.","Her third eye moved toward the Celestial Prison.","BOOM!","White-golden flames struck another barrier. The entire prison trembled.","Another Dao King.","Her gaze shifted toward the black and crimson figure beside it, whose destroyed torso was already reconstructing itself while demonic, vampiric, and divine energies circulated through its foundation.","Another Dao King.","Then she looked toward the swordsman standing protectively before Liam. The third avatar hadn’t moved.","Its sword remained lowered beside its body, yet the Sword Dao surrounding Green Mountain continued gathering toward it. Thousands of swords throughout the sect trembled in response, and the longer Xerathuna examined the avatar, the more uncomfortable she became.","Its aura was too pure. There were none of the unstable fluctuations she would have expected from someone who had recently entered the realm. Its cultivation didn’t feel borrowed or forcibly elevated, nor did it resemble a temporary secret technique that sacrificed foundation in exchange for power.","It genuinely possessed the foundation of a Dao King.","Three fucking Dao Kings!","Xerathuna slowly looked past the sword avatar. Liam stood behind it with his hands clasped behind his back. He was still just a transcendent from a backwater world. How could he possibly accomplish something like this? Did he perhaps make that heavenly treasure submit?","\"What are you?\" She mumbled as panic and dread filler her eyes. She had made a mistake. She had underestimated this person terribly. She had allowed him to live for too long. And now she was going to pay for everything.","Just as her mind scrambled, suddenly crimson portals opened up all around her.","\"Did you miss me, sweetheart?\" A sweet voice resounded as a dashing young man stepped out."]},{"number":1465,"title":"Chapter 1465: The armies arrive","paragraphs":["Liam knew exactly who it was. It was the same Blood Prince guy. Was he and the priestess in some sort of relationship? Considering how fucked up everyone involved seemed to be, Liam couldn’t exactly rule it out. Not that it mattered to him.","Xerathuna’s reaction only made him more curious. The panic that had begun creeping into her expression disappeared almost immediately, replaced first by surprise and then to fake happiness?","Liam could only stare in shock as he watched the high and mighty priestess turn into a damsel in distress in a single second.","If Liam hadn’t personally watched her screaming about insignificant rats while trying to murder him less than a minute ago, he might actually have believed that she was some graceful celestial maiden welcoming her beloved after a long separation.","The Blood Prince appeared to be enjoying every second of it.","Liam almost respected the shamelessness.","Xerathuna moved slightly closer to the Blood Prince. \"Your timing couldn’t have been better. This man murdered several members of the Celestial Court and has repeatedly escaped judgment. I was just about to deal with him when—\"","\"When three Dao Kings appeared?\" The Blood Prince’s crimson eyes moved past her.","Xerathuna’s smile stiffened.","The sword avatar stood silently before Liam, its silver blade still lowered, although its Sword Dao remained locked upon both newcomers. Farther away, the Celestial Prison continued shaking as white-golden fire and black-crimson energy attacked it from within.","Xerathuna tightened her fingers around his hand. \"They are merely soul incarnations.\"","\"Whatever strange technique he has used, his real cultivation is still only Transcendent. If we destroy the original, the incarnations should collapse with him.\"","\"Even if they are not, I will still take care of them for you, my love. You know I would do anythng for you.\"","Xerathuna shook her head. \"No, my dearest. I don’t want you to risk your life. This is my fate. This is my struggle. I have to defeat this evil with my own hands.\"","\"Nonsense. You will do no such thing.\"","\"But... I... I really don’t want to risk your life, my love. What if he uses some unorthodox technique?\"","\"My angel, relax. I can end this rat in a single attack but just for you, I will summon the entire blood court. Alright? Are you happy now?\"","Xerathuna smiled as the Blood Prince gently stroked her head. However, when her cold gaze met Liam’s, the softness disappeared from her eyes and was replaced by naked contempt.","A backwater piece of shit would always remain a backwater piece of shit. A few lucky encounters could never amount to anything before true power.","So what if he had somehow created three Dao King soul incarnations? So what if he had obtained some ancient inheritance or even managed to subdue that mysterious heavenly treasure?","The fact that he possessed such things only proved that his luck was heaven-defying, while the fact that he had displayed all of them before her proved that he was still the same ignorant fool who had no understanding of the forces he was provoking.","He had spent his entire existence struggling upward from some insignificant mortal world. She had the Celestial Court behind her. And now, because of his own stupidity, he was about to face the Blood Court as well.","Xerathuna almost wanted to laugh. While the blood prince summoned the vampire court, Xerathuna had already summoned the entire celestial court.","Sure, the bastard might have had a fighting chance if he had overwhelmed her instantly and done something. But he had played all his cards wrong, and now his time was up. She had been frightened for nothing.","\"Your fate will not change. You will die and rot here today.\" She smiled as numerous portals opened up all over the Green Mountain.","The first were crimson. They tore through space one after another until enormous blood-red rifts covered half the sky, each of them releasing such dense Blood Dao energy that the sunlight itself seemed to take on a crimson hue.","Ancient formations appeared around the portals and locked them into place, while enormous silhouettes gradually became visible beyond them. Then came the gold.","DONG!","A bell resounded from somewhere impossibly distant. The sound passed through the world itself.","Golden circles appeared across the other half of the heavens, expanding rapidly until they formed enormous gates covered in divine inscriptions. Some were hundreds of meters tall, while others stretched for kilometers, and behind every gate stood rows upon rows of figures dressed in silver-white armor and ceremonial robes.","All of a sudden, two entire elite armies belonging to factions that stood at the very top of the cosmos were arriving on a single world. The scale of it was almost impossible to comprehend.","Green Mountain had existed for an unimaginably long time, and although its disciples traveled beyond their home world, fought in secret realms, and occasionally encountered powerful outsiders, the world itself remained insignificant when viewed against the vastness of the cosmos.","It possessed no legendary resources that could attract the attention of supreme factions, nor was it positioned along some vital inter-world route worth fighting over. Yet now the Celestial Court and the Blood Court were both descending upon it.","DONG!","Another golden gate opened. Thousands of Celestial paladins marched through in perfect formation, their individual divine auras merging into a single overwhelming presence. Behind them came priestesses, Archons, ancient war chariots, and enormous floating temples whose shadows stretched across entire mountain ranges.","WOOOOONG!","The crimson portals answered.","Vampire legions poured through them by the thousands as gigantic blood-red warships pushed their way across the spatial boundary. Ancient vampires who had ruled territories for longer than some civilizations had existed appeared one after another, while terrifying crimson auras spread across the opposite half of the heavens.","The sky was being divided before everyone’s eyes. Gold on one side. Crimson on the other.","The sheer concentration of powerful cultivators had begun affecting the world itself. Spiritual energy churned violently, spatial fractures appeared and disappeared across the upper atmosphere, while the laws surrounding Green Mountain strained beneath the presence of beings that this world had never been meant to accommodate in such numbers.","On the outside, this whole sector of the cosmos was suddenly in chaos.","Had a cosmic war begun? Had Green Mountain discovered some supreme inheritance? Had an ancient treasure appeared?","News spread at a terrifying speed. Green Mountain’s world might have been insignificant on the cosmic scale, but the surrounding region was anything but empty.","Hundreds of inhabited worlds were scattered throughout the nearby void, connected through spatial passages, teleportation formations, trading routes, and territories controlled by factions of varying strength.","The moment the Celestial Court began opening large-scale gates, every sufficiently powerful organization in the region detected the spatial disturbance. Then the Blood Court arrived. That was when everything escalated.","On a prosperous cultivation world several spatial crossings away, an enormous communication formation erupted with light inside the palace of a local dynasty. The emperor had been discussing border disputes with his ministers when one of his intelligence officers rushed into the hall without waiting for permission.","\"Your Majesty! Massive spatial activity has been detected in the Green Mountain sector.\"","The emperor frowned. \"From whom?\"","\"The Celestial Court.\"","Silence immediately descended over the hall. Before anyone could properly react, another intelligence officer rushed inside. \"Your Majesty! The Blood Court has also opened large-scale passages into the same world!\"","The emperor stood so quickly that his throne cracked beneath his hand. \"Both?\"","\"Yes!\"","The emperor’s expression changed completely. \"Close the spatial borders.\"","\"But our merchants-\"","\"Fuck the merchants! Shut down every long-distance spatial formation connected to that sector and recall anyone important enough to recall. If those two factions are starting a war, I don’t want a single ship from this dynasty anywhere near it.\"","Orders spread immediately. The same scene repeated across world after world. Ancient sects activated emergency formations. Merchant organizations redirected entire fleets.","Independent cultivators who had been traveling toward Green Mountain’s region abruptly changed destinations, while information brokers began paying absurd prices for even the smallest fragment of reliable intelligence.","Within an hour, countless communication networks were flooded with reports. The Celestial Court had mobilized. The Blood Court had mobilized. Multiple Dao King presences had been detected. Elite forces were crossing between worlds. The destination was Green Mountain.","Nobody knew why. That last part drove everyone insane. If a supreme treasure had appeared, they needed to know what it was.","If the Celestial Court and Blood Court were beginning a war, every major faction needed to know why, because a conflict between powers of their scale could redraw territories across enormous regions of the cosmos.","If Green Mountain had somehow offended both... Then everyone wanted to know what kind of suicidal lunatic was running Green Mountain.","Rumors multiplied faster than facts could catch them. Some claimed an inheritance belonging to an existence above the Dao King realm had appeared beneath Green Mountain.","Others insisted an ancient tomb had opened. One particularly popular rumor claimed Green Mountain had discovered a primordial weapon capable of destroying entire worlds.","Another claimed that the Celestial Court had secretly attacked the Blood Court and that Green Mountain was merely where the retaliation had begun.","Within another hour, someone confidently announced that an ancient Celestial princess had eloped with a Blood Court prince and hidden herself inside Green Mountain. That particular rumor spread disturbingly quickly.","Regardless, many started taking note of this event. A few rogue Dao Kings started teleporting to Green Mountain. Other empires also started sending their top experts.","Dao Kings were not fruits growing on trees for every random empire to possess a dozen, but the ancient clans, supreme sects, immortal dynasties, and other great powers spread throughout the surrounding regions naturally had monsters of their own.","More importantly, many of those monsters had been alive for an absurdly long time. It was natural for these factions to possess a good deal of Dao Kings. Though not everyone was available at the moment, some took note and became interested. No one wanted to miss a heavenly treasure in case something like that had popped up in Green Mountain.","So many more started teleporting into Green Mountain. Now it was not just the Blood Court and the Celestial Court. There were all sorts of forces.","Some newcomers arrived through enormous teleportation formations that announced their identities from the moment they appeared, while others slipped quietly through tiny spatial cracks and concealed themselves somewhere far from Green Mountain.","There were ancient clans whose names were recognized across hundreds of worlds, imperial dynasties that had survived for millions of years, supreme sects whose territories stretched across entire star regions, and solitary cultivators who belonged to absolutely nobody.","Naturally, none of them were stupid enough to immediately join the confrontation. Most stopped far away.","Some remained beyond Green Mountain’s defensive formations, while the more cautious ones didn’t even enter the world itself, choosing instead to hover within the surrounding void and observe through treasures capable of piercing enormous distances.","WOOOONG!","A massive blue formation suddenly unfolded several thousand kilometers from Green Mountain, covering the sky like an enormous flower. Nine figures emerged from its center, led by a middle-aged woman wearing dark-blue robes embroidered with silver stars.","Several Green Mountain elders recognized the emblem on her shoulder.","\"Nine Star Palace...\"","Before they could recover, space distorted elsewhere.","KACHA!","A black crack split the heavens. An enormous golden chariot burst through it, pulled by six creatures resembling winged lions. Hundreds of armored cultivators accompanied it, and an old man sat cross-legged at the center with his eyes closed.","\"Golden Lion Dynasty.\"","Another formation activated. Then another. And another.","The arrivals spread across the horizon until the Green Mountain elders stopped trying to identify everyone. Some came alone. Others brought entourages.","A few ancient clans apparently decided that subtlety was for poor people and arrived aboard enormous ships that immediately began competing with the Blood Court and Celestial Court for space in the upper atmosphere.","The world became absurdly crowded."]},{"number":1466,"title":"Chapter 1466: Give me a show I will not forget in this lifetime","paragraphs":["Finally, the Green Mountain Ancestor could no longer hold it in. He threw his head back and broke into loud, raucous laughter that rolled across the surrounding peaks. \"Brat, you have done it! You are going to completely destroy my world, aren’t you?\"","Liam awkwardly smiled. \"I apologize. Please accept the treasure land world as compensation. I have completely cleared it out.\"","The Green Mountain ancestor’s eyes sparkled with a mysterious glint. \"Completely, huh? Then I assume you have achieved what you set out to achieve.\"","\"Indeed, senior, I have.\"","\"Are you sure about this? I can still help you teleport out of this mess.\"","Liam smiled and bowed a little. He knew exactly how much the ancestor would have to sacrifice to get him out of a situation like this. He was grateful that the ancestor still offered to help him. However, he firmly shook his head.","\"Senior, I have no intention of leaving this place. I have run for a long time. I want to stop running now.\"","The ancestor became silent for a moment. He then nodded. \"Go. Fight to your heart’s content. Give me a show I will not forget in this lifetime.\" He then turned around and activated a teleportation formation. All of the sect members gathered in the great hall immediately used this formation and left the world.","The ancestor did not leave. Instead, he found himself a comfortable place atop one of the distant peaks and sat down, casually producing a wine gourd as though he were preparing to watch an entertaining tournament rather than a confrontation involving some of the strongest forces in the cosmos.","Liam lightly chuckled, turning his attention to the many forces gathering in the world.","With the Green Mountain disciples gone, the sect suddenly felt strangely empty despite the absurd number of cultivators filling its skies.","Golden fortresses belonging to the Celestial Court occupied one side of the heavens while crimson warships belonging to the Blood Court stretched across the other.","Between those two enormous forces were representatives from ancient clans, dynasties, supreme sects, and organizations that had traveled across enormous distances merely to discover what could possibly have caused such a gathering. More continued arriving.","Spatial passages opened throughout the upper atmosphere, while others appeared beyond the world itself as the more cautious factions chose to observe from a distance.","Ancient cultivators concealed themselves within folded layers of space, communication treasures transmitted everything they witnessed toward distant worlds, and countless divine senses repeatedly swept across Green Mountain as information about the confrontation continued spreading throughout the surrounding regions.","Yet for all the cultivators now occupying his home, Liam was almost completely alone.","Liam stood between two of the greatest factions in the cosmos with only his three soul avatars, two of them caged, and compared with the armies surrounding them, the four identical figures looked almost insignificant.","Xerathuna naturally noticed this as well.","Her earlier unease gradually disappeared as she watched the last traces of Green Mountain’s teleportation formation fade. The old bastard had chosen not to interfere, exactly as he had promised, while Liam had inexplicably refused the opportunity to escape and remained behind to face her.","Did he really think possessing a few soul incarnations was going to help him survive this? She gnashed her teeth, wanting to already be done with all of this. The rat bastard had bothered her long enough.","The Blood Prince also finally spared a glance to take note of Liam. \"So that’s him?\" He muttered indifferently.","Xerathuna glanced toward him. \"Yes.\"","\"Don’t worry, I will take care of him. I will also make sure whatever treasure he stole from you returns to your hands.\"","\"Yes, my love. I trust you.\" Xerathuna sweetly smiled.","Around them, the other factions were reaching similar conclusions. Most had arrived because the simultaneous mobilization of the Celestial Court and Blood Court suggested that something extraordinary had happened within Green Mountain. However, now their attention shifted.","Everyone started paying attention to the insignificant young man standing at the center of everything. Questions spread rapidly.","Who was he?","Why did the Celestial Court want him?","Why was the Blood Court involved?","And why did three Dao Kings have exactly the same face as a Transcendent?","Liam could feel the divine senses examining him from every direction. Some disappeared the instant his misty-white eyes turned toward them, while others belonged to cultivators powerful enough that they didn’t bother hiding their curiosity. He ignored all of them.","Liam’s gaze moved toward Xerathuna. She was already watching him. Neither spoke.","The distance between them was enormous, yet Liam could clearly see the satisfaction gradually returning to her face as more Celestial forces emerged through the golden gates behind her.","Perhaps she thought his decision to remain was arrogance, or perhaps she believed he had finally realized there was nowhere left to run.","Liam didn’t particularly care which explanation she preferred. He had already made his decision. He was going to fight today. He was going to fight with everything he had, and he was going to see this all to the very end.","Now the only question was when should he...","Snapping him out of his thoughts, a disturbance caught his attention. Liam initially did not care about it, as spatial passages had been opening left and right, almost continuously for some time, but something about this one felt strangely familiar.","His gaze shifted toward the distant sky as a relatively modest portal stabilized between two mountain peaks, looking almost laughably unimpressive compared with the colossal gates and formations surrounding it.","A man stepped through. He took perhaps three steps before stopping.","As soon as Liam saw him, his expression immediately changed.","Derek!","So many questions instantly flooded his mind? Where did he go? How was he doing now? Was he too late for Derek, just like he had been for Mia? Did he also suffer just like Mia did?","But before he could do anything, Derek himself teleported right next to him, silently standing by his side.","Liam looked at him. The two of them exchanged glances. There was no need for anything else to be said. Liam could see it was still the same Derek after all these days. His gaze then fell on the giant axe resting on Derek’s back. The weapon had a mysterious gleam to it.","It looked like Derek had personally gone through something and won in the end. His heart raced in excitement. He always knew Derek was meant for great things. This only proved it.","\"Welcome back, brother.\"","Derek smiled. \"Good to be back.\"","Liam chuckled. Good to be back? To get slaughtered? And yet the man was genuinely happy.","There were countless things Liam wanted to ask him, and judging from the way Derek’s eyes briefly moved over the three soul avatars, there were probably just as many questions going in the opposite direction.","Neither of them chose to ask anything now, however, because this was hardly the place for catching up after a long separation. Still, Liam couldn’t stop himself from taking another look at Derek. He had changed.","The difference wasn’t merely his cultivation, although that had clearly undergone a tremendous transformation.","There was a steadiness to Derek that hadn’t been there before, something Liam recognized immediately because he had seen the same thing countless times in cultivators who had been pushed to their limits and somehow emerged from the other side.","Whatever had happened after they separated, Derek hadn’t spent that time peacefully cultivating somewhere.","\"How did you know to come here right now?\"","\"That oracle guy sent me a message. I completely lost track of time in that place, but thanks to him, I was able to recover and get out.\"","Liam was a little surprised, but he also knew why Kedan was going above and beyond. \"I don’t need you here, you know. You can go back home. Your family has missed you a long time.\"","Derek shook his head with a firm smile. \"I am right where I belong.\"","Countless divine senses immediately shifted toward the newcomer, attempting to identify his cultivation, origin, faction, or anything else that might explain why he had crossed the battlefield without hesitation and positioned himself beside the person both supreme factions had apparently come for.","Several ancient cultivators searched their memories for Derek’s face and came up empty, while others became far more interested in the enormous axe resting across his back.","Xerathuna barely spared him a second glance. One more person hardly mattered.","If anything, she found it amusing that Liam’s acquaintances were beginning to crawl out of whatever holes they had been hiding in. Let them come. Once Liam was dead, anyone foolish enough to stand beside him could be dealt with according to how deeply they had involved themselves.","Soon another interesting spatial disturbance emerged.","The heavens several thousand kilometers away suddenly darkened as enormous amounts of demonic energy poured through a rapidly expanding spatial fracture.","Unlike the countless controlled teleportation passages that had been opening throughout Green Mountain, this one seemed to force itself directly through the surrounding spatial restrictions, tearing open a jagged wound that spread several kilometers across the sky.","The Celestial Court reacted immediately.","Golden formations illuminated across several fortresses while ranks of paladins turned toward the disturbance, their combined divine energy surging in response to the unmistakable demonic presence.","Two figures stepped through. Both were women. Both were demons.","Many were shocked to see the demons suddenly showing interest in this sector, but among everyone, Liam was the most surprised. How could he possibly not recognize them? His two wives!"]},{"number":1467,"title":"Chapter 1467: I sentence you to death","paragraphs":["The moment the two demonesses spotted him, whatever imposing presence they had maintained while stepping through the spatial fracture disappeared. Their eyes lit up.","\"Husband~~ We have suffered a lot all these days without you~~ How could you forget about us?\"","Before Liam could react, both women had already grabbed onto him.","\"Husband, you abandoned us for so long!\"","\"Do you know how worried we were?\"","\"We thought something terrible happened to you!\"","\"Something terrible did happen to me.\"","Neither appeared particularly interested in that explanation.","Xerathuna’s face twitched. What the hell was this?","She had mobilized the Celestial Court, the Blood Prince had brought the Blood Court, and enough powerful cultivators had gathered around Green Mountain to turn this insignificant world into the center of attention for half the region.","Yet these two women had somehow turned the entire confrontation into a fucking family reunion.","More irritatingly, Liam didn’t seem particularly bothered by it.","One demoness had practically wrapped herself around his arm, pressing tightly against his side while complaining about how heartless he was, while the other hugged him from behind with her chin resting comfortably on his shoulder.","\"Husband, you have become thinner.\"","\"I haven’t.\"","\"You have.\"","\"How could you possibly know?\"","\"We know everything about Husband.\"","Eventually, Liam cleared his throat and gently disentangled himself from the two women. \"Can you both wait until we go back home?\"","The two demonesses paused. They looked at Liam, then at each other, and the word home seemed to immediately improve their mood. After everything that had happened and all the time they had spent apart, they both wanted nothing more than to go back home with him.","\"Husband is taking us home?\"","\"Of course.\"","The two women instantly became obedient.","\"Okay!\"","\"We can wait.\"","Liam smiled. \"Good.\"","They finally released him, although neither went particularly far. One settled on his left while the other moved to his right. If they couldn’t cling to their husband, standing close enough to immediately resume doing so later was an acceptable compromise.","Watching the scene, Xerathuna scoffed. \"Pathetic. Do you really think your handful of allies are going to save you? You are only leading them to their death. You are going to die and rot here. They will also be joining you!\"","Liam chuckled. \"I really don’t want more company. But I think... I have a feeling some more are arriving.\"","Just as he finished speaking, another portal opened up. Shockingly, a little girl came running out of the portal. Following her was a man who seemed like a butler. \"Miss Itzel, Miss Itzel, wait. You cannot come out by yourself. Your sisters will kill me. Miss Itzel, please.\"","\"No, Karim. The message said big bro needs my help. I have to go immediately. Big bro. Big bro!\" The little girl looked around, and finally, when her gaze landed on Liam, a brilliant smile bloomed on her lips.","\"Big bro!\" The little girl completely ignored the various factions surrounding and ran over to Liam and tightly hugged him. \"Big bro! Why did you give me a different name? I have been searching for you all these days!\"","Liam smiled bitterly. He remembered all too well who this little girl was. It was the little friend he had made back when he had visited the Milky Way auction house city through the game.","He later on learned that it was a very real place and was actually located outside the game world, but going there would have been a dead giveaway. This was why he had chosen to wait.","\"My friend, the Oracle, sent you here?\"","\"Yes, he did.\" Itzel beamed. \"Big bro, that person is a little naughty, but I think he is a good guy.\"","Liam chuckled. \"Do you know something? You are a very good judge of character.\"","\"Hmmm?\"","Liam laughed and hugged her. \"You always know who to make friends with.\"","\"Why wouldn’t you say that?\" Another chilly voice sounded as a woman walked out of the same portal. \"Taking advantage of my little sister, are we?\"","People were already starting to suspect with the appearance of the little girl, but now that with the entrance of the second party, no one had any doubts.","\"Hey, isn’t this the young mistress of the Milky Way auction house?\"","The woman who had stepped through the portal was breathtakingly beautiful, but that was hardly enough to attract attention among cultivators at this level.","What mattered was her identity. Several ancient experts recognized her immediately, and those who didn’t quickly received answers from the people around them.","\"The Milky Way Auction House?\"","\"That Milky Way Auction House?\"","\"Who else could it be?\"","\"What are they doing here?\"","The whispers rapidly spread. Xerathuna’s face fell. She knew exactly who the Milky Way family were.","Their strength alone wasn’t the problem. The Celestial Court had stood at the summit of countless worlds for far too long to be frightened simply because another ancient force had appeared.","What made the Milky Way family troublesome was that they had spent an absurd amount of time building relationships with practically everyone worth knowing.","Supreme sects bought from them. Ancient clans sold through them. Top dynasties borrowed from them, invested through them, stored treasures with them, and used their auction houses to quietly move resources that they didn’t want appearing in official records.","Even the Celestial Court had dealt with them before. More importantly, nobody truly knew how deep their foundation went.","The Milky Way Auction House presented itself as a merchant organization, but only an idiot would believe an organization capable of operating safely across so many worlds had survived purely because people respected commerce.","Xerathuna’s gaze became colder. Why were they here? Her eyes moved toward Itzel. The little girl was still hugging Liam. Then there was that woman...","The woman had already appeared in front of Liam. Her eyes first fell upon Itzel, who was still happily hugging Liam, before slowly rising toward Liam himself. Her expression remained perfectly composed, but the coldness in her eyes made it abundantly clear that she hadn’t forgotten him.","Itzel immediately looked between them. \"Big sis, I found him!\"","Liam smiled awkwardly. \"I really did not call her here.\"","The woman laughed coldly. \"Oh? You didn’t mean to call her here and get out of whatever this is by using our family name?\"","Her gaze briefly swept across the battlefield, taking in the golden fortresses, crimson warships, gathered Dao Kings, and the countless factions watching from every direction before returning to Liam.","Itzel nodded enthusiastically beside him. \"Big Bro didn’t call me! The naughty Oracle did.\"","Her sister looked down at her. \"And how exactly did this Oracle know you?\"","Itzel blinked. \"He found me.\"","\"Of course he did.\"","Karim finally managed to reach them and immediately bowed toward the woman. \"Young Mistress, I apologize. Miss Itzel opened the portal before I could stop her. I tried to convince her to wait for the others, but she-\"","\"It was my idea,\" Itzel interrupted.","The woman sighed as if she was tired. She then completely ignored Liam and Itzel and instead addressed the many people gathered here. \"Whatever is going on here today, me and our family has nothing to do with it. We will not interfere.\"","Several cultivators who had become nervous at the appearance of the Milky Way Auction House visibly relaxed, while Xerathuna’s expression eased slightly as well. This was the response she had expected from an organization like theirs. Merchants survived because they understood when to involve themselves and, more importantly, when to stay out of conflicts that had nothing to do with them.","The Blood Prince smiled faintly. \"A sensible woman.\"","The young mistress didn’t acknowledge him. Instead, she looked toward Karim. \"Take Itzel back.\"","Karim immediately straightened. \"Yes, Young Mistress.\"","Itzel’s eyes widened. \"No.\"","The young mistress’s eyebrow twitched. \"Itzel.\"","\"No.\"","\"We are going home.\"","\"No!\"","\"Itzel.\"","\"Big Bro needs help!\" The little girl tightened both arms around Liam as though Karim might attempt to drag her away at any moment.","Her sister took a slow breath. \"He has somehow managed to involve himself in a dispute between the Celestial Court and the Blood Court. That has nothing to do with us.\"","\"It has something to do with Big Bro and Big Bro has something to do with me.\"","The young mistress stared at her.","Itzel stared right back.","Liam could almost see the argument becoming increasingly dangerous. He quickly placed a hand on Itzel’s head. \"She’s right.\"","Itzel immediately looked up at him in betrayal. \"Big Bro!\"","Liam smiled. \"You came to see me. You found me. That’s enough.\"","\"But the Oracle said you needed help.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","Itzel looked around. She slowly examined the Celestial Court and then the Blood Court. Then the numerous Dao Kings spread throughout the surroundings before finally looking at the two soul avatars still imprisoned within Xerathuna’s Celestial Prison. Her gaze returned to Liam. \"You don’t look fine.\"","Liam coughed. \"Appearances can be misleading.\"","\"No.\"","\"No?\"","\"You are surrounded.\"","That was difficult to deny. Liam glanced around once before nodding thoughtfully. \"I suppose I am.\"","Itzel’s sister gave him a flat look. \"You suppose?\"","Liam ignored her. He crouched slightly so that he was closer to Itzel’s height. \"Listen. I really didn’t call you here, and I definitely don’t want your family getting involved because of me. Whatever happens next is something I need to deal with myself.\"","Itzel frowned. \"But we’re friends.\"","\"We are.\"","\"Good friends?\"","\"Very good friends.\"","\"Then I should help.\"","Liam smiled. \"Do you see the grandpa sitting on the mountain there? Why don’t you go and sit with him? Your big bro will show you something soon. It will be very nice to watch.\"","Itzel immediately turned toward the distant mountain.","The Green Mountain Ancestor was still sitting comfortably upon the peak with his wine gourd in hand, seemingly completely detached from the confrontation below. The old man had been watching everything with obvious amusement, and when Itzel’s gaze landed on him, he lifted the gourd slightly in greeting.","Itzel looked back at Liam. \"Really?\"","\"Really.\"","\"What are you going to show me?\"","Liam’s smile widened. \"A surprise.\"","Her eyes immediately lit up. \"I like surprises!\"","\"I know.\" Itzel finally released him, although she still looked somewhat reluctant to leave. \"Will Big Bro come over afterward?\"","\"Of course.\"","\"Promise?\"","\"Promise.\"","That seemed to settle everything. Itzel turned toward Karim. \"Let’s go!\"","Karim stared at her. A moment ago, he had been practically begging the heavens for some way to remove her from the center of the battlefield, yet now she was willingly leaving because Liam had promised to show her something. He looked toward Liam with a complicated expression.","\"Thank you.\"","Liam nodded solemnly. \"You’re welcome.\"","The young mistress, however, wasn’t nearly as relieved. Her eyes narrowed at Liam. She then turned towards the celestial court and the blood court. \"What did he do?\"","Xerathuna calmly answered. \"He stole property belonging to the Celestial Court, murdered those sent to retrieve it, repeatedly resisted judgment, escaped from my hands, and continued slaughtering members of the Court afterward. Most recently, he murdered an Archon.\"","She then personally raised her voice and continued. \"I have no idea why so many people have gathered here to witness a relatively simple matter, but allow me to make one thing clear. The Celestial Court has no quarrel with any of you.\"","\"Whatever rumors brought you here are irrelevant. There is no ancient inheritance being opened today, nor is the Celestial Court declaring war upon the Blood Court or any other faction. We are here for one person.\"","Her golden eyes settled upon Liam. \"Him.\"","Liam smiled. That seemed to irritate her even more.","Xerathuna continued, \"Those who wish to watch may watch. Those who wish to leave may leave. But anyone who interferes in the Celestial Court’s judgment will be treated as having willingly involved themselves in this matter.\"","Itzel’s sister gave a nod and then continued walking. She joined Itzel and Green Mountain in the distance.","Several factions exchanged glances. Most of them had come because the simultaneous appearance of the Celestial Court and Blood Court had made it seem as though something extraordinary had happened on Green Mountain. Rumors of ancient inheritances, primordial treasures, secret realms, and even the birth of something beyond the Dao King realm had already spread across countless communication networks.","If all of this really was because of one man... that too a transcendent... It was definitely not worth getting involved. Many started backing away.","Xerathuna smirked. This was exactly what she wanted.","The vultures who had rushed here hoping to pick up some benefit were finally beginning to understand that there was nothing for them to gain. Several spatial passages had already opened in the distance, while the weaker factions retreated farther from Green Mountain, unwilling to risk becoming collateral damage in a conflict involving multiple Dao Kings.","There was no need for them to be here. More importantly, there was no need for them to see what Liam possessed.","Once he was dead, she would personally search every spatial treasure on his body, tear apart his soul if necessary, and find out exactly how a mere Transcendent had managed to create three Dao King soul incarnations.","Next to her, the blood prince patted her on the back, reminding her. \"I think we have waited long enough. Why don’t we just end this quickly so everyone can go about their business?\"","\"Of course, my love.\" Xerathuna smiled and then turned to Liam, her eyes cold. \"You have committed multiple crimes against the Celestial Court. You stole from us, murdered our people, resisted judgment, and even killed an Archon. By the authority granted to me as High Priestess, I sentence you to death.\"","\"And here I thought you will never start!\" Liam chuckled.","Xerathuna’s blood boiled. A mere insect dared to be this arrogant in front of her? Today she would show him what is heaven and what is trash! Without another word, she initiated the first attack.","The next second something shocking happened. Liam took out something from his spatial ring. A few herbs. About a hundred SSS ranked herbs to be more precise.","In front of everyone, he packaged each bundle of herb into different vials and sent out all the vials in different directions. Immediately all hell broke loose."]},{"number":1468,"title":"Chapter 1468: Trapped","paragraphs":["Hundreds of divine senses swept across the vials flying in every direction, and the moment they penetrated the thin protective formations Liam had placed around them, the expressions of the watching cultivators changed. They all panted like dogs in heat rushing forward at full speed.","\"SSS-ranked!\"","\"That’s a Nine-Revolution Soul Lotus!\"","\"There’s a Heavenly Marrow Fruit in that one!\"","\"Move!\"","BOOOOOOM!","The battlefield exploded. Cultivators who had been retreating turned around so violently that several nearly collided with their own people. Spatial passages that had been seconds away from closing were abandoned, ancient warships changed direction, and dozens of figures shot toward the scattered vials.","The weaker cultivators weren’t even given a chance. Dao Lords and Dao Generals were blasted aside by the pressure of Dao Masters. Dao Masters cursed as Grand Masters passed over them, while several of the Dao Kings who had been observing from a dignified distance suddenly seemed to forget every trace of their previous dignity.","An old man tore through three spatial barriers and grabbed one vial. \"Hahaha! Mine!\"","A golden hand immediately descended from above. \"Old bastard, put it down!\"","\"Fuck off!\"","BOOOOOOM!","The two collided.","Elsewhere, five cultivators reached another vial simultaneously. Nobody bothered negotiating. The sky descended into complete chaos.","Xerathuna’s attack stopped halfway. She stared at the scene. Then at Liam. \"You—\"","Liam smiled. \"Sorry. You were saying something?\"","Xerathuna’s face twisted. He had done that deliberately. \"If you think that just this much is enough to escape your fate today, then you are sorely mistaken. You are to die here!\"","\"Honey, calm down. I will take care of him.\" The blood prince smiled charmingly. \"This mortal here has truly tested you, so I will let you take your time with this kill.\"","The next second, five blood effigies towered Liam, completely surrounding him.","Each stood hundreds of meters tall, their bodies formed from condensed crimson blood that flowed continuously beneath translucent skin. They possessed no faces, only smooth heads and enormous humanoid bodies, yet the moment they appeared, the pressure around Liam multiplied several times over.","Multiple tendrils shot from the effigies towards Liam and, in the blink of an eye, bound him completely. The crimson tendrils wrapped around his arms, legs, waist, and neck. They tightened until his body was almost completely hidden, while the five enormous effigies stood around him like pillars supporting some grotesque crimson prison.","Another effigy engaged the Sword dao avatar, and two more kept Derek and the demonesses occupied. In just a second, it seemed as if Liam’s entire effort went to shit. He was completely trapped.","\"There you go. He is all yours now, my love.\" The blood prince smiled.","Xerathuna smiled coyly. \"You spoil me too much, my love.\" She then slowly descended.","Golden divine energy curled around her body as she passed between the enormous blood effigies, and unlike the countless cultivators still tearing the battlefield apart for Liam’s herbs, she had eyes for only one person.","Liam.","The crimson tendrils had wrapped around almost every part of him. His arms were pinned against his sides, his legs were bound together, and another thick strand had wound around his throat tightly enough that faint cracks already appeared beneath his skin.","His Sword Dao avatar couldn’t reach him. Derek couldn’t reach him. The two demonesses couldn’t reach him. Even his other two ridiculous incarnations remained locked inside her Celestial Prison.","Finally, the rat had nowhere left to run.","Xerathuna stopped directly in front of him. \"You know, I have imagined this moment several times.\"","BOOM!","Golden energy struck Liam’s stomach. Blood sprayed from his mouth.","One of the demonesses exploded with demonic energy and tried to break past the blood effigy blocking her path, only for another crimson arm to sweep down and force her backward.","Derek roared and swung his axe.","BOOOOOOM!","The effigy facing him staggered several kilometers, half its torso splitting apart beneath the blow, but before Derek could pursue, the damaged sections liquefied and immediately began reconstructing.","The Sword avatar was having the same problem.","Every time its silver blade severed part of the effigy opposing it, the creature simply turned into blood and reformed. Worse, the blood wasn’t merely regenerating; it was spreading around the avatar, continuously forcing it farther from Liam.","The Blood Prince watched everything with obvious satisfaction.","\"There, sweetheart. Take your time.\"","Xerathuna’s expression softened immediately as she glanced at him. Her head then snapped back to Liam, a cold sneer appearing on her face.","\"You are done. You are trapped. You have nowhere to run and no one to help you. Oh, don’t worry. I won’t kill you just yet. You will stay with me for a long time as my personal puppet. Now let’s get your soul baptised, shall we? From now on, I will be your God and your master.\"","She took another step forward when suddenly Liam looked up and smiled. \"Are you sure?\" He mumbled.","\"Hmmm?\"","\"Are you sure that I am the one who is trapped?\" A cold, murderous glint flashed in Liam’s eyes as he completely revealed all of his killing intent.","A chill ran down Xerathuna’s spine as she unwittingly took a step back. What was he saying? What did he mean? Wasn’t he completely overpowered? What other secret card could he possibly have?","\"Have you become delirious, you fool-\" Before she completed her sentence, someone appeared behind her.","Xerathuna turned to see a familiar face. Her heart instantly dropped. For some reason, she had a bad feeling. She immediately teleported back to the Blood Prince for safety.","\"He-\" She opened her mouth when she noticed that even the man in front of her had frozen in shock. The Blood Prince seemed even paler than usual as he stared at something with utter disbelief on his face.","Xerathuna swallowed as she turned to see what was going on, and when her gaze finally landed on the scene awaiting her, her mind instantly exploded.","There was another Liam.","He stood exactly where Xerathuna had been only moments earlier, dressed in simple dark robes with his hands resting casually behind his back. There was no crimson tendril wrapped around him, no blood effigy restraining him, and no trace of injury on his body. His face was identical to Liam’s, but what made Xerathuna’s heart sink wasn’t his appearance.","It was his cultivation. He was a Dao King.","Before she could process that fact, another figure appeared beside him. Then another. And another.","Each one had Liam’s face.","Some wore white robes. Others wore black, crimson, gray, blue, or simple clothes without any distinctive markings at all. One carried a spear across his shoulder. Another held a massive black saber. One had his hands tucked into his sleeves like some wandering scholar, while another stood surrounded by faint arcs of lightning that distorted the surrounding space with every movement.","However, every single one released the aura of a Dao King.","And the insanity did not stop.","Dao King auras began appearing faster than anyone could count.","Twenty.","Thirty.","Fifty.","The heavens trembled.","The countless cultivators who had been fighting over Liam’s SSS-ranked herbs froze where they stood. One elderly Dao King still had his hand wrapped around another man’s throat, while the other had a sword pressed against his stomach, yet neither seemed capable of remembering why they had been fighting.","Both stared toward Liam, toward the many Liams all over the place. There were seventy, eighty, a hundred? No one dared to count anymore.","Each aura alone could dominate an ordinary world. Each represented a cultivator who had crossed a boundary countless geniuses spent hundreds of thousands of years trying and failing to reach.","Now they were appearing one after another, all with the same face, and all surrounding the battlefield. How could a single being even accomplish something like this? Was this a nightmare? How could this be possible?","She was the prodigal high priestess. She was the Goddess whom her entire faction worshiped. How could this rat possibly stand above her?","Xerathuna’s mouth slowly opened. \"No.\"","Another group appeared above the Celestial Court’s golden fortresses. More appeared behind the Blood Court’s warships.","\"No... This isn’t possible.\"","Xerathuna’s thoughts became increasingly frantic as another dozen Liams appeared in the distance.","She had personally hunted him. She remembered exactly how weak he had been, how desperately he had fled from her, and how many ridiculous tricks he had needed simply to survive whenever she closed in on him. Back then, killing him would have required almost no effort and now...","How long had it been since then? A few years?","To her, that amount of time was nothing. She had once spent longer than that meditating upon a single flaw in one divine technique, while some of her breakthroughs had required thousands or even tens of thousands of years of accumulation.","And this bastard had somehow created hundreds of Dao Kings?","\"No...\"","Her divine sense swept across them again. She had to be mistaken.","There had to be an illusion somewhere, some formation manipulating her perception or some heavenly treasure temporarily projecting false cultivation. Perhaps only a handful were real, while the rest were empty shells designed to frighten them.","Her third eye opened fully. Golden divine light swept across the battlefield. However, no matter how many times she scanned, there was only one truth. They were real.","\"Impossible...\" She looked around in a daze at the utterly ridiculous scene unfolding in front of her. This man was a true monster. Liam was not the one who was trapped. They all were."]},{"number":1469,"title":"Chapter 1469: Slaughter","paragraphs":["In the midst of this madness, two Dao Kings accompanied Derek and the two demonesses, teleporting them to the distant place where the Green Mountain ancestor, the little girl, her sister, and the butler were already seated. That group was not faring all that better.","The Green Mountain ancestor was also dumbstruck. He truly hadn’t expected something like this. He had asked for a show, and the brat had given him a spectacle!","Itzel was having the exact opposite reaction. \"Big Bro!\" She shot to her feet and pointed excitedly toward the battlefield. \"Big Sis! Look! Look! There are so many Big Bros!\"","Her sister didn’t respond. Her sister was staring at the sky with an expression Itzel had almost never seen on her face. Complete bewilderment.","Karim wasn’t doing much better. As someone who had served the Milky Way family for many years, he had accompanied its members across worlds and met beings whose names alone could alter the price of resources across entire regions.","The Auction House’s business naturally brought him into contact with powerful cultivators, and while he himself couldn’t claim to stand at their level, he at least knew enough to understand what he was looking at. That knowledge wasn’t helping. If anything, it made everything worse.","\"Young Mistress...\" He opened and closed his mouth speechlessly.","When Derek and the two demonesses arrived next to them along with the two soul avatars, the whole group sat together in shock and awe, slowly trying to digest what was happening. They did not know whether to stare at the five Liams now standing guard around them or at the chaotic, unbelievable scene unfolding in front of them.","Not just them, but many beings on the battlefield were beginning to question whether what they were seeing was real.","These weren’t inexperienced cultivators who could be frightened by a little pressure.","Many had lived for tens or even hundreds of thousands of years, traveled across countless worlds, witnessed the rise and destruction of great factions, explored ancient ruins, survived secret realms, and encountered geniuses whose names had once shaken entire regions.","Several were Dao Kings themselves, ancient monsters who had reached a level of cultivation most beings could only dream about. Yet none of that experience helped them understand the scene before them.","Across the battlefield, the fighting over Liam’s herbs had almost completely ceased. Cultivators who had been willing to tear each other apart moments earlier now floated silently with priceless vials still clutched in their hands, their attention entirely consumed by what was happening around them.","Even those who had successfully obtained SSS-ranked treasures had forgotten to celebrate.","An old man slowly looked down at the vial in his hand. Then toward Liam. Then back at the vial. His expression became complicated. A terrifying thought had occurred to him.","This bastard had just thrown around a hundred treasures like this simply to prevent people from leaving. What kind of fucking wealth allowed someone to do that? More importantly, why had he wanted them to stay?","And then it began.","The hundreds of soul avatars simply moved, and people started dying.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","The first explosion came from the western edge of the battlefield, where seven avatars descended upon one of the Blood Court’s enormous crimson warships. The ancient vessel had crossed countless worlds and survived wars between supreme factions, its hull reinforced with formations powerful enough to endure attacks from Dao Grand Masters.","It lasted less than three seconds.","A Liam surrounded by violent arcs of purple lightning appeared above the vessel and brought one hand down. Lightning spread across the entire warship like a living web, instantly overloading hundreds of formations, while two more avatars tore through the weakened barriers from opposite sides. Before the vampires aboard could react, another Liam appeared beneath the vessel and punched upward.","KARAKABOOOOOM!","The kilometer-long warship folded in half.","Crimson metal, broken formations, and thousands of vampires scattered through the sky as the vessel exploded. Several powerful figures managed to escape the initial destruction, only to discover three more Liams already waiting outside.","There was nowhere to go.","Across the battlefield, the Celestial Court suffered the same fate.","\"FORMATION!\"","A Celestial commander roared as dozens of golden arrays activated simultaneously. Thousands of paladins moved with extraordinary discipline, their divine energy connecting together until an enormous golden barrier covered several floating temples and war chariots.","For a moment, the formation looked magnificent. Then a Liam carrying a black spear appeared above it. A thin black point appeared in the center of the barrier. Then cracks spread outward.","KACHA!","The entire formation shattered. Five avatars descended through it. The sky became gold and blood.","The Celestial Court had numbers. It had discipline. It had ancient formations, powerful artifacts, terrifying war machines, and cultivators who had conquered worlds beneath its banner.","None of that changed one simple fact. Most of them weren’t Dao Kings. The difference was horrifying. A Dao Lord couldn’t meaningfully interfere. A Dao General could barely withstand the pressure. Dao Masters survived longer, while Grand Masters might actually exchange several attacks depending on their foundations and treasures.","But when dozens upon dozens of genuine Dao Kings descended simultaneously?","They died, and thousands of years of cultivation disappeared along with them in seconds.","BOOM!","A golden chariot exploded.","BOOOOOOM!","A crimson fortress split apart.","KARAKABOOOOOM!","Three Celestial formations collapsed simultaneously as a massive blade of condensed wind tore across hundreds of kilometers.","Everywhere the watching cultivators looked, there was another Liam.","One avatar moved through a formation of vampires without carrying any weapon at all. Every time he touched someone, their body withered and collapsed, while another Liam behind him swept his hand through the air and released a sea of blue flames that swallowed an entire Blood Court battalion.","A Celestial Archon intercepted the flames. \"Impudent!\" His divine staff struck downward. The flaming avatar raised one hand.","BOOOOOOM!","The Archon’s expression changed when his staff stopped. Another Liam appeared behind him. The Archon sensed him and spun instantly, golden divine energy exploding from his body. It was too late. A palm struck his back, and his divine armor shattered.","He shot forward directly toward the first avatar, who caught him by the throat. For one horrible moment, the Archon found himself suspended between two identical faces. Then both attacked.","BOOM!","His body disappeared. The soul tried to escape, but it didn’t get far. Misty-white energy swept across it. The Archon’s soul vanished into Liam’s grasp. Several ancient cultivators watching from a distance noticed that detail. Their expressions became even stranger.","An elderly Dao King narrowed his eyes. The old man looked across the battlefield more carefully. He realized the massacre wasn’t random.","Whenever a sufficiently powerful cultivator died, one of Liam’s avatars collected the soul almost immediately. Spatial rings, weapons, rare artifacts, and valuable materials were left behind as trash, but the soul was collected instantly. The man’s mouth twitched.","Was this bastard looting souls while slaughtering supreme factions in the entire sector? Where did this monster even come from?","He did not have time to think as another Liam appeared in front of him. \"Fuck!\" The guy’s heart dropped, and a moment later, his head dropped to the ground.","A woman holding a Nine-Revolution Soul Lotus immediately threw the vial away as if it had burned her hand. \"I don’t want it!\" She turned and fled. Three Liams appeared in front of her. Her face went white. \"I have nothing to do with the Celestial Court!\" She died anyway.","Blood rained, and the entire world trembled. Yet no one was able to escape. It did not matter which faction, family, or sect they were from. It looked like everyone gathered here was simply sentenced to death."]},{"number":1470,"title":"Chapter 1470: The true might of a soulweaver","paragraphs":["The Blood Prince’s gaze swept across the hundreds of Liams surrounding the battlefield, yet unlike everyone else, there was no fear in his eyes. The initial shock had disappeared. In its place was cold arrogance.","\"So this is your great trump card?\"","The remaining cultivators turned toward him.","The Blood Prince looked at the shattered Blood Court warships, the mountains of corpses, and the hundreds of Dao King soul avatars steadily closing around him. His expression grew colder with every passing second, but there was still no desperation.","Instead, he seemed offended. \"Do you truly believe this is enough to destroy me?\"","The Blood Prince raised his head. \"What exactly do you think I am?\"","Crimson energy began leaking from his body. At first, it seemed no different from the Blood Dao aura he had already displayed. Then the surrounding Dao Kings began noticing something wrong.","Their Daos were reacting. The lightning surrounding one of Liam’s avatars suddenly became unstable. Several sword avatars felt their blades tremble. The divine laws surrounding Xerathuna bent away from the Blood Prince, while the enormous sea of blood covering the battlefield abruptly became perfectly still.","The Blood Prince took one step forward.","DONG!","The entire world sank. Mountains collapsed beneath an invisible weight. Spatial fractures that had covered the heavens were forcibly compressed, while cultivators below Dao Master dropped from the sky by the thousands.","Even Dao Grand Masters staggered. The Dao Kings barely remained standing.","The Blood Prince’s crimson eyes glowed. \"I am the Blood Prince.\"","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!","His aura erupted. The heavens turned crimson.","An enormous pillar of blood-red light tore through the sky and continued upward until it disappeared beyond the world itself. The laws surrounding Green Mountain screamed beneath the pressure, and the ancient formations buried throughout the sect activated simultaneously as they struggled to prevent the whole world from exploding.","The hundreds of Dao King avatars surrounding the Blood Prince were forced backward. For the first time since Liam had revealed his army, the encirclement was pushed outward.","Across the battlefield, every surviving Dao King froze. They knew this pressure. Or, at the very least, they knew what it represented.","The difference between Dao Grand Master and Dao King was already a chasm that buried countless geniuses.","But above the King stood another throne.","An existence whose Dao no longer merely established authority within the laws surrounding it, but could suppress the authority of other Dao Kings through sheer superiority.","A realm that countless Dao Kings pursued for hundreds of thousands of years without ever touching.","Someone whispered the words. \"Dao... Emperor.\"","Then the entire battlefield erupted.","\"DAO EMPEROR?!\"","\"Impossible!\"","\"The Blood Prince broke through?!\"","\"When?!\"","Ancient monsters who had remained relatively composed even after seeing hundreds of Dao Kings finally lost that composure.","A Dao Emperor had appeared. That changed everything. Hundreds of Dao Kings were an army capable of terrifying supreme factions.","A Dao Emperor was a calamity.","Several of the oldest cultivators present looked genuinely frightened. They understood better than anyone that cultivation at this level could no longer be measured through simple numbers.","A hundred ants couldn’t necessarily kill a dragon simply because there were a hundred of them. And Dao Kings were certainly no ants. But neither was a Dao Emperor merely a stronger Dao King.","The Blood Prince slowly floated upward.","His crimson robes fluttered around him as an enormous blood-red crown materialized above his head. Behind him, the blood filling the battlefield rose from the shattered mountains and ruined warships, forming a crimson ocean that stretched beyond the horizon.","His five blood effigies changed as well. The Sword Dao avatar that had been fighting one of them tightened its grip upon its blade. The effigy moved.","BOOM!","The Sword avatar disappeared. A moment later, it smashed through seven distant mountains. The watching cultivators sucked in cold breaths.","The Blood Prince didn’t even look toward it. His eyes scanned the battleground for the real Liam. \"Do you understand now? I admit you surprised me. Hundreds of Dao King incarnations. Even I have never encountered such an absurd technique. But surprise is all you’ve accomplished.\"","Crimson pressure descended.","BOOOOOOM!","Dozens of Liam’s avatars immediately released their Daos to resist, but it was simply impossible.","The Blood Prince smiled coldly. \"You gathered an army of Kings, but I am an Emperor. Learn to bow in front of me.\" With each of his words, more and more soul avatars started to explode.","Far away, Xerathuna stared at the blood prince.","Her silver-white robes were torn. Golden blood stained her face, her carefully maintained hair had fallen into disorder, and the divine radiance that normally made her appear untouchable had weakened considerably.","She looked like she had already died once. She had watched her Court slaughtered. She had watched hundreds of Dao Kings appear from nowhere. She had experienced something she hadn’t truly experienced in longer than she could remember, true desperation.","For those few terrible minutes, Xerathuna had genuinely believed she was going to die. She was fucking going to die at the hands of a transcendent rat.","She was the High Priestess of the Celestial Court, a woman worshiped as a goddess across countless worlds. Yet she had watched her forces collapse while Liam’s identical faces multiplied across the heavens until there seemed to be no end to them.","Every new Dao King had driven her a little deeper into despair, until even the possibility of escape had begun to feel distant. Then the Blood Prince revealed his true cultivation.","Dao Emperor.","Color slowly returned to Xerathuna’s face as she stared at the crimson figure floating above the battlefield. The suffocating pressure that had been crushing her chest finally loosened. Relief washed through her so powerfully that her legs almost weakened beneath her.","Then another Liam exploded.","BOOOOOOM!","Crimson pressure crushed the avatar from every direction, breaking apart its Dao authority before tearing through the soul body itself.","The avatar resisted, white-golden energy erupting desperately around it, but the difference in cultivation was simply too great. Cracks raced across its body before it burst into countless particles of soul energy. Another followed. Then another.","Xerathuna watched them disappear, and the terror that had dominated her expression slowly transformed into something else. The familiar arrogance she had carried for countless years began returning with every avatar that shattered.","Of course. How could she have allowed herself to become so frightened?","Hundreds of Dao Kings were terrifying, but cultivation had never been a simple game of numbers. The higher one climbed, the more meaningless such comparisons became, because every great realm represented a transformation that those beneath it could barely comprehend.","Liam had created an army of Kings. So what?","An Emperor stood before them.","Xerathuna straightened her back as golden divine energy once again gathered around her battered body. Her robes remained torn, blood still stained her face, and most of the Celestial army she had brought here was either dead or desperately trying to survive, but none of that seemed quite as important anymore.","Liam would die.","That single certainty made everything bearable. A smile slowly spread across her face.","However, all of that lasted only for a mere second. Before she could even feel the full relief of seeing Liam’s impossible army collapse, something changed.","The soul energy released by the destroyed avatars did not disperse. All of it started rushing towards a single glowing avatar. Immediately, Xerathuna felt it. Everything was once again about to change, and then it happened.","The avatar began to transform.","At first, the change was almost impossible to notice because its cultivation remained firmly within the Dao King realm. The Blood Prince’s pressure continued suppressing it along with every other avatar, yet the enormous amount of soul energy pouring into it showed no sign of stopping.","One destroyed avatar.","Then another.","Then ten more.","Every time the Blood Prince crushed one of Liam’s soul avatars, the resulting energy crossed the battlefield and entered the same body. The glowing avatar absorbed everything without hesitation, and with each new influx, the aura surrounding it became denser.","Xerathuna’s newly recovered smile slowly disappeared. \"What is he doing?\"","The Blood Prince heard her, but he didn’t answer. His crimson eyes had already locked onto the glowing avatar, and for the first time since revealing his true cultivation, the cold arrogance was wavering.","He could feel it too. Something was accumulating. The Blood Prince raised his hand and deliberately increased the pressure upon the battlefield.","BOOOOOOM!","Another dozen avatars exploded. Their soul energy immediately rushed toward the glowing Liam. This time, everyone saw it.","Streams of brilliant energy crossed the ruined heavens from every direction, twisting around the avatar before sinking into its body. Then suddenly, a powerful aura erupted from the soul avatar.","BOOOOM!","Crimson light exploded across the heavens.","For the briefest moment, everyone assumed the Blood Prince had attacked again. The color was almost identical to his own power, and the thick scent of blood that suddenly filled the world carried the unmistakable authority of the Blood Dao.","Then the Blood Prince’s expression changed. The crimson ocean behind him trembled. He hadn’t commanded it.","Every vampire who remained alive on the battlefield felt their blood surge violently through their veins, while the weaker members of the Blood Court dropped to their knees before they even understood what was happening. Their bloodlines were reacting instinctively to the presence emerging before them, recognizing an authority that stood far beyond that of a Dao King.","At the center of the phenomenon stood Liam.","Or rather, one of his soul avatars.","The avatar’s appearance hadn’t changed much, but his pale skin now carried faint crimson patterns while his misty-white eyes had become a deep, almost black shade of red. Two elongated fangs appeared when his lips parted, and behind him the accumulated soul energy continued compressing until an enormous crimson moon slowly manifested in the heavens.","Itzel’s sister stood up in shook. The Green Mountain ancestor dropped his gourd. They both could see what was happening but they simply couldn’t believe it.","The last traces of his Dao King aura disappeared. What replaced them made the surviving cultivators stop breathing. A Dao Emperor! Another Dao Emperor had emerged in this world!","A Dao King had actually broken through to become a Dao Emperor right in front of their eyes!","The Blood Prince’s expression darkened. \"You...\"","The crimson Liam looked at him. \"You said I had to bow to you?\"","There had been no heavenly tribulation, no desperate attempt to comprehend a higher realm, and none of the long accumulation that normally preceded such a breakthrough. Liam had simply gathered the energy of his destroyed avatars into a single body, and somehow, impossibly, that body had crossed the boundary.","The Blood Prince gritted his teeth. Before he could react, another powerful aura erupted somewhere in the distance.","This time golden inscriptions appeared behind him. Xerathuna’s third eye snapped open. She felt her Divine Dao respond. Her face turned white. \"Stop him!\"","The Blood Prince was already moving. He crossed the battlefield instantly, crimson energy gathering around his hand as he appeared directly above the divine avatar.","There was no arrogance in his movements anymore. He brought his palm down with enough force to collapse the surrounding space. But before it could reach the soul avatar, the crimson Liam appeared. \"Your opponent is me.\"","The Blood Prince’s palm crashed into the crimson Liam’s raised fist.","BOOOOM!","The collision tore the heavens apart. Crimson light swallowed everything for thousands of kilometers as two Blood Dao authorities collided head-on, forcing the enormous ocean suspended above Green Mountain to divide down the middle.","The crimson Liam was pushed backward.","His arm cracked beneath the Blood Prince’s overwhelming power, crimson fractures spreading from his fist toward his shoulder, yet he never lost control of his body. He twisted in the air, stopped himself, and before the Blood Prince could continue toward the Divine Dao avatar, the crimson Liam stepped forward again.","The Blood Prince’s eyes narrowed. \"You think breaking through makes you my equal?\"","\"No.\" The crimson Liam glanced at his damaged arm as the fractures slowly closed.","\"I’m new at this.\"","The Blood Prince’s expression became colder. \"Then know your place.\" His body disappeared. Another terrifying aura erupted.","The crimson Liam moved at almost the same instant. Their figures vanished from the perception of everyone below Dao King, and even the Dao Kings could barely follow the crimson flashes colliding across the heavens.","Every impact shattered another section of space, while mountains hundreds of kilometers away collapsed beneath shockwaves that hadn’t even been directed toward them.","The difference between them became obvious almost immediately.","His control over the Blood Dao was vastly more refined, his movements carried the instinctive precision of someone who had fought with this power for an absurd length of time, and every exchange forced the crimson Liam backward.","Within seconds, cracks had spread across the avatar’s chest and one side of his face, while the Blood Prince remained almost untouched.","Yet the crimson Liam kept coming.","Every time the Blood Prince attempted to disengage and attack the Divine Dao avatar, he appeared in front of him again. When the Blood Prince tried to move around him, dozens of Dao King avatars interfered from every direction, forcing him to destroy them before continuing.","And every avatar he destroyed became more soul energy.","Soon, a pillar of divine energy erupted and the unmistakable aura of another Dao Emperor emerged."]},{"number":1471,"title":"Chapter 1471: How far can you go?","paragraphs":["The Blood Prince stared in utter shock at the two Dao Emperors standing in front of him. As if this were not enough, the other Dao Kings started reforming one after the other.","The soul energy scattered throughout the battlefield surged back toward them, gathering into streams of misty-white light that rapidly reconstructed the bodies that had been destroyed only moments earlier.","Some returned surrounded by fire, others by lightning, frost, darkness, sword intent, and dozens of different Dao authorities, until the empty spaces the Blood Prince had carved through Liam’s army began filling almost as quickly as he had created them.","Within moments, the hundreds of identical figures once again surrounded the battlefield.","The Blood Prince’s expression stiffened.","He had assumed the destroyed incarnations were being sacrificed to create the two Dao Emperors, which would at least have placed some comprehensible limitation upon Liam’s technique.","Creating an Emperor from the accumulated foundations of several Kings was already absurd beyond reason, but if those Kings were permanently consumed in the process, then there was still an exchange taking place.","Yet the avatars were returning.","Their auras were weaker than before, and several flickered slightly as their bodies stabilized, but their foundations remained unmistakably within the Dao King realm.","The energy Liam had drawn from them hadn’t destroyed what they were; somehow, he had taken enough from their accumulated power to push two avatars across the boundary while preserving the structures that allowed the others to reconstruct.","How was this possible? No. This monster has to be cut down today no matter what. Otherwise, if he were allowed to grow more, there is no telling what could happen.","The Blood Prince gritted his teeth and took out a token. At the same time, a pair of crimson eyes opened in a distant world. \"What happened? My dearest little brother offended someone whom he should not have?\"","The Blood Prince’s expression immediately darkened. \"Shut up.\"","A soft laugh came through the token.","That laugh alone made several of the ancient vampires still alive on the battlefield stiffen. They recognized the voice, and although none dared interrupt, more than one instinctively lowered their head.","The Blood Prince ignored them. \"I need you here.\"","\"You need me?\"","\"Yes.\"","Another brief silence followed. Then the voice returned, much more interested than before. \"Now I really want to know what you’ve managed to get yourself into. The last time you asked me for help, half a galaxy disappeared, and you still spent the next ten thousand years insisting you had everything under control.\"","\"I said I need you here.\"","\"Yes, yes, I heard you.\" The distant figure sounded delighted. \"I’m simply enjoying the moment.\"","The Blood Prince’s grip tightened around the token. A crack appeared along its edge.","His elder brother laughed again. \"Careful. Break that and you’ll have to solve your own problem.\"","The Blood Prince nearly crushed it anyway. Then another wave of Dao Emperor pressure rolled across the battlefield. His expression changed.","The crimson Liam had taken another step forward. The enormous crimson moon behind the avatar rotated slowly as his newly formed Dao Emperor authority continued stabilizing, while the Divine Dao Emperor remained farther away, surrounded by endless golden inscriptions.","Around them, hundreds of reconstructed Dao Kings steadily recovered, their weakened auras growing stronger with every passing moment.","The Blood Prince no longer had time for pride.","\"Come to Green Mountain.\"","\"Green Mountain?\" His elder brother paused. \"Never heard of it.\"","\"An insignificant world.\"","\"And an insignificant world forced the mighty Blood Prince to call his elder brother?\"","The Blood Prince’s eyes twitched. \"There is an irregular here.\"","\"Hmmm?\"","\"He is only a Transcendent, but he has hundreds of Dao King soul incarnations and two Dao Emperor soul incarnations.\"","\"Little brother.\"","\"What?\"","\"Have you been drinking?\"","The Blood Prince’s face went black. \"Fuck you.\"","The next second, the connection broke. Good, his brother was coming. The Blood Prince raised his head. His crimson eyes met Liam’s. \"I underestimated you, but you will die today.\"","He barely finished talking when an even more powerful aura erupted. The whole world started cracking apart, unable to bear it any longer. Several of the dao kings and the lower-level cultivators instantly got crushed.","Naturally, Liam sucked in all of the soul energy without fail. His face still did not show any signs of fear. He calmly looked on as the powerful aura descended. In the background, some of his soul avatars even continued with the slaughter, slowly pulling in more and more soul energy.","Every single person assembled here was a monster in their own right. They had centuries of cultivation under their belt. So each kill was extremely valuable. Since he had already decided to go all out here, Liam was not planning to let off even a single person.","The stage was set for carnage, and everyone had to die. By now, many of the vampires, the divine priests and paladins, and most of the others gathered in Green Mountain had already died. However, the Blood Prince seemed to no longer care about that.","He stared at Liam with raging killing intent as people behind him died left and right. Beside him, the powerful aura continued building up as an enormous tornado of crimson formed. The pressure on the world became even more unbearable.","Even Liam had to dismiss all of his Dao Kings. Now only his two Dao Emperors remained standing.","As for the others, some managed to escape using this disturbance. But most simply died. In the distance, the Green Mountain ancestor quickly shot up and started a teleportation circle. But Itzel’s sister interrupted him. \"It’s not necessary.\"","She then took out a treasure that instantaneously formed a protective bubble around them. \"We should be safe here.\"","The Green Mountain ancestor examined the barrier for a moment before nodding in agreement. \"Good stuff. You people really are rich,\" the old man muttered.","Itzel’s sister ignored him. Her expression had become unusually serious as she stared through the barrier. \"This isn’t merely another Dao Emperor.\"","The old man’s smile faded slightly. \"I noticed.\"","Karim swallowed. \"Young Mistress, who is coming?\"","She didn’t answer immediately. She didn’t need to. The surviving vampires already knew.","The Blood Prince finally smiled. \"He’s here.\"","Liam heard him. His misty-white eyes remained fixed upon the tornado.","The pressure had already forced him to dismiss every Dao King avatar. The two Dao Emperors remained outside, one surrounded by the crimson moon while the other stood amid layers of golden-white divine inscriptions, but neither looked as relaxed as before.","That alone told Liam enough. Whoever was coming was stronger than the Blood Prince.","The crimson tornado suddenly stopped expanding. For a fraction of a second, the world became completely silent. Then boom! Crimson light devoured the sky. Blood rivers started flowing. Blood rain started pouring.","The remaining mountains throughout Green Mountain cracked apart as a figure slowly emerged from the center of the storm.","The newly ascended crimson Liam narrowed his eyes. His blood moon trembled. Then the newcomer opened his eyes. Two crimson pupils appeared within the storm.","DONG!","The crimson Liam was forced backward. His feet tore two enormous trenches through the ruined ground before he stabilized himself several kilometers away. At almost the same instant, the Divine Dao Emperor released a wave of golden authority.","Liam felt his chest tighten. His soul trembled.","The Blood Prince had been terrifying after revealing his Dao Emperor cultivation, but Liam’s two newly ascended Emperors had at least been capable of resisting him. The existence descending now felt completely different.","The depth behind the aura was so enormous that comparing it to his newly ascended avatars almost felt unfair.","The Blood Prince laughed.","\"Here! This is my brother!\" He spread his arms toward the figure descending through the rivers of blood as though presenting some supreme treasure. \"He is a Blood Sovereign! What can you do now? Can you become a Sovereign now?\"","The words struck the remaining cultivators like thunder. Inside the protective barrier, Itzel’s sister went completely still. The Green Mountain Ancestor’s eyes narrowed.","The Blood Prince was a Dao Emperor, an existence already powerful enough to suppress Dao Kings through sheer cultivation and turn the entire battle around by himself. Yet the newcomer had crossed even that boundary.","A Sovereign.","The Blood Prince’s elder brother finally stepped out of the crimson storm.","He was a remarkably handsome man who looked to be somewhere in his early thirties, with long dark-red hair falling loosely across his shoulders and crimson eyes almost identical to those of the Blood Prince.","Unlike his younger brother, however, he wore nothing extravagant, only simple black robes embroidered with thin crimson lines, while a faint smile rested upon his face.","The Blood Sovereign glanced toward his younger brother. \"Are you showing me off, little brother?\"","The Blood Prince’s smile stiffened. \"What?\"","The Sovereign chuckled. \"You haven’t changed at all. How many years has it been, and you’re still running around telling people how impressive your elder brother is?\"","\"I wasn’t showing you off!\"","\"Of course.\"","\"I was explaining his situation!\"","\"Naturally.\"","The Blood Prince’s expression went black.","The Blood Sovereign was still smiling when his gaze finally shifted toward Liam. More specifically, toward the crimson Liam standing beneath the blood moon. His smile vanished.","The Blood Prince noticed immediately. \"What?\"","The Sovereign didn’t answer. His crimson eyes had narrowed as they examined the avatar with an intensity that hadn’t existed moments earlier.","The newly ascended Vampire Dao Emperor stared back at him. For several seconds, neither moved. Then the Blood Sovereign looked toward the Divine Dao Emperor. His expression changed again.","His perception spread across the two bodies, examining their structure, their foundations, the strange soul energy from which they had been formed, and finally the almost invisible connection extending from both of them toward somewhere else.","The Sovereign’s eyes widened slightly. \"This...\" He appeared directly before the crimson avatar.","The Blood Prince barely saw him move. The Sovereign raised one hand and placed two fingers against the avatar’s shoulder. Crimson Liam immediately struck.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","His fist passed through empty space. The Blood Sovereign had already moved several meters away. He wasn’t looking at the avatar anymore. He was looking at the place where his fingers had touched it. \"Soul body.\"","The Blood Prince frowned. \"I told you. They’re soul incarnations.\"","His brother ignored him. The Sovereign’s eyes slowly brightened. \"Independent Dao foundation...\" His perception swept across the avatar again. \"Independent cultivation.\" Then toward the Divine Emperor. \"Yet both are connected to the same source.\" His expression became increasingly strange.","The Blood Prince finally became impatient. \"Yes! That is what I was trying to explain!\"","\"No.\" The Blood Sovereign shook his head. \"You don’t understand. You cannot win here. No matter what you do, you will only end up deeper and deeper in his trap.\"","The Blood Prince paused. His brother looked toward the crimson avatar again. Then he asked quietly, \"Where did you find him? Where did you find the Soul Weaver?\"","The Blood Prince’s expression changed. \"Soul Weaver?\"","The Sovereign looked back toward the avatar. \"So you don’t even know who you’re fighting?\"","Something about his tone bothered the Blood Prince. \"Who is a Soul Weaver?\"","The Sovereign didn’t answer immediately. His crimson eyes continued examining the two avatars. Then he laughed softly. \"Someone whom you should never have engaged in the first place. Now run.\""]},{"number":1472,"title":"Chapter 1472: All gone?","paragraphs":["The Blood Prince gritted his teeth indignantly. He was not one to flee from a fight, and now he was forced to do so. It did not sit well with him. He opened his mouth to say something to his brother when suddenly a frighteningly powerful aura erupted from the soul avatar.","\"He... He is breaking through again?\" Blood Prince felt as if his mind was about to explode. What was this reality unfolding in front of him? He opened his mouth again when the sovereign forcefully shoved him into a teleportation circle.","\"Do you still not get it? He is strong because of the armies you brought to his doorstep! Soulweavers devour to reach the pinnacle. I told you to leave, didn’t I!\"","The teleportation circle closed quickly and the spell activated, but the Blood Prince could still feel it. The aura that emerged newly was none other than the aura of a Sovereign! He listlessly collapsed on the ground, kneeling down, his eyes empty.","Someone actually broke through to the Sovereign realm in a matter of minutes. No, not even minutes. They achieved that breakthrough in seconds. Then what was the meaning of his goddamn life?","What the hell had he been doing up until now? What were all those years of cultivation for? What was the point of the countless secret realms he had entered, the bloodlines he had devoured, the enemies he had killed, the treasures he had fought over, and the endless years he had spent comprehending the Blood Dao?","He had nearly died more times than he could remember. He had once spent three thousand years trapped at a single bottleneck. He had considered himself fortunate when he finally broke through.","And that bastard had just gone from Dao King to Dao Emperor and then from Dao Emperor to Sovereign while they were standing there watching.","The Blood Prince remained on his knees.","Xerathuna appeared beside him a moment later, thrown through the teleportation passage by the Sovereign just before it closed. She stumbled several steps before stabilizing herself, her robes torn and her normally immaculate appearance reduced to a miserable state.","She looked toward the Blood Prince. \"My love—\"","The Blood Prince raised one hand. \"Don’t.\"","Xerathuna froze. He slowly rose to his feet, but he didn’t spare her another glance. His expression remained hollow as he brushed the dust from his robes.","\"I have some work to do.\"","\"What work?\"","The Blood Prince ignored her. Xerathuna reached for him, but he casually flung her aside with a wave of his hand and disappeared into the depths of the Blood Court.","Xerathuna landed several dozen meters away. Her expression darkened. \"That bastard.\" She pushed herself upright and glared in the direction he had disappeared.","\"Did he really think only he could call upon a Sovereign?\" The more she thought about it, the more irritated she became.","The Blood Prince had summoned his elder brother and suddenly acted as though the appearance of a Sovereign had changed everything. Worse, even that Sovereign had ordered them to flee without attempting to finish Liam.","Both of them were just cowards, good-for-nothing cowards!","Xerathuna’s golden third eye flickered. \"My father is already a Dao Emperor. He is standing at the very peak of the realm. He has been preparing for his breakthrough for years, and everyone knows he could become a Sovereign at any time.\"","She lifted her chin. \"When Father breaks through, I would like to see who dares humiliate me like this again.\"","Her father was no ordinary cultivator. His position within the Celestial Court was immense, his Divine Dao had been refined across countless years, and even among Dao Emperors, few dared provoke him casually. His breakthrough was merely a matter of time.","Then he would become a Sovereign as well. What was there to fear?","Liam had simply reached the realm slightly earlier through some grotesque Soulweaver method. That was all.","Xerathuna’s expression gradually relaxed. In fact, the more she thought about it, the more obvious the explanation became.","\"That fucking rat.\" Her hands clenched. \"This is all because of him!\"","She remembered the humiliation of being forced to her knees beneath the Divine avatar’s authority, the slaughter of the Celestial Court forces she had brought with her, and worst of all, the expression on Liam’s face throughout the entire battle. That damned smile.","\"I will kill him.\" Golden light flashed around her. \"I will fucking kill him one day, even if he dares to become a damned God!\"","She paused and then snorted. \"As if he will ever become one.\" Her anger slowly transformed into contempt. \"The damned fool probably burnt all of his potential today.\"","She begrudgingly stood up and took out a token. She then vanished, reappearing in the Celestial court. She was just about to barge into her father’s palace to vent all her grievances when suddenly a few new system notifications caught her eye.","\"Hmmm? What is going on with the soul collector?\" She immediately teleported again to take a look. While many things needed her attention at the moment, this one was still the top priority.","She hurriedly walked over to the main domain where the grand array was set up. There were a total of five hundred array crystals, and all of them were active. So the problem was not with the array or the array crystals. Then what could be the issue?","Xerathuna tiredly pondered as she examined everything. Her gaze finally landed on the artifact that was starting to take shape. An excited gleam appeared in her eyes as soon as she saw the artifact. This was it. This would be the ultimate weapon that would cement her ascension into Godhood.","With this weapon, she would become the Celestial Goddess who ruled over millions of galaxies! With this weapon, there would be no one who could stop her!","Xerathuna could already imagine crushing that little rat and whatever tricks he had. With a weapon like this, no matter what parlour tricks the rat used, it would all amount to nothing.","Xerathuna’s breathing steadied. A smile returned to her face.","She reached out and ran her fingers through one of the streams feeding the artifact. Countless indistinct whispers brushed against her consciousness before disappearing into the golden light.","Soon she wouldn’t have to tolerate anyone looking down upon her again.","The Blood Prince could crawl back and apologize if he wanted. His brother could keep running from every fucking Soulweaver he encountered. Even her father—","Xerathuna stopped. Her gaze moved back toward the stream beneath her hand. Something had changed. She frowned and touched it again. The pale river continued flowing normally.","Xerathuna watched it for several breaths before turning toward the nearest array crystal. By the time she had inspected the twentieth crystal, irritation had begun replacing her excitement.","\"What the hell?\" She flicked her hand. Golden symbols appeared before her.","Only 1.72%? Xerathuna blinked in a daze.","The five hundred crystals were active. She could feel every one of them. The spatial channels remained connected, and soul energy was clearly pouring into the domain from countless collection points. Yet the artifact was starving?","Then where the heck was all the soul energy going? Could her father or someone else from the Celestial court... Impossible! Except for her, no one even had access to this domain. It was only open to her and-","Her thoughts froze as a frightening possibility surfaced. The training world! Someone could have entered the training world and accessed the grand array!","Immediately, everything began clicking into place, and a familiar face popped up in her mind. Xerathuna’s entire body trembled from top to bottom as she slumped lifelessly on the ground.","Liam!","All those overpowered breakthroughs and the appearance of hundreds of soul clones... Xerathuna’s eyes slowly moved toward the pale stream flowing into the unfinished artifact. Her lips trembled. \"No... No... No...\"","Had that bastard actually used her for everything? From the beginning, he had planned all of this and used her own grand array for his ascension?","Xerathuna’s breathing became increasingly uneven. She remembered the training world.","The first time she had seen Liam there, he had been nothing. An insignificant mortal struggling through a place designed to grind down countless challengers and harvest what remained. She hadn’t even bothered to remember how weak he had been.","Then he escaped. After that, everything had gone wrong. Her fingers slowly curled against the ground. It was over. It was truly all over.","Her centuries of hard work, the countless resources she had poured into the training world, the formations she had secretly constructed, the favors she had traded, the worlds she had connected one after another to the grand array... all of it had been for this moment.","Her gaze drifted toward the unfinished artifact.","Golden light continued flowing across its surface, but it suddenly looked painfully thin to her. The magnificent object that had seemed only a short distance from completion now appeared hollow, almost skeletal, with entire sections flickering as the grand array struggled to fill them.","Xerathuna stared at it. She had imagined this moment so many times. The artifact completing, the heavens shaking, her stepping beyond her father, beyond the Blood Prince, beyond every bastard who had ever looked at her and seen only the daughter of someone greater.","Her fingers trembled. \"Mine...\" Her voice came out hoarse. She dragged herself toward the artifact. \"This was supposed to be mine.\" The golden barrier surrounding it stopped her hand.","Xerathuna pressed her palm against it anyway. For centuries, whenever something went wrong, she had simply pushed harder. More resources. More cultivators. More worlds. More souls. There had always been something else she could sacrifice to keep the project moving.","Now the number hovering beside the artifact remained unchanged.","1.72%.","Xerathuna stared at it until her vision blurred. She had to start all over now? How? How could she even fathom doing something like that? She couldn’t possibly operate outside the system rules once more! The price would be unbearable! The system would simply decimate her into nothingness!","Xerathuna smiled. What the hell? \"Ha...\" Her shoulders shook as she started laughing. \"Haha...\" She covered her face. \"Hahahaha...\" The laughter soon turned into rage-filled wailing screams as she completely broke down."]},{"number":1473,"title":"Chapter 1473: I will win everytime","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, back on the battlefield...","The Blood Sovereign stared at Liam. He had watched countless geniuses rise and fall over the ages, and he had personally witnessed more than one Dao Emperor attempt this very breakthrough.","Some had prepared for hundreds of thousands of years only to fail at the final step. Others had succeeded, but even the shortest breakthrough he had ever witnessed had required years of preparation and months of seclusion while the cultivator’s soul underwent its final transformation.","The thing in front of him had done it while fighting.","How powerful!","His crimson eyes narrowed, and then a smile formed on his face. This was exactly what he wanted.","\"A Soulweaver, huh... I have been wanting to fight one for a long time now. Come. Don’t disappoint me.\"","Liam grinned in return. He knew the feeling all too well. He inhaled, feeling power surging within him, so vast and violent that his entire existence seemed to hum beneath it. He had never felt so powerful in his entire lifetime.","His soul was exploding with infinite potential.","It was no longer merely larger or stronger. It had become something fundamentally different, as though a door he had spent his entire existence pushing against had finally opened and revealed an endless world beyond it. Every strand of his soul felt alive, endlessly malleable, capable of becoming something greater than it had been only a moment before.","And Liam was ready. He wanted to know how far he could go. More than that, he wanted to enjoy it. After everything he had endured to reach this point, he wanted to revel in the power he had fought so hard to obtain.","Karakaboom!","Lightning split the heavens. The Blood Sovereign vanished. Liam moved at the same instant.","BOOM!","A crimson fist collided with Liam’s fiery palm. The impact tore the battlefield apart. Space fractured around them in concentric rings, while the earth beneath Liam’s feet collapsed for hundreds of miles as the force of their collision plunged deep into the planet. Mountains in the distance shattered before the sound of the strike even reached them.","Liam’s eyes widened slightly.","The Blood Sovereign smiled. Then his other fist struck Liam in the ribs.","CRACK!","Liam disappeared. His body tore through several mountains before smashing into the ground and carving a trench across the continent.","\"Fuck.\" He rose from the rubble and rolled his shoulder.","The Blood Sovereign descended from above, moving casually through the ruined sky. \"Powerful,\" he said. \"But inexperienced. Just gimmicks alone cannot make you a real sovereign. You cannot defeat me.\" He disappeared again.","Liam grinned. This time, he saw him.","Liam twisted aside as a crimson blade sliced through the place where his neck had been, then drove his elbow backward. The Blood Sovereign blocked it with his forearm, and Liam immediately followed with a kick that sent the ancient Sovereign hurtling across the battlefield.","The Blood Sovereign stopped himself after several hundred miles. His face changed. Something was different. This was not the power that belonged to a newly ascended sovereign.","Across from him, Liam was burning.","White-golden hair drifted behind him. Flames crawled across his skin, flowing across his arms, chest, and face. His eyes had changed as well, their pupils swallowed by white-golden fire.","Before the Blood Sovereign could react, a sphere of white-golden fire erupted outward and swallowed thousands of miles in an instant.","The Blood Sovereign was hurled backward, his crimson robes burning as he tore through several layers of shattered reality before forcing himself to stop. He had barely stabilized when Liam appeared above him.","Liam brought his heel down. The Blood Sovereign crossed both arms.","BOOOOOOM!","The Blood Sovereign plummeted toward the earth like a crimson meteor and struck the ground hard enough to make the entire continent jump. A circular wall of shattered rock erupted around the impact point, rising thousands of miles into the sky before being vaporized by the white-golden fire following Liam’s strike.","Liam descended after him, throwing a punch.","The Blood Sovereign rolled aside, evading the attack. Liam hit the ground instead.","An enormous fissure split outward, extending beyond the horizon, while molten rock exploded from the depths. Liam barely looked at the destruction before twisting around and blocking a crimson spear that appeared beside his head.","Another came from behind. Then ten more.","Liam’s eyes flashed. White-golden fire exploded from his body. The spears melted before touching him.","The Blood Sovereign appeared inside the flames. His fist slammed into Liam’s face.","Liam’s head snapped sideways. His hand immediately shot out and caught the Blood Sovereign’s wrist.","The Blood Sovereign gritted his teeth. \"How are you this strong? It is simply impossible for you to possess powers like this!\"","Liam grinned through the blood running from his lip. Of course, it was impossible, but thanks to the thousands of dragon souls in his black dragon sword, he was able to make the impossible possible.","Soul avatars might have a weaker foundation, but what if the soul avatars were built with dragon soul threads as the foundation?","Liam had gone into the Green Mountain treasure land for two reasons. One for the Dralura souls and the other for finally breaking apart his black dragon sword.","Perhaps one day he might be able to forge that sword to perfection, but right now he was not at that level. So Liam decided to use the sword more creatively. Instead of building it up, he tore it apart.","Just like he had hoped, he found soul thread fibers inside the dragon souls. Even if their rank was not as high as that of an Archon or the vampire or the demon, they still possessed soul threads. Most probably because of the superiority of their race.","This was the catalyst Liam needed. His growth exploded instantly. He created one soul thread after another, and thanks to the cauldron, he was able to weave soul avatars in hundreds. In the blink of an eye, he had an army of 999 soul avatars.","After that, everything fell into place quickly. He had already personally amassed a shit ton of souls. On top of that, there were the dralura souls, which were Dao rich. Finally, he even took another gamble.","Knowing that the priestess would be busy hunting him down before the mark wore off, he tried accessing the tutorial world again. None of the teleportation scrolls or tokens worked, but he had another cheat called Luna. In the end, she was able to teleport him to the game world.","After that, it did not even take him a second to locate the enormous soul core brimming with soul energy. For the risk he took, there was also another reward waiting for him. Through the single soul core, he was able to access many other soul cores connected to it.","It had to be some sort of grand array formation. Liam did not care. The moment he got access to it, he instantly drained it dry. With the 999 soul avatars working hard, he quickly amassed memories and Dao fragments. One by one, the breakthroughs quickly followed.","Liam laughed like a maniac as his forehead smashed into the Blood Sovereign’s face.","CRACK!","Blood sprayed. The Blood Sovereign staggered backward.","\"Why? Why can’t I become strong? Because I am nobody?\" Liam followed him and punched him. One punch after another, he continued pummeling him.","Each strike came faster than the last, white-golden fire gathering around Liam’s fists until every blow detonated with the force of a collapsing star. The Blood Sovereign blocked the first few, deflected another, then took one directly across the jaw. His head snapped sideways.","\"You think just because I am a nobody you can kick me around? You think just because I am a nobody you can kill my family? My world? The weak can also fight back one day!\"","Liam’s knee drove into his stomach. The Blood Sovereign folded. Liam grabbed him by the head and threw him. The ancient Sovereign disappeared through three mountains, blasting apart everything in his path.","Liam immediately followed. The Blood Sovereign had barely torn himself free from the collapsing mountain when Liam appeared in front of him again.","BOOM!","A fist buried itself in his chest.","The Blood Sovereign bent around the strike, blood exploding from his mouth as the force blasted through his body and detonated the mountain range behind him. Before he could recover, Liam grabbed him by the throat and carried him through the air, accelerating until the landscape beneath them blurred into streaks of molten stone and shattered earth.","\"You want to know why I am this strong?\"","Liam slammed him downward.","KABOOOOOM!","The Blood Sovereign crashed into the ground.","Liam followed him into the crater.","\"Because while people like you were sitting on thrones deciding who was allowed to live and who was allowed to die, I was fighting for every fucking thing I had!\"","His fist descended.","The Blood Sovereign twisted aside.","Liam’s punch struck the ground and collapsed another enormous section of the continent, but the Blood Sovereign was already behind him, five crimson claws slicing toward Liam’s spine.","SHRIIIIK!","The claws tore through him from shoulder to waist. Soul energy exploded from Liam’s back. The Blood Sovereign drove his palm forward.","\"Blood Ruin.\"","BOOM!","Liam disappeared into the horizon.","For several seconds, the Blood Sovereign remained where he was. Blood dripped from his broken nose. One side of his chest had collapsed inward. Several ribs protruded through torn flesh, while white-golden flames continued burning stubbornly across his robes and skin. He threw his head back and roared.","The wounds began closing. Bone pulled itself back into place. Torn flesh knitted together as blood surged through his body, and even the flames clinging to him were slowly drowned beneath a layer of dense crimson energy.","In the distance, a white-golden explosion erupted. Liam shot back toward him. The Blood Sovereign raised his gaze, vanishing from his spot. Their fists met once again.","BOOM!","Hundreds of crimson afterimages surrounded Liam as the Blood Sovereign attacked from every direction, each strike landing with terrifying precision. The crimson eyes filled with rage were locked onto him, unwilling to give him a single opening.","Liam’s eyes flashed. He caught the next fist, but the Blood Sovereign was fast. His arm dissolved into blood, and Liam’s hand closed on nothing. The Blood Sovereign reformed behind him and slammed both palms against Liam’s back.","BOOOOOOM!","Liam smashed through the ground. The Blood Sovereign descended after him. \"You die today.\" His foot struck Liam in the chest. The earth collapsed around them.","Liam caught him and turned the table. A red hot fire beam blasted the guy. In the chaos, a blood-red hand punched Liam down. Blood and fire continued clashing until finally, the two could no longer go on.","The Blood Sovereign walked out of the inferno. Half his face was gone. His left arm had been reduced to charred bone, while an enormous hole had been burned directly through his stomach. White-golden fire still crawled across his body, eating away at flesh almost as quickly as it regenerated.","On the other side, Liam did not bother answering him. He only smiled before his aura erupted again. The Blood Sovereign smiled bitterly, immediately recognizing what was happening.","\"I will win every time.\" Liam grinned.","The Blood Sovereign stared incredulously for a moment. However, before Liam could break through, a tremendously powerful force ripped through space out of nowhere. Unable to endure any more abuse, the entire world finally gave up.","KRAAAAAK!","A fracture split across the heavens. Then another and another. An insane amount of energy gathered in the core of the world.","The entire fucking world was exploding. From past experience, Liam knew exactly how dangerous this was, so he instantly teleported out of the vicinity. He stood in space in the middle of nowhere, watching the distant planet tear itself apart.","An impossible amount of energy blasted outward. Liam immediately teleported further away. Waves after waves of destruction followed.","The shockwave passed through the place where he had been standing and continued expanding through space, ripping apart asteroids, swallowing distant moons, and leaving behind a massive distortion that stretched across the void.","Several million miles away, Liam reappeared.","And the moment he did, all of a sudden, he was face to face with that same tremendously powerful aura. He was face to face with a God!","Liam froze. The being in front of him did not look particularly impressive. There was no gigantic body stretching across the stars, no monstrous aura blazing across the void, and no heavenly phenomenon announcing its arrival.","A man simply stood there, barefoot in space, wearing loose white robes. He had pitch-black hair and dark crimson eyes and looked extremely young.","Liam wouldn’t even have known who it was if not for the memories he inherited from the vampire. This was their God, the man nicknamed the Blood God, the ruler of the Blood Court."]},{"number":1474,"title":"Chapter 1474: In front of a God...","paragraphs":["Liam clenched his fists. He was hoping it wouldn’t come to this. He was hoping that a God wouldn’t just randomly appear, but it turned out he was wrong. It was fine. Even though he was hoping for a lucky break, he already knew what was going to happen.","He would only be a fool if he thought he could get away with everything this easily. This world was such. To live, one needs to sacrifice. This finale was inevitable. He had already prepared for it.","He focused inward in his soul space where the last two of his soul avatars rested. Both of them were unique and completely different from the other soul avatars. In fact, they already possessed a complete Dao body.","One had the symbol of a cauldron tattooed on its chest, while the other had a draconian symbol tattooed. Just from a glance, one could tell that immense power rested within them.","Liam was just about to wake one up when suddenly an amused chuckle sounded.","\"Relax, soulweaver. I am not here to fight you. I just came to bring back this one.\" The Blood God waved his hand, and the next second the Blood Sovereign appeared next to him, completely whole and healed. On the other side, the Blood Prince stood with contempt plastered on his face.","Surprisingly, both of them looked almost as shocked as Liam after hearing the Blood God’s words.","\"No, my God, he—\" The Blood Prince opened his mouth when the Blood God turned his head. The Blood Prince froze, every trace of color disappearing from his face.","\"Did I ask for your opinion?\"","The Blood Prince closed his mouth and stood with his head bowed down. The Blood God then turned back to Liam. \"Good to meet the current generation’s soulweaver. You can reach out to me if you need any help with the soul temple’s ruins.\"","Soul Temple ruins?","Liam’s eyes narrowed. Before he could decide whether he actually wanted to engage a God in conversation, the other party chuckled once more. Then he disappeared. The Blood Sovereign and Blood Prince vanished with him.","There was no spatial tear, no burst of power, and not even the slightest disturbance in the surrounding void. All three of them disappeared just like that.","On a distant world with a crimson sky, the Blood God reappeared along with the two guys. Almost immediately, the Blood Prince shot to the ground, kneeling and bowing his head but saying his piece.","\"My God! That bastard should have died today. Please tell me why you chose to let him off? He is just a Dao King who temporarily overshot the ranks. He is nothing. So please tell me why is he not dead right now?\"","The Blood Sovereign also clenched his fists as if he wanted to ask the same thing.","The Blood God, however, said nothing. He simply began walking.","They had appeared atop an enormous black palace suspended over a sea of blood. Crimson clouds rolled beneath its foundations, while distant towers pierced the horizon like spears. Countless figures bowed the instant the Blood God’s presence spread across the world, yet he paid none of them any attention.","The Blood Prince remained kneeling. \"My God?\" He asked again, refused to let this go.","The Blood God stopped. Then he looked back. \"Brat, have you become so useless that you cannot even see a God that too when he is staring right at your face?\"","Huh? God? Blood God? The Blood Prince looked confused for a moment before he fully understood what his God meant. Shock and dread filled his face as the answer truly sank in. He was already a God...?","Not bothering to explain anymore, the Blood God continued walking while mumbling a few words.","\"Besides, you got to think about many things. Do you know why that divine savior bastard never showed up today? This matter should have involved him directly yet he didn’t turn up. As always they just wanted us to fight with each other, thin down the dark faction numbers.\"","\"Whether you realize or not, the grand war is right at our doorstep. So stop messing with your pet priestess and get to work. Achieve some breakthroughs instead of whining.\"","\"Also, do you know how annoying soulweavers are? They are like bloodroaces. You can never truly kill one. You try to kill one and a small soul sliver escapes from you. Then bam, one million years later, the guy comes back to stab you in the back.\"","\"I am not doing that again.\" The Blood God laughed a little and then disappeared.","Both the Blood Prince and the Blood Sovereign could only continue to stare in shock. That man had really become a God already?","****","Liam found himself standing in space all by himself, surrounded on all sides by darkness so vast and absolute that even the distant stars seemed strangely fragile against it.","Behind him, the remains of the destroyed world were still burning, enormous streams of molten rock and shattered land drifting through the void while waves of residual energy slowly dissipated into nothingness.","Only after several more breaths did some of the tension finally leave his shoulders. He relaxed, letting the two soul avatars get back into meditation. They were not needed just yet and he did not want to wake them unnecessarily. The more time he gives them the stronger they will become.","He let out a sigh, taking a look at everything again. Derek, Green Mountain, Itzel and the group had already left the world a long time ago before the fight started. So there was nothing here for him to do. It seemed that the day was finally over.","He silently teleported to his real body which was still in the treasure world and from there Liam teleported back to Earth.","His range was different now. He could teleport right to his home and did not have to go to the system shop. Yet he still decided to stop by the system shop first.","Tilia’s familiar face greeted him.","\"Can you do me a favour? Can you try to collect as many soul strengthening items as possible? But give them to me as you have it. Even one to two to start with is enough.\"","Tilia nodded. She looked at the condition Liam was in and added a few more items to that list.","\"You are always very thoughtful.\" Liam chuckled, seeing the fairy blush. Then unexpectedly, he pulled her closer and gave her a small kiss on the cheek. \"Thank you for everything.\"","Tilia froze. Liam gave her a nod and then walked to his house. Mei Mei, Alex, Shen Yue, Rey, and everyone had already gathered at his house. Derek, the two demonesses, Green Mountain and even Itzel and her sister were there at his house.","Itzel’s sister immediately shot up as soon as she saw Liam. \"I apologize for my earlier attitude. I didn’t mean to-\" However, she was cut off by everyone else rushing over to Liam.","Shen Yue, Alex, Mei Mei and the two demonesses hurriedly ran to Liam and wanted to hug him but Luna beat them to it. She hugged Liam first and pushed everyone else away with her tails.","\"Come on, Luna. This is not fair. He is my brother first.\" Mei Mei pouted.","Shen Yue smiled and did not say anything while Alex simply looked worried. The demonesses on the other hand looked as if they were prepared to go at it with Luna.","Luna did not care at all. She was focused on venting her greivances. \"Why did you fight without me, Master? Why did you not take me with you?\" She continued baraging him with questions.","\"I was only able to fight because you were here guarding everyone.\" Liam laughed helplessly. He was tired, way too tired and simply allowed the idiot to do whatever she wanted.","\"What fight? What happened?\" Everyone had a million questions.","Liam only smiled. \"I brought home a gift.\" He mysteriously said. He then gently retreived someone from his soul space.","Mia’s slender figure appeared in the house.","\"Mia!\" Both Alex and Rey shouted at the same time and rushed to her.","Mia smiled softly. She looked weak and fragile and her boddy wobbled. Both Alex and Rey caught her before she fell.","\"She is fine now. She is just a little weak. Don’t worry, Alex.\" Liam reassured them and then fully collapsed on Luna’s arms. He was completely drained. The last thing he felt was Luna’s tails wrapping around him possessively as she carried him somewhere.","Liam smiled as his eyes slowly closed, and within seconds, sleep claimed him. For the first time in longer than he could remember, he drifted off without fear, without another battle waiting in the back of his mind, and without a single worry weighing on his heart.","When he woke up, the entire world broke into celebrations.","The battle itself had been impossible to hide. Sovereign-level energy had shaken multiple worlds, an entire planet had been destroyed, and countless powerful cultivators had witnessed pieces of what happened before evacuating. The word had spread far and wide.","Liam walked into the living room and everyone quickly arrived one after the other. Mei Mei, Alex, Shen Yue, Mia, Rey, Madan, the Oracle, even the monk. The whole group was there. Derek was standing right beside his sister and his mother and smiling brightly. Even Green Mountain, Itzel and her sister had hung around to wait until Liam was once again awake.","Liam smiled at everyone. He was home."]}]);
